__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"classLore",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return l}});var n=r(d[0]);const t=(0,n.datasetSource)('wiki-class-by-race'),l=[(0,n.lore)({category:'class',slug:'mage',subjectId:'mage',order:1,era:'elder-kingdoms',title:{en:'Mage',tr:'Mage'},summary:{en:'Heirs of the Highborne and the first human magi, mages bend raw arcane power, and every age of the story turns on one of them.',tr:'Highborne\u2019un ve ilk insan b\xfcy\xfcc\xfclerin miras\xe7\u0131lar\u0131 olan Mage\u2019ler saf arkan g\xfcc\xfc b\xfcker; hik\xe2yenin her \xe7a\u011f\u0131 onlardan birinin etraf\u0131nda d\xf6ner.'},body:{en:["Mages wield the arcane, the raw magic of order that once welled up from the Well of Eternity. The night elves' Highborne were the first great sorcerers, and their exiled descendants, the high elves of Quel'Thalas, taught the art to a hundred humans during the Troll Wars. Those first human magi went on to found Dalaran, where the Kirin Tor still guard the secrets of spellcraft.","Every age of the story turns on a mage: Medivh, the last Guardian; his apprentice Khadgar, who destroyed the Dark Portal; Archmage Antonidas, who died defending Dalaran; and Jaina Proudmoore, who now rules Theramore. In year 25 new students train in Stormwind's Mage Quarter and the Undercity's Magic Quarter, and gnome and troll mages have long stood beside humans and Forsaken. Forever opens the path to orcs, whose spellcasters once knew only shamanism and fel magic, and to the High Order, the only Skyborne who may become mages."],tr:["Mage\u2019ler arkan\u0131, yani bir zamanlar Sonsuzluk Kuyusu\u2019ndan kaynayan saf d\xfczen b\xfcy\xfcs\xfcn\xfc kullan\u0131r. \u0130lk b\xfcy\xfck b\xfcy\xfcc\xfcler gece elflerinin Highborne\u2019uydu; onlar\u0131n s\xfcrg\xfcn torunlar\u0131 olan Quel'Thalas y\xfcksek elfleri, Trol Sava\u015flar\u0131 s\u0131ras\u0131nda bu sanat\u0131 y\xfcz insana \xf6\u011fretti. O ilk insan b\xfcy\xfcc\xfcler, Kirin Tor\u2019un h\xe2l\xe2 b\xfcy\xfcc\xfcl\xfc\u011f\xfcn s\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 korudu\u011fu Dalaran\u2019\u0131 kurdu.",'Hik\xe2yenin her \xe7a\u011f\u0131 bir Mage\u2019in etraf\u0131nda d\xf6ner: son Muhaf\u0131z Medivh; Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019i yok eden \xe7\u0131ra\u011f\u0131 Khadgar; Dalaran\u2019\u0131 savunurken \xf6len Ba\u015fb\xfcy\xfcc\xfc Antonidas; ve \u015fimdi Theramore\u2019u y\xf6neten Jaina Proudmoore. 25. y\u0131lda Stormwind\u2019in Mage Quarter\u2019\u0131nda ve Undercity\u2019nin Magic Quarter\u2019\u0131nda yeni \xf6\u011frenciler yeti\u015fiyor; gnom ve trol Mage\u2019ler de uzun zamand\u0131r insanlar\u0131n ve Forsaken\u2019\u0131n yan\u0131nda. Forever bu yolu, b\xfcy\xfcc\xfcleri bir zamanlar yaln\u0131zca \u015famanl\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve fel b\xfcy\xfcs\xfcn\xfc bilen orklara ve Mage olabilen tek Skyborne olan High Order\u2019a da a\xe7\u0131yor.']},links:{classIds:['mage'],raceIds:['human','gnome','skyborne-high-order','orc','troll','undead'],zoneIds:['alterac-mountains'],loreIds:['chapter:arathor-and-the-troll-wars','chapter:guardians-and-the-seven-kingdoms','chapter:exiles-of-quelthalas','term:kirin-tor','term:guardian-of-tirisfal','item:atiesh']},image:'class:mage',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Mage'),(0,n.wiki)('Kirin Tor'),(0,n.wiki)('Antonidas'),t,n.FOREVER.overview],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'class',slug:'warrior',subjectId:'warrior',order:2,era:'elder-kingdoms',title:{en:'Warrior',tr:'Warrior'},summary:{en:"Every people of Azeroth has its warriors, and much of the world's history was written with their steel.",tr:'Azeroth\u2019un her halk\u0131n\u0131n Warrior\u2019lar\u0131 vard\u0131r ve d\xfcnyan\u0131n tarihinin b\xfcy\xfck k\u0131sm\u0131 onlar\u0131n \xe7eli\u011fiyle yaz\u0131ld\u0131.'},body:{en:["Every people of Azeroth has its warriors, and much of its history was written with their steel. The soldiers of Arathor held Thoradin's Wall against the Amani; dwarven thanes fought for Ironforge in the War of the Three Hammers; orc clans lived by the strength of their champions long before the Horde was forged. Warriors trust training, armor and the fury of battle rather than spells.",'Their heroes fill the chronicles: Anduin Lothar, the Lion of Azeroth, who led the Alliance until he fell at Blackrock Spire; Grom Hellscream, whose sacrifice freed the orcs from demon blood on Mount Hyjal; and Danath Trollbane, who stayed behind in Draenor with the Alliance expedition. In year 25 warriors serve every banner, from the guards of Stormwind to the grunts of Orgrimmar, and every playable race can take up arms. Forever adds the Skyborne of both orders to their ranks.'],tr:['Azeroth\u2019un her halk\u0131n\u0131n Warrior\u2019lar\u0131 vard\u0131r ve tarihinin b\xfcy\xfck k\u0131sm\u0131 onlar\u0131n \xe7eli\u011fiyle yaz\u0131ld\u0131. Arathor askerleri Thoradin\u2019s Wall\u2019u Amani\u2019ye kar\u015f\u0131 tuttu; c\xfcce thane\u2019leri \xdc\xe7 \xc7eki\xe7 Sava\u015f\u0131\u2019nda Ironforge i\xe7in sava\u015ft\u0131; ork klanlar\u0131, Horde kurulmadan \xe7ok \xf6nce \u015fampiyonlar\u0131n\u0131n g\xfcc\xfcyle ya\u015f\u0131yordu. Warrior\u2019lar b\xfcy\xfcye de\u011fil e\u011fitime, z\u0131rha ve sava\u015f \xf6fkesine g\xfcvenir.','Kahramanlar\u0131 tarih kitaplar\u0131n\u0131 doldurur: \u0130ttifak\u2019\u0131 Blackrock Spire\u2019da d\xfc\u015fene dek y\xf6neten Azeroth\u2019un Aslan\u0131 Anduin Lothar; fedak\xe2rl\u0131\u011f\u0131yla Mount Hyjal\u2019da orklar\u0131 iblis kan\u0131ndan kurtaran Grom Hellscream; ve \u0130ttifak seferiyle Draenor\u2019da kalan Danath Trollbane. 25. y\u0131lda Warrior\u2019lar Stormwind muhaf\u0131zlar\u0131ndan Orgrimmar\u2019\u0131n grunt\u2019lar\u0131na kadar her sanca\u011fa hizmet ediyor ve oynanabilir her \u0131rk silaha sar\u0131labiliyor. Forever saflar\u0131na iki Skyborne d\xfczenini de ekliyor.']},links:{classIds:['warrior'],raceIds:['human','gnome','night-elf','dwarf','skyborne-high-order','skyborne-windshaper','orc','tauren','troll','undead'],loreIds:['chapter:the-second-war','chapter:battle-for-mount-hyjal','chapter:beyond-the-dark-portal','item:gorehowl']},image:'class:warrior',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Warrior'),(0,n.wiki)('Anduin Lothar'),(0,n.wiki)('Grommash Hellscream'),t],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'class',slug:'paladin',subjectId:'paladin',order:3,era:'second-war',title:{en:'Paladin',tr:'Paladin'},summary:{en:'Holy warriors born in the Second War, the paladins of the Silver Hand were broken by one of their own and now fight on under new banners.',tr:'\u0130kinci Sava\u015f\u2019ta do\u011fan kutsal sava\u015f\xe7\u0131lar olan G\xfcm\xfc\u015f El Paladin\u2019leri kendi i\xe7lerinden biri taraf\u0131ndan par\xe7aland\u0131 ve art\u0131k yeni sancaklar alt\u0131nda sava\u015f\u0131yor.'},body:{en:['Paladins are warrior-priests of the Holy Light. Archbishop Alonsus Faol founded their order, the Knights of the Silver Hand, during the Second War to give the Alliance champions who could heal as well as fight. Uther the Lightbringer was the first of them, and Turalyon, Tirion Fordring and Prince Arthas Menethil all took the oath.','The order was broken by one of its own. Arthas murdered Uther and helped destroy Lordaeron, and the Silver Hand\u2019s survivors scattered: the fanatics of the Scarlet Crusade on one side, the Argent Dawn and the exiled Tirion on the other. Dwarves of Ironforge also carry the Light into battle. Forever\u2019s most surprising change is that the Forsaken can now become paladins too, though the sources used here do not yet explain how the undead came to wield the Light.'],tr:['Paladin\u2019ler Kutsal I\u015f\u0131k\u2019\u0131n (Holy Light) sava\u015f\xe7\u0131-rahipleridir. Ba\u015fpiskopos Alonsus Faol, \u0130ttifak\u2019a hem sava\u015f\u0131p hem iyile\u015ftirebilen \u015fampiyonlar kazand\u0131rmak i\xe7in \u0130kinci Sava\u015f s\u0131ras\u0131nda tarikatlar\u0131n\u0131, G\xfcm\xfc\u015f El \u015e\xf6valyeleri\u2019ni kurdu. \u0130lki Uther the Lightbringer\u2019d\u0131; Turalyon, Tirion Fordring ve Prens Arthas Menethil de yemin edenler aras\u0131ndayd\u0131.','Tarikat kendi i\xe7lerinden biri taraf\u0131ndan par\xe7aland\u0131. Arthas, Uther\u2019i \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc ve Lordaeron\u2019un y\u0131k\u0131m\u0131na ortak oldu; G\xfcm\xfc\u015f El\u2019in sa\u011f kalanlar\u0131 da\u011f\u0131ld\u0131: bir yanda Scarlet Crusade ba\u011fnazlar\u0131, di\u011fer yanda Argent Dawn ve s\xfcrg\xfcndeki Tirion. Ironforge c\xfcceleri de I\u015f\u0131k\u2019\u0131 sava\u015fa ta\u015f\u0131yor. Forever\u2019\u0131n en \u015fa\u015f\u0131rt\u0131c\u0131 de\u011fi\u015fikli\u011fi, Forsaken\u2019\u0131n da art\u0131k Paladin olabilmesi; ancak burada kullan\u0131lan kaynaklar \xf6l\xfcms\xfczlerin I\u015f\u0131k\u2019\u0131 nas\u0131l kullanabildi\u011fini hen\xfcz a\xe7\u0131klam\u0131yor.']},links:{classIds:['paladin'],raceIds:['human','dwarf','undead'],zoneIds:['eastern-plaguelands','western-plaguelands'],instanceIds:['scarlet-monastery-cathedral','stratholme'],loreIds:['chapter:the-second-war','chapter:fall-of-lordaeron','chapter:plaguelands-and-the-scarlet-crusade','term:silver-hand','term:holy-light','term:scarlet-crusade','term:argent-dawn','item:ashbringer']},image:'class:paladin',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Paladin'),(0,n.wiki)('Knights of the Silver Hand'),(0,n.wiki)('Uther the Lightbringer'),t],basis:'established',unknowns:[{en:'How Forsaken paladins came to wield the Light in Forever is not explained by the sources this guide uses.',tr:'Forever\u2019da Forsaken Paladin\u2019lerin I\u015f\u0131k\u2019\u0131 nas\u0131l kullanabildi\u011fi, bu rehberin kulland\u0131\u011f\u0131 kaynaklarda a\xe7\u0131klanm\u0131yor.'}]}),(0,n.lore)({category:'class',slug:'hunter',subjectId:'hunter',order:4,era:'elder-kingdoms',title:{en:'Hunter',tr:'Hunter'},summary:{en:'Rangers, riflemen and beastmasters, hunters live by the bow, the gun and the bond with a loyal animal.',tr:'Korucular, t\xfcfek\xe7iler ve hayvan terbiyecileri olan Hunter\u2019lar yay, t\xfcfek ve sad\u0131k bir hayvanla kurduklar\u0131 ba\u011fla ya\u015far.'},body:{en:["Hunters live by the bow, the gun and the bond with a beast. The rangers of Quel'Thalas, led for generations by the Windrunner family, guarded the elven forests; dwarven riflemen and the Wildhammers' gryphon riders fought in the Second War; night elf Sentinels and troll headhunters stalk the woods of Kalimdor and Stranglethorn.",'Some of the story\u2019s most stubborn survivors are hunters. Alleria Windrunner marched beyond the Dark Portal and never returned, her sister Sylvanas fought Arthas to her last breath, and the beastmaster Rexxar became the Horde\u2019s champion against Daelin Proudmoore. In Forever humans may take up the calling as well, and both Skyborne orders count hunters among their people.'],tr:["Hunter\u2019lar yay, t\xfcfek ve bir hayvanla kurduklar\u0131 ba\u011fla ya\u015far. Ku\u015faklar boyunca Windrunner ailesinin y\xf6netti\u011fi Quel'Thalas korucular\u0131 elf ormanlar\u0131n\u0131 korudu; c\xfcce t\xfcfek\xe7iler ve Wildhammer\u2019lar\u0131n grifon binicileri \u0130kinci Sava\u015f\u2019ta sava\u015ft\u0131; gece elfi Sentinel\u2019ler ve trol kelle avc\u0131lar\u0131 Kalimdor ve Stranglethorn ormanlar\u0131nda iz s\xfcr\xfcyor.",'Hik\xe2yenin en inat\xe7\u0131 hayatta kalanlar\u0131ndan baz\u0131lar\u0131 Hunter\u2019d\u0131r. Alleria Windrunner Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019in \xf6tesine y\xfcr\xfcd\xfc ve hi\xe7 d\xf6nmedi, k\u0131z karde\u015fi Sylvanas son nefesine dek Arthas\u2019la sava\u015ft\u0131 ve hayvan terbiyecisi Rexxar, Daelin Proudmoore\u2019a kar\u015f\u0131 Horde\u2019un \u015fampiyonu oldu. Forever\u2019da insanlar da bu yolu se\xe7ebiliyor ve iki Skyborne d\xfczeninin halk\u0131nda da Hunter\u2019lar var.']},links:{classIds:['hunter'],raceIds:['human','night-elf','dwarf','skyborne-high-order','skyborne-windshaper','orc','tauren','troll'],zoneIds:['hinterlands','stranglethorn-vale'],loreIds:['chapter:beyond-the-dark-portal','chapter:durotar-and-theramore','item:rhokdelar']},image:'class:hunter',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Hunter'),(0,n.wiki)('Alleria Windrunner'),(0,n.wiki)('Rexxar'),t],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'class',slug:'rogue',subjectId:'rogue',order:5,era:'classic',title:{en:'Rogue',tr:'Rogue'},summary:{en:'Spies, thieves and assassins, rogues work where honor would hesitate, and some of their guilds have quietly shaped history.',tr:'Casuslar, h\u0131rs\u0131zlar ve suikast\xe7\u0131lar olan Rogue\u2019lar onurun duraksayaca\u011f\u0131 yerde i\u015f g\xf6r\xfcr; loncalar\u0131ndan baz\u0131lar\u0131 tarihi sessizce bi\xe7imlendirdi.'},body:{en:["Rogues work where honor would hesitate. Thieves, spies and assassins exist in every city, but some of their organizations shape history: Stormwind's intelligence service SI:7, led by Mathias Shaw; the assassins of Ravenholdt, hidden in the Alterac Mountains; the Syndicate, grown from Alterac's disgraced nobility; and the Defias Brotherhood that haunts Westfall.",'The most famous rogue of the early wars was Garona Halforcen, the half-orc spy whose blade killed King Llane. In year 25 rogue trainers teach in Stormwind\u2019s Old Town and the Undercity\u2019s Rogues\u2019 Quarter, and every playable race but the tauren can learn the trade. Forever adds the Skyborne of both orders to the shadows.'],tr:["Rogue\u2019lar onurun duraksayaca\u011f\u0131 yerde i\u015f g\xf6r\xfcr. H\u0131rs\u0131zlar, casuslar ve suikast\xe7\u0131lar her \u015fehirde vard\u0131r, ama baz\u0131 \xf6rg\xfctleri tarihi bi\xe7imlendirir: Mathias Shaw\u2019un y\xf6netti\u011fi Stormwind istihbarat servisi SI:7; Alterac Da\u011flar\u0131\u2019nda saklanan Ravenholdt suikast\xe7\u0131lar\u0131; Alterac\u2019\u0131n g\xf6zden d\xfc\u015fm\xfc\u015f soylular\u0131ndan do\u011fan Syndicate; ve Westfall\u2019u kas\u0131p kavuran Defias Karde\u015fli\u011fi.",'\u0130lk sava\u015flar\u0131n en \xfcnl\xfc Rogue\u2019u, b\u0131\xe7a\u011f\u0131 Kral Llane\u2019i \xf6ld\xfcren yar\u0131 ork casus Garona Halforcen\u2019di. 25. y\u0131lda Rogue e\u011fitmenleri Stormwind\u2019in Old Town b\xf6lgesinde ve Undercity\u2019nin Rogues\u2019 Quarter\u2019\u0131nda ders veriyor; tauren d\u0131\u015f\u0131ndaki her oynanabilir \u0131rk bu zanaat\u0131 \xf6\u011frenebiliyor. Forever g\xf6lgelere iki Skyborne d\xfczenini de ekliyor.']},links:{classIds:['rogue'],raceIds:['human','gnome','night-elf','dwarf','skyborne-high-order','skyborne-windshaper','orc','troll','undead'],zoneIds:['alterac-mountains','westfall','hillsbrad-foothills'],instanceIds:['deadmines'],loreIds:['chapter:the-first-war','chapter:stormwind-in-shadow','term:defias-brotherhood']},image:'class:rogue',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Rogue'),(0,n.wiki)('SI:7'),(0,n.wiki)('Ravenholdt'),(0,n.wiki)('Garona Halforcen'),t],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'class',slug:'priest',subjectId:'priest',order:6,era:'elder-kingdoms',title:{en:'Priest',tr:'Priest'},summary:{en:'Priests serve the Holy Light, the moon goddess Elune or older and darker powers, healing allies and, when they must, unmaking foes.',tr:'Priest\u2019ler Kutsal I\u015f\u0131k\u2019a, ay tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Elune\u2019e ya da daha eski ve karanl\u0131k g\xfc\xe7lere hizmet eder; m\xfcttefiklerini iyile\u015ftirir, gerekti\u011finde d\xfc\u015fmanlar\u0131n\u0131 yok eder.'},body:{en:["Priests serve faith in many forms. The humans' Church of the Holy Light, centered on Stormwind's Cathedral of Light and once led by Archbishop Alonsus Faol, teaches that the Light lives in virtue rather than in any single god, and the dwarves embraced it too. The night elves' priestesses serve the moon goddess Elune in a sisterhood that Tyrande Whisperwind has led since the War of the Ancients.",'Others walk darker paths. Forsaken priests keep a bleak faith of their own, troll priests honor the loa of their ancestors, and shadow magic is part of many priests\u2019 craft. In Forever the gnomes, long known as an engineering people, can become priests for the first time, and Blizzard gave them racial priest spells of their own.'],tr:['Priest\u2019ler inanca pek \xe7ok bi\xe7imde hizmet eder. \u0130nsanlar\u0131n, merkezi Stormwind\u2019deki Cathedral of Light olan ve bir zamanlar Ba\u015fpiskopos Alonsus Faol\u2019un y\xf6netti\u011fi Kutsal I\u015f\u0131k Kilisesi, I\u015f\u0131k\u2019\u0131n tek bir tanr\u0131da de\u011fil erdemde ya\u015fad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 \xf6\u011fretir; c\xfcceler de bu inanc\u0131 benimsedi. Gece elflerinin rahibeleri, Tyrande Whisperwind\u2019in Kadimler Sava\u015f\u0131\u2019ndan beri y\xf6netti\u011fi bir k\u0131z karde\u015flik i\xe7inde ay tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Elune\u2019e hizmet eder.','Baz\u0131lar\u0131 daha karanl\u0131k yollarda y\xfcr\xfcr. Forsaken Priest\u2019leri kendilerine \xf6zg\xfc kasvetli bir inan\xe7 ta\u015f\u0131r, trol Priest\u2019leri atalar\u0131n\u0131n loa\u2019lar\u0131n\u0131 onurland\u0131r\u0131r ve g\xf6lge b\xfcy\xfcs\xfc pek \xe7ok Priest\u2019in zanaat\u0131n\u0131n par\xe7as\u0131d\u0131r. Forever\u2019da uzun zamand\u0131r m\xfchendislikleriyle bilinen gnomlar ilk kez Priest olabiliyor ve Blizzard onlara \u0131rka \xf6zg\xfc Priest b\xfcy\xfcleri verdi.']},links:{classIds:['priest'],raceIds:['human','gnome','night-elf','dwarf','troll','undead'],zoneIds:['elwynn-forest','teldrassil'],loreIds:['chapter:war-of-the-ancients','chapter:the-second-war','term:holy-light','term:elune','term:loa']},image:'class:priest',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Priest'),(0,n.wiki)('Church of the Holy Light'),(0,n.wiki)('Sisterhood of Elune'),(0,n.datasetSource)('blizzard-priest-warrior-deep-dive'),t],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'class',slug:'shaman',subjectId:'shaman',order:7,era:'draenor',title:{en:'Shaman',tr:'Shaman'},summary:{en:'Shaman ask the spirits of earth, fire, water and air for aid; lost to the orcs for a generation, the tradition was restored by Thrall.',tr:'Shaman\u2019lar toprak, ate\u015f, su ve havan\u0131n ruhlar\u0131ndan yard\u0131m ister; orklar bu gelene\u011fi bir ku\u015fak boyunca yitirdi ve Thrall onu yeniden canland\u0131rd\u0131.'},body:{en:["Shaman speak with the spirits of earth, fire, water and air, and they ask rather than command. On Draenor the orc shaman were their people's guides until Ner'zhul's corruption replaced them with warlocks, and for a generation the elements would not answer the orcs at all. Thrall restored the tradition, taught by Drek'Thar of the Frostwolves, and rebuilt the Horde around it.",'The tauren of Mulgore and the Darkspear trolls keep shamanic ways of their own, and Thrall still leads the shaman of Orgrimmar. Forever adds two newcomers: dwarves, who had no shaman in the original game, and the Windshaper Skyborne of Zephras Isle, whose island hangs in Skywall, the Elemental Plane of Air.'],tr:["Shaman\u2019lar toprak, ate\u015f, su ve havan\u0131n ruhlar\u0131yla konu\u015fur; emretmez, rica eder. Draenor\u2019da ork Shaman\u2019lar\u0131, Ner'zhul\u2019un yozla\u015fmas\u0131 onlar\u0131n yerine Warlock\u2019lar\u0131 getirene dek halklar\u0131n\u0131n rehberiydi ve bir ku\u015fak boyunca elementler orklara hi\xe7 yan\u0131t vermedi. Frostwolf\u2019lardan Drek'Thar\u2019\u0131n e\u011fitti\u011fi Thrall bu gelene\u011fi yeniden canland\u0131rd\u0131 ve Horde\u2019u onun \xfczerine yeniden kurdu.",'Mulgore taurenleri ve Darkspear trolleri de kendi \u015famanist geleneklerini s\xfcrd\xfcr\xfcyor; Orgrimmar\u2019\u0131n Shaman\u2019lar\u0131n\u0131 h\xe2l\xe2 Thrall y\xf6netiyor. Forever iki yeni halk ekliyor: \xf6zg\xfcn oyunda hi\xe7 Shaman\u2019\u0131 olmayan c\xfcceler ve adas\u0131 Hava\u2019n\u0131n Elemental D\xfczlemi Skywall\u2019da as\u0131l\u0131 duran Zephras Isle\u2019\u0131n Windshaper Skyborne\u2019u.']},links:{classIds:['shaman'],raceIds:['dwarf','skyborne-windshaper','orc','tauren','troll'],zoneIds:['durotar','mulgore','zephras-isle'],loreIds:['chapter:corruption-of-the-orcs','chapter:thrall-and-the-new-horde','term:elemental-lords','term:skywall','item:doomhammer']},image:'class:shaman',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Shaman'),(0,n.wiki)("Drek'Thar"),(0,n.wiki)('Thrall'),t,n.FOREVER.zephrasIsle],basis:'established',unknowns:[{en:'How dwarves took up shamanism in Forever is not explained by the sources this guide uses.',tr:'Forever\u2019da c\xfccelerin \u015famanl\u0131\u011fa nas\u0131l y\xf6neldi\u011fi, bu rehberin kulland\u0131\u011f\u0131 kaynaklarda a\xe7\u0131klanm\u0131yor.'}]}),(0,n.lore)({category:'class',slug:'warlock',subjectId:'warlock',order:8,era:'draenor',title:{en:'Warlock',tr:'Warlock'},summary:{en:'Masters of fel magic and bound demons, warlocks came to Azeroth with the Horde and walk a narrow line between power and ruin.',tr:'Fel b\xfcy\xfcs\xfcn\xfcn ve ba\u011flanm\u0131\u015f iblislerin ustas\u0131 olan Warlock\u2019lar Azeroth\u2019a Horde\u2019la geldi ve g\xfc\xe7 ile y\u0131k\u0131m aras\u0131ndaki ince bir \xe7izgide y\xfcr\xfcr.'},body:{en:["Warlocks draw power from fel magic and bind demons to their will. The craft came to Azeroth with the Horde: Kil'jaeden taught it to Gul'dan, whose Shadow Council turned the orc shaman into warlocks and drained Draenor's life to fuel their spells. Death knights and the curse of demon blood were among its darkest fruits.",'Not every warlock serves the Legion. Human warlocks gather in secret beneath the Slaughtered Lamb tavern in Stormwind, gnomes and Forsaken study the art, and Thrall\u2019s Horde tolerates its orc warlocks warily. Every warlock walks the same line: the power is real, and so is the risk of being consumed by it. In Forever trolls may also become warlocks.'],tr:["Warlock\u2019lar g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc fel b\xfcy\xfcs\xfcnden al\u0131r ve iblisleri iradelerine ba\u011flar. Bu zanaat Azeroth\u2019a Horde\u2019la geldi: Kil'jaeden onu Gul'dan\u2019a \xf6\u011fretti; Gul'dan\u2019\u0131n G\xf6lge Konseyi ork Shaman\u2019lar\u0131n\u0131 Warlock\u2019a d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc ve b\xfcy\xfcleri i\xe7in Draenor\u2019un ya\u015fam\u0131n\u0131 t\xfcketti. Death knight\u2019lar ve iblis kan\u0131 laneti, en karanl\u0131k meyveleri aras\u0131ndayd\u0131.",'Her Warlock Lejyon\u2019a hizmet etmez. \u0130nsan Warlock\u2019lar Stormwind\u2019deki Slaughtered Lamb meyhanesinin alt\u0131nda gizlice toplan\u0131r, gnomlar ve Forsaken bu sanat\u0131 inceler, Thrall\u2019\u0131n Horde\u2019u ise ork Warlock\u2019lar\u0131na temkinle katlan\u0131r. Her Warlock ayn\u0131 \xe7izgide y\xfcr\xfcr: g\xfc\xe7 ger\xe7ektir, onun taraf\u0131ndan yutulma tehlikesi de. Forever\u2019da troller de Warlock olabiliyor.']},links:{classIds:['warlock'],raceIds:['human','gnome','orc','troll','undead'],loreIds:['chapter:corruption-of-the-orcs','chapter:the-first-war','term:fel','term:burning-legion','item:skull-of-guldan']},image:'class:warlock',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Warlock'),(0,n.wiki)('Shadow Council'),(0,n.wiki)("Gul'dan"),t],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'class',slug:'druid',subjectId:'druid',order:9,era:'ancient-kalimdor',title:{en:'Druid',tr:'Druid'},summary:{en:"Shapeshifting guardians of nature taught first by the demigod Cenarius, druids keep the world's balance from Moonglade to the Emerald Dream.",tr:'\u0130lk kez yar\u0131 tanr\u0131 Cenarius\u2019un e\u011fitti\u011fi, bi\xe7im de\u011fi\u015ftiren do\u011fa koruyucular\u0131 olan Druid\u2019ler d\xfcnyan\u0131n dengesini Moonglade\u2019den Z\xfcmr\xfct R\xfcya\u2019ya kadar g\xf6zetir.'},body:{en:['Druids guard the balance of nature and can take the shapes of beasts. Malfurion Stormrage learned the art from the demigod Cenarius and became the first druid; his followers slept for centuries in the Emerald Dream while the Sentinels kept watch over the night elves\u2019 forests. The Cenarion Circle, based in the sacred glade of Moonglade, now gathers druids of every race.','After the Third War, Malfurion taught the tauren the druidic arts, and Hamuul Runetotem became the first tauren druid. In year 25 druids face grave worries: the World Tree Nordrassil is wounded, Teldrassil grew without the Aspects\u2019 blessing, and a nightmare is spreading through the Emerald Dream. In Forever both Skyborne orders count druids among their people.'],tr:['Druid\u2019ler do\u011fan\u0131n dengesini korur ve hayvan bi\xe7imlerine b\xfcr\xfcnebilir. Malfurion Stormrage bu sanat\u0131 yar\u0131 tanr\u0131 Cenarius\u2019tan \xf6\u011frendi ve ilk Druid oldu; Sentinel\u2019ler gece elflerinin ormanlar\u0131n\u0131 korurken onun takip\xe7ileri Z\xfcmr\xfct R\xfcya\u2019da y\xfczy\u0131llarca uyudu. Kutsal Moonglade vadisinde bulunan Cenarion Circle art\u0131k her \u0131rktan Druid\u2019i bir araya getiriyor.','\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019tan sonra Malfurion taurenlere druidlik sanat\u0131n\u0131 \xf6\u011fretti ve Hamuul Runetotem ilk tauren Druid oldu. 25. y\u0131lda Druid\u2019leri ciddi kayg\u0131lar bekliyor: D\xfcnya A\u011fac\u0131 Nordrassil yaral\u0131, Teldrassil Aspect\u2019lerin kutsamas\u0131 olmadan b\xfcy\xfcd\xfc ve Z\xfcmr\xfct R\xfcya\u2019da bir k\xe2bus yay\u0131l\u0131yor. Forever\u2019da iki Skyborne d\xfczeninin halk\u0131nda da Druid\u2019ler var.']},links:{classIds:['druid'],raceIds:['night-elf','skyborne-high-order','skyborne-windshaper','tauren'],zoneIds:['moonglade','teldrassil','mulgore'],loreIds:['chapter:war-of-the-ancients','chapter:the-long-watch-of-hyjal','term:cenarion-circle','term:emerald-dream','term:nordrassil','item:horn-of-cenarius']},image:'class:druid',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Druid'),(0,n.wiki)('Cenarion Circle'),(0,n.wiki)('Hamuul Runetotem'),t],basis:'established'})]},865,[866]);
__d(function(g,r,_i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),e.lore=function(t){return{id:`${t.category}:${t.slug}`,...t}},e.wiki=n,e.blizzard=i,e.datasetSource=function(n){const i=t.bundledDataset.sources.find(t=>t.id===n);if(!i)throw new Error(`Unknown dataset source ${n}`);if('wiki'!==i.kind)return{title:i.title,url:i.url,publisher:'Blizzard Entertainment'};const o=Number(new URL(i.url).searchParams.get('oldid'))||void 0;return{title:i.title,url:i.url,publisher:'warcraft.wiki.gg',license:'CC BY-SA 4.0',...o?{revision:o}:{}}},e.instanceSource=function(i){const o=t.instanceDataset.instances.find(t=>t.id===i);if(!o||!o.revid)throw new Error(`No pinned wiki page for instance ${i}`);return n(o.page,o.revid)},e.zoneSource=function(i){const o=t.zoneDataset.zones.find(t=>t.id===i);if(!o)throw new Error(`Unknown zone ${i}`);return n(o.source.page,o.source.revid)},Object.defineProperty(e,"FOREVER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});var t=r(d[0]);function n(t,n){const i=t.replace(/ /g,'_');return{title:t,url:`https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/${encodeURI(i)}${n?`?oldid=${n}`:''}`,publisher:'warcraft.wiki.gg',license:'CC BY-SA 4.0',...n?{revision:n}:{}}}function i(t,n){return{title:t,url:n,publisher:'Blizzard Entertainment'}}const o={overview:n('World of Warcraft: Forever',6932760),dungeons:i('Explore the New Dungeons of World of Warcraft: Forever','https://worldofwarcraft.blizzard.com/en-us/news/24301455'),raids:i('World of Warcraft: Forever Raid Overview\u2014Locations, Raid Sizes, and Attunement','https://worldofwarcraft.blizzard.com/en-us/news/24303009/world-of-warcraft-forever-raid-overview-locations-raid-sizes-and-attunement'),zephrasIsle:n('Zephras Isle',6901937),riverglades:n('Riverglades',6931032)}},866,[787]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"glossaryLore",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});var n=r(d[0]);const t=[(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'argent-dawn',title:{en:"Argent Dawn",tr:"Argent Dawn (G\xfcm\xfc\u015f \u015eafak)"},summary:{en:"An order sworn to defend Azeroth from the Scourge without the Scarlet Crusade's blind hatred.",tr:"Azeroth\u2019u Scourge\u2019a kar\u015f\u0131, Scarlet Crusade\u2019in k\xf6r nefretine kap\u0131lmadan savunmaya ant i\xe7mi\u015f tarikat."},body:{en:["When the Silver Hand\u2019s survivors in Lordaeron hardened into the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, some refused to follow. Led by figures such as Lord Maxwell Tyrosus, they formed the Argent Dawn, which welcomes anyone willing to fight the undead. From Light\u2019s Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands, the order watches the Scourge and rewards those who help hold the line."],tr:["Lordaeron\u2019daki G\xfcm\xfc\u015f El kal\u0131nt\u0131lar\u0131 fanatik Scarlet Crusade\u2019e d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcrken baz\u0131lar\u0131 bu yolu izlemeyi reddetti. Lord Maxwell Tyrosus gibi \xf6nderlerle Argent Dawn\u2019u kurdular; tarikat \xf6l\xfcms\xfczlere kar\u015f\u0131 sava\u015fmaya haz\u0131r herkesi kabul eder. Eastern Plaguelands b\xf6lgesindeki Light's Hope Chapel\u2019den Scourge\u2019u g\xf6zler ve hatt\u0131 tutmaya yard\u0131m edenleri \xf6d\xfcllendirir."]},era:'classic',order:1,links:{zoneIds:['eastern-plaguelands','western-plaguelands'],instanceIds:['stratholme','scholomance'],loreIds:['term:scarlet-crusade','term:scourge']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Argent Dawn')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'burning-legion',title:{en:"Burning Legion",tr:"Yanan Lejyon (Burning Legion)"},summary:{en:"The fallen titan Sargeras's endless army of demons, sworn to burn all of creation.",tr:"D\xfc\u015fm\xfc\u015f titan Sargeras\u2019\u0131n b\xfct\xfcn yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015f\u0131 yakmaya ant i\xe7mi\u015f sonsuz iblis ordusu."},body:{en:["Once the champion of the titan Pantheon, Sargeras learned that the powers of the Void sought to corrupt the world-souls and, in despair, resolved to burn creation rather than let it fall to them. He freed the demons he had imprisoned and won over the eredar lords Kil'jaeden and Archimonde to command them. The Legion invaded Azeroth in the War of the Ancients and again in the Third War, and its agents still lurk in places like Felwood and the Blasted Lands."],tr:["Bir zamanlar titan Panteonu\u2019nun \u015fampiyonu olan Sargeras, Hi\xe7lik (Void) g\xfc\xe7lerinin d\xfcnya ruhlar\u0131n\u0131 yozla\u015ft\u0131rmak istedi\u011fini \xf6\u011frendi ve \xe7aresizlik i\xe7inde yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015f\u0131 onlara b\u0131rakmaktansa yakmaya karar verdi. Hapsetti\u011fi iblisleri serbest b\u0131rakt\u0131 ve onlara komuta etmeleri i\xe7in eredar lordlar\u0131 Kil'jaeden ile Archimonde\u2019u kazand\u0131. Lejyon, Azeroth\u2019u Kadimler Sava\u015f\u0131\u2019nda ve \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019ta istila etti; ajanlar\u0131 h\xe2l\xe2 Felwood ve Blasted Lands gibi yerlerde pusuda bekliyor."]},era:'creation',order:2,links:{classIds:['warlock'],zoneIds:['felwood','blasted-lands','ashenvale'],loreIds:['term:titans','term:nathrezim','term:fel','chapter:sargeras-and-the-burning-legion']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Burning Legion'),(0,n.wiki)('Sargeras')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'cenarion-circle',title:{en:"Cenarion Circle",tr:"Cenarion Circle (Cenarius \xc7emberi)"},summary:{en:"The druidic order of night elves and tauren that guards the balance of nature from Moonglade.",tr:"Gece elfleri ile taurenlerin, do\u011fan\u0131n dengesini Moonglade\u2019den koruyan Druid tarikat\u0131."},body:{en:["Named for the demigod Cenarius, who taught the first druids, the Circle unites night elf and tauren druids in a single order. Its heart is the village of Nighthaven in Moonglade, a sanctuary where fighting is forbidden, and its members also watch over the dangers of Silithus from Cenarion Hold."],tr:["\u0130lk Druid\u2019lere yol g\xf6steren yar\u0131 tanr\u0131 Cenarius\u2019un ad\u0131n\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131yan \xc7ember, gece elfi ve tauren Druid\u2019lerini tek bir tarikatta birle\u015ftirir. Kalbi, \xe7at\u0131\u015fman\u0131n yasak oldu\u011fu bir s\u0131\u011f\u0131nak olan Moonglade\u2019deki Nighthaven k\xf6y\xfcd\xfcr; \xfcyeleri Silithus\u2019un tehlikelerini de Cenarion Hold\u2019dan g\xf6zler."]},era:'classic',order:3,links:{classIds:['druid'],raceIds:['night-elf','tauren'],zoneIds:['moonglade','silithus'],loreIds:['term:emerald-dream','term:nordrassil']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Cenarion Circle')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'cult-of-the-damned',title:{en:"Cult of the Damned",tr:"Cult of the Damned (Lanetliler Tarikat\u0131)"},summary:{en:"Kel'Thuzad's cult of the Lich King, which promised eternal life and delivered the plague.",tr:"Kel'Thuzad\u2019\u0131n Lich King\u2019e ba\u011fl\u0131 tarikat\u0131; sonsuz ya\u015fam vaat etti, veba getirdi."},body:{en:["The archmage Kel'Thuzad turned his back on the Kirin Tor to study necromancy and gathered the poor and desperate of Lordaeron with promises of a better, deathless life. The cult hid the Lich King\u2019s plague in shipments of grain, turning whole villages into Scourge. Its necromancers still teach at the Scholomance, in the Barov family\u2019s old keep of Caer Darrow."],tr:["Nekromansi \xe7al\u0131\u015fmak i\xe7in Kirin Tor\u2019a s\u0131rt\u0131n\u0131 d\xf6nen ba\u015fb\xfcy\xfcc\xfc Kel'Thuzad, Lordaeron\u2019un yoksullar\u0131n\u0131 ve \xe7aresizlerini daha iyi, \xf6l\xfcms\xfcz bir ya\u015fam vaadiyle toplad\u0131. Tarikat Lich King\u2019in vebas\u0131n\u0131 tah\u0131l sevkiyatlar\u0131na gizledi ve b\xfct\xfcn k\xf6yleri Scourge\u2019a d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc. Nekromanserleri h\xe2l\xe2 Barov ailesinin eski kalesi Caer Darrow\u2019daki Scholomance okulunda ders veriyor."]},era:'interwar',order:4,links:{zoneIds:['western-plaguelands','eastern-plaguelands'],instanceIds:['scholomance'],loreIds:['term:lich-king','term:scourge','chapter:the-lich-king-and-the-plague']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Cult of the Damned')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'dark-portal',title:{en:"Dark Portal",tr:"Kara Ge\xe7it (Dark Portal)"},summary:{en:"The gateway between Draenor and Azeroth through which the orcish Horde invaded.",tr:"Draenor ile Azeroth aras\u0131ndaki, ork Horde\u2019unun istila i\xe7in kulland\u0131\u011f\u0131 ge\xe7it."},body:{en:["The orc warlock Gul'dan and the possessed Guardian Medivh opened the Dark Portal, linking Draenor to the Black Morass of Azeroth. Its opening began the First War, and the years of Warcraft\u2019s history are still counted from it. The Alliance destroyed it after the Second War, Ner'zhul tore it open again, and Khadgar collapsed it from Draenor\u2019s side. Its dormant frame still towers over the Blasted Lands."],tr:["Ork Warlock Gul'dan ile ele ge\xe7irilmi\u015f Muhaf\u0131z Medivh, Draenor\u2019u Azeroth\u2019un Black Morass b\xf6lgesine ba\u011flayan Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019i a\xe7t\u0131. A\xe7\u0131l\u0131\u015f\u0131 Birinci Sava\u015f\u2019\u0131 ba\u015flatt\u0131; Warcraft tarihinin y\u0131llar\u0131 h\xe2l\xe2 ondan say\u0131l\u0131r. \u0130ttifak onu \u0130kinci Sava\u015f\u2019tan sonra y\u0131kt\u0131, Ner'zhul yeniden y\u0131rtt\u0131, Khadgar da Draenor taraf\u0131ndan \xe7\xf6kertti. S\xf6nm\xfc\u015f \xe7er\xe7evesi h\xe2l\xe2 Blasted Lands b\xf6lgesinin \xfczerinde y\xfckseliyor."]},era:'first-war',order:5,links:{raceIds:['orc'],zoneIds:['blasted-lands','swamp-of-sorrows'],loreIds:['chapter:the-first-war','chapter:beyond-the-dark-portal']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Dark Portal')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'defias-brotherhood',title:{en:"Defias Brotherhood",tr:"Defias Karde\u015fli\u011fi (Defias Brotherhood)"},summary:{en:"Unpaid Stormwind stonemasons turned bandits under Edwin VanCleef.",tr:"Edwin VanCleef \xf6nderli\u011finde haydutlu\u011fa d\xf6nen, \xfccreti \xf6denmemi\u015f Stormwind ta\u015f ustalar\u0131."},body:{en:["The Stonemasons\u2019 Guild rebuilt Stormwind after the Second War, but the nobles refused to pay them. Their leader, Edwin VanCleef, led the angry masons into Westfall and forged them into the Defias Brotherhood, a gang of thieves and saboteurs hidden in the Deadmines. In Forever, its members also turn up inside Alcaz Prison, locked in a struggle with the naga."],tr:["Ta\u015f Ustalar\u0131 Loncas\u0131 Stormwind\u2019i \u0130kinci Sava\u015f\u2019tan sonra yeniden in\u015fa etti, ama soylular \xfccretlerini \xf6demeyi reddetti. \xd6nderleri Edwin VanCleef \xf6fkeli ustalar\u0131 Westfall\u2019a g\xf6t\xfcrd\xfc ve onlar\u0131 Deadmines\u2019ta gizlenen bir h\u0131rs\u0131z ve sabotajc\u0131 \xe7etesine, Defias Karde\u015fli\u011fi\u2019ne d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc. Forever\u2019da karde\u015fli\u011fin \xfcyeleri Alcaz Prison\u2019da da kar\u015f\u0131na \xe7\u0131kar; orada naga ile k\u0131yas\u0131ya \xe7eki\u015firler."]},era:'classic',order:6,links:{raceIds:['human'],zoneIds:['westfall','elwynn-forest','redridge-mountains'],instanceIds:['deadmines','stormwind-stockade','alcaz-prison'],loreIds:['chapter:stormwind-in-shadow']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Defias Brotherhood'),n.FOREVER.dungeons],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'dragon-aspects',title:{en:"Dragon Aspects",tr:"Ejderha Aspect\u2019leri (Dragon Aspects)"},summary:{en:"Five great dragons empowered by the titans to guard Azeroth, each leading a dragonflight.",tr:"Azeroth\u2019u korumalar\u0131 i\xe7in titanlarca g\xfc\xe7lendirilen ve her biri bir ejderha soyunu y\xf6neten be\u015f b\xfcy\xfck ejderha."},body:{en:["The titans chose five dragons and gave each a share of their power: Alexstrasza the Life-Binder of the red flight, Ysera the Dreamer of the green, Nozdormu the Timeless of the bronze, Malygos the Spell-Weaver of the blue, and Neltharion the Earth-Warder of the black. Neltharion\u2019s betrayal turned him into Deathwing, and his children Onyxia and Nefarian still scheme in Azeroth."],tr:["Titanlar be\u015f ejderha se\xe7ip her birine g\xfc\xe7lerinden bir pay verdi: k\u0131z\u0131l soydan Ya\u015fam Ba\u011flay\u0131c\u0131s\u0131 Alexstrasza, ye\u015fil soydan R\xfcyac\u0131 Ysera, bronz soydan Zamans\u0131z Nozdormu, mavi soydan B\xfcy\xfc Dokuyucusu Malygos ve kara soydan Toprak Koruyucusu Neltharion. Neltharion\u2019un ihaneti onu Deathwing\u2019e d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc; \xe7ocuklar\u0131 Onyxia ile Nefarian h\xe2l\xe2 Azeroth\u2019ta entrika \xe7eviriyor."]},era:'creation',order:7,links:{zoneIds:['tanaris','dustwallow-marsh','wetlands'],instanceIds:['onyxias-lair'],loreIds:['item:demon-soul','term:emerald-dream']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Dragon Aspects')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'elemental-lords',title:{en:"Elemental Lords",tr:"Element Lordlar\u0131 (Elemental Lords)"},summary:{en:"The four rulers of fire, earth, air and water, once servants of the Old Gods.",tr:"Ate\u015fin, topra\u011f\u0131n, havan\u0131n ve suyun d\xf6rt h\xfck\xfcmdar\u0131; bir zamanlar Kadim Tanr\u0131lar\u0131n hizmetk\xe2rlar\u0131."},body:{en:["Ragnaros of fire, Therazane of earth, Al'Akir of air and Neptulon of water led the elementals in the Old Gods\u2019 war against the titans\u2019 servants. When the Black Empire fell, the keepers bound them in the Elemental Plane. Shamans seek to keep the elements in balance, while the Dark Iron sorcerer Thaurissan\u2019s blunder brought Ragnaros back into the world beneath Blackrock Mountain."],tr:["Ate\u015ften Ragnaros, topraktan Therazane, havadan Al'Akir ve sudan Neptulon, Kadim Tanr\u0131lar\u0131n titan hizmetk\xe2rlar\u0131na kar\u015f\u0131 sava\u015f\u0131nda elementallere \xf6nderlik etti. Kara \u0130mparatorluk \xe7\xf6kt\xfc\u011f\xfcnde bek\xe7iler onlar\u0131 Elemental D\xfczlem\u2019e ba\u011flad\u0131. Shaman\u2019lar elementlerin dengesini korumaya \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131r; Dark Iron b\xfcy\xfcc\xfcs\xfc Thaurissan\u2019\u0131n hatas\u0131 ise Ragnaros\u2019u Blackrock Da\u011f\u0131\u2019n\u0131n alt\u0131nda yeniden d\xfcnyaya getirdi."]},era:'creation',order:8,links:{classIds:['shaman'],zoneIds:['searing-gorge','burning-steppes'],instanceIds:['blackrock-depths'],loreIds:['term:old-gods','term:skywall','item:sulfuras']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Elemental Lord')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'elune',title:{en:"Elune",tr:"Elune"},summary:{en:"The moon goddess of the night elves, whose priestesses lead their people.",tr:"Gece elflerinin ay tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131; rahibeleri halklar\u0131na \xf6nderlik eder."},body:{en:["The night elves have worshipped Elune since the dawn of their civilization, finding guidance in the light of the moon. The Sisterhood of Elune, led by the high priestess Tyrande Whisperwind, serves as both clergy and leadership in Darnassus, and night elf priests draw their healing from the goddess."],tr:["Gece elfleri uygarl\u0131klar\u0131n\u0131n \u015fafa\u011f\u0131ndan beri Elune\u2019a tapar ve ay \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131nda yol bulur. Ba\u015f rahibe Tyrande Whisperwind\u2019in y\xf6netti\u011fi Elune Rahibeleri (Sisterhood of Elune), Darnassus\u2019ta hem din adaml\u0131\u011f\u0131 hem de y\xf6neticilik yapar; gece elfi Priest\u2019leri \u015fifa g\xfc\xe7lerini tanr\u0131\xe7adan al\u0131r."]},era:'ancient-kalimdor',order:9,links:{raceIds:['night-elf'],classIds:['priest'],zoneIds:['teldrassil'],loreIds:['term:kaldorei']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Elune')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'emerald-dream',title:{en:"Emerald Dream",tr:"Z\xfcmr\xfct R\xfcya (Emerald Dream)"},summary:{en:"A dreaming reflection of Azeroth's untouched wilds, watched over by Ysera and walked by druids.",tr:"Azeroth\u2019un el de\u011fmemi\u015f do\u011fas\u0131n\u0131n r\xfcyadaki yans\u0131mas\u0131; Ysera g\xf6zetir, Druid\u2019ler i\xe7inde dola\u015f\u0131r."},body:{en:["The Emerald Dream mirrors the world as it might have been without mortal hands. Ysera and her green dragonflight guard it, and druids enter it in spirit, sometimes sleeping for centuries. In Azeroth\u2019s present, something is souring the Dream: a creeping nightmare twists Naralex\u2019s dreams in the Wailing Caverns and has driven the green dragons of the Sunken Temple mad."],tr:["Z\xfcmr\xfct R\xfcya, d\xfcnyay\u0131 \xf6l\xfcml\xfc eller dokunmasayd\u0131 nas\u0131l olacaksa \xf6yle yans\u0131t\u0131r. Ysera ve ye\u015fil ejderha soyu onu korur; Druid\u2019ler ruhlar\u0131yla i\xe7ine girer, kimi zaman y\xfczy\u0131llarca uyurlar. Azeroth\u2019un bug\xfcn\xfcnde bir \u015fey R\xfcya\u2019y\u0131 bozuyor: sinsi bir k\xe2bus, Wailing Caverns\u2019ta Naralex\u2019in r\xfcyalar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7arp\u0131t\u0131yor ve Sunken Temple\u2019\u0131n ye\u015fil ejderhalar\u0131n\u0131 delirtti."]},era:'creation',order:10,links:{classIds:['druid'],zoneIds:['moonglade','barrens','swamp-of-sorrows'],instanceIds:['wailing-caverns','temple-of-atalhakkar'],loreIds:['term:dragon-aspects','term:cenarion-circle']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Emerald Dream'),(0,n.wiki)('Emerald Nightmare')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'explorers-league',title:{en:"Explorers' League",tr:"K\xe2\u015fifler Birli\u011fi (Explorers' League)"},summary:{en:"Ironforge's society of dwarven archaeologists, digging for the secrets of the titans.",tr:"Ironforge\u2019un, titanlar\u0131n s\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 kaz\u0131p \xe7\u0131karan c\xfcce arkeologlar toplulu\u011fu."},body:{en:["From the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge, the League sends dwarves across the world in search of relics that might explain where their people came from. Its most famous member is Brann Bronzebeard, the king\u2019s restless brother. League diggers uncovered the titan vaults of Uldaman, and in Forever the strange, time-frozen ruins beyond Whelgar\u2019s Excavation in the Wetlands are exactly the kind of mystery the League chases."],tr:["Ironforge\u2019daki Hall of Explorers\u2019tan y\xf6netilen Birlik, halklar\u0131n\u0131n k\xf6kenini a\xe7\u0131klayabilecek kal\u0131nt\u0131lar bulmak i\xe7in c\xfcceleri d\xfcnyan\u0131n d\xf6rt bir yan\u0131na g\xf6nderir. En \xfcnl\xfc \xfcyesi, kral\u0131n yerinde duramayan karde\u015fi Brann Bronzebeard\u2019d\u0131r. Birli\u011fin kaz\u0131c\u0131lar\u0131 Uldaman\u2019\u0131n titan mahzenlerini g\xfcn \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131na \xe7\u0131kard\u0131; Forever\u2019da Wetlands b\xf6lgesindeki Whelgar\u2019s Excavation\u2019\u0131n \xf6tesinde zamanda donmu\u015f gibi duran tuhaf kal\u0131nt\u0131lar da tam Birli\u011fin pe\u015fine d\xfc\u015fece\u011fi t\xfcrden bir gizem."]},era:'classic',order:11,links:{raceIds:['dwarf'],zoneIds:['badlands','wetlands','dun-morogh'],instanceIds:['uldaman','excavation-site-wetlands'],loreIds:['term:titan-forged','term:titans']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)("Explorers' League"),n.FOREVER.dungeons],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'fel',title:{en:"Fel",tr:"Fel (iblis b\xfcy\xfcs\xfc)"},summary:{en:"The burning, corrupting magic of the Burning Legion.",tr:"Yanan Lejyon\u2019un yak\u0131p kavuran, yozla\u015ft\u0131ran b\xfcy\xfcs\xfc."},body:{en:["Fel is the magic of demons: potent, addictive and ruinous to everything it touches. Gul'dan\u2019s warlocks drained the life from Draenor with it and bound the orcs to the Legion, and its taint turned their skin green. Warlocks still wield it today, and its scars mark Felwood, where demonic corruption has poisoned an ancient forest."],tr:["Fel, iblislerin b\xfcy\xfcs\xfcd\xfcr: g\xfc\xe7l\xfc, ba\u011f\u0131ml\u0131l\u0131k yapan ve dokundu\u011fu her \u015feyi mahveden. Gul'dan\u2019\u0131n Warlock\u2019lar\u0131 onunla Draenor\u2019un ya\u015fam g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc emdi ve orklar\u0131 Lejyon\u2019a ba\u011flad\u0131; bu leke orklar\u0131n derisini ye\u015file \xe7evirdi. Warlock\u2019lar bug\xfcn de onu kullan\u0131r; izleri, iblis yozla\u015fmas\u0131n\u0131n kadim bir orman\u0131 zehirledi\u011fi Felwood\u2019da g\xf6r\xfcl\xfcr."]},era:'draenor',order:12,links:{classIds:['warlock'],raceIds:['orc'],zoneIds:['felwood'],loreIds:['term:burning-legion','chapter:corruption-of-the-orcs']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Fel')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'guardian-of-tirisfal',title:{en:"Guardian of Tirisfal",tr:"Tirisfal Muhaf\u0131z\u0131 (Guardian of Tirisfal)"},summary:{en:"A mage granted the combined power of a secret council to fight the Burning Legion alone.",tr:"Gizli bir konseyin birle\u015fik g\xfcc\xfcyle donat\u0131l\u0131p Yanan Lejyon\u2019la tek ba\u015f\u0131na sava\u015fan Mage."},body:{en:["High elf and human magi formed the secret Council of Tirisfal to stop demons from slipping into the world through careless spellcraft. In each age the council poured its power into a single champion, the Guardian. Aegwynn carried the role for centuries; her son Medivh, the last Guardian, was secretly possessed by Sargeras and opened the way for the orcs."],tr:["Y\xfcksek elf ve insan b\xfcy\xfcc\xfcler, dikkatsiz b\xfcy\xfcler y\xfcz\xfcnden iblislerin d\xfcnyaya s\u0131zmas\u0131n\u0131 \xf6nlemek i\xe7in gizli Tirisfal Konseyi\u2019ni kurdu. Konsey her \xe7a\u011fda g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc tek bir \u015fampiyona, Muhaf\u0131z\u2019a aktard\u0131. Aegwynn bu g\xf6revi y\xfczy\u0131llarca ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131; son Muhaf\u0131z olan o\u011flu Medivh ise gizlice Sargeras\u2019\u0131n denetimindeydi ve orklara yol a\xe7t\u0131."]},era:'elder-kingdoms',order:13,links:{classIds:['mage'],zoneIds:['deadwind-pass'],loreIds:['item:atiesh','chapter:guardians-and-the-seven-kingdoms']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Guardian of Tirisfal'),(0,n.wiki)('Council of Tirisfal')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'highborne',title:{en:"Highborne",tr:"Highborne"},summary:{en:"The arcane aristocracy of the ancient night elf empire, whose hunger for magic invited the Legion.",tr:"Kadim gece elfi imparatorlu\u011funun b\xfcy\xfcye d\xfc\u015fk\xfcn aristokrasisi; b\xfcy\xfc a\xe7l\u0131klar\u0131 Lejyon\u2019u davet etti."},body:{en:["The Highborne served Queen Azshara as her court and her sorcerers, drawing ever deeper on the Well of Eternity until their spells caught the eye of Sargeras. After the Sundering, most survivors were exiled and founded Quel'Thalas as the high elves. Others, the Shen'dralar, stayed hidden in Eldre'Thalas, the city now called Dire Maul."],tr:["Highborne, Krali\xe7e Azshara\u2019n\u0131n saray\u0131 ve b\xfcy\xfcc\xfcleriydi; Sonsuzluk Kuyusu\u2019ndan giderek daha derin g\xfc\xe7 \xe7ektiler ve b\xfcy\xfcleri sonunda Sargeras\u2019\u0131n dikkatini \xe7ekti. B\xfcy\xfck Yar\u0131lma\u2019dan sonra hayatta kalanlar\u0131n \xe7o\u011fu s\xfcrg\xfcn edildi ve y\xfcksek elfler olarak Quel'Thalas\u2019\u0131 kurdu. Shen'dralar adl\u0131 bir ba\u015fka grup ise bug\xfcn Dire Maul denen Eldre'Thalas \u015fehrinde sakl\u0131 kald\u0131."]},era:'ancient-kalimdor',order:14,links:{raceIds:['night-elf'],classIds:['mage'],zoneIds:['azshara','feralas'],instanceIds:['capital-gardens'],loreIds:['term:well-of-eternity','term:queldorei','chapter:rise-of-the-kaldorei']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Highborne'),(0,n.wiki)("Shen'dralar")],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'holy-light',title:{en:"The Holy Light",tr:"Kutsal I\u015f\u0131k (Holy Light)"},summary:{en:"The power of hope and virtue that paladins and priests channel.",tr:"Paladin\u2019lerin ve Priest\u2019lerin kulland\u0131\u011f\u0131 umut ve erdem g\xfcc\xfc."},body:{en:["Humans revere the Light through the Church of the Holy Light, whose clerics heal the wounded and whose cathedrals rise in Stormwind and once rose in Lordaeron. Dwarves embraced it too. During the Second War, Archbishop Alonsus Faol joined faith and steel by founding the paladins of the Silver Hand, and the Light remains the bane of the undead."],tr:["\u0130nsanlar I\u015f\u0131\u011fa, din adamlar\u0131 yaral\u0131lar\u0131 iyile\u015ftiren ve katedralleri Stormwind\u2019de, bir zamanlar da Lordaeron\u2019da y\xfckselen Kutsal I\u015f\u0131k Kilisesi arac\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131yla sayg\u0131 g\xf6sterir. C\xfcceler de onu benimsedi. \u0130kinci Sava\u015f\u2019ta Ba\u015fpiskopos Alonsus Faol, G\xfcm\xfc\u015f El Paladin\u2019lerini kurarak inanc\u0131 \xe7elikle birle\u015ftirdi; I\u015f\u0131k h\xe2l\xe2 \xf6l\xfcms\xfczlerin ba\u015f belas\u0131d\u0131r."]},era:'elder-kingdoms',order:15,links:{classIds:['paladin','priest'],raceIds:['human','dwarf'],loreIds:['term:silver-hand']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Holy Light'),(0,n.wiki)('Church of the Holy Light')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'kaldorei',title:{en:"Kaldorei",tr:"Kaldorei (gece elfleri)"},summary:{en:"The night elves, \u201cchildren of the stars\u201d, one of the oldest civilizations of Kalimdor.",tr:"Gece elfleri, yani \u201cy\u0131ld\u0131zlar\u0131n \xe7ocuklar\u0131\u201d; Kalimdor\u2019un en eski uygarl\u0131klar\u0131ndan biri."},body:{en:["Descended from trolls changed by the Well of Eternity, the night elves built a dazzling empire under Queen Azshara before it drowned in the Sundering. For ten thousand years they lived as druids and Sentinels, kept ageless by Nordrassil, until the Third War cost them their immortality. Today they rule from Darnassus atop Teldrassil and stand with the Alliance."],tr:["Sonsuzluk Kuyusu\u2019nun d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc\u011f\xfc trollerden gelen gece elfleri, Krali\xe7e Azshara\u2019n\u0131n y\xf6netiminde g\xf6z kama\u015ft\u0131r\u0131c\u0131 bir imparatorluk kurdu; imparatorluk B\xfcy\xfck Yar\u0131lma\u2019da sulara g\xf6m\xfcld\xfc. On bin y\u0131l boyunca Nordrassil\u2019in verdi\u011fi ya\u015flanmazl\u0131kla Druid ve Sentinel olarak ya\u015fad\u0131lar; \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f onlara \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfcklerine mal oldu. Bug\xfcn Teldrassil\u2019in tepesindeki Darnassus\u2019tan y\xf6netir ve \u0130ttifak\u2019\u0131n yan\u0131nda dururlar."]},era:'ancient-kalimdor',order:16,links:{raceIds:['night-elf'],classIds:['druid'],factionIds:['alliance'],zoneIds:['teldrassil','darkshore','ashenvale'],loreIds:['term:elune','term:highborne','chapter:rise-of-the-kaldorei']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Night elf')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'kirin-tor',title:{en:"Kirin Tor",tr:"Kirin Tor"},summary:{en:"The ruling council of mages that governs Dalaran and guards dangerous magic.",tr:"Dalaran\u2019\u0131 y\xf6neten ve tehlikeli b\xfcy\xfcleri koruma alt\u0131nda tutan Mage\u2019ler konseyi."},body:{en:["Founded in the city of magi, Dalaran, the Kirin Tor oversee the study of arcane magic and lock away artifacts too dangerous for the world. Archimonde left Dalaran in ruins during the Third War, and in the original game the city lay hidden beneath a violet dome. In Forever that barrier has fallen, revealing a restoration overrun by misfiring arcane chaos."],tr:["B\xfcy\xfcc\xfcler \u015fehri Dalaran\u2019da kurulan Kirin Tor, arkan b\xfcy\xfc \xe7al\u0131\u015fmalar\u0131n\u0131 denetler ve d\xfcnya i\xe7in fazla tehlikeli eserleri kilit alt\u0131nda tutar. Archimonde \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019ta Dalaran\u2019\u0131 yerle bir etti; orijinal oyunda \u015fehir mor bir kubbenin alt\u0131nda gizliydi. Forever\u2019da bu bariyer d\xfc\u015ft\xfc ve ters tepen b\xfcy\xfclerle kaynayan bir yeniden in\u015fa ortaya \xe7\u0131kt\u0131."]},era:'elder-kingdoms',order:17,links:{classIds:['mage'],zoneIds:['alterac-mountains','hillsbrad-foothills'],instanceIds:['city-of-dalaran'],loreIds:['item:book-of-medivh','term:guardian-of-tirisfal']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Kirin Tor'),n.FOREVER.dungeons],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'ley-lines',title:{en:"Ley Lines",tr:"Ley hatlar\u0131 (Ley Lines)"},summary:{en:"Currents of arcane energy that run through Azeroth like veins.",tr:"Azeroth\u2019un i\xe7inden damarlar gibi akan arkan enerji ak\u0131nt\u0131lar\u0131."},body:{en:["Ley lines carry raw arcane power across the world, and where they cross, magic gathers in strength. The high elves raised the Sunwell at such a nexus, and mages have long sought these currents out. In Forever, the High Order Skyborne can tap them through their racial Read Ley Line, which lasts far longer when used near one."],tr:["Ley hatlar\u0131 ham arkan g\xfcc\xfc d\xfcnyan\u0131n bir ucundan \xf6b\xfcr ucuna ta\u015f\u0131r; kesi\u015ftikleri yerde b\xfcy\xfc g\xfc\xe7lenir. Y\xfcksek elfler Sunwell\u2019i b\xf6yle bir kav\u015fakta kurdu; Mage\u2019ler de bu ak\u0131nt\u0131lar\u0131n pe\u015fine hep d\xfc\u015ft\xfc. Forever\u2019da High Order Skyborne, Read Ley Line \u0131rksal yetene\u011fiyle onlardan g\xfc\xe7 \xe7eker; yetenek bir ley hatt\u0131n\u0131n yak\u0131n\u0131nda kullan\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda \xe7ok daha uzun s\xfcrer."]},era:'creation',order:18,links:{classIds:['mage'],raceIds:['skyborne-high-order'],loreIds:['term:sunwell']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Ley line'),(0,n.datasetSource)('wiki-racial-read-ley-line')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'lich-king',title:{en:"Lich King",tr:"Lich King"},summary:{en:"The undying master of the Scourge, enthroned in the ice of Northrend.",tr:"Northrend\u2019in buzlar\u0131nda tahta oturan, Scourge\u2019un \xf6lmeyen efendisi."},body:{en:["Kil'jaeden tore the spirit of the orc shaman Ner'zhul from his body and sealed it in a block of ice atop Icecrown, the Frozen Throne, to prepare Azeroth for the Legion. From there the Lich King raised the Scourge and spread the plague. After the Third War, Prince Arthas climbed to the throne and merged with him, and the united Lich King now waits in Northrend."],tr:["Kil'jaeden ork Shaman\u2019\u0131 Ner'zhul\u2019un ruhunu bedeninden kopard\u0131 ve Azeroth\u2019u Lejyon\u2019a haz\u0131rlamak i\xe7in Icecrown\u2019un tepesindeki bir buz k\xfctlesine, Frozen Throne\u2019a m\xfch\xfcrledi. Lich King oradan Scourge\u2019u aya\u011fa kald\u0131rd\u0131 ve vebay\u0131 yayd\u0131. \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019tan sonra Prens Arthas tahta t\u0131rman\u0131p onunla birle\u015fti; birle\u015fik Lich King \u015fimdi Northrend\u2019de bekliyor."]},era:'interwar',order:19,links:{zoneIds:['eastern-plaguelands','western-plaguelands'],loreIds:['term:scourge','item:frostmourne','chapter:the-lich-king-and-the-plague']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Lich King')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'loa',title:{en:"Loa",tr:"Loa"},summary:{en:"The powerful animal spirits and gods that the trolls worship.",tr:"Trollerin tapt\u0131\u011f\u0131 g\xfc\xe7l\xfc hayvan ruhlar\u0131 ve tanr\u0131lar."},body:{en:["Every troll tribe honours the loa, ancient spirits that often take the form of great beasts, and bargains with them for strength. Some are fickle but fair; others are cruel. Hakkar the Soulflayer, the loa of blood, nearly devoured the Gurubashi Empire, and his followers still stir in Stranglethorn Vale and the Swamp of Sorrows."],tr:["Her trol kabilesi loa\u2019lara sayg\u0131 g\xf6sterir; \xe7o\u011fu zaman b\xfcy\xfck hayvan bi\xe7imine b\xfcr\xfcnen bu kadim ruhlarla g\xfc\xe7 kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131nda pazarl\u0131k eder. Kimi kaprisli ama adildir, kimi ac\u0131mas\u0131z. Kan\u0131n loas\u0131 Hakkar the Soulflayer, Gurubashi \u0130mparatorlu\u011fu\u2019nu neredeyse yuttu; m\xfcritleri Stranglethorn Vale ve Swamp of Sorrows b\xf6lgelerinde h\xe2l\xe2 k\u0131p\u0131rdan\u0131yor."]},era:'ancient-kalimdor',order:20,links:{raceIds:['troll'],zoneIds:['stranglethorn-vale','swamp-of-sorrows'],instanceIds:['temple-of-atalhakkar','zulfarrak'],loreIds:['item:heart-of-hakkar']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Loa')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'nathrezim',title:{en:"Nathrezim",tr:"Nathrezim (deh\u015fet lordlar\u0131)"},summary:{en:"The dreadlords: cunning, vampiric demons who serve the Legion through deceit.",tr:"Deh\u015fet lordlar\u0131: Lejyon\u2019a hileyle hizmet eden kurnaz, vampirimsi iblisler."},body:{en:["The nathrezim prefer whispers to open war. The Legion set dreadlords such as Mal'Ganis, Tichondrius and Balnazzar to watch over the Lich King and guide the Scourge\u2019s conquest of Lordaeron. When the Lich King broke free of them they scattered, yet some still hide in plain sight: Balnazzar wears the face of the Scarlet Crusade\u2019s Grand Crusader."],tr:["Nathrezim a\xe7\u0131k sava\u015f yerine f\u0131s\u0131lt\u0131y\u0131 se\xe7er. Lejyon, Mal'Ganis, Tichondrius ve Balnazzar gibi deh\u015fet lordlar\u0131n\u0131 Lich King\u2019i g\xf6zetmek ve Scourge\u2019un Lordaeron fethini y\xf6nlendirmek i\xe7in g\xf6revlendirdi. Lich King onlar\u0131n boyunduru\u011fundan kurtulunca da\u011f\u0131ld\u0131lar; yine de baz\u0131lar\u0131 g\xf6z \xf6n\xfcnde saklan\u0131yor: Balnazzar, Scarlet Crusade\u2019in B\xfcy\xfck Ha\xe7l\u0131s\u0131\u2019n\u0131n y\xfcz\xfcn\xfc ta\u015f\u0131yor."]},era:'third-war',order:21,links:{zoneIds:['eastern-plaguelands','tirisfal-glades'],instanceIds:['stratholme'],loreIds:['term:burning-legion','term:scarlet-crusade']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Nathrezim')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'nordrassil',title:{en:"Nordrassil",tr:"Nordrassil"},summary:{en:"The World Tree of Mount Hyjal, grown by the Aspects to seal the second Well of Eternity.",tr:"Mount Hyjal\u2019\u0131n D\xfcnya A\u011fac\u0131; Aspect\u2019lerin ikinci Sonsuzluk Kuyusu\u2019nu m\xfch\xfcrlemek i\xe7in b\xfcy\xfctt\xfc\u011f\xfc a\u011fa\xe7."},body:{en:["After the Sundering, Illidan secretly poured stolen water from the Well of Eternity into a lake on Mount Hyjal. To seal this new well, the Dragon Aspects planted an enchanted seed that grew into Nordrassil, and its blessing made the night elves ageless. Archimonde\u2019s fall at its roots wounded the tree, and Forever\u2019s Hyjal Summit raid climbs to the peak beside it."],tr:["B\xfcy\xfck Yar\u0131lma\u2019dan sonra Illidan, Sonsuzluk Kuyusu\u2019ndan \xe7ald\u0131\u011f\u0131 suyu gizlice Mount Hyjal\u2019daki bir g\xf6le d\xf6kt\xfc. Bu yeni kuyuyu m\xfch\xfcrlemek i\xe7in Ejderha Aspect\u2019leri b\xfcy\xfcl\xfc bir tohum ekti; tohum Nordrassil\u2019e d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc ve bereketi gece elflerini ya\u015flanmaz k\u0131ld\u0131. Archimonde\u2019un k\xf6klerinde d\xfc\u015f\xfc\u015f\xfc a\u011fac\u0131 yaralad\u0131; Forever\u2019\u0131n Hyjal Summit bask\u0131n\u0131 onun yan\u0131ndaki zirveye t\u0131rman\u0131r."]},era:'ancient-kalimdor',order:22,links:{raceIds:['night-elf'],classIds:['druid'],instanceIds:['hyjal-summit'],loreIds:['term:well-of-eternity','item:horn-of-cenarius','chapter:the-long-watch-of-hyjal']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Nordrassil'),n.FOREVER.raids],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'old-gods',title:{en:"Old Gods",tr:"Kadim Tanr\u0131lar (Old Gods)"},summary:{en:"Ancient beings of the Void that buried themselves in Azeroth to corrupt its world-soul.",tr:"Azeroth\u2019un d\xfcnya ruhunu yozla\u015ft\u0131rmak i\xe7in kendilerini onun derinliklerine g\xf6men, Hi\xe7lik\u2019ten gelen kadim varl\u0131klar."},body:{en:["Long before mortals walked the world, the Old Gods, among them C'Thun, Yogg-Saron, N'Zoth and Y'Shaarj, crashed into Azeroth and raised a Black Empire. Tearing Y'Shaarj out wounded the world itself, so the titans chose to imprison the others underground instead. Their whispers still drive cults like the Twilight\u2019s Hammer, and C'Thun stirs beneath Ahn'Qiraj in Silithus."],tr:["D\xfcnyada \xf6l\xfcml\xfcler y\xfcr\xfcmeden \xe7ok \xf6nce C'Thun, Yogg-Saron, N'Zoth ve Y'Shaarj gibi Kadim Tanr\u0131lar Azeroth\u2019a \xe7ak\u0131ld\u0131 ve bir Kara \u0130mparatorluk kurdu. Y'Shaarj\u2019\u0131n s\xf6k\xfcl\xfcp at\u0131lmas\u0131 d\xfcnyan\u0131n kendisini yaralad\u0131\u011f\u0131 i\xe7in titanlar di\u011ferlerini yeralt\u0131na hapsetmeyi se\xe7ti. F\u0131s\u0131lt\u0131lar\u0131 h\xe2l\xe2 Twilight's Hammer gibi tarikatlar\u0131 y\xf6nlendiriyor; C'Thun ise Silithus\u2019ta Ahn'Qiraj\u2019\u0131n alt\u0131nda k\u0131p\u0131rdan\u0131yor."]},era:'creation',order:23,links:{zoneIds:['silithus'],loreIds:['term:titans','term:twilights-hammer','chapter:titans-and-old-gods']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Old God')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'silver-hand',title:{en:"Order of the Silver Hand",tr:"G\xfcm\xfc\u015f El Tarikat\u0131 (Silver Hand)"},summary:{en:"The first order of paladins, founded in Lordaeron during the Second War.",tr:"\u0130kinci Sava\u015f s\u0131ras\u0131nda Lordaeron\u2019da kurulan ilk Paladin tarikat\u0131."},body:{en:["Archbishop Alonsus Faol saw that clerics alone could not survive the Horde, so he trained warriors in the ways of the Light. Uther the Lightbringer became the first of the Knights of the Silver Hand. The order fought through the Second War, but Arthas\u2019s fall broke it: Uther died at the hand of his former student, and many survivors drifted into the Scarlet Crusade."],tr:["Ba\u015fpiskopos Alonsus Faol, yaln\u0131z din adamlar\u0131n\u0131n Horde kar\u015f\u0131s\u0131nda ayakta kalamayaca\u011f\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6rd\xfc ve sava\u015f\xe7\u0131lar\u0131 I\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131n yolunda e\u011fitti. Uther the Lightbringer, G\xfcm\xfc\u015f El \u015e\xf6valyeleri\u2019nin ilki oldu. Tarikat \u0130kinci Sava\u015f boyunca sava\u015ft\u0131; ama Arthas\u2019\u0131n d\xfc\u015f\xfc\u015f\xfc onu par\xe7alad\u0131: Uther eski \xf6\u011frencisinin elinde \xf6ld\xfc, hayatta kalanlar\u0131n \xe7o\u011fu Scarlet Crusade\u2019e kayd\u0131."]},era:'second-war',order:24,links:{classIds:['paladin'],raceIds:['human','dwarf'],loreIds:['term:holy-light','term:scarlet-crusade','item:ashbringer']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Knights of the Silver Hand')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'queldorei',title:{en:"Quel'dorei",tr:"Quel'dorei (y\xfcksek elfler)"},summary:{en:"The high elves of Quel'Thalas, heirs of the exiled Highborne.",tr:"Quel'Thalas\u2019\u0131n y\xfcksek elfleri; s\xfcrg\xfcn edilen Highborne\u2019un miras\xe7\u0131lar\u0131."},body:{en:["Nearly seven thousand years before the Dark Portal, exiled Highborne crossed the sea, founded Quel'Thalas and kindled the Sunwell. They allied with the humans of Arathor in the Troll Wars and taught them magic. When Arthas\u2019s Scourge ravaged their kingdom and fouled the Sunwell, most survivors took a new name in memory of their dead: the sin'dorei, or blood elves."],tr:["Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten yakla\u015f\u0131k yedi bin y\u0131l \xf6nce s\xfcrg\xfcndeki Highborne denizi a\u015ft\u0131, Quel'Thalas\u2019\u0131 kurdu ve Sunwell\u2019i tutu\u015fturdu. Trol Sava\u015flar\u0131\u2019nda Arathor insanlar\u0131yla ittifak kurup onlara b\xfcy\xfc \xf6\u011frettiler. Arthas\u2019\u0131n Scourge\u2019u krall\u0131klar\u0131n\u0131 yak\u0131p y\u0131k\u0131p Sunwell\u2019i kirletince hayatta kalanlar\u0131n \xe7o\u011fu \xf6l\xfclerinin an\u0131s\u0131na yeni bir ad ald\u0131: sin'dorei, yani kan elfleri."]},era:'elder-kingdoms',order:25,links:{classIds:['mage'],loreIds:['term:highborne','term:sunwell','chapter:exiles-of-quelthalas']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('High elf'),(0,n.wiki)("Quel'Thalas")],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'scarlet-crusade',title:{en:"Scarlet Crusade",tr:"Scarlet Crusade (K\u0131z\u0131l Ha\xe7l\u0131lar)"},summary:{en:"Zealots who hunt the undead and anyone they suspect of plague, secretly led by a dreadlord.",tr:"\xd6l\xfcms\xfczleri ve vebal\u0131 sand\u0131klar\u0131 herkesi avlayan, gizlice bir deh\u015fet lordunun y\xf6netti\u011fi ba\u011fnazlar."},body:{en:["Born from survivors of Lordaeron\u2019s paladins and soldiers, the Crusade swore to purge the Scourge but grew so fanatical that it attacks the Forsaken and living travellers alike. Its Grand Crusader is secretly the dreadlord Balnazzar. Its strongholds include the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades, Hearthglen and Tyr\u2019s Hand."],tr:["Lordaeron\u2019un Paladin\u2019lerinin ve askerlerinin art\u0131klar\u0131ndan do\u011fan Crusade, Scourge\u2019u temizlemeye ant i\xe7ti; ama \xf6yle ba\u011fnazla\u015ft\u0131 ki Forsaken\u2019a da ya\u015fayan yolculara da sald\u0131r\u0131yor. B\xfcy\xfck Ha\xe7l\u0131s\u0131 gizlice deh\u015fet lordu Balnazzar\u2019d\u0131r. Kaleleri aras\u0131nda Tirisfal Glades b\xf6lgesindeki Scarlet Monastery, Hearthglen ve Tyr's Hand bulunur."]},era:'classic',order:26,links:{classIds:['paladin'],zoneIds:['tirisfal-glades','western-plaguelands','eastern-plaguelands'],instanceIds:['scarlet-monastery-graveyard','scarlet-monastery-library','scarlet-monastery-armory','scarlet-monastery-cathedral'],loreIds:['term:nathrezim','term:argent-dawn','item:taelans-hammer']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Scarlet Crusade')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'scourge',title:{en:"Scourge",tr:"Scourge"},summary:{en:"The Lich King's army of the undead, spread by plague and necromancy.",tr:"Lich King\u2019in veba ve nekromansiyle yay\u0131lan \xf6l\xfcms\xfczler ordusu."},body:{en:["The Scourge are bound to the Lich King\u2019s will: ghouls, abominations, liches and death knights raised from the fallen. The plague that created them swept Lordaeron in the Third War and left the Plaguelands behind. Under Kel'Thuzad, the Scourge still holds Stratholme and Scholomance, and its reach extends as far as Razorfen Downs in the Barrens."],tr:["Scourge, Lich King\u2019in iradesine ba\u011fl\u0131d\u0131r: \xf6l\xfclerden diriltilen gulyabaniler, abominasyonlar, lich\u2019ler ve \xf6l\xfcm \u015f\xf6valyeleri. Onlar\u0131 yaratan veba \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019ta Lordaeron\u2019u kas\u0131p kavurdu ve geride Plaguelands\u2019i b\u0131rakt\u0131. Kel'Thuzad\u2019\u0131n y\xf6netimindeki Scourge h\xe2l\xe2 Stratholme ile Scholomance\u2019\u0131 elinde tutuyor; eli Barrens b\xf6lgesindeki Razorfen Downs\u2019a kadar uzan\u0131yor."]},era:'third-war',order:27,links:{zoneIds:['western-plaguelands','eastern-plaguelands','barrens'],instanceIds:['stratholme','scholomance','razorfen-downs'],loreIds:['term:lich-king','term:cult-of-the-damned']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Scourge')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'skywall',title:{en:"Skywall",tr:"Skywall"},summary:{en:"The Elemental Plane of air, realm of Al'Akir the Windlord.",tr:"Havan\u0131n Elemental D\xfczlemi; R\xfczg\xe2r Lordu Al'Akir\u2019in diyar\u0131."},body:{en:["When the titans\u2019 servants bound the elementals, the lords of air were confined to Skywall, a realm of endless sky ruled by Al'Akir. In Forever, Skywall is also home to Zephras Isle, the floating starting zone of the Skyborne. The island\u2019s air elementals vanished centuries ago, and the magic holding it aloft is slowly failing."],tr:["Titanlar\u0131n hizmetk\xe2rlar\u0131 elementalleri ba\u011flad\u0131\u011f\u0131nda hava lordlar\u0131, Al'Akir\u2019in y\xf6netti\u011fi sonsuz bir g\xf6ky\xfcz\xfc diyar\u0131 olan Skywall\u2019a hapsedildi. Forever\u2019da Skywall, Skyborne\u2019un havada s\xfcz\xfclen ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7 b\xf6lgesi Zephras Isle\u2019a da ev sahipli\u011fi yapar. Adan\u0131n hava elementalleri y\xfczy\u0131llar \xf6nce ortadan kayboldu; aday\u0131 havada tutan b\xfcy\xfc yava\u015f yava\u015f zay\u0131fl\u0131yor."]},era:'creation',order:28,links:{classIds:['shaman'],raceIds:['skyborne-high-order','skyborne-windshaper'],zoneIds:['zephras-isle'],loreIds:['term:elemental-lords','item:thunderfury']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Skywall'),n.FOREVER.zephrasIsle],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'sunwell',title:{en:"Sunwell",tr:"Sunwell (G\xfcne\u015f Kuyusu)"},summary:{en:"The fount of arcane power at the heart of Quel'Thalas.",tr:"Quel'Thalas\u2019\u0131n kalbindeki arkan g\xfc\xe7 kayna\u011f\u0131."},body:{en:["Dath'Remar Sunstrider poured a stolen vial from the Well of Eternity into a lake where ley lines meet, and the Sunwell blazed to life. For millennia it fed the magic and culture of the high elves. During the Third War, Arthas used its waters to raise Kel'Thuzad as a lich and defiled the fount, and its loss left the survivors with a lasting hunger for magic."],tr:["Dath'Remar Sunstrider, Sonsuzluk Kuyusu\u2019ndan \xe7al\u0131nm\u0131\u015f bir \u015fi\u015fe suyu ley hatlar\u0131n\u0131n bulu\u015ftu\u011fu bir g\xf6le d\xf6kt\xfc ve Sunwell alev alev canland\u0131. Binlerce y\u0131l boyunca y\xfcksek elflerin b\xfcy\xfcs\xfcn\xfc ve k\xfclt\xfcr\xfcn\xfc besledi. \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019ta Arthas, Kel'Thuzad\u2019\u0131 lich olarak diriltmek i\xe7in onun sular\u0131n\u0131 kullan\u0131p kayna\u011f\u0131 kirletti; Sunwell\u2019in kayb\u0131 hayatta kalanlarda dinmeyen bir b\xfcy\xfc a\xe7l\u0131\u011f\u0131 b\u0131rakt\u0131."]},era:'elder-kingdoms',order:29,links:{classIds:['mage'],loreIds:['term:queldorei','term:ley-lines','term:well-of-eternity']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Sunwell')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'titan-forged',title:{en:"Titan-forged",tr:"Titan yap\u0131m\u0131 varl\u0131klar (Titan-forged)"},summary:{en:"The keepers and other servants the titans made to bring order to Azeroth.",tr:"Titanlar\u0131n Azeroth\u2019a d\xfczen vermek i\xe7in yaratt\u0131\u011f\u0131 bek\xe7iler ve di\u011fer hizmetk\xe2rlar."},body:{en:["The titans shaped servants to finish their work: towering keepers, and races of stone and metal such as the earthen and the mechagnomes. Over the ages the Old Gods\u2019 Curse of Flesh turned many of them mortal, and the dwarves and gnomes descend from them. Titan-forged guardians still keep vaults like Uldaman, and Forever adds more titan sites, from the Wetlands excavation to Shaper\u2019s Terrace in Un'Goro Crater."],tr:["Titanlar i\u015flerini tamamlamak i\xe7in hizmetk\xe2rlar yaratt\u0131: dev bek\xe7iler ve earthen ile mekagnomlar gibi ta\u015ftan ve metalden \u0131rklar. \xc7a\u011flar boyunca Kadim Tanr\u0131lar\u0131n Et Laneti (Curse of Flesh) bir\xe7o\u011funu \xf6l\xfcml\xfcye d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc; c\xfcceler ve gnomlar onlar\u0131n soyundan gelir. Titan yap\u0131m\u0131 muhaf\u0131zlar h\xe2l\xe2 Uldaman gibi mahzenleri bekler; Forever da Wetlands kaz\u0131s\u0131ndan Un'Goro Crater\u2019daki Shaper's Terrace\u2019a kadar yeni titan mek\xe2nlar\u0131 ekliyor."]},era:'creation',order:30,links:{raceIds:['dwarf','gnome'],zoneIds:['badlands','un-goro-crater','wetlands'],instanceIds:['uldaman','excavation-site-wetlands','shapers-terrace'],loreIds:['term:titans','term:explorers-league']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Titan-forged'),n.FOREVER.dungeons],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'titans',title:{en:"Titans",tr:"Titanlar"},summary:{en:"Colossal world-souls who sought to bring order to the cosmos and shaped Azeroth.",tr:"Evrene d\xfczen getirmeye \xe7al\u0131\u015fan ve Azeroth\u2019a bi\xe7im veren devasa d\xfcnya ruhlar\u0131."},body:{en:["The titans are world-souls awakened into godlike beings. Their Pantheon, led by Aman'Thul, searched the cosmos for sleeping world-souls and found one of great promise within Azeroth. They tore the Old God Y'Shaarj from the world, imprisoned the rest, and left their servants to shape the land. Their mightiest champion, Sargeras, later fell and founded the Burning Legion."],tr:["Titanlar, tanr\u0131sal varl\u0131klara d\xf6n\xfc\u015fm\xfc\u015f uyanm\u0131\u015f d\xfcnya ruhlar\u0131d\u0131r. Aman'Thul\u2019un \xf6nderlik etti\u011fi Panteon, evrende uyuyan d\xfcnya ruhlar\u0131n\u0131 arad\u0131 ve Azeroth\u2019un i\xe7inde b\xfcy\xfck vaat ta\u015f\u0131yan birini buldu. Kadim Tanr\u0131 Y'Shaarj\u2019\u0131 d\xfcnyadan s\xf6k\xfcp att\u0131lar, di\u011ferlerini hapsettiler ve topra\u011f\u0131 bi\xe7imlendirmeyi hizmetk\xe2rlar\u0131na b\u0131rakt\u0131lar. En g\xfc\xe7l\xfc \u015fampiyonlar\u0131 Sargeras ise sonradan d\xfc\u015ft\xfc ve Yanan Lejyon\u2019u kurdu."]},era:'creation',order:31,links:{zoneIds:['un-goro-crater','badlands'],instanceIds:['uldaman'],loreIds:['term:old-gods','term:titan-forged','term:burning-legion','chapter:titans-and-old-gods']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Titan')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'twilights-hammer',title:{en:"Twilight's Hammer",tr:"Twilight's Hammer (Alacakaranl\u0131k \xc7ekici)"},summary:{en:"Once an orc clan, now a doomsday cult that serves the Old Gods.",tr:"Bir zamanlar ork klan\u0131, bug\xfcn Kadim Tanr\u0131lara hizmet eden bir k\u0131yamet tarikat\u0131."},body:{en:["Led by the two-headed ogre mage Cho'gall, the Twilight\u2019s Hammer fought in the Second War as an orc clan before turning into a cult that longs for the end of the world. Its members, drawn from every race, gather in places such as Blackfathom Deeps and Silithus. In Forever, the cult also holds the ruins of Sunnyglade in the Riverglades."],tr:["\u0130ki ba\u015fl\u0131 ogre Mage\u2019i Cho'gall\u2019\xfcn \xf6nderli\u011findeki Twilight's Hammer, \u0130kinci Sava\u015f\u2019ta bir ork klan\u0131 olarak sava\u015ft\u0131; sonra d\xfcnyan\u0131n sonunu \xf6zleyen bir tarikata d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc. Her \u0131rktan \xfcyeleri Blackfathom Deeps ve Silithus gibi yerlerde toplan\u0131r. Forever\u2019da tarikat, Riverglades b\xf6lgesindeki Sunnyglade harabelerini de elinde tutuyor."]},era:'second-war',order:32,links:{zoneIds:['riverglades','silithus','ashenvale'],instanceIds:['blackfathom-deeps'],loreIds:['term:old-gods','chapter:the-second-war']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)("Twilight's Hammer"),n.FOREVER.riverglades],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'term',slug:'well-of-eternity',title:{en:"Well of Eternity",tr:"Sonsuzluk Kuyusu (Well of Eternity)"},summary:{en:"The lake of raw arcane power at the heart of ancient Kalimdor, whose implosion sundered the world.",tr:"Kadim Kalimdor\u2019un kalbindeki ham arkan g\xfc\xe7 g\xf6l\xfc; \xe7\xf6k\xfc\u015f\xfc d\xfcnyay\u0131 par\xe7alad\u0131."},body:{en:["The Well formed where the titans tore Y'Shaarj from the world, and the keepers calmed the bleeding wound into a lake of pure power. The night elves built their empire on its shores, and the reckless spells of the Highborne drew the Legion through it. Its collapse in the War of the Ancients caused the Great Sundering, and the Maelstrom churns where it once lay."],tr:["Kuyu, titanlar\u0131n Y'Shaarj\u2019\u0131 d\xfcnyadan s\xf6k\xfcp att\u0131\u011f\u0131 yerde olu\u015ftu; bek\xe7iler kanayan yaray\u0131 yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131p saf bir g\xfc\xe7 g\xf6l\xfcne d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc. Gece elfleri imparatorluklar\u0131n\u0131 onun k\u0131y\u0131lar\u0131nda kurdu; Highborne\u2019un pervas\u0131z b\xfcy\xfcleri Lejyon\u2019u bu kuyudan i\xe7eri \xe7ekti. Kadimler Sava\u015f\u0131\u2019ndaki \xe7\xf6k\xfc\u015f\xfc B\xfcy\xfck Yar\u0131lma\u2019ya yol a\xe7t\u0131; bir zamanlar bulundu\u011fu yerde bug\xfcn Maelstrom d\xf6ner."]},era:'creation',order:33,links:{raceIds:['night-elf'],zoneIds:['azshara'],loreIds:['term:highborne','term:nordrassil','chapter:war-of-the-ancients']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Well of Eternity')],basis:'established'})]},867,[866]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"instanceLore",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});var n=r(d[0]);const t=[(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'hall-of-thanes',subjectId:'hall-of-thanes',era:'classic',order:1,title:{en:'The Hall of Thanes',tr:'The Hall of Thanes'},summary:{en:"Ironforge's royal crypt, broken into by intruders the dwarves suspect are Dark Irons.",tr:"Ironforge\u2019un kraliyet mezarl\u0131\u011f\u0131; c\xfcceler i\xe7eri zorla giren davetsiz misafirlerin Dark Iron oldu\u011fundan \u015f\xfcpheleniyor."},body:{en:["Beneath Ironforge lies the Hall of Thanes, where the dwarves lay their monarchs to rest and tend the tombs with care. Its entrance waits at the threshold of the High Seat, in the heart of the city: an easy walk for the Alliance, a daring trespass for any Horde group. Now intruders have forced their way into the hallowed tombs. The dwarves suspect the Dark Iron clan, and the old stone is full of ghostly whispers.","Most of its quests are for the Alliance and begin in Kharanos or around Ironforge, though one of the quests inside is offered by a neutral ghost. Four foes block the way: Faldrim Anvilmar, Magmatus, Plunder and Durgen Dirgehammer."],tr:["Ironforge\u2019un alt\u0131nda, c\xfccelerin h\xfck\xfcmdarlar\u0131n\u0131 topra\u011fa verip mezarlar\u0131n\u0131 \xf6zenle korudu\u011fu Hall of Thanes uzan\u0131r. Giri\u015fi \u015fehrin kalbinde, High Seat\u2019in e\u015fi\u011findedir: \u0130ttifak i\xe7in k\u0131sa bir y\xfcr\xfcy\xfc\u015f, herhangi bir Horde (Orda) grubu i\xe7inse c\xfcretk\xe2r bir izinsiz giri\u015f. \u015eimdi davetsiz misafirler kutsal mezarlara zorla girdi. C\xfcceler Dark Iron klan\u0131ndan \u015f\xfcpheleniyor; eski ta\u015flar ise hayalet f\u0131s\u0131lt\u0131lar\u0131yla dolu.","G\xf6revlerinin \xe7o\u011fu \u0130ttifak\u2019a y\xf6neliktir ve Kharanos\u2019ta ya da Ironforge \xe7evresinde ba\u015flar; i\xe7erideki g\xf6revlerden birini ise tarafs\u0131z bir hayalet verir. Yolu d\xf6rt d\xfc\u015fman keser: Faldrim Anvilmar, Magmatus, Plunder ve Durgen Dirgehammer."]},links:{instanceIds:['hall-of-thanes'],zoneIds:['dun-morogh'],raceIds:['dwarf'],factionIds:['alliance'],loreIds:['chapter:war-of-the-three-hammers','chapter:azeroth-in-year-twenty-five']},image:'instance:hall-of-thanes',sources:[n.FOREVER.dungeons,(0,n.instanceSource)('hall-of-thanes')],basis:'forever',unknowns:[{en:'Who the intruders really are; the official text says only that the dwarves suspect the Dark Iron clan.',tr:'Davetsiz misafirlerin ger\xe7ekte kim oldu\u011fu; resm\xee metin yaln\u0131zca c\xfccelerin Dark Iron klan\u0131ndan \u015f\xfcphelendi\u011fini s\xf6yl\xfcyor.'},{en:'What has stirred inside the halls, and the story behind each of the four foes.',tr:'Salonlarda neyin uyand\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve d\xf6rt d\xfc\u015fman\u0131n her birinin hik\xe2yesi.'}]}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'ragefire-chasm',subjectId:'ragefire-chasm',era:'classic',order:2,title:{en:'Ragefire Chasm',tr:'Ragefire Chasm'},summary:{en:"Volcanic caves beneath Orgrimmar where troggs and a demon-serving cult threaten the Horde's new capital.",tr:'Orgrimmar\u2019\u0131n alt\u0131ndaki volkanik ma\u011faralar; trogg\u2019lar ve iblislere hizmet eden bir tarikat Horde\u2019un yeni ba\u015fkentini tehdit ediyor.'},body:{en:['A maze of lava-lit caverns runs beneath Orgrimmar, and the Horde has learned that its new capital does not rest easy. Troggs known as the Ragefire have climbed up from the deep tunnels, and when the tauren elder Magatha Grimtotem tried to make peace with them, she was met only with violence.',"Worse, a sect called the Searing Blade, loyal to the demonic Shadow Council, has hidden in the chasm to plot against everything Thrall's people have built. It is led by Taragaman the Hungerer, a felguard, with the warlock Jergosh the Invoker and the satyr Bazzalan at his side. For many young Horde heroes, these caves are their first dungeon."],tr:['Orgrimmar\u2019\u0131n alt\u0131nda lav \u0131\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131yla ayd\u0131nlanan bir ma\u011fara labirenti uzan\u0131r ve Horde, yeni ba\u015fkentinin rahat uyumad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 \xf6\u011frendi. Ragefire adl\u0131 trogg\u2019lar derin t\xfcnellerden yukar\u0131 t\u0131rmand\u0131; tauren bilgesi Magatha Grimtotem onlarla bar\u0131\u015fmaya \xe7al\u0131\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131nda yaln\u0131zca \u015fiddetle kar\u015f\u0131la\u015ft\u0131.','Daha da k\xf6t\xfcs\xfc, iblis yanl\u0131s\u0131 Shadow Council\u2019a ba\u011fl\u0131 Searing Blade tarikat\u0131, Thrall\u2019\u0131n halk\u0131n\u0131n kurdu\u011fu her \u015feye kar\u015f\u0131 plan yapmak i\xe7in bu yar\u0131\u011fa sakland\u0131. Tarikat\u0131n ba\u015f\u0131nda bir felguard olan Taragaman the Hungerer var; yan\u0131nda Warlock Jergosh the Invoker ve satyr Bazzalan durur. Pek \xe7ok gen\xe7 Horde kahraman\u0131 i\xe7in bu ma\u011faralar ilk zindand\u0131r.']},links:{instanceIds:['ragefire-chasm'],zoneIds:['durotar'],factionIds:['horde'],loreIds:['chapter:durotar-and-theramore']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('ragefire-chasm'),(0,n.wiki)('Searing Blade')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'ruins-of-lordaeron',subjectId:'ruins-of-lordaeron',era:'classic',order:3,title:{en:'Ruins of Lordaeron',tr:'Ruins of Lordaeron'},summary:{en:'The broken capital above the Undercity, where the Forsaken reclaim their past while a necromancer gathers power.',tr:'Undercity\u2019nin \xfczerindeki y\u0131k\u0131k ba\u015fkent; Forsaken ge\xe7mi\u015fini geri almaya \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131rken bir nekromans\xf6r g\xfc\xe7 topluyor.'},body:{en:['The Forsaken are trying to take back the ruined capital above their Undercity. Its rubble still holds treasured heirlooms and memories, but the Scourge haunts the broken streets, and there is word of a necromancer gathering power within the walls. Adventurers are called in to help make the city safe.',"Horde groups reach the entrance easily from the Undercity, while Alliance groups must venture into Horde lands. Both factions find quests: Horde ones begin in the Undercity, Silverpine and Tirisfal, Alliance ones inside the ruins. The way leads past Witherfang, The Baron, Viktor the Vile, The Abandoned and Bjork to the final foe, Rath'mael."],tr:['Forsaken, Undercity\u2019nin \xfczerindeki y\u0131k\u0131k ba\u015fkenti geri almaya \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor. Molozlar\u0131n aras\u0131nda h\xe2l\xe2 de\u011ferli yadig\xe2rlar ve an\u0131lar duruyor; ama y\u0131k\u0131k sokaklarda Scourge dola\u015f\u0131yor ve surlar\u0131n i\xe7inde g\xfc\xe7 toplayan bir nekromans\xf6rden s\xf6z ediliyor. Macerac\u0131lar \u015fehri g\xfcvenli h\xe2le getirmeye yard\u0131m etmek i\xe7in \xe7a\u011fr\u0131l\u0131yor.',"Horde gruplar\u0131 giri\u015fe Undercity\u2019den kolayca ula\u015f\u0131r; \u0130ttifak gruplar\u0131 ise Horde topraklar\u0131na girmek zorundad\u0131r. \u0130ki taraf i\xe7in de g\xf6rev vard\u0131r: Horde g\xf6revleri Undercity, Silverpine ve Tirisfal\u2019da, \u0130ttifak g\xf6revleri ise harabelerin i\xe7inde ba\u015flar. Yol Witherfang, The Baron, Viktor the Vile, The Abandoned ve Bjork\u2019tan ge\xe7ip son d\xfc\u015fman Rath'mael\u2019e var\u0131r."]},links:{instanceIds:['ruins-of-lordaeron'],zoneIds:['tirisfal-glades','silverpine-forest'],raceIds:['undead'],factionIds:['horde'],loreIds:['chapter:fall-of-lordaeron','chapter:rise-of-the-forsaken']},image:'instance:ruins-of-lordaeron',sources:[n.FOREVER.dungeons,(0,n.instanceSource)('ruins-of-lordaeron')],basis:'forever',unknowns:[{en:'Who the necromancer is and what the gathered power is for.',tr:'Nekromans\xf6r\xfcn kim oldu\u011fu ve toplanan g\xfcc\xfcn ne i\xe7in kullan\u0131laca\u011f\u0131.'},{en:'How much of the old capital the Forsaken mean to rebuild.',tr:'Forsaken\u2019\u0131n eski ba\u015fkentin ne kadar\u0131n\u0131 yeniden kurmay\u0131 ama\xe7lad\u0131\u011f\u0131.'}]}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'deadmines',subjectId:'deadmines',era:'classic',order:4,title:{en:'Deadmines',tr:'Deadmines'},summary:{en:"Westfall's abandoned gold mine, where Edwin VanCleef's Defias Brotherhood is building a warship in secret.",tr:'Westfall\u2019un terk edilmi\u015f alt\u0131n madeni; Edwin VanCleef\u2019in Defias Karde\u015fli\u011fi burada gizlice bir sava\u015f gemisi in\u015fa ediyor.'},body:{en:["Before the First War these tunnels were the richest gold mines in human lands; the orcs' sack of Stormwind left them empty. Now the Defias Brotherhood has made them its hidden fortress. Its leader, Edwin VanCleef, was a master stonemason who helped rebuild Stormwind after the war, until the city's nobles refused to pay his guild. Betrayed, his workers turned outlaw and spread through Westfall.",'The way in starts in the ruined village of Moonbrook. Far below, goblins such as Sneed and Gilnid help the Defias finish a great ship in a hidden cove, guarded by Mr. Smite and Captain Greenskin.'],tr:['Birinci Sava\u015f\u2019tan \xf6nce bu t\xfcneller insan topraklar\u0131n\u0131n en zengin alt\u0131n madenleriydi; orklar\u0131n Stormwind\u2019i ya\u011fmalamas\u0131 onlar\u0131 bombo\u015f b\u0131rakt\u0131. \u015eimdi Defias Karde\u015fli\u011fi (Defias Brotherhood) buray\u0131 gizli kalesine \xe7evirdi. Lideri Edwin VanCleef, sava\u015ftan sonra Stormwind\u2019in yeniden in\u015fas\u0131na yard\u0131m eden usta bir ta\u015f\xe7\u0131yd\u0131; ta ki \u015fehrin soylular\u0131 loncas\u0131na \xf6deme yapmay\u0131 reddedene dek. \u0130hanete u\u011frayan i\u015f\xe7ileri kanun ka\xe7a\u011f\u0131na d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc ve Westfall\u2019a yay\u0131ld\u0131.','Giri\u015f, harap Moonbrook k\xf6y\xfcnde ba\u015flar. \xc7ok a\u015fa\u011f\u0131da Sneed ve Gilnid gibi goblinler, gizli bir koyda Defias\u2019\u0131n b\xfcy\xfck gemisini tamamlamas\u0131na yard\u0131m ediyor; gemiyi Mr. Smite ile Captain Greenskin korur.']},links:{instanceIds:['deadmines'],zoneIds:['westfall'],factionIds:['alliance'],loreIds:['chapter:stormwind-in-shadow','chapter:the-first-war']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('deadmines'),(0,n.wiki)('Edwin VanCleef'),(0,n.wiki)('Defias Brotherhood')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'wailing-caverns',subjectId:'wailing-caverns',era:'classic',order:5,title:{en:'Wailing Caverns',tr:'Wailing Caverns'},summary:{en:"Caves beneath the Barrens where the druid Naralex's dream of renewal turned into a nightmare.",tr:'Barrens\u2019\u0131n alt\u0131ndaki ma\u011faralar; Druid Naralex\u2019in yenilenme d\xfc\u015f\xfc burada bir k\xe2busa d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc.'},body:{en:['The Wailing Caverns take their name from the moaning of wind and steam through cracks in the rock. The night elf druid Naralex found them and hoped to link their underground springs to the Emerald Dream, so that green life would spread across the dry Barrens once more. While he meditated, the Emerald Nightmare overwhelmed him instead.','Trapped in sleep, Naralex now pours that corruption into the caves. Their creatures have warped into deviate beasts, and most of his disciples went mad and became the Druids of the Fang, among them Lady Anacondra and Lords Cobrahn, Pythas and Serpentis. Waking Naralex means facing Mutanus the Devourer.'],tr:['Wailing Caverns ad\u0131n\u0131, kayadaki \xe7atlaklardan ge\xe7en r\xfczg\xe2r\u0131n ve buhar\u0131n inlemesinden al\u0131r. Gece elfi Druid Naralex ma\u011faralar\u0131 buldu ve yeralt\u0131 kaynaklar\u0131n\u0131 Z\xfcmr\xfct R\xfcya\u2019ya (Emerald Dream) ba\u011flayarak kurak Barrens\u2019a yeniden ye\u015fil bir hayat yaymay\u0131 umdu. Ama o meditasyondayken Z\xfcmr\xfct K\xe2bus (Emerald Nightmare) onu ele ge\xe7irdi.','Uykusuna hapsolan Naralex \u015fimdi bu bozulmay\u0131 ma\u011faralara ak\u0131t\u0131yor. Buradaki yarat\u0131klar sapk\u0131n (deviate) canavarlara d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc; \xf6\u011frencilerinin \xe7o\u011fu akl\u0131n\u0131 yitirip Druids of the Fang oldu, aralar\u0131nda Lady Anacondra ile Lord Cobrahn, Lord Pythas ve Lord Serpentis de var. Naralex\u2019i uyand\u0131rmak i\xe7in Mutanus the Devourer ile y\xfczle\u015fmek gerekir.']},links:{instanceIds:['wailing-caverns'],zoneIds:['barrens'],classIds:['druid'],raceIds:['night-elf'],loreIds:['chapter:azeroth-in-year-twenty-five']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('wailing-caverns'),(0,n.wiki)('Naralex'),(0,n.wiki)('Druids of the Fang')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'shadowfang-keep',subjectId:'shadowfang-keep',era:'classic',order:6,title:{en:'Shadowfang Keep',tr:'Shadowfang Keep'},summary:{en:'A haunted keep in Silverpine where the mad archmage Arugal shelters the worgen he unleashed.',tr:'Silverpine\u2019da perili bir kale; \xe7\u0131ld\u0131rm\u0131\u015f ba\u015fb\xfcy\xfcc\xfc Arugal, d\xfcnyaya sald\u0131\u011f\u0131 worgen\u2019leri burada bar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131yor.'},body:{en:["The Kirin Tor were losing the Third War's struggle against the Scourge, and every wizard who fell soon stood up again on the enemy's side. Archmage Arugal ignored his colleagues' warnings and reached beyond the world for help, calling up the savage worgen. They ripped into the undead, then into Dalaran's own ranks, and swarmed the keep of Baron Silverlaine on the hill over Pyrewood.","Guilt cracked Arugal's mind. He now calls the wolf-men his children and hides with them in the keep, renamed Shadowfang, guarded by the great wolf Fenrus. The baron's ghost has never left, and the Forsaken of Silverpine want the archmage dead."],tr:['Kirin Tor, \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019ta Scourge\u2019a kar\u015f\u0131 verdi\u011fi m\xfccadeleyi kaybediyordu; d\xfc\u015fen her b\xfcy\xfcc\xfc k\u0131sa s\xfcre sonra d\xfc\u015fman saf\u0131nda yeniden aya\u011fa kalk\u0131yordu. Ba\u015fb\xfcy\xfcc\xfc Arugal meslekta\u015flar\u0131n\u0131n uyar\u0131lar\u0131n\u0131 dinlemedi, yard\u0131m i\xe7in d\xfcnyan\u0131n \xf6tesine uzan\u0131p vah\u015fi worgen\u2019leri \xe7a\u011f\u0131rd\u0131. Kurt adamlar \xf6nce \xf6l\xfcleri, sonra Dalaran\u2019\u0131n kendi saflar\u0131n\u0131 par\xe7alad\u0131 ve Pyrewood\u2019un yukar\u0131s\u0131ndaki tepede duran Baron Silverlaine\u2019in kalesini bast\u0131.','Su\xe7luluk Arugal\u2019\u0131n akl\u0131n\u0131 \xe7atlatt\u0131. Art\u0131k kurt adamlara \xe7ocuklar\u0131m diyor ve onlarla birlikte ad\u0131 Shadowfang olarak de\u011fi\u015fen kaleye saklan\u0131yor; onu dev kurt Fenrus korur. Baronun hayaleti kaleyi hi\xe7 terk etmedi, Silverpine\u2019daki Forsaken ise ba\u015fb\xfcy\xfcc\xfcn\xfcn \xf6l\xfcm\xfcn\xfc istiyor.']},links:{instanceIds:['shadowfang-keep'],zoneIds:['silverpine-forest'],loreIds:['chapter:fall-of-lordaeron']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('shadowfang-keep'),(0,n.wiki)('Arugal')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'excavation-site-wetlands',subjectId:'excavation-site-wetlands',era:'classic',order:7,title:{en:'Excavation Site: Wetlands',tr:'Excavation Site: Wetlands'},summary:{en:"A dig above Whelgar's Excavation has opened onto a place untouched by time, guarded by stray titan constructs.",tr:"Whelgar's Excavation\u2019\u0131n yukar\u0131s\u0131ndaki kaz\u0131, zaman\u0131n dokunmad\u0131\u011f\u0131 bir yere a\xe7\u0131ld\u0131; buray\u0131 ba\u015f\u0131bo\u015f titan yap\u0131tlar\u0131 koruyor."},body:{en:["Something has woken in the hills of the Wetlands, near Thelgen Rock and Dun Algaz. Mist creeps down the slopes above Whelgar's Excavation and light flickers on the skyline. Beyond the dig, the land seems untouched by the passing ages; stray titan machines and fierce wildlife stand guard over secrets that the Explorers' League is eager to uncover.","Alliance quests start in Menethil Harbor, Greenwarden's Grove and Lakeshire, Horde quests in Orgrimmar and Hammerfall. Saltspine and Shadetooth bar the path to the Relic Guardian, whose defeat yields a titan relic that begins a quest for both factions."],tr:["Wetlands\u2019in tepelerinde, Thelgen Rock ve Dun Algaz yak\u0131nlar\u0131nda bir \u015fey uyand\u0131. Whelgar's Excavation\u2019\u0131n yukar\u0131s\u0131ndaki yama\xe7lardan sis s\xfcz\xfcl\xfcyor, ufukta \u0131\u015f\u0131klar titre\u015fiyor. Kaz\u0131n\u0131n \xf6tesindeki topraklara \xe7a\u011flar dokunmam\u0131\u015f gibi; ba\u015f\u0131bo\u015f titan makineleri ve vah\u015fi hayvanlar, Explorers' League\u2019in \xe7\xf6zmeye can att\u0131\u011f\u0131 s\u0131rlar\u0131 bekliyor.","\u0130ttifak g\xf6revleri Menethil Harbor, Greenwarden's Grove ve Lakeshire\u2019da, Horde g\xf6revleri Orgrimmar ve Hammerfall\u2019da ba\u015flar. Saltspine ve Shadetooth, Relic Guardian\u2019a giden yolu keser; onun yenilgisi, iki taraf i\xe7in de bir g\xf6rev ba\u015flatan bir titan kal\u0131nt\u0131s\u0131 b\u0131rak\u0131r."]},links:{instanceIds:['excavation-site-wetlands'],zoneIds:['wetlands','arathi-highlands','redridge-mountains'],loreIds:['chapter:titans-and-old-gods']},image:'instance:excavation-site-wetlands',sources:[n.FOREVER.dungeons,(0,n.instanceSource)('excavation-site-wetlands')],basis:'forever',unknowns:[{en:'What has woken beyond the dig, and what causes the mist and the lights.',tr:'Kaz\u0131n\u0131n \xf6tesinde neyin uyand\u0131\u011f\u0131; sisin ve \u0131\u015f\u0131klar\u0131n neden kaynakland\u0131\u011f\u0131.'},{en:'Who built the place and what the titan relic is for.',tr:'Buray\u0131 kimin kurdu\u011fu ve titan kal\u0131nt\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n ne i\u015fe yarad\u0131\u011f\u0131.'}]}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'stormwind-stockade',subjectId:'stormwind-stockade',era:'classic',order:8,title:{en:'Stormwind Stockade',tr:'Stormwind Stockade'},summary:{en:"Stormwind's prison, seized by its own inmates in a riot led by the Defias.",tr:'Stormwind\u2019in hapishanesi; Defias\u2019\u0131n \xf6nderlik etti\u011fi bir isyanla mahk\xfbmlar\u0131n eline ge\xe7ti.'},body:{en:['The Stockade sits in the heart of Stormwind City and holds thieves, murderers and political prisoners. Not long ago the inmates rose up, revealed their loyalty to the Defias Brotherhood and drove out the guards; now they run the cell blocks themselves.','Their ringleader is Bazil Thredd, a Defias agent. Among the prisoners are the Blackrock orc Targorr the Dread, the Dark Iron dwarf Kam Deepfury and the grave robber Dextren Ward. Several were condemned to death, but noble red tape kept stalling the sentences, so Lakeshire, Darkshire and even Ironforge quietly send adventurers in to settle the matter.'],tr:['Stockade, Stormwind City\u2019nin g\xf6be\u011finde yer al\u0131r; h\u0131rs\u0131zlar\u0131, katilleri ve siyasi mahk\xfbmlar\u0131 bar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131r. K\u0131sa s\xfcre \xf6nce mahk\xfbmlar ayakland\u0131, Defias Karde\u015fli\u011fi\u2019ne ba\u011fl\u0131l\u0131klar\u0131n\u0131 a\xe7\u0131\u011fa vurdu ve gardiyanlar\u0131 kovdu; ko\u011fu\u015flar\u0131 art\u0131k kendileri y\xf6netiyor.','Eleba\u015flar\u0131 Defias ajan\u0131 Bazil Thredd\u2019dir. Mahk\xfbmlar aras\u0131nda Blackrock orku Targorr the Dread, Dark Iron c\xfccesi Kam Deepfury ve mezar soyguncusu Dextren Ward da var. Baz\u0131lar\u0131 \xf6l\xfcme mahk\xfbm edildi, ama soylular\u0131n b\xfcrokrasisi infazlar\u0131 durmadan erteledi; bu y\xfczden Lakeshire, Darkshire ve hatta Ironforge i\u015fi bitirmeleri i\xe7in sessizce macerac\u0131lar g\xf6nderiyor.']},links:{instanceIds:['stormwind-stockade'],zoneIds:['elwynn-forest'],factionIds:['alliance'],loreIds:['chapter:stormwind-in-shadow']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('stormwind-stockade'),(0,n.wiki)('Bazil Thredd')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'city-of-dalaran',subjectId:'city-of-dalaran',era:'classic',order:9,title:{en:'City of Dalaran',tr:'City of Dalaran'},summary:{en:"The Kirin Tor's city in the Alterac Mountains, where the barrier over its restoration has fallen and magic runs wild.",tr:'Kirin Tor\u2019un Alterac Mountains\u2019taki \u015fehri; onar\u0131m \xe7al\u0131\u015fmalar\u0131n\u0131 gizleyen bariyer d\xfc\u015ft\xfc ve b\xfcy\xfc kontrolden \xe7\u0131kt\u0131.'},body:{en:['For a time, a magical barrier hid the work of restoring Dalaran. Now that shield has fallen and the city stands revealed in arcane chaos: spells misfire, constructs run loose and raw magic spills through the streets. The Kirin Tor need help, but only from people they trust.','Alliance heroes earn that trust starting with Emissary Jacques in Southshore; Horde heroes begin with Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill. Both roads lead to an image of Archmage Modera on the southern shore of Lordamere Lake, who hands over the Dalaran Sewer Key. From the sewers, groups choose their own route through the city toward the source of the trouble; the last foe is the Shade of the Archmage.'],tr:['Bir s\xfcre boyunca b\xfcy\xfcl\xfc bir bariyer, Dalaran\u2019\u0131 onarma \xe7al\u0131\u015fmalar\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6zlerden saklad\u0131. \u015eimdi o kalkan d\xfc\u015ft\xfc ve \u015fehir arkan bir karga\u015fan\u0131n ortas\u0131nda ortaya \xe7\u0131kt\u0131: b\xfcy\xfcler ters tepiyor, yapay muhaf\u0131zlar ba\u015f\u0131bo\u015f dola\u015f\u0131yor, ham b\xfcy\xfc sokaklara ta\u015f\u0131yor. Kirin Tor\u2019un yard\u0131ma ihtiyac\u0131 var, ama yaln\u0131zca g\xfcvendi\u011fi ki\u015filerden.','\u0130ttifak kahramanlar\u0131 bu g\xfcveni Southshore\u2019daki Emissary Jacques ile kazanmaya ba\u015flar, Horde kahramanlar\u0131 ise Tarren Mill\u2019deki Magus Wordeen Voidglare ile. \u0130ki yol da Lordamere Lake\u2019in g\xfcney k\u0131y\u0131s\u0131ndaki Archmage Modera imgesine \xe7\u0131kar; o da Dalaran Sewer Key\u2019i teslim eder. Gruplar la\u011f\u0131mlardan girip karga\u015fan\u0131n kayna\u011f\u0131na giden yolu kendileri se\xe7er; son d\xfc\u015fman Shade of the Archmage\u2019dir.']},links:{instanceIds:['city-of-dalaran'],zoneIds:['alterac-mountains','hillsbrad-foothills','silverpine-forest'],classIds:['mage'],loreIds:['chapter:guardians-and-the-seven-kingdoms']},image:'instance:city-of-dalaran',sources:[n.FOREVER.dungeons,(0,n.instanceSource)('city-of-dalaran')],basis:'forever',unknowns:[{en:'What caused the disruption, and whose shade the final foe is.',tr:'Karga\u015faya neyin yol a\xe7t\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve son d\xfc\u015fman\u0131n kimin g\xf6lgesi oldu\u011fu.'},{en:'How far the restoration of Dalaran has come.',tr:'Dalaran\u2019\u0131n onar\u0131m\u0131n\u0131n ne kadar ilerledi\u011fi.'}]}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'blackfathom-deeps',subjectId:'blackfathom-deeps',era:'classic',order:10,title:{en:'Blackfathom Deeps',tr:'Blackfathom Deeps'},summary:{en:'A drowned temple of Elune on the Ashenvale coast, now a shrine where cultists tend a beast of the Old Gods.',tr:'Ashenvale k\u0131y\u0131s\u0131nda sulara g\xf6m\xfclm\xfc\u015f bir Elune tap\u0131na\u011f\u0131; \u015fimdi tarikat\xe7\u0131lar\u0131n Kadim Tanr\u0131lar\u2019\u0131n bir canavar\u0131na bakt\u0131\u011f\u0131 bir mabet.'},body:{en:["A stair-ringed shaft on Ashenvale's Zoram Strand drops into flooded halls that once formed a temple of Elune, the night elves' moon goddess. The Great Sundering broke the shrine and dragged it under the sea, where it slept for ages until naga and satyrs, hungry for the power still lingering there, came to explore it.","Today the Twilight's Hammer cult worships in the deepest pools under Twilight Lord Kelris, tending Aku'mai, a monstrous beast cherished by the Old Gods. Shamans of the Earthen Ring have come to stop them, knowing that any summons to the Old Gods endangers the whole world."],tr:['Ashenvale\u2019in Zoram Strand k\u0131y\u0131s\u0131nda, merdivenlerle \xe7evrili bir kuyu, bir zamanlar gece elflerinin ay tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Elune\u2019a adanm\u0131\u015f bir tap\u0131nak olan sular alt\u0131ndaki salonlara iner. B\xfcy\xfck Yar\u0131lma (Great Sundering) mabedi par\xe7alay\u0131p denizin dibine \xe7ekti; naga\u2019lar ve satyr\u2019ler orada h\xe2l\xe2 dola\u015fan g\xfcc\xfcn pe\u015fine d\xfc\u015f\xfcp ke\u015ffe gelene dek \xe7a\u011flar boyunca uyudu.',"Bug\xfcn Twilight's Hammer tarikat\u0131, Twilight Lord Kelris \xf6nderli\u011finde en derin havuzlarda ibadet ediyor ve Kadim Tanr\u0131lar\u2019\u0131n (Old Gods) g\xf6zde canavar\u0131 Aku'mai\u2019ye bak\u0131yor. Earthen Ring Shaman\u2019lar\u0131, Kadim Tanr\u0131lar\u2019a yap\u0131lan her \xe7a\u011fr\u0131n\u0131n b\xfct\xfcn d\xfcnyay\u0131 tehlikeye att\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 bildikleri i\xe7in onlar\u0131 durdurmaya geldi."]},links:{instanceIds:['blackfathom-deeps'],zoneIds:['ashenvale'],raceIds:['night-elf'],loreIds:['chapter:war-of-the-ancients','chapter:titans-and-old-gods']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('blackfathom-deeps'),(0,n.wiki)("Aku'mai")],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'razorfen-kraul',subjectId:'razorfen-kraul',era:'classic',order:11,title:{en:'Razorfen Kraul',tr:'Razorfen Kraul'},summary:{en:"The quilboar's ancestral warren, grown from the thorns that sprang from a fallen demigod's blood.",tr:'Quilboar\u2019lar\u0131n atadan kalma yuvas\u0131; d\xfc\u015fm\xfc\u015f bir yar\u0131 tanr\u0131n\u0131n kan\u0131ndan f\u0131\u015fk\u0131ran dikenlerden b\xfcy\xfcd\xfc.'},body:{en:['The quilboar worship Agamaggan, the great boar demigod who was killed in the War of the Ancients. Where his blood fell, giant thorny vines burst from the earth, and the greatest knot of them, in the far south of the Barrens, is the Razorfen, the place the quilboar honour as his grave.',"Razorfen Kraul is their ancestral home, a maze of bramble-roofed dens and tunnels ruled by Charlga Razorflank, the Crone. Priests of the Death's Head tribe already walk its passages, and scouts report undead gathering in the region, a fear that the Scourge has set its sights on Kalimdor."],tr:['Quilboar\u2019lar, Kadimler Sava\u015f\u0131\u2019nda (War of the Ancients) \xf6ld\xfcr\xfclen b\xfcy\xfck yaban domuzu yar\u0131 tanr\u0131s\u0131 Agamaggan\u2019a tapar. Kan\u0131n\u0131n d\xf6k\xfcld\xfc\u011f\xfc yerde topraktan dev dikenli sarma\u015f\u0131klar f\u0131\u015fk\u0131rd\u0131; bunlar\u0131n en b\xfcy\xfck yuma\u011f\u0131, Barrens\u2019\u0131n en g\xfcneyindeki Razorfen\u2019dir ve quilboar\u2019lar oray\u0131 onun mezar\u0131 sayar.',"Razorfen Kraul onlar\u0131n atadan kalma yurdudur: dikenlerle \xf6rt\xfcl\xfc inlerden ve t\xfcnellerden olu\u015fan bu labirenti Kocakar\u0131 (the Crone) Charlga Razorflank y\xf6netir. Death's Head kabilesinin Priest\u2019leri \u015fimdiden ge\xe7itlerde dola\u015f\u0131yor; ke\u015fif kollar\u0131 da b\xf6lgede toplanan \xf6l\xfcler g\xf6rd\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc bildiriyor ve Scourge\u2019un g\xf6z\xfcn\xfc Kalimdor\u2019a dikti\u011finden korkuluyor."]},links:{instanceIds:['razorfen-kraul','razorfen-downs'],zoneIds:['barrens'],loreIds:['chapter:war-of-the-ancients']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('razorfen-kraul'),(0,n.wiki)('Agamaggan'),(0,n.wiki)('Charlga Razorflank')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'gnomeregan',subjectId:'gnomeregan',era:'classic',order:12,title:{en:'Gnomeregan',tr:'Gnomeregan'},summary:{en:"The gnomes' lost capital in Dun Morogh, poisoned by a radiation purge after a trogg invasion and a traitor's advice.",tr:'Gnomlar\u0131n Dun Morogh\u2019daki kay\u0131p ba\u015fkenti; trogg istilas\u0131n\u0131n ve bir hainin tavsiyesinin ard\u0131ndan yap\u0131lan radyasyon ar\u0131nd\u0131rmas\u0131yla zehirlendi.'},body:{en:["Built deep inside the mountains of Dun Morogh, Gnomeregan was the gnomes' greatest wonder of engineering. Then troggs boiled up from below and overran it. High Tinker Mekkatorque followed the advice of his adviser, Sicco Thermaplugg, and flooded the city with radiation to kill the invaders, but the purge slew most of the gnomes as well. The survivors fled to Ironforge.",'It was betrayal. Thermaplugg stayed behind, crowned himself lord of the ruins and now commands leper gnomes, troggs and mad machines such as the Electrocutioner 6000 and the Crowd Pummeler 9-60. The exiles have sworn to take their home back.'],tr:['Dun Morogh da\u011flar\u0131n\u0131n derinliklerine kurulan Gnomeregan, gnomlar\u0131n en b\xfcy\xfck m\xfchendislik harikas\u0131yd\u0131. Sonra a\u015fa\u011f\u0131dan trogg\u2019lar ta\u015f\u0131p \u015fehri istila etti. Y\xfcksek Tamirci (High Tinker) Mekkatorque, dan\u0131\u015fman\u0131 Sicco Thermaplugg\u2019\u0131n tavsiyesine uyup i\u015fgalcileri \xf6ld\xfcrmek i\xe7in \u015fehri radyasyonla doldurdu; ama bu ar\u0131nd\u0131rma gnomlar\u0131n \xe7o\u011funu da \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc. Hayatta kalanlar Ironforge\u2019a s\u0131\u011f\u0131nd\u0131.','Bu bir ihanetti. Thermaplugg geride kald\u0131, kendini harabelerin efendisi ilan etti ve \u015fimdi c\xfczzaml\u0131 gnomlara, trogg\u2019lara, Electrocutioner 6000 ile Crowd Pummeler 9-60 gibi \xe7\u0131lg\u0131n makinelere komuta ediyor. S\xfcrg\xfcndeki gnomlar yurtlar\u0131n\u0131 geri almaya yemin etti.']},links:{instanceIds:['gnomeregan'],zoneIds:['dun-morogh'],raceIds:['gnome'],factionIds:['alliance'],loreIds:['chapter:stormwind-in-shadow']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('gnomeregan'),(0,n.wiki)('Sicco Thermaplugg')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'scarlet-monastery-graveyard',subjectId:'scarlet-monastery-graveyard',era:'classic',order:13,title:{en:'Scarlet Monastery Graveyard',tr:'Scarlet Monastery Graveyard'},summary:{en:"The crypts of the Scarlet Crusade's monastery, where its inquisitor works and the dead refuse to rest.",tr:'Scarlet Crusade manast\u0131r\u0131n\u0131n mahzenleri; sorgucusunun \xe7al\u0131\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve \xf6l\xfclerin huzur bulamad\u0131\u011f\u0131 yer.'},body:{en:["The monastery in northern Tirisfal Glades was built as a house of study for Lordaeron's priests. After the Scourge swept the kingdom in the Third War, the zealots of the Scarlet Crusade seized it and made it their stronghold. They suspect every non-human of carrying the plague and greet strangers with blades rather than questions.",'The Graveyard is the first wing most groups visit. Its cells belong to Interrogator Vishas, Bloodmage Thalnos lurks among the tombs, and restless dead such as Azshir the Sleepless, Ironspine and the Fallen Champion stalk the crypts.'],tr:['Tirisfal Glades\u2019in kuzeyindeki manast\u0131r, Lordaeron Priest\u2019leri i\xe7in bir ilim yuvas\u0131 olarak kuruldu. \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019ta Scourge krall\u0131\u011f\u0131 silip s\xfcp\xfcr\xfcnce Scarlet Crusade\u2019in ba\u011fnazlar\u0131 buray\u0131 ele ge\xe7irip kalelerine \xe7evirdi. \u0130nsan olmayan herkesin vebay\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131ndan \u015f\xfcphelenirler ve yabanc\u0131lar\u0131 soruyla de\u011fil k\u0131l\u0131\xe7la kar\u015f\u0131larlar.','Graveyard, gruplar\u0131n \xe7o\u011funun ilk u\u011frad\u0131\u011f\u0131 kanatt\u0131r. H\xfccreleri Interrogator Vishas\u2019\u0131nd\u0131r; Bloodmage Thalnos mezarlar\u0131n aras\u0131nda pusuya yatar, Azshir the Sleepless, Ironspine ve Fallen Champion gibi huzursuz \xf6l\xfcler de mahzenlerde dola\u015f\u0131r.']},links:{instanceIds:['scarlet-monastery-graveyard','scarlet-monastery-library','scarlet-monastery-armory','scarlet-monastery-cathedral'],zoneIds:['tirisfal-glades'],loreIds:['chapter:plaguelands-and-the-scarlet-crusade']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('scarlet-monastery-graveyard'),(0,n.wiki)('Scarlet Monastery')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'scarlet-monastery-library',subjectId:'scarlet-monastery-library',era:'classic',order:14,title:{en:'Scarlet Monastery Library',tr:'Scarlet Monastery Library'},summary:{en:"The Scarlet Crusade's archive, where a houndmaster and an arcanist guard the order's books.",tr:'Scarlet Crusade\u2019in ar\u015fivi; tarikat\u0131n kitaplar\u0131n\u0131 bir taz\u0131 ustas\u0131 ile bir arkanist korur.'},body:{en:["Lordaeron's priests once came to this Tirisfal monastery to study. The Scarlet Crusade, which took it after the Third War, kept the books but lost the gentleness: its zealots believe any non-human might be spreading the plague, and they guard their archive as fiercely as their walls.","Houndmaster Loksey and his dogs hunt intruders in the outer halls, and Arcanist Doan watches over the inner stacks. Many come for the books themselves: scholars in Ironforge want a volume on the mythology of the titans, while the Forsaken seek the Crusade's own chronicle of the fallen."],tr:['Lordaeron\u2019un Priest\u2019leri bir zamanlar okumak i\xe7in Tirisfal\u2019daki bu manast\u0131ra gelirdi. \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019tan sonra buray\u0131 ele ge\xe7iren Scarlet Crusade kitaplar\u0131 korudu ama yumu\u015fakl\u0131\u011f\u0131 yitirdi: ba\u011fnazlar\u0131 insan olmayan herkesin vebay\u0131 yayabilece\u011fine inan\u0131r ve ar\u015fivlerini surlar\u0131 kadar s\u0131k\u0131 korur.','Houndmaster Loksey ve k\xf6pekleri d\u0131\u015f salonlarda davetsiz misafirleri avlar; Arcanist Doan ise i\xe7 raflara g\xf6z kulak olur. Pek \xe7o\u011fu kitaplar\u0131n kendisi i\xe7in gelir: Ironforge\u2019daki bilginler titanlar\u0131n mitolojisine dair bir cildi isterken Forsaken, tarikat\u0131n d\xfc\u015fm\xfc\u015fler hakk\u0131nda tuttu\u011fu kay\u0131tlar\u0131n pe\u015findedir.']},links:{instanceIds:['scarlet-monastery-library','scarlet-monastery-graveyard','scarlet-monastery-armory','scarlet-monastery-cathedral'],zoneIds:['tirisfal-glades'],loreIds:['chapter:plaguelands-and-the-scarlet-crusade']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('scarlet-monastery-library'),(0,n.wiki)('Scarlet Crusade')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'drowned-city',subjectId:'drowned-city',era:'classic',order:15,title:{en:'The Drowned City',tr:'The Drowned City'},summary:{en:'Ancient troll ruins that have risen from the sea off Stranglethorn Vale, now roamed by trolls and naga.',tr:'Stranglethorn Vale a\xe7\u0131klar\u0131nda denizden y\xfckselen kadim trol harabeleri; \u015fimdi troller ve naga\u2019lar dola\u015f\u0131yor.'},body:{en:["Off Stranglethorn Vale, west of Grom'gol, a troll city that the sea had claimed has risen again. Streets that no one has walked for ages now lie open to the air, trolls and naga have already moved in, and a pirate ship close by appears to have come to a very bad end.",'To get in, groups dive and search for the way below the waterline. Once inside, they fight under the open sky while the weather worsens, mist turning to rain and rain to a full storm by the final battle.'],tr:["Stranglethorn Vale a\xe7\u0131klar\u0131nda, Grom'gol\u2019\xfcn bat\u0131s\u0131nda, denizin yuttu\u011fu bir trol \u015fehri yeniden y\xfckseldi. \xc7a\u011flard\u0131r kimsenin y\xfcr\xfcmedi\u011fi sokaklar art\u0131k a\xe7\u0131kta; troller ve naga\u2019lar \xe7oktan yerle\u015fti, yak\u0131ndaki bir korsan gemisi ise \xe7ok k\xf6t\xfc bir sonla kar\u015f\u0131la\u015fm\u0131\u015f g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcyor.",'\u0130\xe7eri girmek i\xe7in gruplar dalar ve su seviyesinin alt\u0131ndaki yolu arar. \u0130\xe7eride a\xe7\u0131k g\xf6ky\xfcz\xfc alt\u0131nda sava\u015f\u0131rken hava giderek bozulur; son sava\u015fa var\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda sis ya\u011fmura, ya\u011fmur da tam bir f\u0131rt\u0131naya d\xf6n\xfc\u015fm\xfc\u015ft\xfcr.']},links:{instanceIds:['drowned-city'],zoneIds:['stranglethorn-vale'],loreIds:['chapter:azeroth-in-year-twenty-five']},image:'instance:drowned-city',sources:[n.FOREVER.dungeons],basis:'forever-partial',unknowns:[{en:'Why the city has risen now, and which troll people built it.',tr:'\u015eehrin neden \u015fimdi y\xfckseldi\u011fi ve onu hangi trol halk\u0131n\u0131n kurdu\u011fu.'},{en:"Who leads the trolls and naga inside; this guide's data lists no bosses yet.",tr:'\u0130\xe7erideki trollere ve naga\u2019lara kimin \xf6nderlik etti\u011fi; bu rehberin verisinde hen\xfcz boss listesi yok.'},{en:'What befell the pirate ship.',tr:'Korsan gemisinin ba\u015f\u0131na ne geldi\u011fi.'}]}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'scarlet-monastery-armory',subjectId:'scarlet-monastery-armory',era:'classic',order:16,title:{en:'Scarlet Monastery Armory',tr:'Scarlet Monastery Armory'},summary:{en:"The Scarlet Crusade's training grounds and arsenal, ruled by its champion Herod.",tr:'Scarlet Crusade\u2019in talim alan\u0131 ve cephaneli\u011fi; \u015fampiyonu Herod\u2019un h\xfckm\xfcnde.'},body:{en:["Behind the monastery's walls in Tirisfal Glades, the Scarlet Crusade drills its soldiers. The order was born from the ruin of Lordaeron in the Third War and believes that anyone who is not human may carry the plague, so its recruits are taught to strike first.","The Armory holds the training yards, barracks and weapon stores, and its master is Herod, the Scarlet Champion, a towering brute who swings a huge axe and whirls through his attackers. Beating him proves a group is ready for the cathedral at the monastery's heart."],tr:['Tirisfal Glades\u2019teki manast\u0131r\u0131n duvarlar\u0131 ard\u0131nda Scarlet Crusade askerlerini e\u011fitir. Tarikat, \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019ta Lordaeron\u2019un y\u0131k\u0131nt\u0131lar\u0131ndan do\u011fdu ve insan olmayan herkesin vebay\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131yabilece\u011fine inan\u0131r; bu y\xfczden acemilerine \xf6nce vurmay\u0131 \xf6\u011fretir.','Armory; talim alanlar\u0131n\u0131, ko\u011fu\u015flar\u0131 ve silah depolar\u0131n\u0131 bar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131r. Efendisi, devasa baltas\u0131n\u0131 savurup sald\u0131rganlar\u0131n aras\u0131nda kas\u0131rga gibi d\xf6nen iri yar\u0131 Herod, the Scarlet Champion\u2019d\u0131r. Onu yenmek, bir grubun manast\u0131r\u0131n kalbindeki katedrale haz\u0131r oldu\u011funu kan\u0131tlar.']},links:{instanceIds:['scarlet-monastery-armory','scarlet-monastery-graveyard','scarlet-monastery-library','scarlet-monastery-cathedral'],zoneIds:['tirisfal-glades'],loreIds:['chapter:plaguelands-and-the-scarlet-crusade']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('scarlet-monastery-armory'),(0,n.wiki)('Herod')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'razorfen-downs',subjectId:'razorfen-downs',era:'classic',order:17,title:{en:'Razorfen Downs',tr:'Razorfen Downs'},summary:{en:"The quilboar's ancient burial grounds, seized by the Scourge under the lich Amnennar the Coldbringer.",tr:'Quilboar\u2019lar\u0131n kadim mezar alan\u0131; lich Amnennar the Coldbringer \xf6nderli\u011findeki Scourge taraf\u0131ndan ele ge\xe7irildi.'},body:{en:["Razorfen Downs grows from the same giant thorns as the Kraul and is where the quilboar bury their dead. Their high priests, the Death's Head, once kept these grounds holy. That changed when the Scourge reached Kalimdor: the lich Amnennar the Coldbringer took the tribe's priests into his service and filled the brambles with risen dead.","Free quilboar now struggle to win back their burial city before the lich's power creeps over the rest of the Barrens. A group must cut past Tuten'kash, Mordresh Fire Eye, Glutton and Plaguemaw the Rotting to reach Amnennar himself."],tr:["Razorfen Downs, Kraul ile ayn\u0131 dev dikenlerden y\xfckselir ve quilboar\u2019lar\u0131n \xf6l\xfclerini g\xf6md\xfc\u011f\xfc yerdir. Death's Head adl\u0131 y\xfcksek Priest\u2019leri bir zamanlar bu topraklar\u0131 kutsal tutard\u0131. Scourge Kalimdor\u2019a ula\u015f\u0131nca her \u015fey de\u011fi\u015fti: lich Amnennar the Coldbringer kabilenin Priest\u2019lerini hizmetine ald\u0131 ve dikenlerin aras\u0131n\u0131 dirilmi\u015f \xf6l\xfclerle doldurdu.","\xd6zg\xfcr kalan quilboar\u2019lar, lich\u2019in g\xfcc\xfc Barrens\u2019\u0131n geri kalan\u0131na yay\u0131lmadan mezar \u015fehirlerini geri almak i\xe7in m\xfccadele ediyor. Amnennar\u2019a ula\u015fmak isteyen bir grup Tuten'kash, Mordresh Fire Eye, Glutton ve Plaguemaw the Rotting\u2019i a\u015fmak zorundad\u0131r."]},links:{instanceIds:['razorfen-downs','razorfen-kraul'],zoneIds:['barrens'],loreIds:['chapter:the-lich-king-and-the-plague']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('razorfen-downs'),(0,n.wiki)('Amnennar the Coldbringer')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'scarlet-monastery-cathedral',subjectId:'scarlet-monastery-cathedral',era:'classic',order:18,title:{en:'Scarlet Monastery Cathedral',tr:'Scarlet Monastery Cathedral'},summary:{en:'The heart of the Scarlet Monastery, where Commander Mograine leads the faithful and High Inquisitor Whitemane raises the fallen.',tr:'Scarlet Monastery\u2019nin kalbi; Commander Mograine sad\u0131klara \xf6nderlik eder, High Inquisitor Whitemane d\xfc\u015fenleri diriltir.'},body:{en:["The cathedral is the heart of the Scarlet Crusade's monastery in Tirisfal Glades and the seat of its leaders there. Scarlet Commander Mograine commands the zealous garrison, yet real authority belongs to High Inquisitor Whitemane, a priestess who can call her fallen champion back to fight again.","The Crusade was born from Lordaeron's fall and still sees the plague in every outsider. Here its conviction burns hottest: the commander fights to the last, and when he falls, Whitemane steps from the chancel to fight on and raise him again."],tr:['Katedral, Scarlet Crusade\u2019in Tirisfal Glades\u2019teki manast\u0131r\u0131n\u0131n kalbi ve oradaki liderlerinin makam\u0131d\u0131r. Ba\u011fnaz garnizona Scarlet Commander Mograine komuta eder; ama as\u0131l s\xf6z sahibi, d\xfc\u015fen \u015fampiyonunu yeniden sava\u015fa \xe7a\u011f\u0131rabilen rahibe High Inquisitor Whitemane\u2019dir.','Tarikat Lordaeron\u2019un \xe7\xf6k\xfc\u015f\xfcnden do\u011fdu ve h\xe2l\xe2 her yabanc\u0131da vebay\u0131 g\xf6r\xfcr. \u0130nanc\u0131 en \xe7ok burada alevlenir: komutan sonuna dek sava\u015f\u0131r, o d\xfc\u015ft\xfc\u011f\xfcnde Whitemane k\xfcrs\xfcn\xfcn ard\u0131ndan inip sava\u015f\u0131 s\xfcrd\xfcr\xfcr ve onu yeniden diriltir.']},links:{instanceIds:['scarlet-monastery-cathedral','scarlet-monastery-graveyard','scarlet-monastery-library','scarlet-monastery-armory'],zoneIds:['tirisfal-glades'],loreIds:['chapter:plaguelands-and-the-scarlet-crusade']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('scarlet-monastery-cathedral'),(0,n.wiki)('Sally Whitemane')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'kroldok-stronghold',subjectId:'kroldok-stronghold',era:'classic',order:19,title:{en:"Krol'dok Stronghold",tr:"Krol'dok Stronghold"},summary:{en:'An ogre fortress in the Riverglades whose raiders kidnap travellers, and from which chanting rises after dark.',tr:'Riverglades\u2019te bir ogre kalesi; ak\u0131nc\u0131lar\u0131 yolcular\u0131 ka\xe7\u0131r\u0131yor, karanl\u0131k \xe7\xf6k\xfcnce i\xe7inden ilahiler y\xfckseliyor.'},body:{en:["Krol'dok is the ogre stronghold of the Riverglades, and its story reaches back to the years after the Second War. When the old Horde's forces in the region besieged Farholde Keep, Fern Crimsonleaf slipped into their camp and killed their leaders. Leaderless, the larger army lost a costly battle to the Brotherhood of the Horse and fled back to Krol'dok.",'Now its ogre outrunners strike all over the Riverglades, carrying off travellers and sacking settlements. Their trail ends at a sprawling fortress of workshops, camps and closely watched passages. Groups go in to stop the raids and to learn the meaning of the strange chanting that rises from the stronghold after dark.'],tr:["Krol'dok, Riverglades\u2019in ogre kalesidir ve hik\xe2yesi \u0130kinci Sava\u015f\u2019\u0131n ard\u0131ndan gelen y\u0131llara uzan\u0131r. B\xf6lgedeki eski Horde (Old Horde) kuvvetleri Farholde Keep\u2019i ku\u015fatt\u0131\u011f\u0131nda Fern Crimsonleaf kamplar\u0131na s\u0131zd\u0131 ve liderlerini \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc. Lidersiz kalan, say\u0131ca \xfcst\xfcn ordu Brotherhood of the Horse\u2019a kar\u015f\u0131 a\u011f\u0131r kay\u0131pl\u0131 bir sava\u015f\u0131 kaybetti ve Krol'dok\u2019a ka\xe7t\u0131.",'\u015eimdi kalenin ogre ak\u0131nc\u0131lar\u0131 Riverglades\u2019in d\xf6rt bir yan\u0131nda yolcular\u0131 ka\xe7\u0131r\u0131p yerle\u015fimleri ya\u011fmal\u0131yor. \u0130zleri; at\xf6lyeler, kamplar ve s\u0131k\u0131 korunan ge\xe7itlerle dolu geni\u015f bir kaleye \xe7\u0131kar. Gruplar bask\u0131nlar\u0131 durdurmak ve karanl\u0131k \xe7\xf6k\xfcnce kaleden y\xfckselen tuhaf ilahilerin anlam\u0131n\u0131 \xe7\xf6zmek i\xe7in i\xe7eri girer.']},links:{instanceIds:['kroldok-stronghold'],zoneIds:['riverglades'],loreIds:['chapter:the-second-war']},image:'instance:kroldok-stronghold',sources:[n.FOREVER.dungeons,(0,n.instanceSource)('kroldok-stronghold'),n.FOREVER.riverglades],basis:'forever',unknowns:[{en:"Who commands the stronghold now; this guide's data lists no bosses yet.",tr:'Kaleye \u015fu anda kimin komuta etti\u011fi; bu rehberin verisinde hen\xfcz boss listesi yok.'},{en:'What the chanting is and who leads it.',tr:'\u0130lahilerin ne oldu\u011fu ve onlara kimin \xf6nderlik etti\u011fi.'},{en:"How these ogres relate to the Twilight's Hammer and the Bolder'ok ogres elsewhere in the Riverglades.",tr:"Bu ogre\u2019lerin, Riverglades\u2019in ba\u015fka yerlerindeki Twilight's Hammer ve Bolder'ok ogre\u2019leriyle ili\u015fkisi."}]}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'uldaman',subjectId:'uldaman',era:'classic',order:20,title:{en:'Uldaman',tr:'Uldaman'},summary:{en:'A titan vault in the Badlands where dwarven diggers woke the troggs and found clues to their own origins.',tr:'Badlands\u2019te bir titan mahzeni; c\xfcce kaz\u0131c\u0131lar burada trogg\u2019lar\u0131 uyand\u0131rd\u0131 ve kendi k\xf6kenlerine dair ipu\xe7lar\u0131 buldu.'},body:{en:["Uldaman is a vault the titans' keepers sealed deep inside the mountains of Khaz Modan, in what is now the Badlands. It was meant to hold the troggs, an early creation the titans judged a failure. Before the Third War, diggers from Ironforge broke in, and the troggs they woke slaughtered most of the expedition.","Now the Explorers' League, Dark Iron raiders and trogg tribes all fight over its halls. Deep inside lie the Discs of Norgannon, titan records that reveal the dwarves descend from the stone-skinned earthen, guarded by the titan-forged Archaedas, who still rises against anyone who disturbs his vault."],tr:['Uldaman, titanlar\u0131n bek\xe7ilerinin (keeper) Khaz Modan da\u011flar\u0131n\u0131n derinliklerinde, bug\xfcnk\xfc Badlands\u2019te m\xfch\xfcrledi\u011fi bir mahzendir. Titanlar\u0131n ba\u015far\u0131s\u0131z sayd\u0131\u011f\u0131 erken bir yarat\u0131m olan trogg\u2019lar\u0131 tutmak i\xe7in yap\u0131ld\u0131. \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019tan \xf6nce Ironforge\u2019lu kaz\u0131c\u0131lar i\xe7eri girdi; uyand\u0131rd\u0131klar\u0131 trogg\u2019lar ke\u015fif heyetinin \xe7o\u011funu katletti.',"\u015eimdi Explorers' League, Dark Iron ak\u0131nc\u0131lar\u0131 ve trogg kabileleri salonlar\u0131 i\xe7in \xe7arp\u0131\u015f\u0131yor. Derinlerde, c\xfccelerin ta\u015f derili earthen\u2019lerden geldi\u011fini ortaya koyan titan kay\u0131tlar\u0131 Discs of Norgannon yatar; onlar\u0131, mahzenini rahats\u0131z eden herkese kar\u015f\u0131 h\xe2l\xe2 aya\u011fa kalkan titan yap\u0131m\u0131 muhaf\u0131z Archaedas korur."]},links:{instanceIds:['uldaman'],zoneIds:['badlands'],raceIds:['dwarf'],loreIds:['chapter:titans-and-old-gods']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('uldaman'),(0,n.wiki)('Archaedas'),(0,n.wiki)('Discs of Norgannon')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'zulfarrak',subjectId:'zulfarrak',era:'classic',order:21,title:{en:"Zul'Farrak",tr:"Zul'Farrak"},summary:{en:'The sun-scorched city of the Sandfury trolls in Tanaris, where a hydra god sleeps in a sacred pool.',tr:'Tanaris\u2019te Sandfury trollerinin g\xfcne\u015fte kavrulan \u015fehri; kutsal bir havuzda hidra bir tanr\u0131 uyuyor.'},body:{en:["Tanaris was once jungle, part of the Gurubashi trolls' lands, and Zul'Farrak was one of their cities. When the Great Sundering turned the region to desert, the Farraki trolls left there adapted and became sand trolls. Today the city belongs to the Sandfury tribe, feared for its cruelty and its dark magic.","Adventurers come for many reasons. Rumour places both halves of the broken troll sword Sul'thraze the Lasher inside its walls, a band of mercenaries on the run from Gadgetzan blundered in and was taken captive, and in a sacred pool at the city's heart sleeps Gahz'rilla, a hydra the Sandfury worship as a demigod and wake only when they have sacrifices to offer."],tr:["Tanaris bir zamanlar Gurubashi trollerinin topraklar\u0131ndaki bir ormand\u0131 ve Zul'Farrak onlar\u0131n \u015fehirlerinden biriydi. B\xfcy\xfck Yar\u0131lma b\xf6lgeyi \xe7\xf6le \xe7evirince orada kalan Farraki trolleri yeni ko\u015fullara uyum sa\u011flay\u0131p kum trollerine d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc. Bug\xfcn \u015fehir, ac\u0131mas\u0131zl\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve karanl\u0131k b\xfcy\xfcleriyle korkulan Sandfury kabilesinindir.","Macerac\u0131lar buraya pek \xe7ok nedenle gelir. S\xf6ylentilere g\xf6re k\u0131r\u0131k trol k\u0131l\u0131c\u0131 Sul'thraze the Lasher\u2019\u0131n iki yar\u0131s\u0131 da surlar\u0131n i\xe7inde; Gadgetzan\u2019dan ka\xe7an bir paral\u0131 asker grubu \u015fehre yanl\u0131\u015fl\u0131kla girip esir d\xfc\u015ft\xfc. \u015eehrin kalbindeki kutsal havuzda ise Sandfury\u2019nin yar\u0131 tanr\u0131 olarak tapt\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve yaln\u0131zca sunacak kurbanlar\u0131 oldu\u011funda uyand\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131 hidra Gahz'rilla uyur."]},links:{instanceIds:['zulfarrak'],zoneIds:['tanaris'],loreIds:['chapter:rise-of-the-kaldorei','chapter:war-of-the-ancients']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('zulfarrak'),(0,n.wiki)("Gahz'rilla")],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'alcaz-prison',subjectId:'alcaz-prison',era:'classic',order:22,title:{en:'Alcaz Prison',tr:'Alcaz Prison'},summary:{en:'A long-rumoured prison on Alcaz Island in Dustwallow Marsh, finally open, where the Defias and naga are at war.',tr:'Dustwallow Marsh\u2019taki Alcaz Island\u2019da uzun s\xfcredir s\xf6ylentilere konu olan hapishane nihayet a\xe7\u0131ld\u0131; i\xe7eride Defias ile naga\u2019lar sava\u015f\u0131yor.'},body:{en:["Dustwallow Marsh has long buzzed with talk of Alcaz Island and the high-ranking captives said to be kept there; some rumours even name Stormwind's King Varian Wrynn. No one could reach the prison to learn the truth. Now its gates stand open.",'Inside, the Defias Brotherhood and the naga are fighting each other. Groups use the chaos to search the cells, confront the people who hold them and gather fresh clues to a mystery the kingdoms already know well.'],tr:['Dustwallow Marsh uzun s\xfcredir Alcaz Island\u2019\u0131 ve orada tutuldu\u011fu s\xf6ylenen \xfcst d\xfczey tutsaklar\u0131 konu\u015fuyor; baz\u0131 s\xf6ylentiler Stormwind Kral\u0131 Varian Wrynn\u2019in ad\u0131n\u0131 bile an\u0131yor. Ger\xe7e\u011fi \xf6\u011frenmek i\xe7in kimse hapishaneye ula\u015famad\u0131. \u015eimdi kap\u0131lar\u0131 ard\u0131na kadar a\xe7\u0131k.','\u0130\xe7eride Defias Karde\u015fli\u011fi ile naga\u2019lar birbirleriyle sava\u015f\u0131yor. Gruplar bu karga\u015fadan yararlan\u0131p h\xfccreleri arar, onlar\u0131 elinde tutanlarla y\xfczle\u015fir ve krall\u0131klar\u0131n zaten iyi bildi\u011fi bir gizeme dair yeni ipu\xe7lar\u0131 toplar.']},links:{instanceIds:['alcaz-prison'],zoneIds:['dustwallow-marsh'],loreIds:['chapter:stormwind-in-shadow']},image:'instance:alcaz-prison',sources:[n.FOREVER.dungeons],basis:'forever-partial',unknowns:[{en:'Whether King Varian Wrynn is or was held here; the official text only reports rumours.',tr:'Kral Varian Wrynn\u2019in burada tutulup tutulmad\u0131\u011f\u0131; resm\xee metin yaln\u0131zca s\xf6ylentilerden s\xf6z ediyor.'},{en:'Who runs the prison and why the Defias and naga are fighting.',tr:'Hapishaneyi kimin y\xf6netti\u011fi ve Defias ile naga\u2019lar\u0131n neden sava\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131.'},{en:"Which bosses wait inside; this guide's data lists none yet.",tr:'\u0130\xe7eride hangi boss\u2019lar\u0131n bekledi\u011fi; bu rehberin verisinde hen\xfcz hi\xe7biri yok.'}]}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'maraudon',subjectId:'maraudon',era:'classic',order:23,title:{en:'Maraudon',tr:'Maraudon'},summary:{en:'Sacred caves of the centaur in Desolace, poisoned by the grief of the earth princess Theradras.',tr:'Desolace\u2019ta centaur\u2019lar\u0131n kutsal ma\u011faralar\u0131; toprak prensesi Theradras\u2019\u0131n kederiyle zehirlendi.'},body:{en:["Legend tells a grim story of the centaur's birth. Their father was Zaetar, a son of the demigod Cenarius; their mother was Princess Theradras, daughter of the elemental lord of earth. The first centaur turned on Zaetar and killed him, and the grieving Theradras is said to have bound his spirit inside Maraudon, a deed whose corruption still poisons the caves.","The centaur clans hold Maraudon as holy burial ground, but restless centaur ghosts, twisted elementals and poisonous plant creatures now fill the Wicked Grotto, Foulspore Cavern and Earth Song Falls. Celebras, Zaetar's nephew, came to free his uncle's spirit and fell to the corruption himself. At the very bottom waits Theradras."],tr:['Efsane, centaur\u2019lar\u0131n do\u011fu\u015funa dair karanl\u0131k bir hik\xe2ye anlat\u0131r. Babalar\u0131 yar\u0131 tanr\u0131 Cenarius\u2019un o\u011flu Zaetar, anneleri ise topra\u011f\u0131n elemental efendisinin k\u0131z\u0131 Prenses Theradras\u2019t\u0131. \u0130lk centaur\u2019lar Zaetar\u2019a sald\u0131r\u0131p onu \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc; kederli Theradras\u2019\u0131n onun ruhunu Maraudon\u2019un i\xe7ine ba\u011flad\u0131\u011f\u0131 s\xf6ylenir ve bu eylemin yayd\u0131\u011f\u0131 bozulma h\xe2l\xe2 ma\u011faralar\u0131 zehirliyor.','Centaur klanlar\u0131 Maraudon\u2019u kutsal bir mezar alan\u0131 sayar; ama \u015fimdi Wicked Grotto, Foulspore Cavern ve Earth Song Falls huzursuz centaur hayaletleri, \xe7arp\u0131k elementaller ve zehirli bitki yarat\u0131klar\u0131yla dolu. Zaetar\u2019\u0131n ye\u011feni Celebras amcas\u0131n\u0131n ruhunu kurtarmaya geldi, ama kendisi de bozulmaya yenik d\xfc\u015ft\xfc. En dipte Theradras bekler.']},links:{instanceIds:['maraudon'],zoneIds:['desolace'],loreIds:['chapter:titans-and-old-gods']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('maraudon'),(0,n.wiki)('Zaetar'),(0,n.wiki)('Celebras')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'temple-of-atalhakkar',subjectId:'temple-of-atalhakkar',era:'classic',order:24,title:{en:"Temple of Atal'Hakkar",tr:"Temple of Atal'Hakkar"},summary:{en:"The Sunken Temple in the Swamp of Sorrows, where Atal'ai priests still try to call their blood god Hakkar.",tr:"Swamp of Sorrows\u2019taki Bat\u0131k Tap\u0131nak; Atal'ai Priest\u2019leri kan tanr\u0131lar\u0131 Hakkar\u2019\u0131 \xe7a\u011f\u0131rmaya h\xe2l\xe2 \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor."},body:{en:["The Atal'ai were troll priests who wanted to bring Hakkar the Soulflayer, the blood god, into the world, and the struggle to stop them tore the Gurubashi Empire apart more than a thousand years ago. Beaten and driven out, they built a temple in the Swamp of Sorrows to ready his return, until the Aspect Ysera discovered the plan and sank it into the mire.","Green dragons have watched the drowned ruins ever since, yet the Atal'ai endured and still pray to Hakkar under Jammal'an the Prophet. Deeper down lingers the Shade of Eranikus, Ysera's consort, his mind darkened by the Emerald Nightmare."],tr:["Atal'ai, kan tanr\u0131s\u0131 Hakkar the Soulflayer\u2019\u0131 d\xfcnyaya getirmek isteyen trol Priest\u2019leriydi; onlar\u0131 durdurma m\xfccadelesi bin y\u0131l\u0131 a\u015fk\u0131n bir s\xfcre \xf6nce Gurubashi \u0130mparatorlu\u011fu\u2019nu par\xe7alad\u0131. Yenilip s\xfcr\xfclen Priest\u2019ler, tanr\u0131lar\u0131n\u0131n d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcne haz\u0131rlanmak i\xe7in Swamp of Sorrows\u2019ta bir tap\u0131nak kurdu; ta ki Aspect Ysera plan\u0131 fark edip tap\u0131na\u011f\u0131 batakl\u0131\u011fa g\xf6mene dek.","O g\xfcnden beri ye\u015fil ejderhalar sular alt\u0131ndaki harabeleri g\xf6zl\xfcyor; yine de Atal'ai hayatta kald\u0131 ve Jammal'an the Prophet \xf6nderli\u011finde Hakkar\u2019a dua etmeyi s\xfcrd\xfcr\xfcyor. Daha derinde, akl\u0131 Z\xfcmr\xfct K\xe2bus (Emerald Nightmare) taraf\u0131ndan karart\u0131lm\u0131\u015f olan Ysera\u2019n\u0131n e\u015fi Eranikus\u2019un g\xf6lgesi (Shade of Eranikus) dola\u015f\u0131r."]},links:{instanceIds:['temple-of-atalhakkar'],zoneIds:['swamp-of-sorrows'],loreIds:['chapter:azeroth-in-year-twenty-five']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('temple-of-atalhakkar'),(0,n.wiki)("Atal'ai tribe"),(0,n.wiki)('Eranikus')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'blackrock-depths',subjectId:'blackrock-depths',era:'classic',order:25,title:{en:'Blackrock Depths',tr:'Blackrock Depths'},summary:{en:"Shadowforge City, the Dark Iron dwarves' capital deep inside Blackrock Mountain, ruled by Emperor Dagran Thaurissan in Ragnaros's shadow.",tr:'Blackrock Mountain\u2019\u0131n derinliklerindeki Dark Iron ba\u015fkenti Shadowforge City; Ragnaros\u2019un g\xf6lgesinde \u0130mparator Dagran Thaurissan y\xf6netiyor.'},body:{en:["More than two centuries ago, the Dark Iron sorcerer-thane Thaurissan tried to win a lost war with a desperate summoning and called up Ragnaros the Firelord instead. The blast raised Blackrock Mountain and bound his clan to the Firelord's will. Their descendants still labour for Ragnaros in the burning tunnels beneath the mountain.",'Blackrock Depths is their realm: a prison, the arena called the Ring of Law, the Grim Guzzler tavern, the Black Forge and Shadowforge City itself. There Emperor Dagran Thaurissan sits on his throne beside Princess Moira Bronzebeard, whose father, King Magni of Ironforge, believes she is held there by a spell.'],tr:['\u0130ki y\xfczy\u0131l\u0131 a\u015fk\u0131n bir s\xfcre \xf6nce Dark Iron b\xfcy\xfcc\xfc-reisi (sorcerer-thane) Thaurissan, kaybedilmi\u015f bir sava\u015f\u0131 umutsuz bir \xe7a\u011fr\u0131yla kazanmaya \xe7al\u0131\u015ft\u0131, ama Ate\u015f Efendisi Ragnaros\u2019u \xe7a\u011f\u0131rd\u0131. Patlama Blackrock Mountain\u2019\u0131 y\xfckseltti ve klan\u0131n\u0131 Ragnaros\u2019un iradesine ba\u011flad\u0131. Torunlar\u0131 h\xe2l\xe2 da\u011f\u0131n alt\u0131ndaki yanan t\xfcnellerde onun i\xe7in \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor.','Blackrock Depths onlar\u0131n diyar\u0131d\u0131r: bir hapishane, Ring of Law arenas\u0131, Grim Guzzler meyhanesi, Black Forge ve Shadowforge City\u2019nin kendisi. Burada \u0130mparator Dagran Thaurissan, Prenses Moira Bronzebeard\u2019\u0131n yan\u0131nda taht\u0131na kurulur; Moira\u2019n\u0131n babas\u0131 Ironforge Kral\u0131 Magni, k\u0131z\u0131n\u0131n bir b\xfcy\xfcyle tutuldu\u011funa inan\u0131yor.']},links:{instanceIds:['blackrock-depths','lower-blackrock-spire'],zoneIds:['burning-steppes','searing-gorge'],raceIds:['dwarf'],loreIds:['chapter:war-of-the-three-hammers','chapter:fire-beneath-blackrock']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('blackrock-depths'),(0,n.wiki)('Dagran Thaurissan'),(0,n.wiki)('Moira Thaurissan')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'warpwood-quarter',subjectId:'warpwood-quarter',era:'classic',order:26,title:{en:'Warpwood Quarter',tr:'Warpwood Quarter'},summary:{en:"The eastern district of ruined Eldre'Thalas, overgrown with corrupted plants under the satyr Alzzin the Wildshaper.",tr:"Harap Eldre'Thalas\u2019\u0131n do\u011fu mahallesi; satyr Alzzin the Wildshaper\u2019\u0131n h\xfckm\xfcnde bozulmu\u015f bitkilerle kapl\u0131."},body:{en:["Dire Maul in Feralas was once Eldre'Thalas, a city where Queen Azshara's most secretive arcanists guarded her treasured knowledge. The Great Sundering left it broken, and over the ages ogres, satyrs and stranger things moved into its districts.",'The Warpwood Quarter in the east has fallen to Alzzin the Wildshaper, a satyr who corrupted the Fruit of Fertility so that it now yields vile felvine. Twisted ancients, lashers, demons and satyrs answer to him, and the whole district has grown wild. Even the mischievous imp Pusillin leads intruders on a merry chase through its halls.'],tr:["Feralas\u2019taki Dire Maul bir zamanlar Eldre'Thalas\u2019t\u0131: Krali\xe7e Azshara\u2019n\u0131n en ketum arkanistlerinin onun de\u011ferli bilgilerini korudu\u011fu bir \u015fehir. B\xfcy\xfck Yar\u0131lma \u015fehri par\xe7alad\u0131; \xe7a\u011flar boyunca mahallelerine ogre\u2019ler, satyr\u2019ler ve daha tuhaf varl\u0131klar yerle\u015fti.",'Do\u011fudaki Warpwood Quarter, Fruit of Fertility\u2019yi bozup ondan i\u011fren\xe7 felvine \xfcretmeye ba\u015flayan satyr Alzzin the Wildshaper\u2019\u0131n eline ge\xe7ti. \xc7arp\u0131k ancient\u2019lar, lasher\u2019lar, iblisler ve satyr\u2019ler ona boyun e\u011fer; b\xfct\xfcn mahalle yabanile\u015fti. Muzip imp Pusillin bile davetsiz misafirleri salonlarda ne\u015feli bir kovalamacaya s\xfcr\xfckler.']},links:{instanceIds:['warpwood-quarter','capital-gardens','gordok-commons'],zoneIds:['feralas'],loreIds:['chapter:the-long-watch-of-hyjal','chapter:war-of-the-ancients']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('warpwood-quarter'),(0,n.wiki)('Dire Maul'),(0,n.wiki)('Alzzin the Wildshaper')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'blackmaw-hold',subjectId:'blackmaw-hold',era:'classic',order:27,title:{en:'Blackmaw Hold',tr:'Blackmaw Hold'},summary:{en:'A great furbolg city behind a long-sealed gate in Azshara, where the Blackmaw clan fights a spreading corruption.',tr:'Azshara\u2019da uzun s\xfcre m\xfch\xfcrl\xfc kalm\u0131\u015f bir kap\u0131n\u0131n ard\u0131nda b\xfcy\xfck bir furbolg \u015fehri; Blackmaw klan\u0131 yay\u0131lan bir bozulmayla sava\u015f\u0131yor.'},body:{en:['Behind a gate in Azshara that stayed shut for a very long time lies a great city of the furbolgs. The Blackmaw clan who live there are fighting a corruption that is seeping through their groves and along the winding tunnels under the mountains.',"The hold is a long adventure for groups at the level cap, with several routes and many bosses. Its deepest reaches are said to hide a way leading even further beneath Azeroth, and Blizzard's raid overview lists Blackmaw Hold as one of the ways into the Barrow Deeps."],tr:['Azshara\u2019da \xe7ok uzun s\xfcre kapal\u0131 kalm\u0131\u015f bir kap\u0131n\u0131n ard\u0131nda b\xfcy\xfck bir furbolg \u015fehri uzan\u0131r. Orada ya\u015fayan Blackmaw klan\u0131, korular\u0131na ve da\u011flar\u0131n alt\u0131ndaki k\u0131vr\u0131ml\u0131 t\xfcnellere s\u0131zan bir bozulmaya kar\u015f\u0131 sava\u015f\u0131yor.','Buras\u0131, azami seviyedeki gruplar i\xe7in birka\xe7 farkl\u0131 yolu ve \xe7ok say\u0131da boss\u2019u olan uzun bir macerad\u0131r. En derin k\xf6\u015felerinde Azeroth\u2019un daha da alt\u0131na inen bir yol sakl\u0131 oldu\u011fu s\xf6ylenir; Blizzard\u2019\u0131n bask\u0131n tan\u0131t\u0131m\u0131 da Blackmaw Hold\u2019u Barrow Deeps\u2019e a\xe7\u0131lan giri\u015flerden biri olarak sayar.']},links:{instanceIds:['blackmaw-hold','barrow-deeps'],zoneIds:['azshara']},image:'instance:blackmaw-hold',sources:[n.FOREVER.dungeons,n.FOREVER.raids],basis:'forever-partial',unknowns:[{en:'What the corruption is and where it comes from.',tr:'Bozulman\u0131n ne oldu\u011fu ve nereden geldi\u011fi.'},{en:'Who sealed the gate, and why.',tr:'Kap\u0131y\u0131 kimin, neden m\xfch\xfcrledi\u011fi.'},{en:"Which bosses wait inside; this guide's data lists none yet.",tr:'\u0130\xe7eride hangi boss\u2019lar\u0131n bekledi\u011fi; bu rehberin verisinde hen\xfcz hi\xe7biri yok.'}]}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'lower-blackrock-spire',subjectId:'lower-blackrock-spire',era:'classic',order:28,title:{en:'Lower Blackrock Spire',tr:'Lower Blackrock Spire'},summary:{en:"The lower halls of the spire atop Blackrock Mountain, barracks of Rend Blackhand's Dark Horde.",tr:'Blackrock Mountain\u2019\u0131n tepesindeki kulenin alt salonlar\u0131; Rend Blackhand\u2019in Dark Horde\u2019unun k\u0131\u015flas\u0131.'},body:{en:['For centuries the spire crowning Blackrock Mountain was a Dark Iron stronghold. That ended when Nefarian, son of Deathwing, took its upper levels with his dragonspawn and turned on the dwarves. He found an ally in Rend Blackhand, an orc who calls himself Warchief of a Dark Horde that refuses to follow Thrall.',"Lower Blackrock Spire is the barracks of that Dark Horde. Blackrock orc legions, Spirestone ogres under Highlord Omokk, Smolderthorn trolls of Shadow Hunter Vosh'gajin and the spiders around Mother Smolderweb share its ruined halls under Overlord Wyrmthalak. The elite and the dragons wait higher still, in the upper spire."],tr:['Blackrock Mountain\u2019\u0131n tepesindeki kule y\xfczy\u0131llar boyunca bir Dark Iron kalesiydi. Bu, Deathwing\u2019in o\u011flu Nefarian\u2019\u0131n ejderha soyundan yarat\u0131klar\u0131yla \xfcst katlar\u0131 al\u0131p c\xfccelere sald\u0131rmas\u0131yla sona erdi. Nefarian, Thrall\u2019a boyun e\u011fmeyi reddeden bir Dark Horde\u2019un sava\u015f \u015fefi oldu\u011funu ilan eden ork Rend Blackhand\u2019de bir m\xfcttefik buldu.',"Lower Blackrock Spire, o Dark Horde\u2019un k\u0131\u015flas\u0131d\u0131r. Blackrock orklar\u0131n\u0131n lejyonlar\u0131, Highlord Omokk\u2019un Spirestone ogre\u2019leri, Shadow Hunter Vosh'gajin\u2019in Smolderthorn trolleri ve Mother Smolderweb\u2019in \xe7evresindeki \xf6r\xfcmcekler, Overlord Wyrmthalak\u2019\u0131n y\xf6netimindeki harap salonlar\u0131 payla\u015f\u0131r. Se\xe7kin birlikler ve ejderhalar daha yukar\u0131da, \xfcst kulede bekler."]},links:{instanceIds:['lower-blackrock-spire','blackrock-depths'],zoneIds:['burning-steppes','searing-gorge'],raceIds:['orc'],loreIds:['chapter:fire-beneath-blackrock']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('lower-blackrock-spire'),(0,n.wiki)("Dal'rend Blackhand"),(0,n.wiki)('Dark Horde')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'capital-gardens',subjectId:'capital-gardens',era:'classic',order:29,title:{en:'Capital Gardens',tr:'Capital Gardens'},summary:{en:"The western district of Eldre'Thalas, where the last Highborne of the Shen'dralar feed on a caged demon.",tr:"Eldre'Thalas\u2019\u0131n bat\u0131 mahallesi; Shen'dralar\u2019\u0131n son Highborne\u2019lar\u0131 kafeslenmi\u015f bir iblisle besleniyor."},body:{en:["Eldre'Thalas, now called Dire Maul, was built to keep Queen Azshara's arcane secrets, and its keepers, the Shen'dralar, outlived the Great Sundering. Starved of the Well of Eternity's power, their leader Prince Tortheldrin had five pylons raised to cage the demon Immol'thar, and his people drew on its energy to stay immortal.","Over the centuries the prison weakened. To keep his own power, Tortheldrin turned on his fellow Shen'dralar and drained them. The Capital Gardens, once the Highborne's park and court, now hold his last loyal followers, withered trees, angry ancients and the caged demon itself."],tr:["Bug\xfcn Dire Maul denen Eldre'Thalas, Krali\xe7e Azshara\u2019n\u0131n arkan s\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 saklamak i\xe7in kuruldu; s\u0131rlar\u0131n bek\xe7ileri Shen'dralar, B\xfcy\xfck Yar\u0131lma\u2019dan sa\u011f \xe7\u0131kt\u0131. Sonsuzluk Kuyusu\u2019nun (Well of Eternity) g\xfcc\xfcnden yoksun kal\u0131nca liderleri Prens Tortheldrin, iblis Immol'thar\u2019\u0131 kafeslemek i\xe7in be\u015f pylon diktirdi; halk\u0131 da \xf6l\xfcms\xfcz kalmak i\xe7in iblisin enerjisini emdi.","Y\xfczy\u0131llar i\xe7inde hapis zay\u0131flad\u0131. Tortheldrin kendi g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc korumak i\xe7in Shen'dralar karde\u015flerine d\xf6nd\xfc ve onlar\u0131 t\xfcketti. Bir zamanlar Highborne\u2019lar\u0131n bah\xe7esi ve saray\u0131 olan Capital Gardens\u2019ta art\u0131k onun son sad\u0131k m\xfcritleri, kurumu\u015f a\u011fa\xe7lar, \xf6fkeli ancient\u2019lar ve kafesteki iblisin kendisi var."]},links:{instanceIds:['capital-gardens','warpwood-quarter','gordok-commons'],zoneIds:['feralas'],loreIds:['chapter:the-long-watch-of-hyjal','chapter:war-of-the-ancients']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('capital-gardens'),(0,n.wiki)("Immol'thar"),(0,n.wiki)('Prince Tortheldrin')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'scholomance',subjectId:'scholomance',era:'classic',order:30,title:{en:'Scholomance',tr:'Scholomance'},summary:{en:"Kel'Thuzad's school of necromancy in the crypts under Caer Darrow, handed to the Scourge by the Barov family.",tr:"Caer Darrow\u2019un alt\u0131ndaki mahzenlerde Kel'Thuzad\u2019\u0131n nekromansi okulu; Barov ailesi onu Scourge\u2019a teslim etti."},body:{en:["On an island in Darrowmere Lake, in the Western Plaguelands, stands Caer Darrow, once the keep of the noble Barov family. When the wizard Kel'Thuzad gathered followers for his Cult of the Damned, he promised immortality in the Lich King's name, and the Barovs gave him their keep and its crypts. The cult turned the crypts into the Scholomance, a school where necromancers trained to spread the plague.",'The Barovs got their wish in the worst way and now haunt the halls as undead. The lich Ras Frostwhisper rules the school for the Scourge, Darkmaster Gandling serves as its headmaster, and the Ravenian lurks below, ready to devour weak students.'],tr:["Western Plaguelands\u2019te, Darrowmere Lake\u2019teki bir adada, bir zamanlar soylu Barov ailesinin kalesi olan Caer Darrow y\xfckselir. B\xfcy\xfcc\xfc Kel'Thuzad, Cult of the Damned i\xe7in m\xfcritler toplarken Lich King ad\u0131na \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck vaat etti; Barov\u2019lar da kalelerini ve mahzenlerini ona verdi. Tarikat mahzenleri, vebay\u0131 yaymak \xfczere nekromans\xf6rlerin yeti\u015fti\u011fi bir okula, Scholomance\u2019a d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc.",'Barov\u2019lar dileklerine en k\xf6t\xfc bi\xe7imde kavu\u015ftu ve art\u0131k salonlarda \xf6l\xfcms\xfcz olarak dola\u015f\u0131yor. Okulu Scourge ad\u0131na lich Ras Frostwhisper y\xf6netir, m\xfcd\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc Darkmaster Gandling yapar; Ravenian ise a\u015fa\u011f\u0131da, zay\u0131f \xf6\u011frencileri yutmaya haz\u0131r bekler.']},links:{instanceIds:['scholomance'],zoneIds:['western-plaguelands'],loreIds:['chapter:the-lich-king-and-the-plague','chapter:plaguelands-and-the-scarlet-crusade']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('scholomance'),(0,n.wiki)('Barov'),(0,n.wiki)('Ras Frostwhisper')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'shapers-terrace',subjectId:'shapers-terrace',era:'classic',order:31,title:{en:"Shaper's Terrace",tr:"Shaper's Terrace"},summary:{en:"An ancient titan facility in the northern hills of Un'Goro Crater, worked with power crystals gathered across the crater.",tr:"Un'Goro Crater\u2019\u0131n kuzey tepelerinde kadim bir titan tesisi; kraterden toplanan g\xfc\xe7 kristalleriyle \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor."},body:{en:["On the northern heights of Un'Goro Crater, an ancient titan facility looks down on a land that time seems to have left alone. Dinosaurs, tar pits, titan structures and glowing crystals all belong to this expedition, which is meant for groups near the level cap.",'Its puzzle reaches beyond the walls: groups collect power crystals out in the crater and use them at consoles inside the terrace, so what they find in the wild shapes the challenges within.'],tr:["Un'Goro Crater\u2019\u0131n kuzey tepelerinde kadim bir titan tesisi, zaman\u0131n dokunmad\u0131\u011f\u0131 izlenimi veren bir diyara bakar. Dinozorlar, katran \xe7ukurlar\u0131, titan yap\u0131lar\u0131 ve par\u0131ldayan kristaller, azami seviyeye yakla\u015fan gruplar i\xe7in tasarlanan bu ke\u015fif yolculu\u011funun par\xe7as\u0131d\u0131r.",'Bulmacas\u0131 duvarlar\u0131n d\u0131\u015f\u0131na ta\u015far: gruplar kraterin d\xf6rt bir yan\u0131ndan g\xfc\xe7 kristalleri toplar ve onlar\u0131 teras\u0131n i\xe7indeki konsollarda kullan\u0131r; b\xf6ylece d\u0131\u015far\u0131da bulunanlar i\xe7erideki s\u0131navlar\u0131 \u015fekillendirir.']},links:{instanceIds:['shapers-terrace'],zoneIds:['un-goro-crater'],loreIds:['chapter:titans-and-old-gods']},image:'instance:shapers-terrace',sources:[n.FOREVER.dungeons],basis:'forever-partial',unknowns:[{en:'Who built the terrace and what it was for.',tr:'Teras\u0131 kimin kurdu\u011fu ve ne ama\xe7la kullan\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131.'},{en:"What the consoles do and which bosses wait inside; this guide's data lists none yet.",tr:'Konsollar\u0131n ne i\u015fe yarad\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve i\xe7eride hangi boss\u2019lar\u0131n bekledi\u011fi; bu rehberin verisinde hen\xfcz hi\xe7biri yok.'}]}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'stratholme',subjectId:'stratholme',era:'classic',order:32,title:{en:'Stratholme',tr:'Stratholme'},summary:{en:"The burning ruin of Lordaeron's great northern city, split between Baron Rivendare's Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade.",tr:'Lordaeron\u2019un b\xfcy\xfck kuzey \u015fehrinin yanan harabesi; Baron Rivendare\u2019in Scourge\u2019u ile Scarlet Crusade aras\u0131nda b\xf6l\xfcnm\xfc\u015f.'},body:{en:['Stratholme was the proudest city of northern Lordaeron and the birthplace of the Order of the Silver Hand. In the Third War, Prince Arthas put it to the sword rather than let its plague-touched people rise as undead, breaking with his mentor Uther. The Scourge moved in soon after, and the city has burned ever since.',"Today two enemies divide it. The Scarlet Crusade holds one side under Grand Crusader Dathrohan, never guessing that he is the dreadlord Balnazzar in disguise. The other side belongs to the Scourge and the death knight Baron Rivendare, a rich Stratholme landowner and friend of Kel'Thuzad before he joined the Cult of the Damned."],tr:['Stratholme, kuzey Lordaeron\u2019un en gururlu \u015fehri ve G\xfcm\xfc\u015f El\u2019in (Order of the Silver Hand) do\u011fdu\u011fu yerdi. \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019ta Prens Arthas, vebaya bula\u015fm\u0131\u015f halk\u0131n \xf6l\xfc olarak dirilmesine izin vermek yerine \u015fehri k\u0131l\u0131\xe7tan ge\xe7irdi ve ak\u0131l hocas\u0131 Uther\u2019le yollar\u0131n\u0131 ay\u0131rd\u0131. Scourge k\u0131sa s\xfcre sonra \u015fehre yerle\u015fti; Stratholme o g\xfcnden beri yan\u0131yor.',"Bug\xfcn iki d\xfc\u015fman \u015fehri b\xf6l\xfc\u015f\xfcyor. Bir yan\u0131n\u0131 Scarlet Crusade tutuyor; ba\u015flar\u0131ndaki Grand Crusader Dathrohan\u2019\u0131n asl\u0131nda k\u0131l\u0131k de\u011fi\u015ftirmi\u015f deh\u015fet efendisi (dreadlord) Balnazzar oldu\u011fundan haberleri yok. \xd6teki yan, Cult of the Damned\u2019e kat\u0131lmadan \xf6nce Stratholme\u2019un zengin bir toprak sahibi ve Kel'Thuzad\u2019\u0131n dostu olan \xf6l\xfcm \u015f\xf6valyesi Baron Rivendare ile Scourge\u2019a ait."]},links:{instanceIds:['stratholme'],zoneIds:['eastern-plaguelands'],classIds:['paladin'],loreIds:['chapter:fall-of-lordaeron','chapter:plaguelands-and-the-scarlet-crusade']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('stratholme'),(0,n.wiki)('Baron Rivendare'),(0,n.wiki)('Balnazzar')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'gordok-commons',subjectId:'gordok-commons',era:'classic',order:33,title:{en:'Gordok Commons',tr:'Gordok Commons'},summary:{en:'The northern district of Dire Maul, seat of King Gordok and his ogres, where whoever kills the king takes the crown.',tr:'Dire Maul\u2019un kuzey mahallesi; Kral Gordok ve ogre\u2019lerinin merkezi; kral\u0131 \xf6ld\xfcren tac\u0131 al\u0131r.'},body:{en:["Ogres of the Gordunni clan have taken over the northern quarter of ancient Eldre'Thalas, the ruined Highborne city now called Dire Maul. Their strongest warriors, the Gordok, rule from the Commons, and their king takes the name King Gordok.","Ogre custom here is simple: whoever slays the king becomes the new King Gordok. Clever groups slip past the guards Mol'dar, Fengus and Slip'kik, Stomper Kreeg and Captain Kromcrush to strike only at the king, and the ogres who survive treat the victors as their new rulers and pay them tribute. Cho'Rush the Observer stands at the king's side."],tr:["Gordunni klan\u0131n\u0131n ogre\u2019leri, bug\xfcn Dire Maul denen harap Highborne \u015fehri Eldre'Thalas\u2019\u0131n kuzey mahallesini ele ge\xe7irdi. En g\xfc\xe7l\xfc sava\u015f\xe7\u0131lar\u0131 Gordok\u2019lar, Commons\u2019tan h\xfck\xfcm s\xfcrer; krallar\u0131 da King Gordok ad\u0131n\u0131 al\u0131r.","Buradaki ogre gelene\u011fi basittir: kral\u0131 \xf6ld\xfcren yeni King Gordok olur. Ak\u0131ll\u0131 gruplar, muhaf\u0131zlar Mol'dar, Fengus ve Slip'kik ile Stomper Kreeg ve Captain Kromcrush\u2019\u0131n yan\u0131ndan sessizce ge\xe7ip yaln\u0131zca krala sald\u0131r\u0131r; hayatta kalan ogre\u2019ler de galipleri yeni h\xfck\xfcmdarlar\u0131 say\u0131p hara\xe7 \xf6der. Cho'Rush the Observer kral\u0131n yan\u0131nda durur."]},links:{instanceIds:['gordok-commons','warpwood-quarter','capital-gardens'],zoneIds:['feralas'],loreIds:['chapter:the-long-watch-of-hyjal']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('gordok-commons'),(0,n.wiki)('Dire Maul'),(0,n.wiki)('King Gordok')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'barrow-deeps',subjectId:'barrow-deeps',era:'classic',order:34,title:{en:'Barrow Deeps',tr:'Barrow Deeps'},summary:{en:'A ten-player raid into the prison beneath Kalimdor that held Illidan Stormrage for ten thousand years.',tr:'Kalimdor\u2019un alt\u0131ndaki, Illidan Stormrage\u2019\u0131 on bin y\u0131l tutsak eden hapishaneye inen on ki\u015filik bask\u0131n.'},body:{en:['Deep under Kalimdor, the Barrow Deeps kept Illidan Stormrage captive for ten thousand years. Now the way into its tunnels stands open, and raiders go down to find out what happened to the ones left in the dark and what the wardens mean to do about the threat stirring beneath.',"Three ways lead in, connected to Mount Hyjal, Winterspring and Blackmaw Hold. Ten players face eight bosses on the way down, from the Deepscar Matriarch and Khalith the Dreadspinner to Del'lynar Songwood, and last of all Sonya Darkhallow."],tr:['Kalimdor\u2019un \xe7ok alt\u0131nda Barrow Deeps, Illidan Stormrage\u2019\u0131 on bin y\u0131l boyunca tutsak etti. \u015eimdi t\xfcnellerine giden yol a\xe7\u0131k; bask\u0131nc\u0131lar karanl\u0131kta geride kalanlar\u0131n ba\u015f\u0131na ne geldi\u011fini ve gardiyanlar\u0131n a\u015fa\u011f\u0131da k\u0131p\u0131rdanan tehlikeye kar\u015f\u0131 ne yapmay\u0131 planlad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 \xf6\u011frenmek i\xe7in a\u015fa\u011f\u0131 iniyor.',"\u0130\xe7eri, Mount Hyjal, Winterspring ve Blackmaw Hold\u2019a ba\u011flanan \xfc\xe7 yol a\xe7\u0131l\u0131r. On oyuncu a\u015fa\u011f\u0131 inerken Deepscar Matriarch ve Khalith the Dreadspinner\u2019dan Del'lynar Songwood\u2019a uzanan sekiz boss\u2019la kar\u015f\u0131la\u015f\u0131r; en sonda Sonya Darkhallow bekler."]},links:{instanceIds:['barrow-deeps','blackmaw-hold','hyjal-summit'],zoneIds:['winterspring'],loreIds:['chapter:the-long-watch-of-hyjal']},sources:[n.FOREVER.raids,(0,n.instanceSource)('barrow-deeps')],basis:'forever',unknowns:[{en:'Who opened the passages, and what the danger below is.',tr:'Ge\xe7itleri kimin a\xe7t\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve a\u015fa\u011f\u0131daki tehlikenin ne oldu\u011fu.'},{en:'Who the wardens are, and the stories of the eight bosses.',tr:'Gardiyanlar\u0131n kim oldu\u011fu ve sekiz boss\u2019un hik\xe2yeleri.'}]}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'hyjal-summit',subjectId:'hyjal-summit',era:'classic',order:35,title:{en:'Hyjal Summit',tr:'Hyjal Summit'},summary:{en:'A twenty-player raid on the peak of Mount Hyjal near the World Tree Nordrassil, with thirteen bosses and many paths.',tr:'Mount Hyjal\u2019\u0131n zirvesinde, D\xfcnya A\u011fac\u0131 Nordrassil yak\u0131n\u0131nda on \xfc\xe7 boss\u2019lu ve bir\xe7ok yolu olan yirmi ki\u015filik bask\u0131n.'},body:{en:['Hyjal Summit sits at the top of Mount Hyjal, near the World Tree Nordrassil. An ancient guardian bars the way at the start; after that, raiders pick their own routes over the mountain, through ruins on the surface and beneath it, fighting whatever threatens Hyjal until the path to the final battles opens.','Twenty players face thirteen bosses, among them Bandalar, the Time-Lost Battalion, the Council of Thorns, the Wild King and the Ancient of Decay. The last of all is Nythus the Dreambound.'],tr:['Hyjal Summit, Mount Hyjal\u2019\u0131n tepesinde, D\xfcnya A\u011fac\u0131 Nordrassil\u2019in yak\u0131n\u0131nda yer al\u0131r. Ba\u015fta yolu kadim bir muhaf\u0131z keser; ard\u0131ndan bask\u0131nc\u0131lar da\u011f\u0131n \xfczerinden, yerin \xfcst\xfcndeki ve alt\u0131ndaki harabelerden ge\xe7en kendi yollar\u0131n\u0131 se\xe7er ve son sava\u015flara giden yol a\xe7\u0131lana dek Hyjal\u2019\u0131 tehdit eden her \u015feyle \xe7arp\u0131\u015f\u0131r.','Yirmi oyuncu on \xfc\xe7 boss\u2019la kar\u015f\u0131la\u015f\u0131r; aralar\u0131nda Bandalar, Time-Lost Battalion, Council of Thorns, The Wild King ve Ancient of Decay de var. En sonuncusu Nythus the Dreambound\u2019dur.']},links:{instanceIds:['hyjal-summit','barrow-deeps'],loreIds:['chapter:the-long-watch-of-hyjal','chapter:battle-for-mount-hyjal']},sources:[n.FOREVER.raids,(0,n.instanceSource)('hyjal-summit')],basis:'forever-partial',unknowns:[{en:'What force threatens Hyjal; the official overview does not name it.',tr:'Hyjal\u2019\u0131 tehdit eden g\xfcc\xfcn ne oldu\u011fu; resm\xee tan\u0131t\u0131m bunu adland\u0131rm\u0131yor.'},{en:'Who the ancient guardian is, and who Nythus the Dreambound is.',tr:'Kadim muhaf\u0131z\u0131n ve Nythus the Dreambound\u2019un kim oldu\u011fu.'}]}),(0,n.lore)({category:'instance',slug:'onyxias-lair',subjectId:'onyxias-lair',era:'classic',order:36,title:{en:"Onyxia's Lair",tr:"Onyxia's Lair"},summary:{en:'The lair of Onyxia, brood mother of the black dragonflight, in Dustwallow Marsh; only bearers of the Drakefire Amulet may enter.',tr:'Kara ejderha soyunun ana krali\xe7esi Onyxia\u2019n\u0131n Dustwallow Marsh\u2019taki ini; yaln\u0131zca Drakefire Amulet ta\u015f\u0131yanlar girebilir.'},body:{en:['In the Wyrmbog of Dustwallow Marsh, Onyxia, daughter of Deathwing and sister of Nefarian, guards her brood in a cavern of fire. Her greater weapon is deceit. Wearing human form as Lady Katrana Prestor, she whispers at the court of Stormwind and works to turn the mortal kingdoms against one another.',"Forty players face her in a three-phase battle of flame, so raids gather fire resistance first. Each member must also carry the Drakefire Amulet, earned through a long quest chain: the Alliance through Marshal Windsor's escape from Blackrock Depths and the unmasking at Stormwind, the Horde through Rexxar and the drake Emberstrife, both ending with General Drakkisath in Upper Blackrock Spire."],tr:['Dustwallow Marsh\u2019\u0131n Wyrmbog b\xf6lgesinde, Deathwing\u2019in k\u0131z\u0131 ve Nefarian\u2019\u0131n k\u0131z karde\u015fi Onyxia, ate\u015fle dolu bir ma\u011farada yavrular\u0131n\u0131 korur. Daha b\xfcy\xfck silah\u0131 ise aldatmacad\u0131r: Lady Katrana Prestor ad\u0131yla insan k\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131na girip Stormwind saray\u0131nda f\u0131s\u0131ldar ve \xf6l\xfcml\xfc krall\u0131klar\u0131 birbirine d\xfc\u015f\xfcrmeye \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131r.','K\u0131rk oyuncu onunla alevlerle dolu \xfc\xe7 a\u015famal\u0131 bir sava\u015fta kar\u015f\u0131la\u015f\u0131r; bu y\xfczden bask\u0131nlar \xf6nce ate\u015f direnci toplar. Her \xfcyenin uzun bir g\xf6rev zinciriyle kazan\u0131lan Drakefire Amulet\u2019i ta\u015f\u0131mas\u0131 da gerekir: \u0130ttifak i\xe7in Marshal Windsor\u2019un Blackrock Depths\u2019ten ka\xe7\u0131\u015f\u0131 ve Stormwind\u2019deki maskenin d\xfc\u015f\xfcr\xfclmesi, Horde i\xe7in Rexxar ve drake Emberstrife; iki yol da Upper Blackrock Spire\u2019daki General Drakkisath ile biter.']},links:{instanceIds:['onyxias-lair','blackrock-depths'],zoneIds:['dustwallow-marsh'],loreIds:['chapter:stormwind-in-shadow','chapter:fire-beneath-blackrock']},sources:[(0,n.instanceSource)('onyxias-lair'),(0,n.wiki)('Onyxia'),n.FOREVER.raids],basis:'established'})]},868,[866]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"itemLore",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});var n=r(d[0]);const t=[(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'demon-soul',title:{en:"The Dragon Soul (Demon Soul)",tr:"Ejderha Ruhu (Dragon Soul / Demon Soul)"},summary:{en:"A golden disc forged by Neltharion to master all dragons; it gave birth to Deathwing and, ages later, chained the red dragonflight to the Horde.",tr:"Neltharion\u2019un b\xfct\xfcn ejderhalara h\xfckmetmek i\xe7in yapt\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131 alt\u0131n disk; Deathwing\u2019i do\u011furdu, \xe7a\u011flar sonra k\u0131z\u0131l ejderha soyunu Horde\u2019a zincirledi."},body:{en:["Before the War of the Ancients, the Earth-Warder Neltharion had his goblin servants craft a plain-looking golden disc, secretly steeped in the corruption of the Old Gods. He persuaded the other Aspects to pour part of their power into it to fight the Burning Legion, then turned it on demons and allies alike. The Dragon Soul\u2019s energies tore at his body, and Neltharion became Deathwing.","After the Sundering, the Aspects hid the disc deep beneath what is now Redridge. Following Deathwing\u2019s visions, the Dragonmaw clan recovered it, renamed it the Demon Soul and used it to enslave Alexstrasza at Grim Batol. It was finally shattered there, and the red dragons went free."],tr:["Kadimler Sava\u015f\u0131\u2019ndan \xf6nce Toprak Koruyucusu Neltharion, goblin hizmetk\xe2rlar\u0131na sade g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcml\xfc alt\u0131n bir disk yapt\u0131rd\u0131; disk gizlice Kadim Tanr\u0131lar\u0131n (Old Gods) yozla\u015fmas\u0131yla doluydu. \xd6teki Aspect\u2019leri Yanan Lejyon\u2019a kar\u015f\u0131 g\xfc\xe7lerinin bir k\u0131sm\u0131n\u0131 bu diske aktarmaya ikna etti, sonra onu iblislere de m\xfcttefiklerine de \xe7evirdi. Ejderha Ruhu\u2019nun enerjisi bedenini par\xe7alad\u0131 ve Neltharion, Deathwing\u2019e d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc.","B\xfcy\xfck Yar\u0131lma\u2019dan sonra Aspect\u2019ler diski bug\xfcnk\xfc Redridge\u2019in derinliklerine gizledi. Deathwing\u2019in g\xf6nderdi\u011fi g\xf6r\xfcnt\xfclerin pe\u015finden giden Dragonmaw klan\u0131 onu buldu, ad\u0131n\u0131 Demon Soul (\u0130blis Ruhu) koydu ve Grim Batol\u2019da Alexstrasza\u2019y\u0131 k\xf6lele\u015ftirmek i\xe7in kulland\u0131. Disk sonunda orada par\xe7aland\u0131 ve k\u0131z\u0131l ejderhalar \xf6zg\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfcne kavu\u015ftu."]},era:'ancient-kalimdor',order:1,links:{zoneIds:['redridge-mountains','wetlands'],loreIds:['term:dragon-aspects','chapter:war-of-the-ancients']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Demon Soul')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'atiesh',title:{en:"Atiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian",tr:"Atiesh, Muhaf\u0131z\u0131n B\xfcy\xfck Asas\u0131"},summary:{en:"The staff of the Guardians of Tirisfal, last carried by Medivh, later shattered and hunted by Kel'Thuzad.",tr:"Tirisfal Muhaf\u0131zlar\u0131n\u0131n asas\u0131; son olarak Medivh ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131, sonra par\xe7aland\u0131 ve Kel'Thuzad\u2019\u0131n av hedefi oldu."},body:{en:["Atiesh passed from Guardian to Guardian for generations, ending with Medivh, the last of them. Legends say it grew from a \u201cseed of hate\u201d and grants its bearer endless power; ravens gather around it, and it can open a way to Karazhan. After Medivh fell, the Kirin Tor locked the staff away in Dalaran, where every mage who touched it met a grim end.","When Archimonde destroyed Dalaran, Atiesh broke into dozens of pieces that scattered across Azeroth, and Kel'Thuzad set out to gather them. In the original game, raiders pried its splinters from his necropolis of Naxxramas, had the frame restored with the help of the bronze dragon Anachronos, and then had to cleanse the staff in Stratholme by defeating the demon imprisoned within it."],tr:["Atiesh nesiller boyunca bir Muhaf\u0131zdan \xf6tekine ge\xe7ti ve sonuncular\u0131 olan Medivh\u2019le sona erdi. Efsaneye g\xf6re bir \u201cnefret tohumundan\u201d do\u011fdu ve sahibine t\xfckenmez g\xfc\xe7 verir; kuzgunlar \xe7evresinde toplan\u0131r, Karazhan\u2019a da yol a\xe7abilir. Medivh d\xfc\u015ft\xfckten sonra Kirin Tor asay\u0131 Dalaran\u2019da kilit alt\u0131na ald\u0131; ona dokunan her Mage ac\u0131 bir sonla kar\u015f\u0131la\u015ft\u0131.","Archimonde Dalaran\u2019\u0131 y\u0131kt\u0131\u011f\u0131nda Atiesh onlarca par\xe7aya b\xf6l\xfcn\xfcp Azeroth\u2019a da\u011f\u0131ld\u0131 ve Kel'Thuzad par\xe7alar\u0131n pe\u015fine d\xfc\u015ft\xfc. Orijinal oyunda bask\u0131nc\u0131lar k\u0131ym\u0131klar\u0131 onun Naxxramas nekropol\xfcnden s\xf6k\xfcp ald\u0131, bronz ejderha Anachronos\u2019un yard\u0131m\u0131yla \xe7er\xe7eveyi yeniden kurdu, ard\u0131ndan asay\u0131 Stratholme\u2019da ar\u0131nd\u0131rmak i\xe7in i\xe7ine hapsedilmi\u015f iblisi yenmek zorunda kald\u0131."]},era:'elder-kingdoms',order:2,links:{classIds:['mage'],zoneIds:['deadwind-pass','alterac-mountains','eastern-plaguelands'],instanceIds:['stratholme'],itemIds:[22589,22630,22631,22632,22726,22727,22737],loreIds:['term:guardian-of-tirisfal','term:kirin-tor']},image:'icon:inv_staff_medivh',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Atiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'scepter-of-the-shifting-sands',title:{en:"The Scepter of the Shifting Sands",tr:"Kayan Kumlar Asas\u0131 (Scepter of the Shifting Sands)"},summary:{en:"The key to the Scarab Wall that sealed Ahn'Qiraj, shattered by a grieving Fandral Staghelm.",tr:"Ahn'Qiraj\u2019\u0131 m\xfch\xfcrleyen Scarab Duvar\u0131\u2019n\u0131n anahtar\u0131; yas i\xe7indeki Fandral Staghelm taraf\u0131ndan par\xe7aland\u0131."},body:{en:["Nearly a thousand years before the First War, the insectoid qiraji poured out of Ahn'Qiraj, urged on by the Old God C'Thun. Archdruid Fandral Staghelm led the night elves against them, but his son Valstann was cut down before his eyes, and the war turned. Only with the help of four dragonflights were the swarms driven back and sealed behind the Scarab Wall.","The wall could be opened only by striking the Scarab Gong with this scepter. Fandral, in the fury of his grief, shattered it, and its pieces were scattered. In the original game, adventurers reassembled the scepter, rang the gong and opened Ahn'Qiraj once more."],tr:["Birinci Sava\u015f\u2019tan neredeyse bin y\u0131l \xf6nce b\xf6ce\u011fe benzeyen qiraji\u2019ler, Kadim Tanr\u0131 C'Thun\u2019un k\u0131\u015fk\u0131rtmas\u0131yla Ahn'Qiraj\u2019dan d\u0131\u015far\u0131 ta\u015ft\u0131. Ba\u015f Druid Fandral Staghelm gece elflerini onlara kar\u015f\u0131 y\xf6netti; ancak o\u011flu Valstann g\xf6zlerinin \xf6n\xfcnde katledildi ve sava\u015f\u0131n gidi\u015fat\u0131 de\u011fi\u015fti. S\xfcr\xfcler ancak d\xf6rt ejderha soyunun yard\u0131m\u0131yla geri p\xfcsk\xfcrt\xfcl\xfcp Scarab Duvar\u0131\u2019n\u0131n ard\u0131na m\xfch\xfcrlendi.","Duvar yaln\u0131zca bu asayla Scarab Gongu\u2019na vurularak a\xe7\u0131labilirdi. Fandral yas\u0131n\u0131n \xf6fkesiyle asay\u0131 k\u0131rd\u0131 ve par\xe7alar\u0131 da\u011f\u0131ld\u0131. Orijinal oyunda macerac\u0131lar asay\u0131 yeniden birle\u015ftirdi, gongu \xe7ald\u0131 ve Ahn'Qiraj\u2019\u0131 bir kez daha a\xe7t\u0131."]},era:'elder-kingdoms',order:3,links:{raceIds:['night-elf'],zoneIds:['silithus','tanaris'],itemIds:[21175],loreIds:['term:old-gods']},image:'icon:inv_hammer_25',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('The Scepter of the Shifting Sands'),(0,n.wiki)('War of the Shifting Sands')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'doomhammer',title:{en:"Doomhammer",tr:"Doomhammer (K\u0131yamet \xc7ekici)"},summary:{en:"The heirloom warhammer of the Doomhammer line, carried by Orgrim through two wars and handed to Thrall.",tr:"Doomhammer soyunun ku\u015faktan ku\u015fa\u011fa ge\xe7en sava\u015f \xe7ekici; Orgrim\u2019in iki sava\u015f boyunca ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve sonunda Thrall\u2019a verdi\u011fi silah."},body:{en:["Forged long ago on Draenor, the great black-stoned hammer passed from father to son within a single orc family, and an old Blackrock prophecy hung over it: the last of the line would bring the orcs first salvation and then doom, before a stranger raised the hammer for justice. Orgrim Doomhammer wielded it in the First and Second Wars and struck down Anduin Lothar with it, shattering the knight\u2019s runeblade.","After the Horde\u2019s defeat, Orgrim escaped captivity and fought to free his people from the internment camps. Mortally wounded in one of those battles, he gave the hammer to Thrall, who was neither of his clan nor of his blood. Thrall carried it as the symbol of a reborn Horde, and the prophecy found its stranger."],tr:["Uzun zaman \xf6nce Draenor\u2019da d\xf6v\xfclen bu kara ta\u015fl\u0131 b\xfcy\xfck \xe7eki\xe7, tek bir ork ailesinde babadan o\u011fula ge\xe7ti ve \xfczerinde eski bir Blackrock kehaneti vard\u0131: soyun sonuncusu orklara \xf6nce kurtulu\u015f, sonra felaket getirecek, ard\u0131ndan bir yabanc\u0131 \xe7ekici adalet i\xe7in kald\u0131racakt\u0131. Orgrim Doomhammer onu Birinci ve \u0130kinci Sava\u015f\u2019ta kulland\u0131; Anduin Lothar\u2019\u0131 bu \xe7eki\xe7le yere serdi ve \u015f\xf6valyenin r\xfcnl\xfc k\u0131l\u0131c\u0131n\u0131 parampar\xe7a etti.","Horde\u2019un yenilgisinden sonra Orgrim esaretten ka\xe7t\u0131 ve halk\u0131n\u0131 esir kamplar\u0131ndan kurtarmak i\xe7in sava\u015ft\u0131. Bu \xe7arp\u0131\u015fmalardan birinde \xf6l\xfcmc\xfcl yara ald\u0131\u011f\u0131nda \xe7ekici, ne klan\u0131ndan ne de kan\u0131ndan olan Thrall\u2019a verdi. Thrall onu yeniden do\u011fan Horde\u2019un simgesi olarak ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131 ve kehanet bekledi\u011fi yabanc\u0131y\u0131 buldu."]},era:'interwar',order:4,links:{raceIds:['orc'],classIds:['shaman'],zoneIds:['durotar','hillsbrad-foothills'],loreIds:['chapter:thrall-and-the-new-horde','chapter:the-second-war']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Doomhammer')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'book-of-medivh',title:{en:"The Book of Medivh",tr:"Medivh\u2019in Kitab\u0131 (Book of Medivh)"},summary:{en:"Medivh's last surviving spellbook, used twice to tear open the way between worlds.",tr:"Medivh\u2019ten kalan son b\xfcy\xfc kitab\u0131; d\xfcnyalar aras\u0131ndaki yolu iki kez y\u0131rtmak i\xe7in kullan\u0131ld\u0131."},body:{en:["After Medivh\u2019s death his spellbook was kept in the royal library of rebuilt Stormwind, until agents of Alterac stole it. Through a bargain between Alterac\u2019s king and the Horde death knight Teron Gorefiend, it passed to the orcs, and on Draenor Ner'zhul used it with other relics to open new portals, rifts that tore his world apart. Before the Dark Portal fell, Khadgar recovered the book and sent it home by gryphon.","The Kirin Tor sealed it in a vault in Dalaran. During the Third War, Kel'Thuzad shattered that vault, and with the book\u2019s power he opened the rift through which Archimonde and the Burning Legion entered Azeroth. Afterwards the book stayed in the lich\u2019s hands."],tr:["Medivh\u2019in \xf6l\xfcm\xfcnden sonra b\xfcy\xfc kitab\u0131 yeniden kurulan Stormwind\u2019in kraliyet k\xfct\xfcphanesinde sakland\u0131; ta ki Alterac ajanlar\u0131 onu \xe7alana dek. Alterac kral\u0131 ile Horde\u2019un \xf6l\xfcm \u015f\xf6valyesi Teron Gorefiend aras\u0131ndaki bir pazarl\u0131kla kitap orklara ge\xe7ti. Draenor\u2019da Ner'zhul onu ba\u015fka kal\u0131nt\u0131larla birlikte yeni ge\xe7itler a\xe7mak i\xe7in kulland\u0131; bu yar\u0131klar d\xfcnyas\u0131n\u0131 parampar\xe7a etti. Kara Ge\xe7it \xe7\xf6kmeden \xf6nce Khadgar kitab\u0131 geri ald\u0131 ve bir grifonla Azeroth\u2019a yollad\u0131.","Kirin Tor kitab\u0131 Dalaran\u2019da bir mahzene kilitledi. \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019ta Kel'Thuzad bu mahzeni par\xe7alad\u0131 ve kitab\u0131n g\xfcc\xfcyle, Archimonde ile Yanan Lejyon\u2019un Azeroth\u2019a girdi\u011fi yar\u0131\u011f\u0131 a\xe7t\u0131. Sonras\u0131nda kitap lich\u2019in elinde kald\u0131."]},era:'interwar',order:5,links:{zoneIds:['alterac-mountains'],loreIds:['term:kirin-tor','chapter:beyond-the-dark-portal']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Book of Medivh')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'frostmourne',title:{en:"Frostmourne",tr:"Frostmourne"},summary:{en:"The Lich King's runeblade, which claimed Arthas Menethil's soul in the ice of Northrend.",tr:"Lich King\u2019in r\xfcnl\xfc k\u0131l\u0131c\u0131; Northrend\u2019in buzlar\u0131 aras\u0131nda Arthas Menethil\u2019in ruhunu ald\u0131."},body:{en:["Frostmourne was bound to the Lich King\u2019s prison in Icecrown, and Ner'zhul pushed it out of the Frozen Throne to lure a champion. It waited in a frozen cavern in Northrend, guarded, and bearing a warning that its power would scar the soul of whoever took it up. Prince Arthas, desperate to stop the plague, ignored the warning and seized the blade while Muradin Bronzebeard lay struck down by a shard of ice.","The sword devours the souls of those it slays. With it Arthas killed the dreadlord Mal'Ganis, then his own father, King Terenas, and his old mentor Uther. By year 25 it rests at the side of the Lich King himself. In later stories, beyond Classic, Tirion Fordring shattered it with the Ashbringer."],tr:["Frostmourne, Lich King\u2019in Icecrown\u2019daki hapishanesine ba\u011fl\u0131yd\u0131; Ner'zhul onu bir \u015fampiyonu cezbetmek i\xe7in Frozen Throne\u2019dan d\u0131\u015far\u0131 itti. K\u0131l\u0131\xe7 Northrend\u2019de donmu\u015f bir ma\u011farada, bek\xe7ilerin ard\u0131nda bekliyordu ve onu alan\u0131n ruhunun bu g\xfc\xe7le yaralanaca\u011f\u0131na dair bir uyar\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131yordu. Vebay\u0131 durdurmak i\xe7in \xe7aresiz kalan Prens Arthas uyar\u0131y\u0131 dinlemedi; Muradin Bronzebeard bir buz par\xe7as\u0131yla yere serilmi\u015fken k\u0131l\u0131c\u0131 kavrad\u0131.","K\u0131l\u0131\xe7, \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfcklerinin ruhlar\u0131n\u0131 yutar. Arthas onunla deh\u015fet lordu Mal'Ganis\u2019i, ard\u0131ndan babas\u0131 Kral Terenas\u2019\u0131 ve eski hocas\u0131 Uther\u2019i \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc. 25. y\u0131lda k\u0131l\u0131\xe7 bizzat Lich King\u2019in yan\u0131ndad\u0131r. Classic sonras\u0131ndaki hik\xe2yelerde Tirion Fordring onu Ashbringer ile par\xe7alad\u0131."]},era:'third-war',order:6,links:{raceIds:['human'],zoneIds:['tirisfal-glades'],loreIds:['term:lich-king','item:ashbringer','chapter:fall-of-lordaeron']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Frostmourne')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'ashbringer',title:{en:"Ashbringer",tr:"Ashbringer (K\xfcl Getiren)"},summary:{en:"A holy blade forged in Ironforge to burn the undead to ash, then betrayed and corrupted in the Plaguelands.",tr:"\xd6l\xfcms\xfczleri k\xfcle \xe7evirmek i\xe7in Ironforge\u2019da d\xf6v\xfclen kutsal k\u0131l\u0131\xe7; Plaguelands b\xf6lgesinde ihanetle yozla\u015ft\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131."},body:{en:["During the Second War, Highlord Alexandros Mograine of the Silver Hand found a dark crystal on a slain orc warlock. When the Scourge threatened Lordaeron, the order\u2019s leaders tried to destroy it with holy magic; instead the crystal drank in the Light and turned radiant. King Magni Bronzebeard forged it into a sword on the Great Anvil of Ironforge, and in Mograine\u2019s hands the Ashbringer reduced the undead to ash.","The dreadlord Balnazzar and Kel'Thuzad plotted his fall. Mograine\u2019s son Renault led him into a Scourge ambush at Stratholme and killed him with his own sword, corrupting it. In year 25, Alexandros serves Kel'Thuzad as a death knight, while Renault commands the Scarlet Monastery. Only in later stories was the blade cleansed."],tr:["\u0130kinci Sava\u015f s\u0131ras\u0131nda G\xfcm\xfc\u015f El\u2019in Y\xfcce Lordu Alexandros Mograine, \xf6ld\xfcr\xfclm\xfc\u015f bir ork Warlock\u2019unun \xfczerinde karanl\u0131k bir kristal buldu. Scourge Lordaeron\u2019u tehdit etti\u011finde tarikat\u0131n \xf6nderleri onu kutsal b\xfcy\xfcyle yok etmeye \xe7al\u0131\u015ft\u0131; kristal ise I\u015f\u0131\u011f\u0131 i\xe7ine \xe7ekip \u0131\u015f\u0131l \u0131\u015f\u0131l parlad\u0131. Kral Magni Bronzebeard onu Ironforge\u2019un B\xfcy\xfck \xd6rs\u2019\xfcnde bir k\u0131l\u0131ca d\xf6vd\xfc ve Mograine\u2019in elinde Ashbringer \xf6l\xfcms\xfczleri k\xfcle \xe7evirdi.","Deh\u015fet lordu Balnazzar ile Kel'Thuzad onun d\xfc\u015f\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfc planlad\u0131. Mograine\u2019in o\u011flu Renault, babas\u0131n\u0131 Stratholme\u2019da bir Scourge pususuna g\xf6t\xfcrd\xfc ve onu kendi k\u0131l\u0131c\u0131yla \xf6ld\xfcrerek k\u0131l\u0131c\u0131 yozla\u015ft\u0131rd\u0131. 25. y\u0131lda Alexandros, Kel'Thuzad\u2019a \xf6l\xfcm \u015f\xf6valyesi olarak hizmet ederken Renault, Scarlet Monastery\u2019nin ba\u015f\u0131ndad\u0131r. K\u0131l\u0131\xe7 ancak sonraki hik\xe2yelerde ar\u0131nd\u0131."]},era:'third-war',order:7,links:{classIds:['paladin'],raceIds:['human','dwarf'],zoneIds:['eastern-plaguelands','tirisfal-glades','dun-morogh'],instanceIds:['stratholme','scarlet-monastery-cathedral'],itemIds:[13262],loreIds:['term:silver-hand','term:scarlet-crusade','chapter:plaguelands-and-the-scarlet-crusade']},image:'icon:inv_sword_2h_ashbringercorrupt',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Ashbringer')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'skull-of-guldan',title:{en:"The Skull of Gul'dan",tr:"Gul'dan\u2019\u0131n Kafatas\u0131 (Skull of Gul'dan)"},summary:{en:"The warlock's skull, a demonic relic that opened portals, poisoned Ashenvale and remade Illidan.",tr:"Warlock\u2019un kafatas\u0131; ge\xe7itler a\xe7an, Ashenvale\u2019i zehirleyen ve Illidan\u2019\u0131 d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcren iblis kal\u0131nt\u0131s\u0131."},body:{en:["Gul'dan was torn apart by demons in the Tomb of Sargeras, but his skull kept a sliver of his malice. It passed through several orc hands until Grom Hellscream brought it to Ner'zhul, who used it to help reopen the Dark Portal. Khadgar later sent it to Dalaran together with the Book of Medivh, and the Kirin Tor guarded both.","As Dalaran fell in the Third War, the dreadlord Tichondrius stole the skull, and its power fouled the forests of Ashenvale and Felwood. Illidan Stormrage consumed its magic, became half demon, and slew Tichondrius with that power. The husk of the skull stayed with Illidan."],tr:["Gul'dan, Sargeras\u2019\u0131n Mezar\u0131\u2019nda iblisler taraf\u0131ndan par\xe7aland\u0131; ama kafatas\u0131 kininin bir k\u0131r\u0131nt\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131may\u0131 s\xfcrd\xfcrd\xfc. Kafatas\u0131 birka\xe7 orkun elinden ge\xe7ti; sonunda Grom Hellscream onu Ner'zhul\u2019a g\xf6t\xfcrd\xfc ve Ner'zhul onu Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019i yeniden a\xe7makta kulland\u0131. Khadgar daha sonra kafatas\u0131n\u0131 Medivh\u2019in Kitab\u0131 ile birlikte Dalaran\u2019a yollad\u0131 ve Kirin Tor ikisini de korudu.","\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019ta Dalaran d\xfc\u015ferken deh\u015fet lordu Tichondrius kafatas\u0131n\u0131 \xe7ald\u0131; onun g\xfcc\xfc Ashenvale ve Felwood ormanlar\u0131n\u0131 zehirledi. Illidan Stormrage kafatas\u0131n\u0131n b\xfcy\xfcs\xfcn\xfc i\xe7ine \xe7ekerek yar\u0131 iblise d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc ve Tichondrius\u2019u bu g\xfc\xe7le \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc. Kafatas\u0131n\u0131n kabu\u011fu Illidan\u2019da kald\u0131."]},era:'third-war',order:8,links:{raceIds:['orc','night-elf'],classIds:['warlock'],zoneIds:['ashenvale','felwood'],loreIds:['term:fel','term:nathrezim','item:book-of-medivh']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)("Skull of Gul'dan")],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'gorehowl',title:{en:"Gorehowl",tr:"Gorehowl"},summary:{en:"The howling axe of the Hellscream family, which felled both Cenarius and Mannoroth.",tr:"Hellscream ailesinin uluyan baltas\u0131; hem Cenarius\u2019u hem Mannoroth\u2019u yere serdi."},body:{en:["Gorehowl was forged generations before Grom Hellscream inherited it, and Warsong legend says the axe was tempered with the hearts of mighty gronn. Grom, chieftain of the Warsong clan, was the first to drink the blood of the pit lord Mannoroth, binding the orcs to the Burning Legion. In Ashenvale he drank again, and with Gorehowl he slew the demigod Cenarius.","Thrall freed him from the demon\u2019s grip, and together they confronted Mannoroth. Grom split the pit lord\u2019s weapon and killed him with a single stroke, breaking the curse on his people at the cost of his own life. Thrall kept the axe in Orgrimmar afterwards."],tr:["Gorehowl, Grom Hellscream ona sahip olmadan nesiller \xf6nce d\xf6v\xfclm\xfc\u015ft\xfc; Warsong efsanesine g\xf6re balta g\xfc\xe7l\xfc gronn\u2019lar\u0131n y\xfcrekleriyle sertle\u015ftirildi. Warsong klan\u0131n\u0131n \u015fefi Grom, \xe7ukur lordu Mannoroth\u2019un kan\u0131n\u0131 i\xe7en ilk ork oldu ve orklar\u0131 Yanan Lejyon\u2019a ba\u011flad\u0131. Ashenvale\u2019de kan\u0131 yeniden i\xe7ti ve Gorehowl ile yar\u0131 tanr\u0131 Cenarius\u2019u \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc.","Thrall onu iblisin pen\xe7esinden kurtard\u0131 ve birlikte Mannoroth\u2019un kar\u015f\u0131s\u0131na \xe7\u0131kt\u0131lar. Grom \xe7ukur lordunun silah\u0131n\u0131 ikiye ay\u0131rd\u0131 ve onu tek darbeyle \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc; halk\u0131n\u0131n \xfczerindeki laneti kendi can\u0131 pahas\u0131na k\u0131rd\u0131. Thrall baltay\u0131 sonras\u0131nda Orgrimmar\u2019da saklad\u0131."]},era:'third-war',order:9,links:{raceIds:['orc'],classIds:['warrior'],zoneIds:['ashenvale','durotar'],loreIds:['term:burning-legion','chapter:battle-for-mount-hyjal']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Gorehowl')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'horn-of-cenarius',title:{en:"The Horn of Cenarius",tr:"Cenarius\u2019un Borusu (Horn of Cenarius)"},summary:{en:"The demigod's horn, which woke the druids from their long sleep and called the night elves' ancestors at Hyjal.",tr:"Druid\u2019leri uzun uykular\u0131ndan uyand\u0131ran ve Hyjal\u2019de gece elflerinin atalar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7a\u011f\u0131ran yar\u0131 tanr\u0131n\u0131n borusu."},body:{en:["After Cenarius fell, his horn remained on Moonglade under the watch of ancient guardians. When the Burning Legion returned in the Third War, the priestess Tyrande Whisperwind recovered it and used it to wake Malfurion Stormrage from his long dreaming. Malfurion in turn sounded it to rouse the sleeping druids of the Talon and the Claw.","At the climax of the Battle of Mount Hyjal, Malfurion blew the horn once more. Thousands of ancestral spirits answered and swarmed Archimonde, destroying the demon lord at the foot of the World Tree, though the power unleashed left Nordrassil wounded."],tr:["Cenarius \xf6ld\xfckten sonra borusu, kadim muhaf\u0131zlar\u0131n g\xf6zetiminde Moonglade\u2019de kald\u0131. Yanan Lejyon \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019ta geri d\xf6nd\xfc\u011f\xfcnde rahibe Tyrande Whisperwind boruyu bulup Malfurion Stormrage\u2019i uzun r\xfcyas\u0131ndan uyand\u0131rd\u0131. Malfurion da boruyu \xe7alarak uyuyan Talon ve Claw Druid\u2019lerini aya\u011fa kald\u0131rd\u0131.","Mount Hyjal Sava\u015f\u0131\u2019n\u0131n doruk an\u0131nda Malfurion boruyu bir kez daha \xe7ald\u0131. \xc7a\u011fr\u0131ya binlerce ata ruhu kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131k verdi ve Archimonde\u2019un \xfczerine \xe7ullanarak iblis lordunu D\xfcnya A\u011fac\u0131\u2019n\u0131n ete\u011finde yok etti; a\xe7\u0131\u011fa \xe7\u0131kan g\xfc\xe7 Nordrassil\u2019i de yaralad\u0131."]},era:'third-war',order:10,links:{raceIds:['night-elf'],classIds:['druid'],zoneIds:['moonglade'],instanceIds:['hyjal-summit'],loreIds:['term:nordrassil','chapter:battle-for-mount-hyjal']},image:'icon:inv_misc_horn_01',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Horn of Cenarius'),(0,n.wiki)('Battle of Mount Hyjal')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'sulfuras',title:{en:"Sulfuras, Hand of Ragnaros",tr:"Sulfuras, Ragnaros\u2019un Eli (Hand of Ragnaros)"},summary:{en:"The Firelord's burning hammer, and the smaller copy that master blacksmiths learned to forge in its image.",tr:"Ate\u015f Lordu\u2019nun alevli \xe7ekici ve usta demircilerin onun suretinde d\xf6vmeyi \xf6\u011frendi\u011fi k\xfc\xe7\xfck kopyas\u0131."},body:{en:["Sulfuras is the colossal hammer of Ragnaros, a mass of flaming red elementium the Firelord never lets go of. In the elemental wars of the distant past he struck down Thunderaan, Prince of Air, with it. Since Thaurissan\u2019s summoning, Ragnaros has ruled the Molten Core beneath Blackrock Mountain with the hammer in hand.","The true weapon is far too vast for mortal hands, but its likeness can be made. In the original game, a master blacksmith earned the plans for a Sulfuron Hammer from Lokhtos Darkbargainer of the Thorium Brotherhood in Blackrock Depths, then joined it with the rare Eye of Sulfuras taken from Ragnaros himself, creating a mortal-sized Hand of Ragnaros."],tr:["Sulfuras, Ragnaros\u2019un devasa \xe7ekicidir; Ate\u015f Lordu\u2019nun elinden hi\xe7 b\u0131rakmad\u0131\u011f\u0131 alevli k\u0131z\u0131l bir elementium k\xfctlesi. Uzak ge\xe7mi\u015fteki element sava\u015flar\u0131nda Ragnaros, Hava Prensi Thunderaan\u2019\u0131 bu \xe7eki\xe7le yere serdi. Thaurissan onu d\xfcnyaya \xe7a\u011f\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131ndan beri Ragnaros, Blackrock Da\u011f\u0131\u2019n\u0131n alt\u0131ndaki Molten Core\u2019da \xe7ekici elinde h\xfck\xfcm s\xfcr\xfcyor.","Ger\xe7ek silah \xf6l\xfcml\xfc eller i\xe7in fazlas\u0131yla b\xfcy\xfckt\xfcr, ama bir benzeri yap\u0131labilir. Orijinal oyunda usta bir demirci, Blackrock Depths\u2019teki Thorium Brotherhood temsilcisi Lokhtos Darkbargainer\u2019dan Sulfuron Hammer plan\u0131n\u0131 kazan\u0131r, sonra onu Ragnaros\u2019tan d\xfc\u015fen nadir Eye of Sulfuras ile birle\u015ftirerek \xf6l\xfcml\xfc boyutlarda bir Ragnaros\u2019un Eli yarat\u0131rd\u0131."]},era:'classic',order:11,links:{zoneIds:['burning-steppes','searing-gorge'],instanceIds:['blackrock-depths'],itemIds:[17182,17204],loreIds:['term:elemental-lords','item:thunderfury','chapter:fire-beneath-blackrock']},image:'icon:inv_hammer_unique_sulfuras',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Sulfuras'),(0,n.wiki)('Sulfuras, Hand of Ragnaros')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'thunderfury',title:{en:"Thunderfury, Blessed Blade of the Windseeker",tr:"Thunderfury, R\xfczg\xe2r Aray\u0131c\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n Kutsanm\u0131\u015f K\u0131l\u0131c\u0131"},summary:{en:"A sword forged around the last essence of Thunderaan, Prince of Air, whom Ragnaros had imprisoned.",tr:"Ragnaros\u2019un hapsetti\u011fi Hava Prensi Thunderaan\u2019\u0131n son \xf6z\xfcn\xfcn etraf\u0131nda d\xf6v\xfclen k\u0131l\u0131\xe7."},body:{en:["In an ancient war between fire and air, Ragnaros and his lieutenants Garr and Baron Geddon defeated Thunderaan, Prince of Air. The Firelord fed on his essence but could not devour all of it, so he sealed the remainder in a talisman, broke it in two, and gave one half to each lieutenant: the Bindings of the Windseeker.","In the original game, raiders took both halves from Garr and Geddon in the Molten Core and brought them to Highlord Demitrian in Silithus. With the Firelord\u2019s own essence and bars of enchanted elementium, the bindings summoned the weakened Prince; once he was defeated, Demitrian forged his remaining power into Thunderfury, a blade that crackles with living storm."],tr:["Ate\u015f ile hava aras\u0131ndaki kadim bir sava\u015fta Ragnaros ve komutanlar\u0131 Garr ile Baron Geddon, Hava Prensi Thunderaan\u2019\u0131 yendi. Ate\u015f Lordu onun \xf6z\xfcyle beslendi ama tamam\u0131n\u0131 yutamad\u0131; kalan\u0131n\u0131 bir t\u0131ls\u0131ma m\xfch\xfcrledi, t\u0131ls\u0131m\u0131 ikiye b\xf6ld\xfc ve her yar\u0131y\u0131 bir komutan\u0131na verdi: Bindings of the Windseeker.","Orijinal oyunda bask\u0131nc\u0131lar iki yar\u0131y\u0131 Molten Core\u2019da Garr ile Geddon\u2019dan al\u0131p Silithus\u2019taki Highlord Demitrian\u2019a g\xf6t\xfcr\xfcrd\xfc. Ate\u015f Lordu\u2019nun kendi \xf6z\xfc ve b\xfcy\xfcl\xfc elementium k\xfcl\xe7eleriyle prangalar zay\u0131flam\u0131\u015f Prensi \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131rd\u0131; Prens yenildi\u011finde Demitrian onun kalan g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc, canl\u0131 bir f\u0131rt\u0131nayla \xe7at\u0131rdayan Thunderfury k\u0131l\u0131c\u0131na d\xf6vd\xfc."]},era:'classic',order:12,links:{zoneIds:['silithus'],itemIds:[19019,18563,18564],loreIds:['item:sulfuras','term:elemental-lords','term:skywall']},image:'icon:inv_sword_39',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Thunderfury, Blessed Blade of the Windseeker'),(0,n.wiki)('Thunderaan')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'seal-of-ascension',title:{en:"Seal of Ascension",tr:"Y\xfckseli\u015f M\xfchr\xfc (Seal of Ascension)"},summary:{en:"A ring forged in black dragonfire that unlocked the upper citadel of Blackrock Spire.",tr:"Kara ejderha ate\u015finde d\xf6v\xfclen ve Blackrock Spire\u2019\u0131n \xfcst kalesinin kap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 a\xe7an y\xfcz\xfck."},body:{en:["The upper halls of Blackrock Spire, where Rend Blackhand and the black dragonflight held court, were sealed against intruders. In the lower spire, a disguised stranger called Vaelan, in truth the red dragon Vaelastrasz sworn to hunt Nefarian, taught adventurers to make a key: an unadorned seal set with three gems taken from the Spire\u2019s Smolderthorn, Spirestone and Bloodaxe commanders.","The seal then had to be forged in black dragonfire. Heroes travelled to the Wyrmbog in Dustwallow Marsh and bent the drake Emberstrife to breathe on it. The finished ring opened the upper citadel, and in the fight against Rend it could call a projection of Vaelastrasz to the heroes\u2019 side."],tr:["Rend Blackhand ile kara ejderha soyunun h\xfck\xfcm s\xfcrd\xfc\u011f\xfc Blackrock Spire\u2019\u0131n \xfcst salonlar\u0131 davetsiz misafirlere kapal\u0131yd\u0131. Alt kulede Vaelan adl\u0131 k\u0131l\u0131k de\u011fi\u015ftirmi\u015f bir yabanc\u0131, asl\u0131nda Nefarian\u2019\u0131 avlamaya ant i\xe7mi\u015f k\u0131z\u0131l ejderha Vaelastrasz, macerac\u0131lara bir anahtar yapmay\u0131 \xf6\u011fretti: Spire\u2019\u0131n Smolderthorn, Spirestone ve Bloodaxe komutanlar\u0131ndan al\u0131nan \xfc\xe7 m\xfccevherle s\xfcslenecek yal\u0131n bir m\xfch\xfcr.","M\xfchr\xfcn ard\u0131ndan kara ejderha ate\u015finde d\xf6v\xfclmesi gerekiyordu. Kahramanlar Dustwallow Marsh\u2019taki Wyrmbog\u2019a gidip ejder Emberstrife\u2019\u0131 m\xfchr\xfcn \xfczerine ate\u015f p\xfcsk\xfcrtmeye zorlad\u0131. Tamamlanan y\xfcz\xfck \xfcst kaleyi a\xe7ard\u0131; Rend\u2019e kar\u015f\u0131 sava\u015fta Vaelastrasz\u2019\u0131n bir yans\u0131mas\u0131n\u0131 da kahramanlar\u0131n yan\u0131na \xe7a\u011f\u0131rabilirdi."]},era:'classic',order:13,links:{zoneIds:['dustwallow-marsh','burning-steppes'],instanceIds:['lower-blackrock-spire'],itemIds:[12219,12323,12324],loreIds:['item:drakefire-amulet','chapter:fire-beneath-blackrock']},image:'icon:inv_jewelry_ring_01',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Seal of Ascension'),(0,n.wiki)('Vaelastrasz')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'drakefire-amulet',title:{en:"Drakefire Amulet",tr:"Ejder Ate\u015fi Muskas\u0131 (Drakefire Amulet)"},summary:{en:"Onyxia's broken charm, remade with a black dragon's blood into the key to her own lair.",tr:"Onyxia\u2019n\u0131n k\u0131r\u0131lan muskas\u0131; bir kara ejderhan\u0131n kan\u0131yla onun inine a\xe7\u0131lan anahtara d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfcld\xfc."},body:{en:["Disguised as Lady Katrana Prestor, Onyxia worked her way into Stormwind\u2019s court with a pendant called the Dragon\u2019s Eye. It did not command minds outright, yet it stirred hidden desires and turned suspicion away from her. When Marshal Windsor exposed the masquerade, the pendant shattered, and the blue dragon Haleh remade its pieces, with the blood of General Drakkisath, into the Drakefire Amulet.","Horde heroes reach the same amulet by another road, through Rexxar and the trials of the ancient drake Emberstrife. Every raider who enters Onyxia\u2019s Lair must carry it, and Forever keeps this attunement as a separate questline for each faction."],tr:["Lady Katrana Prestor k\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131na giren Onyxia, Dragon\u2019s Eye (Ejderha G\xf6z\xfc) adl\u0131 bir kolyeyle Stormwind saray\u0131na s\u0131zd\u0131. Kolye zihinleri do\u011frudan y\xf6netmiyordu; ama gizli arzular\u0131 k\u0131\u015fk\u0131rt\u0131yor, \u015f\xfcpheleri ondan uzakla\u015ft\u0131r\u0131yordu. Marshal Windsor maskaral\u0131\u011f\u0131 a\xe7\u0131\u011fa \xe7\u0131kard\u0131\u011f\u0131nda kolye par\xe7aland\u0131; mavi ejderha Haleh par\xe7alar\u0131 General Drakkisath\u2019\u0131n kan\u0131yla Drakefire Amulet\u2019e d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc.","Horde kahramanlar\u0131 ayn\u0131 muskaya ba\u015fka bir yoldan, Rexxar ve kadim ejder Emberstrife\u2019\u0131n s\u0131navlar\u0131yla ula\u015f\u0131r. Onyxia\u2019s Lair\u2019e giren her bask\u0131nc\u0131 bu muskay\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131mak zorundad\u0131r; Forever bu eri\u015fim g\xf6revini her taraf i\xe7in ayr\u0131 bir g\xf6rev zinciri olarak korur."]},era:'classic',order:14,links:{factionIds:['alliance','horde'],zoneIds:['dustwallow-marsh','burning-steppes','winterspring'],instanceIds:['onyxias-lair'],itemIds:[16309],loreIds:['item:head-of-onyxia','chapter:stormwind-in-shadow']},image:'icon:inv_jewelry_talisman_11',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Drakefire Amulet'),n.FOREVER.raids],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'head-of-onyxia',title:{en:"Head of Onyxia",tr:"Onyxia\u2019n\u0131n Kellesi (Head of Onyxia)"},summary:{en:"Proof of the Brood Mother's death, raised over the gates of Stormwind or Orgrimmar as a rallying banner.",tr:"Kulu\xe7ka Anas\u0131\u2019n\u0131n \xf6l\xfcm\xfcn\xfcn kan\u0131t\u0131; Stormwind ya da Orgrimmar kap\u0131lar\u0131na bir zafer sanca\u011f\u0131 gibi as\u0131ld\u0131."},body:{en:["Onyxia, daughter of Deathwing and younger sister of Nefarian, guards her brood in a cavern of Dustwallow Marsh while scheming to bend the mortal kingdoms of Azeroth to her will. Defeating her ended one of the black dragonflight\u2019s longest deceptions.","In the original game, her head was carried home as a trophy: Alliance champions presented it in Stormwind, Horde champions to Thrall in Orgrimmar. Raised over the city gates, it granted the Rallying Cry of the Dragonslayer to everyone in the city, and the whole capital celebrated the kill."],tr:["Deathwing\u2019in k\u0131z\u0131 ve Nefarian\u2019\u0131n k\xfc\xe7\xfck k\u0131z karde\u015fi Onyxia, Dustwallow Marsh\u2019taki bir ma\u011farada kulu\xe7kas\u0131n\u0131 korurken Azeroth\u2019un \xf6l\xfcml\xfc krall\u0131klar\u0131n\u0131 kendi iste\u011fine boyun e\u011fdirmenin yollar\u0131n\u0131 arar. Onu yenmek, kara ejderha soyunun en uzun s\xfcren aldatmacalar\u0131ndan birini sona erdirdi.","Orijinal oyunda kellesi bir ganimet olarak eve ta\u015f\u0131n\u0131rd\u0131: \u0130ttifak \u015fampiyonlar\u0131 onu Stormwind\u2019e, Horde \u015fampiyonlar\u0131 Orgrimmar\u2019da Thrall\u2019a sunard\u0131. \u015eehir kap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n \xfczerine as\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda \u015fehirdeki herkese Rallying Cry of the Dragonslayer kutsamas\u0131n\u0131 verir, b\xfct\xfcn ba\u015fkent zaferi kutlard\u0131."]},era:'classic',order:15,links:{factionIds:['alliance','horde'],zoneIds:['dustwallow-marsh','elwynn-forest','durotar'],instanceIds:['onyxias-lair'],itemIds:[18422,18423],loreIds:['item:drakefire-amulet','item:quel-serrar']},image:'icon:inv_misc_head_dragon_01',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Head of Onyxia (Classic)'),n.FOREVER.raids],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'quel-serrar',title:{en:"Quel'Serrar",tr:"Quel'Serrar"},summary:{en:"An ancient night elf blade kept by the Shen'dralar and finished only in a dragon's breath.",tr:"Shen'dralar\u2019\u0131n saklad\u0131\u011f\u0131 kadim gece elfi k\u0131l\u0131c\u0131; ancak bir ejderhan\u0131n nefesiyle tamamlan\u0131r."},body:{en:["Quel'Serrar is one of the prismatic blades that night elf smiths forged long ago with the aid of the dragonflights; its twin, Quel'Delar, was given to the high elves. For thousands of years the Shen'dralar of Eldre'Thalas kept it, waiting for a wielder strong enough to wake it.","In the original game, a warrior or paladin who found an old compendium on dragon slaying brought it to Lorekeeper Lydros in the library of Dire Maul and received an unfired blade. Heated by Onyxia\u2019s deep breath and plunged into the slain dragon, the steel became Quel'Serrar once it was returned to Lydros."],tr:["Quel'Serrar, gece elfi demircilerin ejderha soylar\u0131n\u0131n yard\u0131m\u0131yla \xe7ok eskiden d\xf6vd\xfc\u011f\xfc prizmatik k\u0131l\u0131\xe7lardan biridir; ikizi Quel'Delar y\xfcksek elflere verildi. Binlerce y\u0131l boyunca Eldre'Thalas\u2019\u0131n Shen'dralar\u2019\u0131 k\u0131l\u0131c\u0131 saklad\u0131 ve onu uyand\u0131racak kadar g\xfc\xe7l\xfc bir sava\u015f\xe7\u0131y\u0131 bekledi.","Orijinal oyunda ejderha avc\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131 \xfczerine eski bir derlemeyi bulan Warrior ya da Paladin, onu Dire Maul k\xfct\xfcphanesindeki Lorekeeper Lydros\u2019a g\xf6t\xfcr\xfcr ve hen\xfcz ate\u015fe girmemi\u015f bir k\u0131l\u0131\xe7 al\u0131rd\u0131. Onyxia\u2019n\u0131n derin nefesiyle k\u0131zd\u0131r\u0131l\u0131p \xf6ld\xfcr\xfclen ejderhaya saplanan \xe7elik, Lydros\u2019a geri g\xf6t\xfcr\xfcld\xfc\u011f\xfcnde Quel'Serrar olurdu."]},era:'classic',order:16,links:{classIds:['warrior','paladin'],raceIds:['night-elf'],zoneIds:['feralas'],instanceIds:['capital-gardens','onyxias-lair'],loreIds:['term:highborne','item:head-of-onyxia']},image:'icon:inv_sword_01',sources:[(0,n.wiki)("Quel'Serrar")],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'rhokdelar',title:{en:"Rhok'delar and Lok'delar",tr:"Rhok'delar ve Lok'delar"},summary:{en:"A living longbow and stave shaped by the corrupted Ancients of Felwood for the hunter who avenged them.",tr:"Felwood\u2019un yozla\u015fm\u0131\u015f Ancient\u2019lar\u0131n\u0131n, \xf6\xe7lerini alan Hunter i\xe7in bi\xe7imlendirdi\u011fi canl\u0131 uzun yay ve asa."},body:{en:["When the Burning Legion swept across Kalimdor, it poisoned the valley that became Felwood. Its mightiest Ancients withered into petrified husks, yet their spirits lingered. A leaf from one of them, Vartrus, ended up in the Firelord\u2019s treasure in the Molten Core.","In the original game, a hunter who returned the leaf to Vartrus was sent to hunt four agents of the Legion alone, without even a pet. In return the Ancients crafted Rhok'delar, a longbow that sprouts blossoms of its own accord, and its companion Lok'delar, a stave that glows with the power of nature."],tr:["Yanan Lejyon Kalimdor\u2019u kas\u0131p kavurdu\u011funda, sonradan Felwood ad\u0131n\u0131 alacak vadiyi zehirledi. Vadinin en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc Ancient\u2019lar\u0131 ta\u015fla\u015fm\u0131\u015f kabuklara d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc, ama ruhlar\u0131 orada kald\u0131. Bunlardan biri olan Vartrus\u2019un bir yapra\u011f\u0131, Ate\u015f Lordu\u2019nun Molten Core\u2019daki hazinesine d\xfc\u015ft\xfc.","Orijinal oyunda yapra\u011f\u0131 Vartrus\u2019a geri getiren Hunter, d\xf6rt Lejyon ajan\u0131n\u0131 tek ba\u015f\u0131na, evcil hayvan\u0131 bile olmadan avlamaya g\xf6nderilirdi. Kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131nda Ancient\u2019lar kendili\u011finden \xe7i\xe7ek a\xe7an uzun yay Rhok'delar\u2019\u0131 ve do\u011fan\u0131n g\xfcc\xfcyle parlayan yolda\u015f\u0131 Lok'delar asas\u0131n\u0131 yarat\u0131rd\u0131."]},era:'classic',order:17,links:{classIds:['hunter'],zoneIds:['felwood'],itemIds:[18713,18715],loreIds:['term:burning-legion','term:fel']},image:'icon:inv_weapon_bow_01',sources:[(0,n.wiki)("Rhok'delar, Longbow of the Ancient Keepers"),(0,n.wiki)("Lok'delar, Stave of the Ancient Keepers"),(0,n.wiki)('Vartrus the Ancient')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'taelans-hammer',title:{en:"Taelan's Hammer",tr:"Taelan\u2019\u0131n \xc7ekici (Taelan's Hammer)"},summary:{en:"A child's toy hammer that helped Tirion Fordring reach the son the Scarlet Crusade had taken from him.",tr:"Tirion Fordring\u2019in, Scarlet Crusade\u2019in elinden ald\u0131\u011f\u0131 o\u011fluna ula\u015fmas\u0131n\u0131 sa\u011flayan oyuncak bir \xe7eki\xe7."},body:{en:["On his seventh birthday, young Taelan received a miniature war hammer from his father, Tirion Fordring, a copy of Tirion\u2019s own. After Tirion was exiled for defending the orc Eitrigg, Taelan\u2019s mother told the boy his father had died and took him to a false grave at the Undercroft in the Eastern Plaguelands, where he buried the hammer and the memory with it.","Years later Taelan rose to become Highlord of the Scarlet Crusade in Hearthglen. In the original game, adventurers recovered the hammer for the ageing Tirion and helped Taelan see what the Crusade had become. As he fled Hearthglen, Grand Inquisitor Isillien cut him down before his father\u2019s eyes; Tirion slew Isillien and vowed to reforge the Silver Hand."],tr:["Yedinci do\u011fum g\xfcn\xfcnde k\xfc\xe7\xfck Taelan, babas\u0131 Tirion Fordring\u2019den onun kendi \xe7ekicinin minyat\xfcr bir kopyas\u0131 olan oyuncak bir sava\u015f \xe7ekici ald\u0131. Tirion ork Eitrigg\u2019i savundu\u011fu i\xe7in s\xfcrg\xfcn edildikten sonra Taelan\u2019\u0131n annesi o\u011fluna babas\u0131n\u0131n \xf6ld\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc s\xf6yledi ve onu Eastern Plaguelands b\xf6lgesindeki Undercroft\u2019ta sahte bir mezara g\xf6t\xfcrd\xfc; Taelan \xe7ekici, babas\u0131n\u0131n hat\u0131ras\u0131yla birlikte oraya g\xf6md\xfc.","Y\u0131llar sonra Taelan, Hearthglen\u2019de Scarlet Crusade\u2019in Y\xfcce Lordu oldu. Orijinal oyunda macerac\u0131lar \xe7ekici ya\u015flanan Tirion i\xe7in bulup getirir ve Taelan\u2019\u0131n Crusade\u2019in neye d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc g\xf6rmesine yard\u0131m ederdi. Taelan Hearthglen\u2019den ka\xe7arken Ba\u015f Engizisyoncu Isillien onu babas\u0131n\u0131n g\xf6zleri \xf6n\xfcnde \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc; Tirion da Isillien\u2019i \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc ve G\xfcm\xfc\u015f El\u2019i yeniden kuraca\u011f\u0131na ant i\xe7ti."]},era:'classic',order:18,links:{classIds:['paladin'],raceIds:['human'],zoneIds:['eastern-plaguelands','western-plaguelands'],itemIds:[14613],loreIds:['term:scarlet-crusade','term:silver-hand']},image:'icon:inv_hammer_01',sources:[(0,n.wiki)("Taelan's Hammer"),(0,n.wiki)('Taelan Fordring'),(0,n.wiki)('In Dreams')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'heart-of-hakkar',title:{en:"Heart of Hakkar",tr:"Hakkar\u2019\u0131n Y\xfcre\u011fi (Heart of Hakkar)"},summary:{en:"The still-burning heart of the Blood God, carried to the Zandalari after Hakkar was slain in Zul'Gurub.",tr:"Kan Tanr\u0131s\u0131\u2019n\u0131n h\xe2l\xe2 yanan y\xfcre\u011fi; Hakkar Zul'Gurub\u2019da \xf6ld\xfcr\xfcld\xfckten sonra Zandalarilere g\xf6t\xfcr\xfcld\xfc."},body:{en:["About fifteen centuries before the Dark Portal, the starving Gurubashi trolls turned to Hakkar the Soulflayer, a loa of blood. He gave them power and an empire, then demanded ever more lives until the tribes rose against him and exiled his Atal'ai priests. When the priests raised a temple to bring him back, Ysera smashed it beneath the marshes of the Swamp of Sorrows.","In the original game, the Hakkari priests finally drew the Soulflayer into Zul'Gurub. Heroes rallied by the Zandalar tribe slew him there and carried his still-glowing heart to Molthor on Yojamba Isle, whose rite blessed everyone on the isle and in Booty Bay with the Spirit of Zandalar."],tr:["Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten yakla\u015f\u0131k on be\u015f y\xfczy\u0131l \xf6nce a\xe7 kalan Gurubashi trolleri, kan loas\u0131 Hakkar the Soulflayer\u2019a y\xf6neldi. Hakkar onlara g\xfc\xe7 ve bir imparatorluk verdi, sonra hep daha fazla can istedi; sonunda kabileler ona kar\u015f\u0131 ayakland\u0131 ve Atal'ai Priest\u2019lerini s\xfcrd\xfc. Priest\u2019ler onu geri getirmek i\xe7in bir tap\u0131nak dikti\u011finde Ysera tap\u0131na\u011f\u0131 Swamp of Sorrows batakl\u0131klar\u0131n\u0131n alt\u0131na g\xf6md\xfc.","Orijinal oyunda Hakkari Priest\u2019leri sonunda Soulflayer\u2019\u0131 Zul'Gurub\u2019a \xe7ekmeyi ba\u015fard\u0131. Zandalar kabilesinin toplad\u0131\u011f\u0131 kahramanlar onu orada \xf6ld\xfcr\xfcp h\xe2l\xe2 parlayan y\xfcre\u011fini Yojamba Isle\u2019daki Molthor\u2019a g\xf6t\xfcrd\xfc; Molthor\u2019un ayini adadaki ve Booty Bay\u2019deki herkesi Spirit of Zandalar ile kutsad\u0131."]},era:'classic',order:19,links:{raceIds:['troll'],zoneIds:['stranglethorn-vale','swamp-of-sorrows'],instanceIds:['temple-of-atalhakkar'],itemIds:[19802],loreIds:['term:loa','term:emerald-dream']},image:'icon:inv_misc_gem_bloodstone_02',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Heart of Hakkar'),(0,n.wiki)('The Heart of Hakkar'),(0,n.wiki)('Hakkar the Soulflayer')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'item',slug:'phylactery-of-kelthuzad',title:{en:"The Phylactery of Kel'Thuzad",tr:"Kel'Thuzad\u2019\u0131n Filakteri (Phylactery of Kel'Thuzad)"},summary:{en:"The vessel that holds the archlich's soul, taken from Naxxramas after his defeat.",tr:"Ar\u015flich\u2019in ruhunu bar\u0131nd\u0131ran kap; yenilgisinden sonra Naxxramas\u2019tan al\u0131nd\u0131."},body:{en:["Kel'Thuzad, once an archmage of the Kirin Tor, founded the Cult of the Damned and spread the plague for the Lich King. Slain by Arthas and later carried to the Sunwell to be reborn as a lich, he came to rule the Scourge in Lordaeron from the floating necropolis of Naxxramas.","A lich endures as long as the vessel holding its soul survives. In the original game, raiders who defeated Kel'Thuzad recovered his phylactery and handed it to the Argent Dawn for safekeeping. Later stories revealed that one of its priests, Father Inigo Montoy, betrayed that trust and carried it to Northrend, giving the archlich time to return."],tr:["Bir zamanlar Kirin Tor\u2019un ba\u015fb\xfcy\xfcc\xfclerinden olan Kel'Thuzad, Cult of the Damned\u2019i kurdu ve vebay\u0131 Lich King ad\u0131na yayd\u0131. Arthas taraf\u0131ndan \xf6ld\xfcr\xfcld\xfc, bir lich olarak yeniden do\u011fmak \xfczere Sunwell\u2019e ta\u015f\u0131nd\u0131 ve sonunda Lordaeron\u2019daki Scourge\u2019u havada s\xfcz\xfclen Naxxramas nekropol\xfcnden y\xf6netmeye ba\u015flad\u0131.","Bir lich, ruhunu bar\u0131nd\u0131ran kap var olduk\xe7a ya\u015far. Orijinal oyunda Kel'Thuzad\u2019\u0131 yenen bask\u0131nc\u0131lar filakterini ele ge\xe7irip saklamas\u0131 i\xe7in Argent Dawn\u2019a teslim ederdi. Sonraki hik\xe2yeler, tarikat\u0131n Priest\u2019lerinden Father Inigo Montoy\u2019un bu g\xfcvene ihanet edip filakteri Northrend\u2019e g\xf6t\xfcrd\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc ve ar\u015fliche geri d\xf6nmek i\xe7in zaman kazand\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ortaya \xe7\u0131kard\u0131."]},era:'classic',order:20,links:{zoneIds:['eastern-plaguelands'],itemIds:[22520],loreIds:['term:cult-of-the-damned','term:argent-dawn','term:scourge']},image:'icon:inv_misc_urn_01',sources:[(0,n.wiki)("The Phylactery of Kel'Thuzad")],basis:'established'})]},869,[866]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"raceLore",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});var n=r(d[0]);const l=(0,n.datasetSource)('wiki-class-by-race'),o=[{en:"Where the Skyborne came from and how their two orders formed are not described in the sources this guide uses (the Zephras Isle and Forever wiki pages, racial pages and Blizzard posts).",tr:'Skyborne\u2019un nereden geldi\u011fi ve iki d\xfczeninin nas\u0131l olu\u015ftu\u011fu, bu rehberin kulland\u0131\u011f\u0131 kaynaklarda (Zephras Isle ve Forever wiki sayfalar\u0131, \u0131rk yetene\u011fi sayfalar\u0131 ve Blizzard yaz\u0131lar\u0131) anlat\u0131lm\u0131yor.',de:'Woher die Skyborne kamen und wie ihre beiden Orden entstanden, beschreiben die Quellen dieses Leitfadens nicht (die Wiki-Seiten zu Zephras Isle und Forever, die Seiten zu den Volksf\xe4higkeiten und Blizzard-Beitr\xe4ge).',fr:'Les sources de ce guide (les pages wiki de Zephras Isle et de Forever, les pages des techniques raciales et les articles de Blizzard) ne d\xe9crivent ni l\u2019origine des Skyborne ni la formation de leurs deux ordres.',es:'Las fuentes que usa esta gu\xeda (las p\xe1ginas wiki de Zephras Isle y de Forever, las de las habilidades raciales y los art\xedculos de Blizzard) no describen de d\xf3nde vienen los Skyborne ni c\xf3mo se formaron sus dos \xf3rdenes.','pt-BR':'As fontes que este guia usa (as p\xe1ginas wiki de Zephras Isle e de Forever, as p\xe1ginas de habilidades raciais e as publica\xe7\xf5es da Blizzard) n\xe3o descrevem de onde vieram os Skyborne nem como suas duas ordens se formaram.',it:'Le fonti usate da questa guida (le pagine wiki di Zephras Isle e di Forever, le pagine delle abilit\xe0 razziali e gli articoli di Blizzard) non descrivono da dove vengano gli Skyborne n\xe9 come si siano formati i loro due ordini.',ru:'\u041e\u0442\u043a\u0443\u0434\u0430 \u043f\u0440\u0438\u0448\u043b\u0438 Skyborne \u0438 \u043a\u0430\u043a \u0441\u043b\u043e\u0436\u0438\u043b\u0438\u0441\u044c \u0434\u0432\u0430 \u0438\u0445 \u043e\u0440\u0434\u0435\u043d\u0430, \u0438\u0441\u0442\u043e\u0447\u043d\u0438\u043a\u0438 \u044d\u0442\u043e\u0433\u043e \u043f\u0443\u0442\u0435\u0432\u043e\u0434\u0438\u0442\u0435\u043b\u044f (\u0432\u0438\u043a\u0438-\u0441\u0442\u0440\u0430\u043d\u0438\u0446\u044b Zephras Isle \u0438 Forever, \u0441\u0442\u0440\u0430\u043d\u0438\u0446\u044b \u0440\u0430\u0441\u043e\u0432\u044b\u0445 \u0441\u043f\u043e\u0441\u043e\u0431\u043d\u043e\u0441\u0442\u0435\u0439 \u0438 \u043f\u0443\u0431\u043b\u0438\u043a\u0430\u0446\u0438\u0438 Blizzard) \u043d\u0435 \u043e\u043f\u0438\u0441\u044b\u0432\u0430\u044e\u0442.',ko:'Skyborne\uc774 \uc5b4\ub514\uc5d0\uc11c \uc654\ub294\uc9c0, \uadf8\ub9ac\uace0 \ub450 \ubd84\ud30c\uac00 \uc5b4\ub5bb\uac8c \uc0dd\uaca8\ub0ac\ub294\uc9c0\ub294 \uc774 \uc548\ub0b4\uc11c\uac00 \uc4f0\ub294 \uc790\ub8cc(Zephras Isle\uacfc Forever \uc704\ud0a4 \ubb38\uc11c, \uc885\uc871 \ud2b9\uc131 \ubb38\uc11c, \ube14\ub9ac\uc790\ub4dc \uac8c\uc2dc\ubb3c)\uc5d0 \ub098\uc624\uc9c0 \uc54a\ub294\ub2e4.','zh-CN':'Skyborne\u4ece\u4f55\u800c\u6765\u3001\u4ed6\u4eec\u7684\u4e24\u4e2a\u6d3e\u7cfb\u5982\u4f55\u5f62\u6210\uff0c\u672c\u6307\u5357\u6240\u7528\u7684\u8d44\u6599\uff08Zephras Isle\u548cForever\u7684\u7ef4\u57fa\u9875\u9762\u3001\u79cd\u65cf\u7279\u957f\u9875\u9762\u4ee5\u53ca\u66b4\u96ea\u6587\u7ae0\uff09\u5747\u672a\u63cf\u8ff0\u3002','zh-TW':'Skyborne\u5f9e\u4f55\u800c\u4f86\u3001\u4ed6\u5011\u7684\u5169\u500b\u6d3e\u7cfb\u5982\u4f55\u5f62\u6210\uff0c\u672c\u6307\u5357\u6240\u4f7f\u7528\u7684\u8cc7\u6599\uff08Zephras Isle\u548cForever\u7684\u7dad\u57fa\u9801\u9762\u3001\u7a2e\u65cf\u7279\u9577\u9801\u9762\u4ee5\u53ca\u66b4\u96ea\u6587\u7ae0\uff09\u7686\u672a\u63cf\u8ff0\u3002'},{en:"Why Zephras Isle's air elementals vanished, and how the Skyborne came to join the Alliance and the Horde, is not explained there either.",tr:'Zephras Isle\u2019\u0131n hava elementallerinin neden kayboldu\u011fu ve Skyborne\u2019un \u0130ttifak\u2019a ve Horde\u2019a nas\u0131l kat\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131 da orada a\xe7\u0131klanm\u0131yor.',de:'Warum die Luftelementare von Zephras Isle verschwanden und wie die Skyborne zur Allianz und zur Horde kamen, wird dort ebenfalls nicht erkl\xe4rt.',fr:'Elles n\u2019expliquent pas non plus pourquoi les \xe9l\xe9mentaires d\u2019air de Zephras Isle ont disparu, ni comment les Skyborne ont rejoint l\u2019Alliance et la Horde.',es:'Tampoco explican por qu\xe9 desaparecieron los elementales de aire de Zephras Isle ni c\xf3mo llegaron los Skyborne a unirse a la Alianza y a la Horda.','pt-BR':'Elas tamb\xe9m n\xe3o explicam por que os elementais do ar de Zephras Isle desapareceram, nem como os Skyborne passaram a se juntar \xe0 Alian\xe7a e \xe0 Horda.',it:'Non spiegano nemmeno perch\xe9 gli elementali dell\u2019aria di Zephras Isle siano scomparsi, n\xe9 come gli Skyborne si siano uniti all\u2019Alleanza e all\u2019Orda.',ru:'\u041f\u043e\u0447\u0435\u043c\u0443 \u0438\u0441\u0447\u0435\u0437\u043b\u0438 \u0432\u043e\u0437\u0434\u0443\u0448\u043d\u044b\u0435 \u044d\u043b\u0435\u043c\u0435\u043d\u0442\u0430\u043b\u0438 Zephras Isle \u0438 \u043a\u0430\u043a Skyborne \u043e\u043a\u0430\u0437\u0430\u043b\u0438\u0441\u044c \u0432 \u0410\u043b\u044c\u044f\u043d\u0441\u0435 \u0438 \u041e\u0440\u0434\u0435, \u0442\u0430\u043c \u0442\u043e\u0436\u0435 \u043d\u0435 \u043e\u0431\u044a\u044f\u0441\u043d\u044f\u0435\u0442\u0441\u044f.',ko:'Zephras Isle\uc758 \ubc14\ub78c \uc815\ub839\ub4e4\uc774 \uc65c \uc0ac\ub77c\uc84c\ub294\uc9c0, \uadf8\ub9ac\uace0 Skyborne\uc774 \uc5b4\ub5bb\uac8c \uc5bc\ub77c\uc774\uc5b8\uc2a4\uc640 \ud638\ub4dc\uc5d0 \ud569\ub958\ud558\uac8c \ub418\uc5c8\ub294\uc9c0\ub3c4 \uadf8\uacf3\uc5d0\uc11c \uc124\uba85\ud558\uc9c0 \uc54a\ub294\ub2e4.','zh-CN':'Zephras Isle\u7684\u98ce\u5143\u7d20\u4e3a\u4f55\u6d88\u5931\uff0c\u4ee5\u53caSkyborne\u5982\u4f55\u52a0\u5165\u8054\u76df\u548c\u90e8\u843d\uff0c\u8fd9\u4e9b\u8d44\u6599\u540c\u6837\u6ca1\u6709\u89e3\u91ca\u3002','zh-TW':'Zephras Isle\u7684\u98a8\u5143\u7d20\u70ba\u4f55\u6d88\u5931\uff0c\u4ee5\u53caSkyborne\u5982\u4f55\u52a0\u5165\u806f\u76df\u548c\u90e8\u843d\uff0c\u9019\u4e9b\u8cc7\u6599\u540c\u6a23\u6c92\u6709\u89e3\u91cb\u3002'}],t=[(0,n.lore)({category:'race',slug:'human',subjectId:'human',order:1,era:'elder-kingdoms',title:{en:'Human',tr:'\u0130nsan'},summary:{en:"Heirs of Arathor and the backbone of the Alliance, humans have paid for every war in Azeroth's history and still rebuild.",tr:'Arathor\u2019un miras\xe7\u0131lar\u0131 ve \u0130ttifak\u2019\u0131n bel kemi\u011fi olan insanlar Azeroth tarihindeki her sava\u015f\u0131n bedelini \xf6dedi ve yine de yeniden in\u015fa ediyor.'},body:{en:['Humans descend from the tribes that King Thoradin united into Arathor nearly three thousand years before the Dark Portal. Arathor\u2019s heirs founded the seven human kingdoms, the elves taught their first magi, and their faith in the Holy Light later gave rise to the paladins. Humanity carried the Alliance through the First, Second and Third Wars, and paid dearly: Stormwind burned once, and Lordaeron fell to the Scourge.','In year 25 Stormwind is the heart of human power, rebuilt in white stone yet troubled by the Defias, the missing King Varian and a royal court under the spell of Lady Prestor. New humans begin at Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest. Forever lets humans become hunters, a calling the original game kept for other races.'],tr:['\u0130nsanlar, Kral Thoradin\u2019in Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten neredeyse \xfc\xe7 bin y\u0131l \xf6nce Arathor\u2019da birle\u015ftirdi\u011fi kabilelerin soyundan gelir. Arathor\u2019un varisleri yedi insan krall\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 kurdu, elfler ilk b\xfcy\xfcc\xfclerini e\u011fitti ve Kutsal I\u015f\u0131k\u2019a duyduklar\u0131 inan\xe7 daha sonra Paladin\u2019leri do\u011furdu. \u0130nsanl\u0131k \u0130ttifak\u2019\u0131 Birinci, \u0130kinci ve \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f boyunca ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131 ve bunun bedelini a\u011f\u0131r \xf6dedi: Stormwind bir kez yand\u0131, Lordaeron ise Scourge\u2019a d\xfc\u015ft\xfc.','25. y\u0131lda Stormwind insan g\xfcc\xfcn\xfcn kalbi; beyaz ta\u015fla yeniden in\u015fa edildi ama Defias, kay\u0131p Kral Varian ve Lady Prestor\u2019un b\xfcy\xfcs\xfc alt\u0131ndaki bir saray y\xfcz\xfcnden huzursuz. Yeni insanlar maceralar\u0131na Elwynn Forest\u2019taki Northshire Abbey\u2019de ba\u015flar. Forever insanlara, \xf6zg\xfcn oyunun ba\u015fka \u0131rklara ay\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131 Hunter yolunu da a\xe7\u0131yor.']},links:{raceIds:['human'],factionIds:['alliance'],classIds:['warrior','paladin','hunter','rogue','priest','mage','warlock'],zoneIds:['elwynn-forest','westfall','redridge-mountains','duskwood'],loreIds:['chapter:arathor-and-the-troll-wars','chapter:stormwind-in-shadow','term:holy-light','term:silver-hand']},image:'race:human',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Human'),(0,n.wiki)('Stormwind City'),l],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'race',slug:'gnome',subjectId:'gnome',order:2,era:'elder-kingdoms',title:{en:'Gnome',tr:'Gnom'},summary:{en:"Brilliant tinkerers whose ancestors were titan-forged machines, the gnomes have lost their city of Gnomeregan and live in exile in Ironforge.",tr:'Atalar\u0131 titan-forged makineler olan parlak tamirciler gnomlar, Gnomeregan \u015fehirlerini kaybetti ve Ironforge\u2019da s\xfcrg\xfcnde ya\u015f\u0131yor.'},body:{en:['Gnomes are small in stature and enormous in ingenuity. Their ancestors, the mechagnomes, were titan-forged machines later afflicted by the curse of flesh, which turned them into living beings. In Dun Morogh they built Gnomeregan, a city of gears and steam, and became firm allies of the dwarves of nearby Ironforge, fighting beside them in the Second War.','That city is lost. Troggs surged up from below, and Mekgineer Sicco Thermaplugg\u2019s advice to flood Gnomeregan with radiation poisoned it instead; many gnomes died, and some survivors became twisted leper gnomes. High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque led the rest into exile in Ironforge, while Thermaplugg rules the ruins. Forever opens the priesthood to gnomes for the first time.'],tr:['Gnomlar boyca k\xfc\xe7\xfck ama yarat\u0131c\u0131l\u0131kta devasad\u0131r. Atalar\u0131 olan mechagnome\u2019lar, sonradan et laneti ile canl\u0131 varl\u0131klara d\xf6n\xfc\u015fen titan-forged makinelerdi. Dun Morogh\u2019da di\u015fliler ve buhardan bir \u015fehir olan Gnomeregan\u2019\u0131 kurdular ve yak\u0131ndaki Ironforge c\xfccelerinin sad\u0131k m\xfcttefiki olup \u0130kinci Sava\u015f\u2019ta onlarla omuz omuza sava\u015ft\u0131lar.','O \u015fehir art\u0131k yitik. Trogglar derinlerden f\u0131\u015fk\u0131rd\u0131; Mekgineer Sicco Thermaplugg\u2019\u0131n Gnomeregan\u2019\u0131 radyasyonla doldurma \xf6nerisi ise \u015fehri zehirledi. Pek \xe7ok gnom \xf6ld\xfc, baz\u0131 sa\u011f kalanlar \xe7arp\u0131k c\xfczaml\u0131 gnomlara d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc. Y\xfcce Tamirci Gelbin Mekkatorque kalanlar\u0131 Ironforge\u2019a s\xfcrg\xfcne g\xf6t\xfcrd\xfc; Thermaplugg ise harabelere h\xfckmediyor. Forever Priest yolunu gnomlara ilk kez a\xe7\u0131yor.']},links:{raceIds:['gnome'],factionIds:['alliance'],classIds:['warrior','rogue','priest','mage','warlock'],zoneIds:['dun-morogh'],instanceIds:['gnomeregan'],loreIds:['chapter:war-of-the-three-hammers','chapter:stormwind-in-shadow','term:titan-forged']},image:'race:gnome',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Gnome'),(0,n.wiki)('Gnomeregan'),(0,n.wiki)('Gelbin Mekkatorque'),l],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'race',slug:'night-elf',subjectId:'night-elf',order:3,era:'ancient-kalimdor',title:{en:'Night Elf',tr:'Gece Elfi'},summary:{en:'The ancient kaldorei kept watch over Kalimdor for ten thousand years; now mortal, they have planted a new World Tree and joined the Alliance.',tr:'Kadim kaldorei on bin y\u0131l boyunca Kalimdor\u2019u g\xf6zetti; art\u0131k \xf6l\xfcml\xfcler, yeni bir D\xfcnya A\u011fac\u0131 diktiler ve \u0130ttifak\u2019a kat\u0131ld\u0131lar.'},body:{en:['The night elves, or kaldorei, are the oldest of the playable peoples. Descended from trolls changed by the Well of Eternity, they built an empire of magic, survived the War of the Ancients and spent ten thousand years as a reclusive people of druids and Sentinels in the shadow of Mount Hyjal. Arcane magic remains forbidden among them.','The Third War cost them their immortality, when Nordrassil was wounded to destroy Archimonde. With Malfurion lost in the Emerald Dream, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm grew a new World Tree, Teldrassil, off the coast of Darkshore, and the capital Darnassus rose in its branches. Under Tyrande Whisperwind the night elves joined the Alliance. New night elves begin among Teldrassil\u2019s glades.'],tr:['Gece elfleri, yani kaldorei, oynanabilir halklar\u0131n en eskisidir. Sonsuzluk Kuyusu\u2019nun d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc\u011f\xfc trollerin soyundan gelirler; bir b\xfcy\xfc imparatorlu\u011fu kurdular, Kadimler Sava\u015f\u0131\u2019ndan sa\u011f \xe7\u0131kt\u0131lar ve on bin y\u0131l boyunca Mount Hyjal\u2019\u0131n g\xf6lgesinde Druid\u2019ler ve Sentinel\u2019lerden olu\u015fan i\xe7ine kapan\u0131k bir halk olarak ya\u015fad\u0131lar. Arkan b\xfcy\xfc aralar\u0131nda h\xe2l\xe2 yasak.','Archimonde\u2019u yok etmek i\xe7in Nordrassil yaraland\u0131\u011f\u0131nda \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f onlara \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfcklerine mal oldu. Malfurion Z\xfcmr\xfct R\xfcya\u2019da kaybolmu\u015fken Ba\u015f Druid Fandral Staghelm, Darkshore k\u0131y\u0131lar\u0131n\u0131n a\xe7\u0131\u011f\u0131nda yeni bir D\xfcnya A\u011fac\u0131, Teldrassil\u2019i b\xfcy\xfctt\xfc ve ba\u015fkent Darnassus onun dallar\u0131nda y\xfckseldi. Tyrande Whisperwind \xf6nderli\u011finde gece elfleri \u0130ttifak\u2019a kat\u0131ld\u0131. Yeni gece elfleri maceralar\u0131na Teldrassil\u2019in korular\u0131nda ba\u015flar.']},links:{raceIds:['night-elf'],factionIds:['alliance'],classIds:['warrior','hunter','rogue','priest','druid'],zoneIds:['teldrassil','darkshore','ashenvale'],loreIds:['chapter:rise-of-the-kaldorei','chapter:war-of-the-ancients','chapter:battle-for-mount-hyjal','term:kaldorei','term:elune','term:nordrassil']},image:'race:night-elf',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Night elf'),(0,n.wiki)('Teldrassil'),(0,n.wiki)('Fandral Staghelm'),l],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'race',slug:'dwarf',subjectId:'dwarf',order:4,era:'elder-kingdoms',title:{en:'Dwarf',tr:'C\xfcce'},summary:{en:"Children of the titans' earthen, the dwarves of Ironforge are stubborn allies, tireless explorers and keepers of a divided heritage.",tr:'Titanlar\u0131n earthen\u2019lar\u0131n\u0131n \xe7ocuklar\u0131 olan Ironforge c\xfcceleri inat\xe7\u0131 m\xfcttefikler, yorulmaz k\xe2\u015fifler ve b\xf6l\xfcnm\xfc\u015f bir miras\u0131n bek\xe7ileridir.'},body:{en:["Dwarves are stubborn, warm-hearted and born of stone: their ancestors were the earthen, titan-forged guardians changed by the curse of flesh. Ironforge, carved into a mountain in Dun Morogh, has been their capital for ages. The War of the Three Hammers split the clans; the Bronzebeards held the city, the Wildhammers settled the Hinterlands and the Dark Irons fell into Ragnaros' service.","Under King Magni Bronzebeard the dwarves have fought in every war of the Alliance, and the Explorers' League, in which his brother Brann is a leading figure, digs through titan ruins such as Uldaman in search of the dwarves' origins. Magni's daughter Moira has become the wife of the Dark Iron emperor, a wound the king takes personally. Forever adds the Hall of Thanes beneath Ironforge, the resting place of dwarven monarchs, now broken into by intruders thought to be Dark Irons, and dwarves may walk the path of the shaman."],tr:['C\xfcceler inat\xe7\u0131, s\u0131cakkanl\u0131 ve ta\u015ftan do\u011fmad\u0131r: atalar\u0131, et lanetiyle de\u011fi\u015fmi\u015f titan-forged koruyucular olan earthen\u2019lard\u0131. Dun Morogh\u2019da bir da\u011f\u0131n i\xe7ine oyulmu\u015f Ironforge \xe7a\u011flard\u0131r ba\u015fkentleri. \xdc\xe7 \xc7eki\xe7 Sava\u015f\u0131 klanlar\u0131 b\xf6ld\xfc; Bronzebeard\u2019lar \u015fehri tuttu, Wildhammer\u2019lar Hinterlands\u2019e yerle\u015fti, Dark Iron\u2019lar ise Ragnaros\u2019un hizmetine d\xfc\u015ft\xfc.',"Kral Magni Bronzebeard \xf6nderli\u011finde c\xfcceler \u0130ttifak\u2019\u0131n her sava\u015f\u0131nda yer ald\u0131; karde\u015fi Brann\u2019\u0131n \xf6nde gelen isimlerinden oldu\u011fu K\xe2\u015fifler Birli\u011fi, c\xfccelerin k\xf6kenini arayarak Uldaman gibi titan harabelerini kaz\u0131yor. Magni\u2019nin k\u0131z\u0131 Moira, Dark Iron imparatorunun e\u015fi oldu; kral bunu ki\u015fisel bir yara olarak ta\u015f\u0131yor. Forever, Ironforge\u2019un alt\u0131nda c\xfcce h\xfck\xfcmdarlar\u0131n\u0131n ebedi istirahatg\xe2h\u0131 olan ve Dark Iron oldu\u011fu d\xfc\u015f\xfcn\xfclen davetsiz misafirlerin girdi\u011fi Hall of Thanes\u2019i ekliyor; c\xfcceler art\u0131k Shaman da olabiliyor."]},links:{raceIds:['dwarf'],factionIds:['alliance'],classIds:['warrior','paladin','hunter','rogue','priest','shaman'],zoneIds:['dun-morogh','loch-modan','hinterlands','badlands'],instanceIds:['hall-of-thanes','uldaman','blackrock-depths'],loreIds:['chapter:war-of-the-three-hammers','chapter:fire-beneath-blackrock','term:titan-forged','term:explorers-league']},image:'race:dwarf',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Dwarf'),(0,n.wiki)('Ironforge'),(0,n.wiki)("Explorers' League"),n.FOREVER.dungeons,l],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'race',slug:'skyborne-high-order',subjectId:'skyborne-high-order',order:5,era:'classic',title:{en:'Skyborne: High Order',tr:'Skyborne: High Order'},summary:{en:"Forever's new people from Zephras Isle, an island floating in the Elemental Plane of Air; the High Order stand with the Alliance.",tr:'Hava\u2019n\u0131n Elemental D\xfczlemi\u2019nde s\xfcz\xfclen Zephras Isle adas\u0131ndan gelen Forever\u2019\u0131n yeni halk\u0131; High Order \u0130ttifak\u2019\u0131n yan\u0131nda duruyor.',de:'Das neue Volk aus Forever von Zephras Isle, einer Insel, die in der Elementarebene der Luft schwebt; der High Order steht an der Seite der Allianz.',fr:'Le nouveau peuple de Forever, venu de Zephras Isle, une \xeele qui flotte dans le plan \xc9l\xe9mentaire de l\u2019Air ; le High Order se tient aux c\xf4t\xe9s de l\u2019Alliance.',es:'El nuevo pueblo de Forever, procedente de Zephras Isle, una isla que flota en el Plano Elemental del Aire; la High Order est\xe1 del lado de la Alianza.','pt-BR':'O novo povo de Forever, vindo de Zephras Isle, uma ilha que flutua no Plano Elemental do Ar; a High Order est\xe1 ao lado da Alian\xe7a.',it:'Il nuovo popolo di Forever, originario di Zephras Isle, un\u2019isola che fluttua nel Piano Elementale dell\u2019Aria; l\u2019High Order sta al fianco dell\u2019Alleanza.',ru:'\u041d\u043e\u0432\u044b\u0439 \u043d\u0430\u0440\u043e\u0434 Forever \u0441 Zephras Isle, \u043e\u0441\u0442\u0440\u043e\u0432\u0430, \u043f\u0430\u0440\u044f\u0449\u0435\u0433\u043e \u0432 \u0421\u0442\u0438\u0445\u0438\u0439\u043d\u043e\u043c \u041f\u043b\u0430\u043d\u0435 \u0412\u043e\u0437\u0434\u0443\u0445\u0430; High Order \u0441\u0442\u043e\u0438\u0442 \u043d\u0430 \u0441\u0442\u043e\u0440\u043e\u043d\u0435 \u0410\u043b\u044c\u044f\u043d\u0441\u0430.',ko:'\ubc14\ub78c\uc758 \uc815\ub839\uacc4\uc5d0 \ub5a0 \uc788\ub294 \uc12c Zephras Isle\uc5d0\uc11c \uc628 Forever\uc758 \uc0c8 \uc885\uc871. High Order\ub294 \uc5bc\ub77c\uc774\uc5b8\uc2a4 \ud3b8\uc5d0 \uc120\ub2e4.','zh-CN':'Forever\u7684\u65b0\u79cd\u65cf\uff0c\u6765\u81ea\u6f02\u6d6e\u5728\u98ce\u4e4b\u5143\u7d20\u4f4d\u9762\u4e2d\u7684\u5c9b\u5c7fZephras Isle\uff1bHigh Order\u7ad9\u5728\u8054\u76df\u4e00\u65b9\u3002','zh-TW':'Forever\u7684\u65b0\u7a2e\u65cf\uff0c\u4f86\u81ea\u6f02\u6d6e\u5728\u98a8\u4e4b\u5143\u7d20\u754c\u4e2d\u7684\u5cf6\u5dbcZephras Isle\uff1bHigh Order\u7ad9\u5728\u806f\u76df\u4e00\u65b9\u3002'},body:{en:['The Skyborne are the new playable people of World of Warcraft: Forever, and the High Order is the branch that stands with the Alliance. Their home is Zephras Isle, an island floating in Skywall, the Elemental Plane of Air, ruled by High Elder Talaanis Shadowsong, with the town of Valanaar as its main settlement. The air elementals who once lived on the island with the Skyborne vanished centuries ago, its sustaining magic is fading, and contact with the sister islands of Anvilas and Siroccas has been lost as refugees flee to Zephras.','High Order adventurers leave the isle by airship from Valanaar to Dalaran in the Alterac Mountains. They may be warriors, hunters, rogues, druids or mages, and they are the only Skyborne who study the arcane. Their gifts reflect their home: they glide down on the wind, act with quickened haste, strike elementals harder, and read nearby ley lines to restore health and mana. Playing them requires the optional Skyborne Heroic or Epic Pack.'],tr:['Skyborne, World of Warcraft: Forever\u2019\u0131n yeni oynanabilir halk\u0131d\u0131r; High Order ise onlar\u0131n \u0130ttifak\u2019\u0131n yan\u0131nda duran koludur. Yurtlar\u0131, Hava\u2019n\u0131n Elemental D\xfczlemi Skywall\u2019da s\xfcz\xfclen Zephras Isle adas\u0131; aday\u0131 Y\xfcce Bilge Talaanis Shadowsong y\xf6netiyor ve en b\xfcy\xfck yerle\u015fimi Valanaar kasabas\u0131. Bir zamanlar adada Skyborne\u2019la birlikte ya\u015fayan hava elementalleri y\xfczy\u0131llar \xf6nce kayboldu, aday\u0131 ayakta tutan b\xfcy\xfc zay\u0131fl\u0131yor ve m\xfclteciler Zephras\u2019a ka\xe7arken karde\u015f adalar Anvilas ve Siroccas ile ba\u011flant\u0131 koptu.','High Order macerac\u0131lar\u0131 adadan Valanaar\u2019dan kalkan hava gemisiyle Alterac Da\u011flar\u0131\u2019ndaki Dalaran\u2019a gider. Warrior, Hunter, Rogue, Druid ya da Mage olabilirler; arkan\u0131 inceleyen tek Skyborne onlard\u0131r. Yetenekleri yurtlar\u0131n\u0131 yans\u0131t\u0131r: r\xfczg\xe2rda s\xfcz\xfclerek iner, daha seri sald\u0131r\u0131r ve b\xfcy\xfc yapar, elementallere daha sert vurur ve yak\u0131ndaki ley hatlar\u0131n\u0131 okuyarak can ve mana yeniler. Onlar\u0131 oynamak i\xe7in iste\u011fe ba\u011fl\u0131 Skyborne Heroic veya Epic Pack gerekir.']},links:{raceIds:['skyborne-high-order','skyborne-windshaper'],factionIds:['alliance'],classIds:['warrior','hunter','mage','rogue','druid'],zoneIds:['zephras-isle','alterac-mountains'],loreIds:['chapter:azeroth-in-year-twenty-five','term:skywall','term:ley-lines']},sources:[n.FOREVER.zephrasIsle,n.FOREVER.overview,l,(0,n.datasetSource)('wiki-racial-read-ley-line'),(0,n.datasetSource)('wiki-racial-walk-on-air'),(0,n.datasetSource)('wiki-racial-wind-blessed'),(0,n.datasetSource)('wiki-racial-elemental-insight')],basis:'forever-partial',unknowns:o}),(0,n.lore)({category:'race',slug:'skyborne-windshaper',subjectId:'skyborne-windshaper',order:6,era:'classic',title:{en:'Skyborne: Windshapers',tr:'Skyborne: Windshaper\u2019lar'},summary:{en:'The Skyborne who stand with the Horde: shaman, druids and wanderers from a failing island in Skywall, the Elemental Plane of Air.',tr:'Horde\u2019un yan\u0131nda duran Skyborne: Hava\u2019n\u0131n Elemental D\xfczlemi Skywall\u2019daki \xe7\xf6ken bir adadan gelen Shaman\u2019lar, Druid\u2019ler ve gezginler.',de:'Die Skyborne an der Seite der Horde: Schamanen, Druiden und Wanderer von einer zerfallenden Insel in Skywall, der Elementarebene der Luft.',fr:'Les Skyborne qui se tiennent aux c\xf4t\xe9s de la Horde : chamans, druides et vagabonds venus d\u2019une \xeele en perdition de Skywall, le plan \xc9l\xe9mentaire de l\u2019Air.',es:'Los Skyborne que est\xe1n del lado de la Horda: chamanes, druidas y errantes de una isla en decadencia de Skywall, el Plano Elemental del Aire.','pt-BR':'Os Skyborne que est\xe3o ao lado da Horda: xam\xe3s, druidas e andarilhos de uma ilha em ru\xedna em Skywall, o Plano Elemental do Ar.',it:'Gli Skyborne che stanno al fianco dell\u2019Orda: sciamani, druidi e viandanti di un\u2019isola in declino di Skywall, il Piano Elementale dell\u2019Aria.',ru:'Skyborne, \u0441\u0442\u043e\u044f\u0449\u0438\u0435 \u043d\u0430 \u0441\u0442\u043e\u0440\u043e\u043d\u0435 \u041e\u0440\u0434\u044b: \u0448\u0430\u043c\u0430\u043d\u044b, \u0434\u0440\u0443\u0438\u0434\u044b \u0438 \u0441\u0442\u0440\u0430\u043d\u043d\u0438\u043a\u0438 \u0441 \u0433\u0438\u0431\u043d\u0443\u0449\u0435\u0433\u043e \u043e\u0441\u0442\u0440\u043e\u0432\u0430 \u0432 Skywall, \u0421\u0442\u0438\u0445\u0438\u0439\u043d\u043e\u043c \u041f\u043b\u0430\u043d\u0435 \u0412\u043e\u0437\u0434\u0443\u0445\u0430.',ko:'\ud638\ub4dc \ud3b8\uc5d0 \uc120 Skyborne. \ubc14\ub78c\uc758 \uc815\ub839\uacc4 Skywall\uc758 \ubb34\ub108\uc838 \uac00\ub294 \uc12c\uc5d0\uc11c \uc628 \uc8fc\uc220\uc0ac, \ub4dc\ub8e8\uc774\ub4dc, \ubc29\ub791\uc790\ub4e4\uc774\ub2e4.','zh-CN':'\u7ad9\u5728\u90e8\u843d\u4e00\u65b9\u7684Skyborne\uff1a\u6765\u81ea\u98ce\u4e4b\u5143\u7d20\u4f4d\u9762Skywall\u4e2d\u4e00\u5ea7\u65e5\u6e10\u5d29\u6bc1\u7684\u5c9b\u5c7f\u7684\u8428\u6ee1\u796d\u53f8\u3001\u5fb7\u9c81\u4f0a\u548c\u6d41\u6d6a\u8005\u3002','zh-TW':'\u7ad9\u5728\u90e8\u843d\u4e00\u65b9\u7684Skyborne\uff1a\u4f86\u81ea\u98a8\u4e4b\u5143\u7d20\u754cSkywall\u4e2d\u4e00\u5ea7\u65e5\u6f38\u5d29\u6bc0\u7684\u5cf6\u5dbc\u7684\u85a9\u6eff\u3001\u5fb7\u9b6f\u4f0a\u548c\u6d41\u6d6a\u8005\u3002'},body:{en:['The Windshapers are the Skyborne who stand with the Horde. Like the High Order, they come from Zephras Isle in Skywall, the Elemental Plane of Air, an island whose air elementals vanished centuries ago and whose sustaining magic is slowly failing. As islands such as Anvilas and Siroccas fall silent, refugees crowd onto Zephras, and even Zephras has begun to fall apart.','Windshapers leave Valanaar by airship for Skywatcher Plateau in Mulgore. They may be warriors, hunters, rogues, druids or shaman, and they are the only Skyborne who walk the shaman\u2019s path. They glide on the wind, fight with quickened haste and strike elementals harder, and their own gift, Skysight, speeds their travel and lasts far longer near an elemental convergence. Like the High Order, they require the optional Skyborne Heroic or Epic Pack.'],tr:['Windshaper\u2019lar, Horde\u2019un yan\u0131nda duran Skyborne\u2019dur. High Order gibi onlar da Hava\u2019n\u0131n Elemental D\xfczlemi Skywall\u2019daki Zephras Isle\u2019dan gelir; adan\u0131n hava elementalleri y\xfczy\u0131llar \xf6nce kayboldu ve aday\u0131 ayakta tutan b\xfcy\xfc yava\u015f yava\u015f t\xfckeniyor. Anvilas ve Siroccas gibi adalardan ses gelmez olduk\xe7a m\xfclteciler Zephras\u2019a dolu\u015fuyor; Zephras bile da\u011f\u0131lmaya ba\u015flad\u0131.','Windshaper\u2019lar Valanaar\u2019dan hava gemisiyle Mulgore\u2019daki Skywatcher Plateau\u2019ya gider. Warrior, Hunter, Rogue, Druid ya da Shaman olabilirler; Shaman yolunda y\xfcr\xfcyen tek Skyborne onlard\u0131r. R\xfczg\xe2rda s\xfcz\xfcl\xfcr, h\u0131zlanm\u0131\u015f bir \xe7eviklikle sava\u015f\u0131r ve elementallere daha sert vururlar; kendilerine \xf6zg\xfc Skysight yetene\u011fi yolculuklar\u0131n\u0131 h\u0131zland\u0131r\u0131r ve bir elemental birle\u015fiminin yak\u0131n\u0131nda \xe7ok daha uzun s\xfcrer. High Order gibi onlar i\xe7in de iste\u011fe ba\u011fl\u0131 Skyborne Heroic veya Epic Pack gerekir.']},links:{raceIds:['skyborne-windshaper','skyborne-high-order'],factionIds:['horde'],classIds:['warrior','hunter','rogue','shaman','druid'],zoneIds:['zephras-isle','mulgore'],loreIds:['chapter:azeroth-in-year-twenty-five','term:skywall','term:elemental-lords']},sources:[n.FOREVER.zephrasIsle,n.FOREVER.overview,l,(0,n.datasetSource)('wiki-racial-skysight'),(0,n.datasetSource)('wiki-racial-walk-on-air'),(0,n.datasetSource)('wiki-racial-wind-blessed'),(0,n.datasetSource)('wiki-racial-elemental-insight')],basis:'forever-partial',unknowns:o}),(0,n.lore)({category:'race',slug:'orc',subjectId:'orc',order:7,era:'draenor',title:{en:'Orc',tr:'Ork'},summary:{en:'Once enslaved by demon blood, the orcs were freed by Thrall and now rebuild their honor in the red land of Durotar.',tr:'Bir zamanlar iblis kan\u0131n\u0131n k\xf6lesi olan orklar Thrall sayesinde \xf6zg\xfcrle\u015fti ve \u015fimdi Durotar\u2019\u0131n k\u0131z\u0131l topraklar\u0131nda onurlar\u0131n\u0131 yeniden in\u015fa ediyor.'},body:{en:["Orcs came to Azeroth from Draenor as the Horde, driven by demon blood and by Gul'dan's warlocks. Defeated in the Second War, they wasted away in internment camps until Thrall, son of the Frostwolf chieftain Durotan, freed them and restored the shamanic ways of their ancestors.",'After the Third War, Thrall led his people to Kalimdor and founded Durotar and its capital, Orgrimmar, where the warchief now rules a Horde shared with the tauren, the Darkspear trolls and the Forsaken. Orcs are proud, direct and fiercely loyal, yet their bloody past lingers in the Burning Blade cultists of Durotar and in the Blackrock clan that never joined Thrall. New orcs begin in the Valley of Trials. In Forever orcs can also become mages.'],tr:["Orklar Azeroth\u2019a Draenor\u2019dan, iblis kan\u0131 ve Gul'dan\u2019\u0131n Warlock\u2019lar\u0131 taraf\u0131ndan s\xfcr\xfcklenen Horde olarak geldi. \u0130kinci Sava\u015f\u2019ta yenilince toplama kamplar\u0131nda eriyip gittiler; ta ki Frostwolf reisi Durotan\u2019\u0131n o\u011flu Thrall onlar\u0131 \xf6zg\xfcrle\u015ftirip atalar\u0131n\u0131n \u015famanist yollar\u0131n\u0131 yeniden canland\u0131rana dek.",'\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019tan sonra Thrall halk\u0131n\u0131 Kalimdor\u2019a g\xf6t\xfcrd\xfc ve Durotar\u2019\u0131 ve ba\u015fkenti Orgrimmar\u2019\u0131 kurdu; sava\u015f reisi \u015fimdi oradan taurenler, Darkspear trolleri ve Forsaken ile payla\u015f\u0131lan bir Horde\u2019u y\xf6netiyor. Orklar gururlu, dolays\u0131z ve son derece sad\u0131kt\u0131r; ama kanl\u0131 ge\xe7mi\u015fleri Durotar\u2019daki Burning Blade tarikat\xe7\u0131lar\u0131nda ve Thrall\u2019a hi\xe7 kat\u0131lmayan Blackrock klan\u0131nda ya\u015famaya devam ediyor. Yeni orklar Valley of Trials\u2019da ba\u015flar. Forever\u2019da orklar Mage de olabiliyor.']},links:{raceIds:['orc'],factionIds:['horde'],classIds:['warrior','hunter','rogue','shaman','warlock','mage'],zoneIds:['durotar','barrens','burning-steppes'],instanceIds:['ragefire-chasm','lower-blackrock-spire'],loreIds:['chapter:corruption-of-the-orcs','chapter:thrall-and-the-new-horde','chapter:durotar-and-theramore','term:fel','item:doomhammer']},image:'race:orc',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Orc'),(0,n.wiki)('Orgrimmar'),(0,n.wiki)('Burning Blade clan'),l],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'race',slug:'tauren',subjectId:'tauren',order:8,era:'new-homes',title:{en:'Tauren',tr:'Tauren'},summary:{en:'Gentle giants of the plains who honor the Earth Mother, the tauren found a home in Mulgore and joined the Horde out of gratitude.',tr:'Toprak Ana\u2019ya sayg\u0131 duyan ovalar\u0131n nazik devleri taurenler Mulgore\u2019da yurt buldu ve minnetle Horde\u2019a kat\u0131ld\u0131.'},body:{en:["The tauren are towering, peaceful nomads who honor the Earth Mother and have roamed the plains of Kalimdor for ages. In the years of the Third War they were hounded by the centaur, until Thrall's newly arrived Horde helped Cairne Bloodhoof's people reach the safety of Mulgore.",'Cairne united many scattered tribes and founded Thunder Bluff on great mesas above Mulgore\u2019s grasslands, and the tauren joined the Horde out of gratitude and respect. Their druids learned from Malfurion Stormrage himself, and their shaman and hunters keep old traditions alive. Rival tribes such as the Grimtotem, who resent the bond with the orcs, remain a constant worry. Young tauren begin at Camp Narache in Mulgore.'],tr:['Taurenler, Toprak Ana\u2019ya sayg\u0131 duyan ve \xe7a\u011flard\u0131r Kalimdor ovalar\u0131nda dola\u015fan iri yar\u0131, bar\u0131\u015f\xe7\u0131l g\xf6\xe7ebelerdir. \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f y\u0131llar\u0131nda kentaurlar onlar\u0131 amans\u0131zca kovalad\u0131; ta ki Kalimdor\u2019a yeni gelen Thrall\u2019\u0131n Horde\u2019u Cairne Bloodhoof\u2019un halk\u0131n\u0131n Mulgore\u2019un g\xfcvenli\u011fine ula\u015fmas\u0131na yard\u0131m edene dek.','Cairne da\u011f\u0131n\u0131k kabilelerin \xe7o\u011funu birle\u015ftirdi ve Thunder Bluff\u2019\u0131 Mulgore otlaklar\u0131n\u0131n \xfczerindeki y\xfcksek d\xfczl\xfcklerde kurdu; taurenler minnet ve sayg\u0131yla Horde\u2019a kat\u0131ld\u0131. Druid\u2019leri bizzat Malfurion Stormrage\u2019den \xf6\u011frendi; Shaman\u2019lar\u0131 ve Hunter\u2019lar\u0131 eski gelenekleri ya\u015fat\u0131yor. Orklarla kurulan ba\u011fa k\u0131zan Grimtotem gibi rakip kabileler ise s\xfcrekli bir kayg\u0131 kayna\u011f\u0131. Gen\xe7 taurenler Mulgore\u2019daki Camp Narache\u2019de ba\u015flar.']},links:{raceIds:['tauren'],factionIds:['horde'],classIds:['warrior','hunter','shaman','druid'],zoneIds:['mulgore','barrens','thousand-needles'],loreIds:['chapter:battle-for-mount-hyjal','chapter:durotar-and-theramore','term:cenarion-circle']},image:'race:tauren',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Tauren'),(0,n.wiki)('Cairne Bloodhoof'),(0,n.wiki)('Thunder Bluff'),l],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'race',slug:'troll',subjectId:'troll',order:9,era:'ancient-kalimdor',title:{en:'Troll',tr:'Trol'},summary:{en:'Heirs of fallen empires, most trolls still hate the other races; the Darkspear tribe instead swore itself to Thrall and the Horde.',tr:'\xc7\xf6km\xfc\u015f imparatorluklar\u0131n miras\xe7\u0131s\u0131 trollerin \xe7o\u011fu di\u011fer \u0131rklardan h\xe2l\xe2 nefret ediyor; Darkspear kabilesi ise kendini Thrall\u2019a ve Horde\u2019a adad\u0131.'},body:{en:['Trolls once ruled vast empires: the Gurubashi in the southern jungles, the Amani in the forests of the north, and the Zandalari, who call themselves the first of all trolls. Wars with the night elves, the high elves and the humans broke those empires, and most tribes still nurse old hatreds and pray to the loa, the spirit gods of their ancestors.',"The Darkspear tribe is different. Exiled from Stranglethorn by rival tribes, the Darkspears were fighting for their island home when Thrall's storm-tossed fleet arrived; their chieftain Sen'jin died there, and his son Vol'jin swore the tribe to the Horde. They settled the Echo Isles off Durotar, though the witch doctor Zalazane's dark magic has driven them to Sen'jin Village on the mainland. In Forever Darkspear Raiders also contest the Darkspear Islands off Dustwallow Marsh, and trolls can become warlocks."],tr:['Troller bir zamanlar u\xe7suz bucaks\u0131z imparatorluklara h\xfckmederdi: g\xfcneyin ormanlar\u0131nda Gurubashi, kuzeyin ormanlar\u0131nda Amani ve kendilerini t\xfcm trollerin ilki sayan Zandalari. Gece elfleri, y\xfcksek elfler ve insanlarla yap\u0131lan sava\u015flar bu imparatorluklar\u0131 y\u0131kt\u0131; kabilelerin \xe7o\u011fu h\xe2l\xe2 eski nefretleri besliyor ve atalar\u0131n\u0131n ruh tanr\u0131lar\u0131 olan loa\u2019lara dua ediyor.',"Darkspear kabilesi farkl\u0131d\u0131r. Rakip kabileler taraf\u0131ndan Stranglethorn\u2019dan s\xfcr\xfclen Darkspear\u2019lar, Thrall\u2019\u0131n f\u0131rt\u0131naya tutulmu\u015f filosu geldi\u011finde ada yurtlar\u0131 i\xe7in sava\u015f\u0131yordu; reisleri Sen'jin orada \xf6ld\xfc, o\u011flu Vol'jin de kabileyi Horde\u2019a ba\u011flad\u0131. Durotar a\xe7\u0131klar\u0131ndaki Echo Isles\u2019a yerle\u015ftiler; ama b\xfcy\xfcc\xfc doktor Zalazane\u2019\u0131n kara b\xfcy\xfcs\xfc onlar\u0131 anakaradaki Sen'jin Village\u2019a \xe7ekilmeye zorlad\u0131. Forever\u2019da Darkspear Raiders, Dustwallow Marsh a\xe7\u0131klar\u0131ndaki Darkspear Islands i\xe7in de sava\u015f\u0131yor ve troller Warlock olabiliyor."]},links:{raceIds:['troll'],factionIds:['horde'],classIds:['warrior','hunter','rogue','priest','shaman','mage','warlock'],zoneIds:['durotar','stranglethorn-vale','hinterlands','dustwallow-marsh'],instanceIds:['zulfarrak','temple-of-atalhakkar'],loreIds:['chapter:rise-of-the-kaldorei','chapter:arathor-and-the-troll-wars','chapter:durotar-and-theramore','term:loa','item:heart-of-hakkar']},image:'race:troll',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Troll'),(0,n.wiki)('Darkspear tribe'),(0,n.wiki)("Vol'jin"),(0,n.datasetSource)('blizzard-darkspear-islands'),l],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'race',slug:'undead',subjectId:'undead',order:10,era:'third-war',title:{en:'Undead',tr:'Hortlak'},summary:{en:"Risen victims of the plague who broke free of the Lich King, the Forsaken rule the Undercity beneath Lordaeron's ruins and trust no one.",tr:'Lich King\u2019den kurtulan, vebayla \xf6l\xfcp dirilmi\u015f kurbanlar olan Forsaken, Lordaeron harabelerinin alt\u0131ndaki Undercity\u2019ye h\xfckmeder ve kimseye g\xfcvenmez.'},body:{en:["The Forsaken were once citizens of Lordaeron, slain by the plague and raised by the Scourge, who regained their free will when the Lich King's power faltered. Led by the banshee queen Sylvanas Windrunner, they claimed the ruins of Lordaeron's capital and made the Undercity beneath it their home. Their lands, Tirisfal Glades and Silverpine Forest, are contested by the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade.","The Forsaken joined the Horde as allies of necessity; few of the living trust them, and the Royal Apothecary Society's secret work on a new plague gives their partners good reason. New Forsaken rise in Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades. Forever adds the Ruins of Lordaeron dungeon, where the Forsaken work to reclaim the shattered city above the Undercity, and it allows Forsaken paladins, a pairing the sources used here do not yet explain."],tr:['Forsaken bir zamanlar Lordaeron\u2019un yurtta\u015flar\u0131yd\u0131; vebayla \xf6l\xfcp Scourge taraf\u0131ndan diriltildiler ve Lich King\u2019in g\xfcc\xfc sars\u0131l\u0131nca \xf6zg\xfcr iradelerini geri kazand\u0131lar. Banshee krali\xe7e Sylvanas Windrunner \xf6nderli\u011finde Lordaeron\u2019un ba\u015fkentinin harabelerini sahiplendiler ve alt\u0131ndaki Undercity\u2019yi yurt edindiler. Topraklar\u0131 olan Tirisfal Glades ve Silverpine Forest, Scourge ve Scarlet Crusade ile \xe7eki\u015fme i\xe7inde.','Forsaken, Horde\u2019a zorunluluktan do\u011fan m\xfcttefikler olarak kat\u0131ld\u0131; ya\u015fayanlar\u0131n pek az\u0131 onlara g\xfcvenir ve Kraliyet Eczac\u0131lar Cemiyeti\u2019nin yeni bir veba \xfczerindeki gizli \xe7al\u0131\u015fmalar\u0131 ortaklar\u0131na hakl\u0131 bir ku\u015fku veriyor. Yeni Forsaken, Tirisfal Glades\u2019teki Deathknell\u2019de dirilir. Forever, Forsaken\u2019\u0131n Undercity\u2019nin \xfczerindeki par\xe7alanm\u0131\u015f \u015fehri geri almaya \xe7al\u0131\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131 Ruins of Lordaeron zindan\u0131n\u0131 ekliyor ve Forsaken Paladin\u2019lere izin veriyor; burada kullan\u0131lan kaynaklar bu e\u015fle\u015fmeyi hen\xfcz a\xe7\u0131klam\u0131yor.']},links:{raceIds:['undead'],factionIds:['horde'],classIds:['warrior','paladin','rogue','priest','mage','warlock'],zoneIds:['tirisfal-glades','silverpine-forest','western-plaguelands'],instanceIds:['ruins-of-lordaeron','shadowfang-keep'],loreIds:['chapter:fall-of-lordaeron','chapter:rise-of-the-forsaken','term:scourge','term:lich-king']},image:'race:undead',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Forsaken'),(0,n.wiki)('Undercity'),(0,n.wiki)('Royal Apothecary Society'),n.FOREVER.dungeons,l],basis:'established',unknowns:[{en:'How Forsaken paladins came to be in Forever is not explained by the sources this guide uses.',tr:'Forever\u2019da Forsaken Paladin\u2019lerin nas\u0131l ortaya \xe7\u0131kt\u0131\u011f\u0131, bu rehberin kulland\u0131\u011f\u0131 kaynaklarda a\xe7\u0131klanm\u0131yor.'}]})]},870,[866]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"timelineChapters",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});var n=r(d[0]);const t=[(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'titans-and-old-gods',order:1,era:'creation',when:{en:'Before recorded history',tr:'Yaz\u0131l\u0131 tarihten \xf6nce'},title:{en:'The Titans and the Old Gods',tr:'Titanlar ve Kadim Tanr\u0131lar'},summary:{en:'Before any mortal kingdom, the titans of the Pantheon fought the Old Gods for the soul of a young world, and Azeroth still carries the scars.',tr:'Hi\xe7bir \xf6l\xfcml\xfc krall\u0131k yokken Panteon\u2019un titanlar\u0131, gen\xe7 bir d\xfcnyan\u0131n ruhu i\xe7in Kadim Tanr\u0131lar\u2019la (Old Gods) sava\u015ft\u0131; Azeroth o yaralar\u0131 h\xe2l\xe2 ta\u015f\u0131yor.'},body:{en:['Long before mortals kept records, the titans walked the Great Dark Beyond: world-souls grown into living giants. The noblest of them gathered as the Pantheon and searched the stars for sleeping world-souls like their own. Deep inside Azeroth they sensed one of extraordinary promise, but darker powers had found it first.',"The void lords had hurled their servants, the Old Gods, onto the young world. Y'Shaarj, C'Thun, Yogg-Saron and N'Zoth sank their bodies into the crust and raised the Black Empire, with the elemental lords of fire, earth, air and water as their generals. When the Pantheon arrived, its titan-forged armies broke the empire's citadels. Highfather Aman'Thul tore Y'Shaarj from the ground, but the blow opened a wound that bled the world's arcane lifeblood. The titans understood that killing the rest might kill Azeroth itself.","So the keepers chose prisons instead. C'Thun, Yogg-Saron and N'Zoth were chained deep below the earth, and the elemental lords were banished to the Elemental Plane, whose realms include Skywall and the Firelands. The keepers calmed the bleeding wound into a shining lake, the Well of Eternity, shaped mountains and seas, and left titan vaults such as Uldaman behind. After a monstrous proto-dragon named Galakrond fell, the Pantheon empowered five great dragons as Aspects to guard the world, then departed into the stars."],tr:['\xd6l\xfcml\xfcler kay\u0131t tutmaya ba\u015flamadan \xe7ok \xf6nce titanlar, B\xfcy\xfck Karanl\u0131k \xd6te\u2019de (Great Dark Beyond) dola\u015f\u0131rd\u0131: canl\u0131 devlere d\xf6n\xfc\u015fm\xfc\u015f d\xfcnya ruhlar\u0131. Aralar\u0131ndaki en soylular Panteon\u2019da (Pantheon) topland\u0131 ve y\u0131ld\u0131zlar aras\u0131nda kendileri gibi uyuyan d\xfcnya ruhlar\u0131 arad\u0131. Azeroth\u2019un derinliklerinde ola\u011fan\xfcst\xfc vaat ta\u015f\u0131yan bir ruh sezdiler; ama daha karanl\u0131k g\xfc\xe7ler onu \xf6nce bulmu\u015ftu.',"Bo\u015fluk efendileri (void lords), hizmetk\xe2rlar\u0131 olan Kadim Tanr\u0131lar\u2019\u0131 (Old Gods) gen\xe7 d\xfcnyaya f\u0131rlatm\u0131\u015ft\u0131. Y'Shaarj, C'Thun, Yogg-Saron ve N'Zoth bedenlerini yer kabu\u011funa g\xf6md\xfc ve ate\u015f, toprak, hava ve suyun elemental lordlar\u0131n\u0131 generalleri yaparak Kara \u0130mparatorluk\u2019u (Black Empire) kurdu. Panteon geldi\u011finde titan-forged ordular\u0131 imparatorlu\u011fun kalelerini y\u0131kt\u0131. Y\xfcce Baba Aman'Thul, Y'Shaarj\u2019\u0131 topraktan s\xf6k\xfcp att\u0131; ama bu darbe d\xfcnyan\u0131n arkan can kan\u0131n\u0131 ak\u0131tan bir yara a\xe7t\u0131. Titanlar, kalanlar\u0131 \xf6ld\xfcrmenin Azeroth\u2019un kendisini de \xf6ld\xfcrebilece\u011fini anlad\u0131.","Bu y\xfczden bek\xe7iler (keepers) zindanlar\u0131 se\xe7ti. C'Thun, Yogg-Saron ve N'Zoth topra\u011f\u0131n derinliklerine zincirlendi; elemental lordlar ise Skywall ve Firelands gibi diyarlar\u0131 olan Elemental D\xfczlem\u2019e s\xfcr\xfcld\xfc. Bek\xe7iler kanayan yaray\u0131 yat\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131p \u0131\u015f\u0131ldayan bir g\xf6le, Sonsuzluk Kuyusu\u2019na (Well of Eternity) d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc; da\u011flar\u0131 ve denizleri bi\xe7imlendirdi, ard\u0131nda Uldaman gibi titan mahzenleri b\u0131rakt\u0131. Galakrond adl\u0131 canavarca ilk ejderha d\xfc\u015ft\xfckten sonra Panteon be\u015f b\xfcy\xfck ejderhay\u0131 d\xfcnyay\u0131 korumalar\u0131 i\xe7in Aspect olarak g\xfc\xe7lendirdi ve y\u0131ld\u0131zlara \xe7ekildi."]},links:{loreIds:['term:titans','term:titan-forged','term:old-gods','term:elemental-lords','term:well-of-eternity','term:dragon-aspects'],zoneIds:['badlands'],instanceIds:['uldaman']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Titan'),(0,n.wiki)('Old God'),(0,n.wiki)('Black Empire'),(0,n.wiki)('Well of Eternity'),(0,n.wiki)('Dragon Aspects')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'sargeras-and-the-burning-legion',order:2,era:'creation',when:{en:'Long before the night elves',tr:'Gece elflerinden \xe7ok \xf6nce'},title:{en:'Sargeras and the Burning Legion',tr:'Sargeras ve Yanan Lejyon'},summary:{en:"The Pantheon's greatest champion lost his faith in creation and raised a demonic crusade to burn it, and Azeroth became the prize he wanted most.",tr:'Panteon\u2019un en b\xfcy\xfck sava\u015f\xe7\u0131s\u0131 yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015fa olan inanc\u0131n\u0131 yitirdi ve onu yakmak i\xe7in iblislerden bir ha\xe7l\u0131 ordusu kurdu; Azeroth en \xe7ok istedi\u011fi ganimet oldu.'},body:{en:["Sargeras was the Pantheon's champion, the titan who hunted demons across the cosmos and locked them in a prison world called Mardum. Over ages of war he learned what the void lords truly wanted: to corrupt a world-soul and birth a dark titan of their own. Convinced that creation was flawed beyond saving, he decided it would be kinder to burn everything.","He shattered the prison of Mardum and set its demons loose as the first ranks of the Burning Legion. On the world of Argus he offered the eredar knowledge and power; their leaders Kil'jaeden and Archimonde accepted, while the prophet Velen fled with those who refused, the people later called the draenei. The Pantheon tried to stop their former champion and were struck down by his hand.",'From then on the Legion moved from world to world, led by Sargeras and served by the eredar, the dreadlords called nathrezim and countless lesser demons. Azeroth mattered more than most: a world-soul still sleeping, already marked by the Old Gods. By the time of World of Warcraft the Legion had invaded it twice, and its whispers shaped the history of elves, orcs and humans alike.'],tr:['Sargeras, Panteon\u2019un \u015fampiyonuydu; kozmosta iblisleri avlayan ve onlar\u0131 Mardum adl\u0131 bir zindan d\xfcnyas\u0131na kapatan titan. \xc7a\u011flar s\xfcren sava\u015flarda bo\u015fluk efendilerinin as\u0131l amac\u0131n\u0131 \xf6\u011frendi: bir d\xfcnya ruhunu bozup kendilerine ait karanl\u0131k bir titan do\u011furtmak. Yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015f\u0131n kurtar\u0131lamayacak kadar kusurlu oldu\u011funa inanan Sargeras, her \u015feyi yakman\u0131n daha merhametli olaca\u011f\u0131na karar verdi.',"Mardum\u2019un zindan\u0131n\u0131 par\xe7alad\u0131 ve iblislerini Yanan Lejyon\u2019un (Burning Legion) ilk saflar\u0131 olarak sal\u0131verdi. Argus d\xfcnyas\u0131nda eredar halk\u0131na bilgi ve g\xfc\xe7 teklif etti; liderleri Kil'jaeden ve Archimonde kabul etti, k\xe2hin Velen ise reddedenlerle birlikte ka\xe7t\u0131; bu halk sonradan draenei diye an\u0131lacakt\u0131. Panteon eski \u015fampiyonunu durdurmaya \xe7al\u0131\u015ft\u0131 ve onun eliyle y\u0131k\u0131ld\u0131.",'O g\xfcnden sonra Lejyon, ba\u015f\u0131nda Sargeras, yan\u0131nda eredar, nathrezim denen deh\u015fet lordlar\u0131 (dreadlords) ve say\u0131s\u0131z k\xfc\xe7\xfck iblisle d\xfcnyadan d\xfcnyaya ilerledi. Azeroth \xe7o\u011fundan daha \xf6nemliydi: h\xe2l\xe2 uyuyan ve Kadim Tanr\u0131lar\u2019\u0131n damgas\u0131n\u0131 \xe7oktan ta\u015f\u0131yan bir d\xfcnya ruhu. World of Warcraft d\xf6nemine gelindi\u011finde Lejyon Azeroth\u2019u iki kez istila etmi\u015fti; f\u0131s\u0131lt\u0131lar\u0131 elflerin, orklar\u0131n ve insanlar\u0131n tarihini bi\xe7imlendirdi.']},links:{loreIds:['term:burning-legion','term:nathrezim','term:fel','term:titans']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Sargeras'),(0,n.wiki)('Burning Legion'),(0,n.wiki)('Eredar'),(0,n.wiki)('Mardum, the Shattered Abyss')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'rise-of-the-kaldorei',order:3,era:'ancient-kalimdor',when:{en:'Roughly 15,000 to 10,000 years before the Dark Portal',tr:'Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten kabaca 15.000 ila 10.000 y\u0131l \xf6nce'},title:{en:'The Rise of the Kaldorei',tr:'Kaldorei\u2019nin Y\xfckseli\u015fi'},summary:{en:'Trolls ruled ancient Kalimdor until a tribe drawn to the Well of Eternity became the night elves, whose queen Azshara built an empire of breathtaking magic.',tr:'Kadim Kalimdor\u2019a troller h\xfckmediyordu; ta ki Sonsuzluk Kuyusu\u2019na \xe7ekilen bir kabile gece elflerine d\xf6n\xfc\u015fene ve krali\xe7eleri Azshara g\xf6z kama\u015ft\u0131r\u0131c\u0131 bir b\xfcy\xfc imparatorlu\u011fu kurana dek.'},body:{en:["In the ages after the titans left, Kalimdor was a single great continent. Trolls led by the Zandalari fought a long war against the insect-like aqir, remnants of the Old Gods' servants, and drove them to the far north and south of the land, where their descendants would become the nerubians and the qiraji. In victory the trolls split into rival empires such as the Gurubashi and the Amani.","One troll tribe chose a quieter path. It settled on the shores of the Well of Eternity, and over generations the Well's power changed it: its people grew taller and longer-lived, revered the moon goddess Elune and called themselves kaldorei, 'children of the stars'. Guided by the demigod Cenarius and other ancient spirits of the wild, they soon outshone their troll cousins.","Their greatest ruler was Queen Azshara, adored by her people and served by the Highborne, an aristocracy of sorcerers who drew ever more power from the Well. Her palace at Zin-Azshari stood on its shore, and her empire spread across Kalimdor. The Highborne's hunger for magic, however, sent ripples far beyond the world, and something vast in the Twisting Nether felt them."],tr:['Titanlar\u0131n gidi\u015finden sonraki \xe7a\u011flarda Kalimdor tek ve b\xfcy\xfck bir k\u0131tayd\u0131. Zandalari \xf6nderli\u011findeki troller, Kadim Tanr\u0131lar\u2019\u0131n hizmetk\xe2rlar\u0131ndan kalan b\xf6ce\u011fimsi aqir ile uzun bir sava\u015fa girdi ve onlar\u0131 k\u0131tan\u0131n uzak kuzeyine ve g\xfcneyine s\xfcrd\xfc; aqir\u2019in torunlar\u0131 nerubian ve qiraji halklar\u0131na d\xf6n\xfc\u015fecekti. Zaferin ard\u0131ndan troller, Gurubashi ve Amani gibi rakip imparatorluklara b\xf6l\xfcnd\xfc.','Bir trol kabilesi daha sessiz bir yol se\xe7ti. Sonsuzluk Kuyusu\u2019nun k\u0131y\u0131lar\u0131na yerle\u015fti ve ku\u015faklar boyunca Kuyu\u2019nun g\xfcc\xfc onu de\u011fi\u015ftirdi: halk\u0131 daha uzun boylu ve uzun \xf6m\xfcrl\xfc oldu, ay tanr\u0131\xe7as\u0131 Elune\u2019e tapt\u0131 ve kendine \u2018y\u0131ld\u0131zlar\u0131n \xe7ocuklar\u0131\u2019 anlam\u0131na gelen kaldorei ad\u0131n\u0131 verdi. Yar\u0131 tanr\u0131 Cenarius ve vah\u015fi do\u011fan\u0131n di\u011fer kadim ruhlar\u0131n\u0131n rehberli\u011finde k\u0131sa s\xfcrede trol akrabalar\u0131n\u0131 geride b\u0131rakt\u0131lar.','En b\xfcy\xfck h\xfck\xfcmdarlar\u0131, halk\u0131n\u0131n tapt\u0131\u011f\u0131 Krali\xe7e Azshara\u2019yd\u0131; Kuyu\u2019dan durmadan daha fazla g\xfc\xe7 \xe7eken b\xfcy\xfcc\xfc aristokrasi Highborne ona hizmet ediyordu. Zin-Azshari\u2019deki saray\u0131 Kuyu\u2019nun k\u0131y\u0131s\u0131nda y\xfckseliyor, imparatorlu\u011fu t\xfcm Kalimdor\u2019a yay\u0131l\u0131yordu. Ne var ki Highborne\u2019un b\xfcy\xfc a\xe7l\u0131\u011f\u0131 d\xfcnyan\u0131n \xe7ok \xf6tesine dalgalar yayd\u0131 ve Twisting Nether\u2019daki devasa bir \u015fey bunlar\u0131 hissetti.']},links:{loreIds:['term:kaldorei','term:highborne','term:elune','term:loa','term:well-of-eternity'],raceIds:['night-elf','troll'],zoneIds:['azshara']},image:'race:night-elf',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Kaldorei Empire'),(0,n.wiki)('Night elf'),(0,n.wiki)('Aqir'),(0,n.wiki)('Azshara'),(0,n.wiki)('Highborne')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'war-of-the-ancients',order:4,era:'ancient-kalimdor',when:{en:'About 10,000 years before the Dark Portal',tr:'Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten yakla\u015f\u0131k 10.000 y\u0131l \xf6nce'},title:{en:'The War of the Ancients',tr:'Kadimler Sava\u015f\u0131'},summary:{en:'Azshara opened the way for the Burning Legion, and the world nearly ended before the Well of Eternity tore itself apart.',tr:'Azshara Yanan Lejyon\u2019a kap\u0131y\u0131 a\xe7t\u0131; Sonsuzluk Kuyusu kendini par\xe7alayana dek d\xfcnya neredeyse sona eriyordu.'},body:{en:['Sargeras whispered to Azshara and her Highborne, promising a world remade in their image. They believed him, and through the Well of Eternity they opened a gateway for the Burning Legion. Demons led by Archimonde and Mannoroth poured into Kalimdor and began to slaughter the very kaldorei the queen ruled.','Resistance gathered around unlikely leaders: Malfurion Stormrage, the first night elf to learn druidism from Cenarius; his twin brother Illidan, a gifted sorcerer; and Tyrande Whisperwind, a priestess of Elune. The demigods of the wild and most of the dragonflights fought beside them. The black Aspect Neltharion offered a weapon, the Dragon Soul, but turned it on his allies; that betrayal would earn him the name Deathwing.',"When Sargeras himself tried to step through the portal, Malfurion and his allies disrupted the Highborne's spell. The unstable Well imploded, and the Great Sundering followed: the sea swallowed Zin-Azshari, Kalimdor broke apart, and a storm called the Maelstrom began to spin where the Well had been. Azshara and her court vanished beneath the waves, to return one day as the naga. From one continent came the lands now known as Kalimdor, the Eastern Kingdoms and Northrend."],tr:['Sargeras, Azshara\u2019ya ve Highborne\u2019a f\u0131s\u0131ldayarak d\xfcnyay\u0131 onlar\u0131n suretinde yeniden kuraca\u011f\u0131na s\xf6z verdi. Ona inand\u0131lar ve Sonsuzluk Kuyusu arac\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131yla Yanan Lejyon i\xe7in bir ge\xe7it a\xe7t\u0131lar. Archimonde ve Mannoroth \xf6nderli\u011findeki iblisler Kalimdor\u2019a ak\u0131n etti ve krali\xe7enin h\xfckmetti\u011fi kaldorei\u2019yi katletmeye ba\u015flad\u0131.','Direni\u015f beklenmedik \xf6nderlerin \xe7evresinde topland\u0131: Cenarius\u2019tan druidli\u011fi \xf6\u011frenen ilk gece elfi Malfurion Stormrage; yetenekli bir b\xfcy\xfcc\xfc olan ikiz karde\u015fi Illidan; ve Elune rahibesi Tyrande Whisperwind. Vah\u015fi do\u011fan\u0131n yar\u0131 tanr\u0131lar\u0131 ve ejderha soylar\u0131n\u0131n \xe7o\u011fu onlarla birlikte sava\u015ft\u0131. Kara Aspect Neltharion, Dragon Soul (Ejderha Ruhu) adl\u0131 bir silah sundu ama onu m\xfcttefiklerine \xe7evirdi; bu ihanet ona Deathwing ad\u0131n\u0131 kazand\u0131racakt\u0131.','Sargeras bizzat ge\xe7itten ge\xe7meye \xe7al\u0131\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131nda Malfurion ve m\xfcttefikleri Highborne\u2019un b\xfcy\xfcs\xfcn\xfc bozdu. Dengesini yitiren Kuyu i\xe7ine \xe7\xf6kt\xfc ve ard\u0131ndan B\xfcy\xfck Yar\u0131lma (Great Sundering) geldi: deniz Zin-Azshari\u2019yi yuttu, Kalimdor par\xe7aland\u0131 ve Kuyu\u2019nun yerinde Maelstrom denen bir girdap d\xf6nmeye ba\u015flad\u0131. Azshara ve saray\u0131 dalgalar\u0131n alt\u0131nda kayboldu; bir g\xfcn naga olarak geri d\xf6neceklerdi. Tek k\u0131tadan bug\xfcn Kalimdor, Do\u011fu Krall\u0131klar\u0131 (Eastern Kingdoms) ve Northrend diye bilinen topraklar do\u011fdu.']},links:{loreIds:['term:highborne','term:burning-legion','term:dragon-aspects','term:well-of-eternity','item:demon-soul'],raceIds:['night-elf'],classIds:['druid','priest'],zoneIds:['azshara']},image:'class:druid',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('War of the Ancients'),(0,n.wiki)('Great Sundering'),(0,n.wiki)('Dragon Soul'),(0,n.wiki)('Malfurion Stormrage')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'the-long-watch-of-hyjal',order:5,era:'ancient-kalimdor',when:{en:'From about 10,000 years before the Dark Portal',tr:'Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten yakla\u015f\u0131k 10.000 y\u0131l \xf6nce ba\u015flayarak'},title:{en:'The Long Watch of Hyjal',tr:'Hyjal\u2019\u0131n Uzun N\xf6beti'},summary:{en:'The survivors grew a World Tree over a second Well, imprisoned Illidan beneath the earth and stood guard for ten thousand years.',tr:'Hayatta kalanlar ikinci bir Kuyu\u2019nun \xfczerinde bir D\xfcnya A\u011fac\u0131 b\xfcy\xfctt\xfc, Illidan\u2019\u0131 yerin alt\u0131na hapsetti ve on bin y\u0131l n\xf6bet tuttu.'},body:{en:["The night elves who escaped the Sundering gathered on Mount Hyjal. There they discovered that Illidan had carried vials of the old Well's water and poured some into a mountain lake, creating a new Well of Eternity. Fearing it would one day call the Legion back, Malfurion and Cenarius imprisoned Illidan in the Barrow Deeps, a prison beneath the earth where the warden Maiev Shadowsong would keep watch over him for ten thousand years.",'Three Aspects, Alexstrasza, Ysera and Nozdormu, answered by growing Nordrassil, the World Tree, over the new Well. Its roots sealed the waters, and its blessing gave the night elves immortality and the druids a bond with the Emerald Dream, where many of them slept for centuries at a time. Tyrande led the Sisterhood of Elune and the Sentinels, who guarded the forests while the druids dreamed. Arcane magic was banned among the kaldorei.',"Not every Highborne obeyed. Some were exiled across the sea and founded Quel'Thalas; others, the Shen'dralar, hid in the city of Eldre'Thalas in what is now Feralas. Its ruins are known today as Dire Maul."],tr:['Yar\u0131lma\u2019dan kurtulan gece elfleri Mount Hyjal\u2019da topland\u0131. Orada Illidan\u2019\u0131n eski Kuyu\u2019nun suyundan \u015fi\u015feler ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ve bir k\u0131sm\u0131n\u0131 bir da\u011f g\xf6l\xfcne d\xf6kerek yeni bir Sonsuzluk Kuyusu yaratt\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ke\u015ffettiler. Bunun bir g\xfcn Lejyon\u2019u geri \xe7a\u011f\u0131raca\u011f\u0131ndan korkan Malfurion ve Cenarius, Illidan\u2019\u0131 yerin alt\u0131ndaki Barrow Deeps zindan\u0131na kapatt\u0131; gardiyan Maiev Shadowsong on bin y\u0131l boyunca orada onun ba\u015f\u0131nda n\xf6bet tutacakt\u0131.','\xdc\xe7 Aspect, yani Alexstrasza, Ysera ve Nozdormu, yeni Kuyu\u2019nun \xfczerinde D\xfcnya A\u011fac\u0131 Nordrassil\u2019i b\xfcy\xfcterek kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131k verdi. A\u011fac\u0131n k\xf6kleri sular\u0131 m\xfch\xfcrledi; kutsamas\u0131 gece elflerine \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck, Druid\u2019lere ise Z\xfcmr\xfct R\xfcya (Emerald Dream) ile bir ba\u011f verdi ve Druid\u2019lerin \xe7o\u011fu orada y\xfczy\u0131llarca uyudu. Tyrande, Elune K\u0131z Karde\u015fli\u011fi\u2019ni ve Druid\u2019ler r\xfcya g\xf6r\xfcrken ormanlar\u0131 koruyan Sentinel\u2019leri y\xf6netti. Kaldorei aras\u0131nda arkan b\xfcy\xfc yasakland\u0131.',"Highborne\u2019un hepsi boyun e\u011fmedi. Bir k\u0131sm\u0131 denizin \xf6tesine s\xfcr\xfcld\xfc ve Quel'Thalas\u2019\u0131 kurdu; Shen'dralar denen di\u011ferleri ise bug\xfcnk\xfc Feralas\u2019taki Eldre'Thalas \u015fehrine sakland\u0131. O \u015fehrin harabeleri bug\xfcn Dire Maul olarak bilinir."]},links:{loreIds:['term:nordrassil','term:emerald-dream','term:kaldorei','term:cenarion-circle'],raceIds:['night-elf'],classIds:['druid'],zoneIds:['feralas'],instanceIds:['barrow-deeps','hyjal-summit','warpwood-quarter','capital-gardens','gordok-commons']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Nordrassil'),(0,n.wiki)('Barrow Deeps'),(0,n.wiki)('Illidan Stormrage'),(0,n.wiki)("Shen'dralar"),n.FOREVER.raids],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'exiles-of-quelthalas',order:6,era:'elder-kingdoms',when:{en:'About 6,800 years before the Dark Portal',tr:'Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten yakla\u015f\u0131k 6.800 y\u0131l \xf6nce'},title:{en:"The Exiles of Quel'Thalas",tr:"Quel'Thalas\u2019\u0131n S\xfcrg\xfcnleri"},summary:{en:'Banished Highborne crossed the sea, kindled the Sunwell and built an elven kingdom in the northern forests of Lordaeron.',tr:'S\xfcrg\xfcn edilen Highborne denizi a\u015ft\u0131, Sunwell\u2019i yakt\u0131 ve Lordaeron\u2019un kuzey ormanlar\u0131nda bir elf krall\u0131\u011f\u0131 kurdu.'},body:{en:["Long after the Sundering, a group of Highborne still could not give up the arcane. Their reckless spells raised storms over Ashenvale, and the night elves finally banished them. Led by Dath'Remar Sunstrider, the exiles sailed east across the Great Sea and wandered the new continent for years, searching for a land where magic ran strong.","Around 6,800 years before the Dark Portal they found it in the north of Lordaeron. Dath'Remar poured a stolen vial of water from the Well of Eternity into a lake on a nexus of ley lines, and the Sunwell blazed into being. Around it rose Quel'Thalas and its capital, Silvermoon. Living under the sun rather than the moon, the exiles changed over the centuries and became the high elves, the quel'dorei.","The land was not empty. It held ancient ruins sacred to the Amani trolls, who attacked the newcomers in overwhelming numbers. The elves held them back with magic and raised Ban'dinoriel, a barrier of runestones that kept the Amani at bay. For some four thousand years Quel'Thalas prospered behind it, while the trolls waited for revenge."],tr:["Yar\u0131lma\u2019dan \xe7ok sonra bir grup Highborne h\xe2l\xe2 arkan b\xfcy\xfcden vazge\xe7emiyordu. Pervas\u0131z b\xfcy\xfcleri Ashenvale \xfczerinde f\u0131rt\u0131nalar kopard\u0131 ve sonunda gece elfleri onlar\u0131 s\xfcrg\xfcn etti. Dath'Remar Sunstrider \xf6nderli\u011findeki s\xfcrg\xfcnler B\xfcy\xfck Deniz\u2019i do\u011fuya do\u011fru a\u015ft\u0131 ve b\xfcy\xfcn\xfcn g\xfc\xe7l\xfc akt\u0131\u011f\u0131 bir toprak arayarak y\u0131llarca yeni k\u0131tada dola\u015ft\u0131.","Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten yakla\u015f\u0131k 6.800 y\u0131l \xf6nce b\xf6yle bir yeri Lordaeron\u2019un kuzeyinde buldular. Dath'Remar, Sonsuzluk Kuyusu\u2019ndan \xe7al\u0131nm\u0131\u015f bir \u015fi\u015fe suyu ley hatlar\u0131n\u0131n kesi\u015fti\u011fi bir g\xf6le d\xf6kt\xfc ve Sunwell parlayarak var oldu. \xc7evresinde Quel'Thalas ve ba\u015fkenti Silvermoon y\xfckseldi. Ay yerine g\xfcne\u015fin alt\u0131nda ya\u015fayan s\xfcrg\xfcnler y\xfczy\u0131llar i\xe7inde de\u011fi\u015fti ve y\xfcksek elfler, yani quel'dorei oldu.","Toprak bo\u015f de\u011fildi. Amani trollerinin kutsal sayd\u0131\u011f\u0131 kadim harabeleri bar\u0131nd\u0131r\u0131yordu ve troller yeni gelenlere ezici say\u0131larla sald\u0131rd\u0131. Elfler onlar\u0131 b\xfcy\xfcyle durdurdu ve Amani\u2019yi uzak tutan, r\xfcn ta\u015flar\u0131ndan bir bariyer olan Ban'dinoriel\u2019i kurdu. Yakla\u015f\u0131k d\xf6rt bin y\u0131l boyunca Quel'Thalas onun ard\u0131nda zenginle\u015fti; troller ise intikam i\xe7in bekledi."]},links:{loreIds:['term:queldorei','term:sunwell','term:highborne','term:ley-lines'],zoneIds:['ashenvale'],raceIds:['troll'],classIds:['mage']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)("Quel'Thalas"),(0,n.wiki)('Sunwell'),(0,n.wiki)("Dath'Remar Sunstrider"),(0,n.wiki)('High elf'),(0,n.wiki)("Ban'dinoriel")],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'arathor-and-the-troll-wars',order:7,era:'elder-kingdoms',when:{en:'About 2,800 years before the Dark Portal',tr:'Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten yakla\u015f\u0131k 2.800 y\u0131l \xf6nce'},title:{en:'Arathor and the Troll Wars',tr:'Arathor ve Trol Sava\u015flar\u0131'},summary:{en:"Humanity's scattered tribes united under King Thoradin, and an alliance with the elves broke the Amani Empire at the foot of the Alterac Mountains.",tr:'\u0130nsanl\u0131\u011f\u0131n da\u011f\u0131n\u0131k kabileleri Kral Thoradin\u2019in \xf6nderli\u011finde birle\u015fti; elflerle kurulan ittifak Amani \u0130mparatorlu\u011fu\u2019nu Alterac Da\u011flar\u0131\u2019n\u0131n ete\u011finde k\u0131rd\u0131.'},body:{en:["For millennia the human tribes of the Eastern Kingdoms fought one another while Amani raiders struck from the north. Around 2,800 years before the Dark Portal, Thoradin of the Arathi tribe saw that a divided humanity would be destroyed. Through marriages, promises and conquest he united the tribes into the kingdom of Arathor and built its capital, the fortress-city of Strom, in today's Arathi Highlands.","The Amani, revived with help from the Zandalari, struck at Quel'Thalas in vast numbers. The elves turned to Arathor. In exchange for human soldiers, they agreed to teach magic to a hundred chosen humans, the first human magi. Elves and humans together crushed the Amani army at the foot of the Alterac Mountains, and the magi's fire scattered the trolls so thoroughly that their empire never recovered.","In gratitude, the elves of Quel'Thalas pledged loyalty to the bloodline of Arathor's kings. Strom flourished, and its people spread across the north. The Amani would rise again many times, and in the Hinterlands and the Arathi Highlands forest troll tribes still haunt the ruins of that old war."],tr:['Binlerce y\u0131l boyunca Do\u011fu Krall\u0131klar\u0131\u2019n\u0131n insan kabileleri birbirleriyle sava\u015f\u0131rken Amani ak\u0131nc\u0131lar\u0131 kuzeyden sald\u0131r\u0131yordu. Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten yakla\u015f\u0131k 2.800 y\u0131l \xf6nce Arathi kabilesinden Thoradin, b\xf6l\xfcnm\xfc\u015f bir insanl\u0131\u011f\u0131n yok olaca\u011f\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6rd\xfc. Evlilikler, vaatler ve fetihle kabileleri Arathor krall\u0131\u011f\u0131nda birle\u015ftirdi ve ba\u015fkenti, kale-\u015fehir Strom\u2019u bug\xfcnk\xfc Arathi Highlands\u2019te kurdu.',"Zandalari\u2019nin yard\u0131m\u0131yla yeniden g\xfc\xe7lenen Amani, Quel'Thalas\u2019a muazzam say\u0131larla sald\u0131rd\u0131. Elfler Arathor\u2019a ba\u015fvurdu. \u0130nsan askerlere kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131k se\xe7ilmi\u015f y\xfcz insana b\xfcy\xfc \xf6\u011fretmeyi kabul ettiler; bunlar ilk insan b\xfcy\xfcc\xfclerdi. Elfler ve insanlar Amani ordusunu Alterac Da\u011flar\u0131\u2019n\u0131n ete\u011finde birlikte ezdi; b\xfcy\xfcc\xfclerin ate\u015fi trolleri \xf6yle da\u011f\u0131tt\u0131 ki imparatorluklar\u0131 bir daha toparlanamad\u0131.","Minnettar Quel'Thalas elfleri, Arathor krallar\u0131n\u0131n soyuna sadakat yemini etti. Strom geli\u015fti ve halk\u0131 kuzeye yay\u0131ld\u0131. Amani pek \xe7ok kez yeniden ayaklanacakt\u0131; Hinterlands\u2019te ve Arathi Highlands\u2019te orman trol\xfc kabileleri o eski sava\u015f\u0131n harabelerinde h\xe2l\xe2 dola\u015f\u0131yor."]},links:{loreIds:['term:queldorei','term:loa'],zoneIds:['arathi-highlands','alterac-mountains','hinterlands'],raceIds:['human','troll'],classIds:['mage']},image:'race:human',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Arathor'),(0,n.wiki)('Troll Wars'),(0,n.wiki)('Thoradin'),(0,n.wiki)('Stromgarde Keep')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'guardians-and-the-seven-kingdoms',order:8,era:'elder-kingdoms',when:{en:'The millennia after the Troll Wars',tr:'Trol Sava\u015flar\u0131\u2019n\u0131 izleyen biny\u0131llar'},title:{en:'Guardians and the Seven Kingdoms',tr:'Muhaf\u0131zlar ve Yedi Krall\u0131k'},summary:{en:'Human magic drew demons, so the magi founded Dalaran and chose Guardians to fight in secret, while Arathor split into seven kingdoms.',tr:'\u0130nsan b\xfcy\xfcs\xfc iblisleri \xe7ekti; b\xfcy\xfcc\xfcler Dalaran\u2019\u0131 kurdu ve gizlice sava\u015facak Muhaf\u0131zlar se\xe7ti, Arathor ise yedi krall\u0131\u011fa b\xf6l\xfcnd\xfc.'},body:{en:["Magic spread through Arathor faster than wisdom. The magi's spells thinned the walls of the world and drew the attention of demons, so the high elves and the human magi formed the Council of Tirisfal. In secret, the council chose a single Guardian to hold its combined power and hunt the agents of the Burning Legion.","The magi also built a city of their own, Dalaran, where the Kirin Tor would rule. Meanwhile Arathor's heirs moved away from Strom, and over the centuries the empire broke into seven human kingdoms: Lordaeron, Stromgarde, Gilneas, Alterac, Kul Tiras, Dalaran and, in the south, Stormwind, which was long called the kingdom of Azeroth.","The most famous Guardian was Aegwynn, who in Northrend struck down an avatar of Sargeras himself and sealed its body in a tomb beneath the sea. She never knew that the dark titan's spirit had slipped into her. When she bore a son, Medivh, the spirit passed to him, and the last Guardian came of age with a traitor hidden in his soul. From his tower of Karazhan he would one day open the door for the orcs."],tr:['B\xfcy\xfc, Arathor\u2019da bilgelikten h\u0131zl\u0131 yay\u0131ld\u0131. B\xfcy\xfcc\xfclerin b\xfcy\xfcleri d\xfcnyan\u0131n duvarlar\u0131n\u0131 inceltti ve iblislerin dikkatini \xe7ekti; bu y\xfczden y\xfcksek elfler ve insan b\xfcy\xfcc\xfcler Tirisfal Konseyi\u2019ni kurdu. Konsey gizlice, birle\u015fik g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc ta\u015f\u0131yacak ve Yanan Lejyon\u2019un ajanlar\u0131n\u0131 avlayacak tek bir Muhaf\u0131z (Guardian) se\xe7ti.','B\xfcy\xfcc\xfcler kendilerine ait bir \u015fehir de kurdu: Kirin Tor\u2019un y\xf6netece\u011fi Dalaran. Bu arada Arathor\u2019un varisleri Strom\u2019dan uzakla\u015ft\u0131 ve y\xfczy\u0131llar i\xe7inde imparatorluk yedi insan krall\u0131\u011f\u0131na b\xf6l\xfcnd\xfc: Lordaeron, Stromgarde, Gilneas, Alterac, Kul Tiras, Dalaran ve g\xfcneyde uzun s\xfcre Azeroth krall\u0131\u011f\u0131 diye an\u0131lan Stormwind.','En \xfcnl\xfc Muhaf\u0131z Aegwynn\u2019di; Northrend\u2019de bizzat Sargeras\u2019\u0131n bir avatar\u0131n\u0131 yere serdi ve bedenini denizin alt\u0131ndaki bir mezara m\xfch\xfcrledi. Karanl\u0131k titan\u0131n ruhunun i\xe7ine s\u0131zd\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 hi\xe7 bilmedi. Medivh ad\u0131nda bir o\u011flu oldu\u011funda ruh ona ge\xe7ti ve son Muhaf\u0131z, ruhunda gizlenmi\u015f bir hainle b\xfcy\xfcd\xfc. Bir g\xfcn Karazhan kulesinden orklara kap\u0131y\u0131 a\xe7acakt\u0131.']},links:{loreIds:['term:guardian-of-tirisfal','term:kirin-tor','item:atiesh'],zoneIds:['alterac-mountains','deadwind-pass','arathi-highlands'],instanceIds:['city-of-dalaran'],classIds:['mage'],raceIds:['human']},image:'class:mage',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Council of Tirisfal'),(0,n.wiki)('Guardian of Tirisfal'),(0,n.wiki)('Aegwynn'),(0,n.wiki)('Medivh'),(0,n.wiki)('Dalaran')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'war-of-the-three-hammers',order:9,era:'elder-kingdoms',when:{en:'About 230 years before the Dark Portal',tr:'Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten yakla\u015f\u0131k 230 y\u0131l \xf6nce'},title:{en:'The War of the Three Hammers',tr:'\xdc\xe7 \xc7eki\xe7 Sava\u015f\u0131'},summary:{en:"Ironforge's three dwarf clans fought for the throne, and a defeated sorcerer-thane summoned Ragnaros, burning the land into Blackrock Mountain.",tr:'Ironforge\u2019un \xfc\xe7 c\xfcce klan\u0131 taht i\xe7in sava\u015ft\u0131; yenilen bir b\xfcy\xfcc\xfc-thane Ragnaros\u2019u \xe7a\u011f\u0131rd\u0131 ve topraklar\u0131 yakarak Blackrock Da\u011f\u0131\u2019n\u0131 yaratt\u0131.'},body:{en:["Beneath the snows of Dun Morogh the dwarves carved Ironforge, a kingdom of stone and craft that traced its roots to the titans' earthen. Three clans shared it uneasily: the Bronzebeards, the Wildhammers and the sorcery-loving Dark Irons. When High King Modimus Anvilmar died, some 230 years before the Dark Portal, their rivalry exploded into civil war.",'The Bronzebeards won and drove the others out. The Wildhammers built Grim Batol to the east, and the Dark Irons founded a kingdom of their own to the south, in the Redridge Mountains. Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan could not accept defeat. He struck at both rivals at once, but his armies were broken, and his wife Modgud fell at Grim Batol.',"In desperation Thaurissan reached for a greater power and summoned Ragnaros the Firelord, an elemental lord the titans had imprisoned. The Firelord's arrival killed the thane, tore the land into the Searing Gorge and the Burning Steppes, and raised Blackrock Mountain, where the surviving Dark Irons became his slaves. The Wildhammers abandoned cursed Grim Batol for the Hinterlands. Their gnome neighbours, whose city of Gnomeregan lay close by, became Ironforge's firm friends."],tr:['Dun Morogh\u2019un karlar\u0131 alt\u0131nda c\xfcceler Ironforge\u2019u oydu: k\xf6kleri titanlar\u0131n earthen\u2019lar\u0131na uzanan, ta\u015f ve zanaat krall\u0131\u011f\u0131. \xdc\xe7 klan onu huzursuzca payla\u015f\u0131yordu: Bronzebeard\u2019lar, Wildhammer\u2019lar ve b\xfcy\xfcye d\xfc\u015fk\xfcn Dark Iron\u2019lar. Y\xfcce Kral Modimus Anvilmar, Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten yakla\u015f\u0131k 230 y\u0131l \xf6nce \xf6ld\xfc\u011f\xfcnde bu rekabet bir i\xe7 sava\u015fa d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc.','Bronzebeard\u2019lar kazand\u0131 ve di\u011ferlerini kovdu. Wildhammer\u2019lar do\u011fuda Grim Batol\u2019u kurdu; Dark Iron\u2019lar ise g\xfcneyde, Redridge Da\u011flar\u0131\u2019nda kendi krall\u0131klar\u0131n\u0131 kurdu. B\xfcy\xfcc\xfc-Thane Thaurissan yenilgiyi kabullenemedi. \u0130ki rakibine ayn\u0131 anda sald\u0131rd\u0131 ama ordular\u0131 da\u011f\u0131ld\u0131 ve kar\u0131s\u0131 Modgud Grim Batol\u2019da d\xfc\u015ft\xfc.','\xc7aresizlik i\xe7inde Thaurissan daha b\xfcy\xfck bir g\xfcce uzand\u0131 ve titanlar\u0131n hapsetti\u011fi bir elemental lord olan Ate\u015f Lordu Ragnaros\u2019u \xe7a\u011f\u0131rd\u0131. Ate\u015f Lordu\u2019nun geli\u015fi thane\u2019i \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc, topra\u011f\u0131 y\u0131rtarak Searing Gorge\u2019u ve Burning Steppes\u2019i olu\u015fturdu ve Blackrock Da\u011f\u0131\u2019n\u0131 y\xfckseltti; hayatta kalan Dark Iron\u2019lar onun k\xf6lesi oldu. Wildhammer\u2019lar lanetli Grim Batol\u2019u b\u0131rak\u0131p Hinterlands\u2019e yerle\u015fti. \u015eehirleri Gnomeregan hemen yak\u0131nda olan gnom kom\u015fular\u0131 ise Ironforge\u2019un sad\u0131k dostlar\u0131 oldu.']},links:{loreIds:['term:elemental-lords','item:sulfuras'],zoneIds:['dun-morogh','redridge-mountains','wetlands','searing-gorge','burning-steppes','hinterlands'],instanceIds:['blackrock-depths','gnomeregan'],raceIds:['dwarf','gnome']},image:'race:dwarf',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('War of the Three Hammers'),(0,n.wiki)('Ironforge'),(0,n.wiki)('Ragnaros'),(0,n.wiki)('Dark Iron clan'),(0,n.wiki)('Grim Batol')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'corruption-of-the-orcs',order:10,era:'draenor',when:{en:'The decades before the Dark Portal',tr:'Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten \xf6nceki on y\u0131llar'},title:{en:'The Corruption of the Orcs',tr:'Orklar\u0131n Yozla\u015fmas\u0131'},summary:{en:"On distant Draenor, Kil'jaeden turned the shamanistic orc clans into a bloodthirsty Horde bound by demon blood.",tr:"Uzak Draenor\u2019da Kil'jaeden, \u015famanist ork klanlar\u0131n\u0131 iblis kan\u0131yla ba\u011fl\u0131, kana susam\u0131\u015f bir Horde\u2019a d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc."},body:{en:["On the world of Draenor the orcs lived as proud clans of hunters and shaman, honoring their ancestors and the spirits of the elements. They shared their world uneasily with the draenei, the eredar who had fled Argus with Velen. Kil'jaeden had never stopped hunting those exiles, and in the orcs he saw a weapon.","Disguised as the spirit of Ner'zhul's dead wife, the demon lord whispered to the elder shaman and turned him against the draenei. When Ner'zhul hesitated, Kil'jaeden found a more willing student in Gul'dan, who founded the secret Shadow Council and taught the orcs fel magic; they were the first warlocks. The elements fell silent, and the orcs' green land began to die.","At a great gathering the clan chieftains drank the blood of the pit lord Mannoroth, and Grom Hellscream of the Warsong clan drank first. Filled with demonic fury, the united Horde fell upon the draenei and nearly wiped them out. Only Durotan's Frostwolf clan stood partly apart. When the killing was over, Gul'dan needed a new war, and Kil'jaeden's master already had one waiting on Azeroth."],tr:["Draenor d\xfcnyas\u0131nda orklar, atalar\u0131n\u0131 ve elementlerin ruhlar\u0131n\u0131 onurland\u0131ran gururlu avc\u0131 ve Shaman klanlar\u0131 olarak ya\u015f\u0131yordu. D\xfcnyalar\u0131n\u0131 Velen\u2019le Argus\u2019tan ka\xe7m\u0131\u015f eredar olan draenei ile huzursuzca payla\u015f\u0131yorlard\u0131. Kil'jaeden bu s\xfcrg\xfcnleri avlamaktan hi\xe7 vazge\xe7memi\u015fti ve orklarda bir silah g\xf6rd\xfc.","\u0130blis lordu, Ner'zhul\u2019un \xf6lm\xfc\u015f kar\u0131s\u0131n\u0131n ruhu k\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131na girerek ya\u015fl\u0131 Shaman\u2019a f\u0131s\u0131ldad\u0131 ve onu draenei\u2019ye kar\u015f\u0131 k\u0131\u015fk\u0131rtt\u0131. Ner'zhul teredd\xfct edince Kil'jaeden daha istekli bir \xf6\u011frenci buldu: gizli G\xf6lge Konseyi\u2019ni (Shadow Council) kuran ve orklara fel b\xfcy\xfcs\xfcn\xfc \xf6\u011freten Gul'dan; ilk Warlock\u2019lar onlard\u0131. Elementler sustu ve orklar\u0131n ye\u015fil topraklar\u0131 \xf6lmeye ba\u015flad\u0131.","B\xfcy\xfck bir toplant\u0131da klan reisleri pit lord Mannoroth\u2019un kan\u0131n\u0131 i\xe7ti; ilk i\xe7en Warsong klan\u0131ndan Grom Hellscream\u2019di. \u0130blis \xf6fkesiyle dolan birle\u015fik Horde, draenei\u2019nin \xfczerine \xe7ulland\u0131 ve onlar\u0131 neredeyse yok etti. Yaln\u0131zca Durotan\u2019\u0131n Frostwolf klan\u0131 k\u0131smen uzak durdu. Katliam bitti\u011finde Gul'dan\u2019\u0131n yeni bir sava\u015fa ihtiyac\u0131 vard\u0131 ve Kil'jaeden\u2019in efendisi Azeroth\u2019ta \xe7oktan bir sava\u015f haz\u0131rlam\u0131\u015ft\u0131."]},links:{loreIds:['term:fel','term:burning-legion','item:gorehowl'],raceIds:['orc'],classIds:['warlock','shaman']},image:'class:warlock',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Old Horde'),(0,n.wiki)("Ner'zhul"),(0,n.wiki)("Gul'dan"),(0,n.wiki)('Shadow Council'),(0,n.wiki)('Draenor')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'the-first-war',order:11,era:'first-war',when:{en:'Year 0: the Dark Portal opens',tr:'0. y\u0131l: Kara Ge\xe7it a\xe7\u0131l\u0131r'},title:{en:'The Dark Portal and the First War',tr:'Kara Ge\xe7it ve Birinci Sava\u015f'},summary:{en:'Medivh helped the orcs open the Dark Portal, and the Horde overran the kingdom of Stormwind.',tr:'Medivh orklar\u0131n Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019i a\xe7mas\u0131na yard\u0131m etti ve Horde, Stormwind krall\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 yerle bir etti.'},body:{en:["Guided by the possessed Medivh, Gul'dan's warlocks and the Guardian opened a rift between Draenor and Azeroth in the Black Morass, the swamp that later withered into the Blasted Lands. Orcs poured through what became known as the Dark Portal, and their scouts soon found the rich fields of the kingdom of Azeroth, today's Stormwind.","King Llane Wrynn and his champion Anduin Lothar fought back for years. Medivh's own apprentice Khadgar discovered his master's betrayal, and with Lothar and the half-orc Garona he confronted the Guardian in Karazhan and killed him. The victory came too late. The Horde's warbands burned their way across the kingdom, and within the Horde the cunning Orgrim Doomhammer struck down Blackhand and became warchief.","Garona, bound by Gul'dan's spells, assassinated King Llane, and Stormwind City fell and burned. Lothar gathered the survivors, among them Llane's young son Varian, and led them across the sea to Lordaeron. Far to the east, in the Riverglades, a region that exists only in Forever, the Horde razed the town of Sunnyglade and carried its survivors off as slaves."],tr:["Ele ge\xe7irilmi\u015f Medivh\u2019in rehberli\u011finde Gul'dan\u2019\u0131n Warlock\u2019lar\u0131 ve Muhaf\u0131z, Black Morass\u2019ta (sonradan kuruyup Blasted Lands\u2019e d\xf6n\xfc\u015fen batakl\u0131k) Draenor ile Azeroth aras\u0131nda bir yar\u0131k a\xe7t\u0131. Orklar Kara Ge\xe7it (Dark Portal) diye an\u0131lacak bu kap\u0131dan ak\u0131n etti ve \xf6nc\xfcleri k\u0131sa s\xfcrede Azeroth krall\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n, bug\xfcnk\xfc Stormwind\u2019in bereketli tarlalar\u0131n\u0131 buldu.",'Kral Llane Wrynn ve \u015fampiyonu Anduin Lothar y\u0131llarca direndi. Medivh\u2019in \xe7\u0131ra\u011f\u0131 Khadgar, ustas\u0131n\u0131n ihanetini ke\u015ffetti; Lothar ve yar\u0131 ork Garona ile birlikte Karazhan\u2019da Muhaf\u0131z\u2019la y\xfczle\u015fip onu \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfcler. Zafer \xe7ok ge\xe7 gelmi\u015fti. Horde\u2019un sava\u015f gruplar\u0131 krall\u0131\u011f\u0131 ba\u015ftan ba\u015fa yak\u0131p y\u0131kt\u0131 ve Horde\u2019un i\xe7inde kurnaz Orgrim Doomhammer, Blackhand\u2019i yenerek sava\u015f reisi (warchief) oldu.',"Gul'dan\u2019\u0131n b\xfcy\xfcleriyle ba\u011fl\u0131 Garona, Kral Llane\u2019i \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc; Stormwind \u015fehri d\xfc\u015ft\xfc ve yand\u0131. Lothar, aralar\u0131nda Llane\u2019in k\xfc\xe7\xfck o\u011flu Varian\u2019\u0131n da bulundu\u011fu sa\u011f kalanlar\u0131 toplad\u0131 ve denizi a\u015farak Lordaeron\u2019a g\xf6t\xfcrd\xfc. \xc7ok do\u011fuda, yaln\u0131zca Forever\u2019da bulunan Riverglades b\xf6lgesinde Horde, Sunnyglade kasabas\u0131n\u0131 yerle bir etti ve sa\u011f kalanlar\u0131 k\xf6le olarak g\xf6t\xfcrd\xfc."]},links:{loreIds:['term:dark-portal','term:guardian-of-tirisfal','item:book-of-medivh','item:doomhammer'],zoneIds:['blasted-lands','elwynn-forest','deadwind-pass','riverglades'],raceIds:['human','orc']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('First War'),(0,n.wiki)('Dark Portal'),(0,n.wiki)('Medivh'),(0,n.wiki)('Anduin Lothar'),n.FOREVER.riverglades],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'the-second-war',order:12,era:'second-war',when:{en:'About five to six years after the Dark Portal',tr:'Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten yakla\u015f\u0131k be\u015f-alt\u0131 y\u0131l sonra'},title:{en:'The Second War',tr:'\u0130kinci Sava\u015f'},summary:{en:"The human kingdoms, elves, dwarves and gnomes united as the Alliance of Lordaeron and broke Doomhammer's Horde at Blackrock Spire.",tr:'\u0130nsan krall\u0131klar\u0131, elfler, c\xfcceler ve gnomlar Lordaeron \u0130ttifak\u0131 olarak birle\u015fti ve Doomhammer\u2019\u0131n Horde\u2019unu Blackrock Spire\u2019da k\u0131rd\u0131.'},body:{en:["Lothar's warning moved King Terenas Menethil of Lordaeron to call the human kingdoms together. They formed the Alliance of Lordaeron with Lothar as supreme commander; the dwarves of Ironforge, the gnomes and, honoring their old oath to Arathor's bloodline, the high elves of Quel'Thalas joined them. To give the soldiers hope, Archbishop Alonsus Faol founded the Knights of the Silver Hand, the first paladins, with Uther the Lightbringer at their head.","Doomhammer's Horde had grown too. Ogres, Amani trolls under Zul'jin and goblin sappers fought beside the orcs; the Dragonmaw clan used Deathwing's Dragon Soul to enslave red dragons at Grim Batol; Gul'dan raised the first death knights. The Horde overran Khaz Modan, burned parts of Quel'Thalas and laid siege to Lordaeron's capital.","At the decisive moment Gul'dan betrayed Doomhammer and sailed off to raise the Tomb of Sargeras, taking two clans with him, the Stormreavers and the Twilight's Hammer. The weakened Horde fell back to Blackrock Mountain. In the battle at Blackrock Spire, Doomhammer killed Lothar, but Lothar's lieutenant Turalyon broke the Horde, and Khadgar destroyed the Dark Portal. The surviving orcs were herded into internment camps. In Forever's Riverglades, Twilight's Hammer ogres and Stormreaver orcs fleeing the Tomb made a new home."],tr:["Lothar\u2019\u0131n uyar\u0131s\u0131, Lordaeron Kral\u0131 Terenas Menethil\u2019i insan krall\u0131klar\u0131n\u0131 bir araya \xe7a\u011f\u0131rmaya y\xf6neltti. Lothar\u2019\u0131 ba\u015fkomutan yaparak Lordaeron \u0130ttifak\u0131\u2019n\u0131 kurdular; Ironforge c\xfcceleri, gnomlar ve Arathor soyuna verdikleri eski yemine sad\u0131k kalan Quel'Thalas\u2019\u0131n y\xfcksek elfleri de kat\u0131ld\u0131. Askerlere umut vermek i\xe7in Ba\u015fpiskopos Alonsus Faol, ba\u015f\u0131na Uther the Lightbringer\u2019\u0131 getirerek ilk Paladin\u2019leri, G\xfcm\xfc\u015f El \u015e\xf6valyeleri\u2019ni (Knights of the Silver Hand) kurdu.","Doomhammer\u2019\u0131n Horde\u2019u da b\xfcy\xfcm\xfc\u015ft\xfc. Orklar\u0131n yan\u0131nda ogreler, Zul'jin \xf6nderli\u011finde Amani trolleri ve goblin istihk\xe2mc\u0131lar\u0131 sava\u015f\u0131yordu; Dragonmaw klan\u0131, Deathwing\u2019in Dragon Soul\u2019uyla Grim Batol\u2019da k\u0131z\u0131l ejderhalar\u0131 k\xf6lele\u015ftirdi; Gul'dan ilk death knight\u2019lar\u0131 yaratt\u0131. Horde, Khaz Modan\u2019\u0131 ele ge\xe7irdi, Quel'Thalas\u2019\u0131n bir k\u0131sm\u0131n\u0131 yakt\u0131 ve Lordaeron\u2019un ba\u015fkentini ku\u015fatt\u0131.","Kritik anda Gul'dan, Doomhammer\u2019a ihanet edip Stormreaver ve Twilight's Hammer klanlar\u0131n\u0131 yan\u0131na alarak Sargeras\u2019\u0131n Mezar\u0131\u2019n\u0131 (Tomb of Sargeras) y\xfckseltmeye yelken a\xe7t\u0131. Zay\u0131flayan Horde, Blackrock Da\u011f\u0131\u2019na \xe7ekildi. Blackrock Spire sava\u015f\u0131nda Doomhammer, Lothar\u2019\u0131 \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc; ama Lothar\u2019\u0131n yard\u0131mc\u0131s\u0131 Turalyon Horde\u2019u k\u0131rd\u0131 ve Khadgar Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019i yok etti. Hayatta kalan orklar toplama kamplar\u0131na s\xfcr\xfcld\xfc. Forever\u2019\u0131n Riverglades b\xf6lgesine ise Mezar\u2019dan ka\xe7an Twilight's Hammer ogreleri ve Stormreaver orklar\u0131 yerle\u015fti."]},links:{loreIds:['term:silver-hand','term:holy-light','term:twilights-hammer','item:demon-soul','item:doomhammer'],zoneIds:['hillsbrad-foothills','wetlands','burning-steppes','arathi-highlands','riverglades'],instanceIds:['lower-blackrock-spire'],raceIds:['human','dwarf','gnome','orc','troll'],classIds:['paladin'],factionIds:['alliance']},image:'class:paladin',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Second War'),(0,n.wiki)('Alliance of Lordaeron'),(0,n.wiki)('Knights of the Silver Hand'),(0,n.wiki)('Siege of Blackrock Spire'),n.FOREVER.riverglades],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'beyond-the-dark-portal',order:13,era:'interwar',when:{en:'Shortly after the Second War',tr:'\u0130kinci Sava\u015f\u2019tan k\u0131sa s\xfcre sonra'},title:{en:'Beyond the Dark Portal',tr:'Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019in \xd6tesinde'},summary:{en:"Ner'zhul reopened the portal and tore Draenor apart, and Kil'jaeden remade the old shaman into the Lich King.",tr:"Ner'zhul ge\xe7idi yeniden a\xe7\u0131p Draenor\u2019u par\xe7alad\u0131; Kil'jaeden de ya\u015fl\u0131 Shaman\u2019\u0131 Lich King\u2019e d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcrd\xfc."},body:{en:["With Gul'dan dead and the Horde imprisoned, old Ner'zhul gathered the orcs who remained on Draenor. He reopened the Dark Portal and sent raiders into Azeroth to steal powerful artifacts, hoping to open gateways to new worlds where his people could escape.","The Alliance answered with an expedition through the portal under Turalyon and Khadgar, joined by the ranger Alleria Windrunner, the dwarf Kurdran Wildhammer and the warrior Danath Trollbane. They fought the new Horde across Draenor, but Ner'zhul's portals were already tearing the world apart. To save Azeroth, the expedition destroyed the Dark Portal from the far side, trapping itself in the shattered remains that would become Outland.","Ner'zhul escaped through one of his rifts, straight into the hands of Kil'jaeden. The demon tore away his body but kept his spirit, bound it into enchanted armor and sealed it in a block of ice together with the runeblade Frostmourne. Hurled into the frozen wastes of Northrend, the Frozen Throne became the seat of a new power: the Lich King, whose task was to spread a plague of undeath and soften Azeroth for the Legion's return."],tr:["Gul'dan \xf6lm\xfc\u015f, Horde esir d\xfc\u015fm\xfc\u015fken ya\u015fl\u0131 Ner'zhul Draenor\u2019da kalan orklar\u0131 toplad\u0131. Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019i yeniden a\xe7t\u0131 ve halk\u0131n\u0131n ka\xe7abilece\u011fi yeni d\xfcnyalara kap\u0131lar a\xe7mak umuduyla g\xfc\xe7l\xfc eserleri \xe7almalar\u0131 i\xe7in Azeroth\u2019a ak\u0131nc\u0131lar yollad\u0131.","\u0130ttifak, Turalyon ve Khadgar komutas\u0131nda; korucu Alleria Windrunner, c\xfcce Kurdran Wildhammer ve sava\u015f\xe7\u0131 Danath Trollbane\u2019in de kat\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131 bir seferi ge\xe7itten g\xf6nderdi. Yeni Horde\u2019la Draenor\u2019un d\xf6rt bir yan\u0131nda sava\u015ft\u0131lar; ama Ner'zhul\u2019un ge\xe7itleri d\xfcnyay\u0131 \xe7oktan par\xe7al\u0131yordu. Azeroth\u2019u kurtarmak i\xe7in sefer heyeti Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019i \xf6b\xfcr taraftan yok etti ve kendini, sonradan Outland olacak parampar\xe7a kal\u0131nt\u0131larda mahsur b\u0131rakt\u0131.","Ner'zhul yar\u0131klar\u0131ndan birinden ka\xe7t\u0131 ve do\u011frudan Kil'jaeden\u2019in eline d\xfc\u015ft\xfc. \u0130blis bedenini par\xe7alad\u0131 ama ruhunu korudu; onu b\xfcy\xfcl\xfc bir z\u0131rha ba\u011flad\u0131 ve r\xfcn k\u0131l\u0131c\u0131 Frostmourne ile birlikte bir buz k\xfctlesine m\xfch\xfcrledi. Northrend\u2019in donmu\u015f \xe7\xf6llerine f\u0131rlat\u0131lan Frozen Throne, yeni bir g\xfcc\xfcn taht\u0131 oldu: g\xf6revi bir \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck vebas\u0131 yay\u0131p Azeroth\u2019u Lejyon\u2019un d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcne haz\u0131rlamak olan Lich King."]},links:{loreIds:['term:dark-portal','term:lich-king','item:frostmourne','item:book-of-medivh','item:skull-of-guldan'],raceIds:['orc'],zoneIds:['blasted-lands']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Beyond the Dark Portal'),(0,n.wiki)("Ner'zhul"),(0,n.wiki)('Outland'),(0,n.wiki)('Lich King'),(0,n.wiki)('Frozen Throne')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'thrall-and-the-new-horde',order:14,era:'interwar',when:{en:'The years before the Third War',tr:'\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019tan \xf6nceki y\u0131llar'},title:{en:'Thrall and the New Horde',tr:'Thrall ve Yeni Horde'},summary:{en:'An orc raised as a slave escaped Durnholde, rediscovered shamanism and freed his people from the internment camps.',tr:'K\xf6le olarak b\xfcy\xfct\xfclen bir ork Durnholde\u2019dan ka\xe7t\u0131, \u015famanl\u0131\u011f\u0131 yeniden ke\u015ffetti ve halk\u0131n\u0131 toplama kamplar\u0131ndan kurtard\u0131.'},body:{en:['In the internment camps the orcs sank into a strange lethargy as the demonic fury drained out of them. Lord Aedelas Blackmoore of Durnholde Keep, in the Hillsbrad Foothills, had found an orphaned orc infant years before and raised him as a gladiator and a future weapon. He named the boy Thrall, a word for slave. Only Taretha Foxton, a servant girl, treated him with kindness, and with her help Thrall finally escaped.',"Free for the first time, Thrall sought out the legends of his own people. Grom Hellscream showed him what an orc could be, the aged Orgrim Doomhammer made him his second, and among the Frostwolf clan in the Alterac Mountains the shaman Drek'Thar taught him to speak with the elements. There he learned that he was the son of Durotan, the Frostwolf chieftain.",'Thrall, Grom and Doomhammer freed camp after camp. Doomhammer fell in battle and passed his black armor and hammer to Thrall, who became warchief of a new Horde built on honor and shamanism rather than demon blood. At Durnholde he defeated Blackmoore, though Taretha did not survive. Now Thrall wanted only a homeland where his people could live in peace.'],tr:['Toplama kamplar\u0131nda iblis \xf6fkesi bedenlerinden \xe7ekildik\xe7e orklar tuhaf bir uyu\u015fuklu\u011fa g\xf6m\xfcld\xfc. Hillsbrad Foothills\u2019teki Durnholde Kalesi\u2019nin efendisi Lord Aedelas Blackmoore, y\u0131llar \xf6nce \xf6ks\xfcz bir ork bebe\u011fi bulmu\u015f ve onu bir gladyat\xf6r, gelece\u011fin silah\u0131 olarak yeti\u015ftirmi\u015fti. \xc7ocu\u011fa \u2018k\xf6le\u2019 anlam\u0131na gelen Thrall ad\u0131n\u0131 verdi. Ona yaln\u0131zca hizmet\xe7i k\u0131z Taretha Foxton iyi davrand\u0131 ve Thrall sonunda onun yard\u0131m\u0131yla ka\xe7t\u0131.',"Hayat\u0131nda ilk kez \xf6zg\xfcr kalan Thrall kendi halk\u0131n\u0131n efsanelerinin pe\u015fine d\xfc\u015ft\xfc. Grom Hellscream ona bir orkun nas\u0131l olabilece\u011fini g\xf6sterdi, ya\u015fl\u0131 Orgrim Doomhammer onu sa\u011f kolu yapt\u0131 ve Alterac Da\u011flar\u0131\u2019ndaki Frostwolf klan\u0131nda Shaman Drek'Thar ona elementlerle konu\u015fmay\u0131 \xf6\u011fretti. Orada Frostwolf reisi Durotan\u2019\u0131n o\u011flu oldu\u011funu \xf6\u011frendi.",'Thrall, Grom ve Doomhammer kamplar\u0131 birer birer \xf6zg\xfcrle\u015ftirdi. Doomhammer sava\u015fta d\xfc\u015ft\xfc ve kara z\u0131rh\u0131n\u0131 ile \xe7ekicini Thrall\u2019a b\u0131rakt\u0131; Thrall, iblis kan\u0131 yerine onur ve \u015famanl\u0131k \xfczerine kurulu yeni bir Horde\u2019un sava\u015f reisi oldu. Durnholde\u2019da Blackmoore\u2019u alt etti, ama Taretha hayatta kalamad\u0131. Thrall art\u0131k yaln\u0131zca halk\u0131n\u0131n bar\u0131\u015f i\xe7inde ya\u015fayabilece\u011fi bir yurt istiyordu.']},links:{loreIds:['item:doomhammer'],zoneIds:['hillsbrad-foothills','alterac-mountains'],raceIds:['orc'],classIds:['shaman','warrior'],factionIds:['horde']},image:'class:shaman',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Thrall'),(0,n.wiki)('Internment camp'),(0,n.wiki)('Durnholde Keep'),(0,n.wiki)('Frostwolf clan')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'the-lich-king-and-the-plague',order:15,era:'interwar',when:{en:'Leading up to the Third War',tr:'\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019a giden y\u0131llar'},title:{en:'The Lich King and the Plague',tr:'Lich King ve Veba'},summary:{en:"From Northrend the Lich King reached south, and the archmage Kel'Thuzad spread a plague of undeath through Lordaeron's grain.",tr:"Lich King Northrend\u2019den g\xfcneye uzand\u0131; ba\u015fb\xfcy\xfcc\xfc Kel'Thuzad da Lordaeron\u2019un tah\u0131l\u0131 arac\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131yla bir \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfck vebas\u0131 yayd\u0131."},body:{en:["Trapped in the Frozen Throne, the Lich King's mind still reached across Northrend. He conquered the spider kingdom of Azjol-Nerub, raised its people as servants and built a fortress around his throne in Icecrown. Then he turned his gaze south, to the war-weary human kingdoms.","In Dalaran the respected archmage Kel'Thuzad had grown obsessed with necromancy. When the Kirin Tor rejected his studies, he answered the Lich King's call, traveled to Northrend and returned as his prophet. He founded the Cult of the Damned, promising the poor of Lordaeron equality and eternal life, and used its members to spread a plague hidden in grain shipments.","The plague killed and then raised its victims as mindless undead, the Scourge. Villages in the north of Lordaeron fell one after another while the kingdoms argued over taxes and the cost of the internment camps. By the time the Kirin Tor and the Silver Hand understood the danger, the plague had spread across Lordaeron's northern provinces. Dreadlords of the Burning Legion watched over the Lich King's work, for it was meant to clear the way for their masters' return."],tr:['Frozen Throne\u2019a hapsolmu\u015f olsa da Lich King\u2019in zihni Northrend\u2019in her yan\u0131na uzan\u0131yordu. \xd6r\xfcmcek krall\u0131\u011f\u0131 Azjol-Nerub\u2019u fethetti, halk\u0131n\u0131 hizmetk\xe2r\u0131 olarak diriltti ve Icecrown\u2019daki taht\u0131n\u0131n \xe7evresine bir kale kurdu. Sonra g\xf6z\xfcn\xfc g\xfcneye, sava\u015ftan yorgun d\xfc\u015fm\xfc\u015f insan krall\u0131klar\u0131na \xe7evirdi.',"Dalaran\u2019da sayg\u0131n ba\u015fb\xfcy\xfcc\xfc Kel'Thuzad nekromansiye tak\u0131nt\u0131l\u0131 h\xe2le gelmi\u015fti. Kirin Tor \xe7al\u0131\u015fmalar\u0131n\u0131 reddedince Lich King\u2019in \xe7a\u011fr\u0131s\u0131na kulak verdi, Northrend\u2019e gitti ve onun peygamberi olarak d\xf6nd\xfc. Lordaeron\u2019un yoksullar\u0131na e\u015fitlik ve sonsuz ya\u015fam vaat eden Lanetliler Tarikat\u0131\u2019n\u0131 (Cult of the Damned) kurdu ve \xfcyelerini tah\u0131l sevkiyatlar\u0131na gizlenmi\u015f bir vebay\u0131 yaymak i\xe7in kulland\u0131.",'Veba kurbanlar\u0131n\u0131 \xf6ld\xfcr\xfcyor, sonra onlar\u0131 ak\u0131ls\u0131z \xf6l\xfcms\xfczler, yani Scourge olarak diriltiyordu. Krall\u0131klar vergiler ve toplama kamplar\u0131n\u0131n masraf\u0131 y\xfcz\xfcnden tart\u0131\u015f\u0131rken Lordaeron\u2019un kuzeyindeki k\xf6yler birer birer d\xfc\u015ft\xfc. Kirin Tor ve G\xfcm\xfc\u015f El tehlikeyi anlad\u0131\u011f\u0131nda veba Lordaeron\u2019un kuzey eyaletlerine \xe7oktan yay\u0131lm\u0131\u015ft\u0131. Yanan Lejyon\u2019un deh\u015fet lordlar\u0131 Lich King\u2019in i\u015fini yak\u0131ndan izliyordu; \xe7\xfcnk\xfc bu i\u015f, efendilerinin d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcne yol a\xe7mak i\xe7indi.']},links:{loreIds:['term:lich-king','term:scourge','term:cult-of-the-damned','term:kirin-tor'],zoneIds:['western-plaguelands','eastern-plaguelands','alterac-mountains'],instanceIds:['scholomance'],raceIds:['undead']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Lich King'),(0,n.wiki)("Kel'Thuzad"),(0,n.wiki)('Cult of the Damned'),(0,n.wiki)('Plague of Undeath')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'fall-of-lordaeron',order:16,era:'third-war',when:{en:'The Third War, about 20 years after the Dark Portal',tr:'\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f; Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten yakla\u015f\u0131k 20 y\u0131l sonra'},title:{en:'The Fall of Lordaeron',tr:'Lordaeron\u2019un D\xfc\u015f\xfc\u015f\xfc'},summary:{en:"Prince Arthas hunted the plague to its source, took up Frostmourne and returned to destroy his own kingdom, Quel'Thalas and Dalaran.",tr:"Prens Arthas vebay\u0131 kayna\u011f\u0131na kadar kovalad\u0131, Frostmourne\u2019u ald\u0131 ve kendi krall\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131, Quel'Thalas\u2019\u0131 ve Dalaran\u2019\u0131 yok etmek i\xe7in geri d\xf6nd\xfc."},body:{en:["Prince Arthas Menethil, a young paladin of the Silver Hand, set out with the sorceress Jaina Proudmoore to stop the plague. At Stratholme he found the city's grain already tainted and ordered its people slain before they could rise as undead. Uther and Jaina refused to follow him. Arthas pursued the dreadlord Mal'Ganis to Northrend, burned his own ships so his men could not leave, and claimed the runeblade Frostmourne. The sword took his soul.","Arthas came home as a death knight of the Lich King and murdered his father, King Terenas, in his own throne room. The Scourge swept over Lordaeron. Uther fell defending the urn that held Terenas' ashes, and Arthas led his army into Quel'Thalas, broke the elves' defenses and used the Sunwell to raise Kel'Thuzad as a lich. Sylvanas Windrunner, ranger-general of Silvermoon, died fighting him and was raised as a banshee.","Kel'Thuzad then summoned the demon lord Archimonde in Dalaran, and the Burning Legion returned to Azeroth. Dalaran was smashed, and Lordaeron, the greatest human kingdom, was gone. In the north only scattered survivors, refugees and zealots remained, while Arthas's undead held the land."],tr:["G\xfcm\xfc\u015f El\u2019in gen\xe7 Paladin\u2019i Prens Arthas Menethil, b\xfcy\xfcc\xfc Jaina Proudmoore ile birlikte vebay\u0131 durdurmak i\xe7in yola \xe7\u0131kt\u0131. Stratholme\u2019da \u015fehrin tah\u0131l\u0131n\u0131n \xe7oktan zehirlendi\u011fini g\xf6rd\xfc ve halk\u0131n \xf6l\xfcms\xfcz olarak dirilmeden \xf6nce \xf6ld\xfcr\xfclmesini emretti. Uther ve Jaina onu izlemeyi reddetti. Arthas deh\u015fet lordu Mal'Ganis\u2019i Northrend\u2019e kadar kovalad\u0131, adamlar\u0131 geri d\xf6nemesin diye kendi gemilerini yakt\u0131 ve r\xfcn k\u0131l\u0131c\u0131 Frostmourne\u2019u ald\u0131. K\u0131l\u0131\xe7 onun ruhunu ald\u0131.","Arthas, Lich King\u2019in bir death knight\u2019\u0131 olarak d\xf6nd\xfc ve babas\u0131 Kral Terenas\u2019\u0131 kendi taht odas\u0131nda \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc. Scourge, Lordaeron\u2019u silip s\xfcp\xfcrd\xfc. Uther, Terenas\u2019\u0131n k\xfcllerinin bulundu\u011fu kavanozu korurken d\xfc\u015ft\xfc; Arthas ordusunu Quel'Thalas\u2019a s\xfcrd\xfc, elflerin savunmas\u0131n\u0131 yard\u0131 ve Sunwell\u2019i kullanarak Kel'Thuzad\u2019\u0131 lich olarak diriltti. Silvermoon\u2019un korucu generali Sylvanas Windrunner ona kar\u015f\u0131 sava\u015f\u0131rken \xf6ld\xfc ve bir banshee olarak diriltildi.","Ard\u0131ndan Kel'Thuzad, Dalaran\u2019da iblis lordu Archimonde\u2019u \xe7a\u011f\u0131rd\u0131 ve Yanan Lejyon Azeroth\u2019a d\xf6nd\xfc. Dalaran ezildi; en b\xfcy\xfck insan krall\u0131\u011f\u0131 Lordaeron yok olmu\u015ftu. Kuzeyde yaln\u0131zca da\u011f\u0131n\u0131k sa\u011f kalanlar, m\xfclteciler ve ba\u011fnazlar kald\u0131; topraklara ise Arthas\u2019\u0131n \xf6l\xfcms\xfczleri h\xfckmediyordu."]},links:{loreIds:['item:frostmourne','term:scourge','term:sunwell','term:nathrezim','term:silver-hand'],zoneIds:['tirisfal-glades','eastern-plaguelands','western-plaguelands','alterac-mountains'],instanceIds:['stratholme','city-of-dalaran'],raceIds:['human','undead'],classIds:['paladin']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Third War'),(0,n.wiki)('Arthas Menethil'),(0,n.wiki)('Culling of Stratholme'),(0,n.wiki)('Frostmourne'),(0,n.wiki)("Scourge invasion of Quel'Thalas")],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'battle-for-mount-hyjal',order:17,era:'third-war',when:{en:'The end of the Third War',tr:'\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019\u0131n sonu'},title:{en:'The Battle for Mount Hyjal',tr:'Mount Hyjal Muharebesi'},summary:{en:'Warned by a prophet, orcs and humans sailed to Kalimdor, where they joined the night elves to stop Archimonde at the World Tree.',tr:'Bir k\xe2hinin uyar\u0131s\u0131yla orklar ve insanlar Kalimdor\u2019a yelken a\xe7t\u0131; orada gece elfleriyle birle\u015fip Archimonde\u2019u D\xfcnya A\u011fac\u0131\u2019nda durdurdular.'},body:{en:["A mysterious prophet, Medivh returned from death, urged Thrall and Jaina to sail west to Kalimdor. Thrall's Horde landed on its shores, befriended the tauren of Cairne Bloodhoof and fought its way across the Barrens, and Jaina led refugees from Lordaeron to the same continent. In the forests of Ashenvale, Grom Hellscream and his Warsong clan drank demon blood again and killed the demigod Cenarius.","Thrall and Jaina worked together for the first time to save Grom. In a final duel Grom slew Mannoroth, freeing the orcs from the blood curse at the cost of his own life. Meanwhile Tyrande Whisperwind woke the druids and freed Illidan from the Barrow Deeps, hoping his power would help. Instead he consumed the Skull of Gul'dan, became half demon and was banished by his own brother.","Archimonde marched on Nordrassil to drain its power. Night elves, humans and orcs held the slopes of Mount Hyjal together, buying time while Malfurion prepared a trap. As the demon reached the tree, thousands of wisps swarmed over him and Nordrassil's power tore him apart. The Legion's army was broken, but the World Tree was badly wounded, and the night elves lost the immortality it had granted."],tr:['\xd6l\xfcmden d\xf6nen Medivh olan gizemli bir k\xe2hin, Thrall ile Jaina\u2019y\u0131 bat\u0131ya, Kalimdor\u2019a yelken a\xe7maya \xe7a\u011f\u0131rd\u0131. Thrall\u2019\u0131n Horde\u2019u k\u0131y\u0131lara \xe7\u0131kt\u0131, Cairne Bloodhoof\u2019un taurenleriyle dost oldu ve Barrens\u2019\u0131 sava\u015farak ge\xe7ti; Jaina da Lordaeron m\xfcltecilerini ayn\u0131 k\u0131taya g\xf6t\xfcrd\xfc. Ashenvale ormanlar\u0131nda Grom Hellscream ve Warsong klan\u0131 yeniden iblis kan\u0131 i\xe7ti ve yar\u0131 tanr\u0131 Cenarius\u2019u \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc.',"Thrall ve Jaina ilk kez Grom\u2019u kurtarmak i\xe7in birlikte \xe7al\u0131\u015ft\u0131. Son bir d\xfcelloda Grom, Mannoroth\u2019u \xf6ld\xfcrd\xfc ve kendi hayat\u0131 pahas\u0131na orklar\u0131 kan lanetinden kurtard\u0131. Bu s\u0131rada Tyrande Whisperwind Druid\u2019leri uyand\u0131rd\u0131 ve g\xfcc\xfcn\xfcn i\u015fe yarayaca\u011f\u0131n\u0131 umarak Illidan\u2019\u0131 Barrow Deeps\u2019ten serbest b\u0131rakt\u0131. Illidan ise Gul'dan\u2019\u0131n Kafatas\u0131\u2019n\u0131 (Skull of Gul'dan) yuttu, yar\u0131 iblise d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc ve kendi karde\u015fi taraf\u0131ndan s\xfcrg\xfcn edildi.",'Archimonde g\xfcc\xfcn\xfc emmek i\xe7in Nordrassil\u2019e y\xfcr\xfcd\xfc. Gece elfleri, insanlar ve orklar Mount Hyjal\u2019\u0131n yama\xe7lar\u0131n\u0131 birlikte tutarak Malfurion\u2019un tuza\u011f\u0131n\u0131 haz\u0131rlamas\u0131 i\xe7in zaman kazand\u0131. \u0130blis a\u011faca ula\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131nda binlerce wisp \xfczerine \xfc\u015f\xfc\u015ft\xfc ve Nordrassil\u2019in g\xfcc\xfc onu par\xe7alad\u0131. Lejyon\u2019un ordusu da\u011f\u0131ld\u0131; ama D\xfcnya A\u011fac\u0131 a\u011f\u0131r yara ald\u0131 ve gece elfleri onun bah\u015fetti\u011fi \xf6l\xfcms\xfczl\xfc\u011f\xfc yitirdi.']},links:{loreIds:['item:gorehowl','item:skull-of-guldan','item:horn-of-cenarius','term:nordrassil'],zoneIds:['ashenvale','barrens','mulgore'],instanceIds:['hyjal-summit','barrow-deeps'],raceIds:['night-elf','orc','tauren','human'],classIds:['druid']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Battle of Mount Hyjal'),(0,n.wiki)('Grommash Hellscream'),(0,n.wiki)('Archimonde'),(0,n.wiki)('Illidan Stormrage')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'rise-of-the-forsaken',order:18,era:'third-war',when:{en:'Just after the Third War',tr:'\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019\u0131n hemen ard\u0131ndan'},title:{en:'The Forsaken Rise',tr:'Forsaken\u2019\u0131n Y\xfckseli\u015fi'},summary:{en:'As the Lich King weakened, Sylvanas Windrunner broke free with other undead and claimed the ruins of Lordaeron as the Forsaken.',tr:'Lich King zay\u0131flad\u0131k\xe7a Sylvanas Windrunner di\u011fer \xf6l\xfcms\xfczlerle birlikte \xf6zg\xfcrle\u015fti ve Lordaeron\u2019un harabelerini Forsaken ad\u0131na sahiplendi.'},body:{en:["After Archimonde's fall, the Lich King's grip began to slip. Illidan, now serving Kil'jaeden, struck at the Frozen Throne, and Arthas rushed north to defend his master. In Lordaeron the dreadlords tried to seize the Scourge for themselves, and in the chaos many undead regained their own wills.",'Sylvanas Windrunner was the first. With her banshees and other free undead, and with the dreadlord Varimathras forced to serve her, she defeated her rivals and claimed the ruined capital of Lordaeron. Beneath it lay the old royal crypts and sewers, which became the Undercity. Her people named themselves the Forsaken: no longer human, unwanted by the living and free of the Lich King.',"Arthas reached Icecrown, took up the Lich King's helm and merged with him upon the Frozen Throne, then fell silent behind the ice. The Forsaken, surrounded by enemies, joined Thrall's Horde as uneasy allies, while the Scourge, the Scarlet Crusade and what remained of Lordaeron's nobles fought over the Plaguelands. Forever's story picks up after Warcraft III: Reforged's 'Forsaken Kingdom' campaign, whose events this guide does not yet cover."],tr:["Archimonde\u2019un d\xfc\u015f\xfc\u015f\xfcnden sonra Lich King\u2019in h\xe2kimiyeti gev\u015femeye ba\u015flad\u0131. Art\u0131k Kil'jaeden\u2019e hizmet eden Illidan, Frozen Throne\u2019a sald\u0131rd\u0131 ve Arthas efendisini korumak i\xe7in kuzeye ko\u015ftu. Lordaeron\u2019da deh\u015fet lordlar\u0131 Scourge\u2019u kendileri i\xe7in ele ge\xe7irmeye \xe7al\u0131\u015ft\u0131 ve bu karga\u015fada pek \xe7ok \xf6l\xfcms\xfcz kendi iradesini geri kazand\u0131.",'\u0130lki Sylvanas Windrunner\u2019d\u0131. Banshee\u2019leri ve di\u011fer \xf6zg\xfcr \xf6l\xfcms\xfczlerle, kendisine hizmete zorlad\u0131\u011f\u0131 deh\u015fet lordu Varimathras\u2019\u0131 da yan\u0131na alarak rakiplerini yendi ve Lordaeron\u2019un y\u0131k\u0131k ba\u015fkentini sahiplendi. Alt\u0131ndaki eski kraliyet mahzenleri ve la\u011f\u0131mlar Undercity oldu. Halk\u0131 kendine Forsaken ad\u0131n\u0131 verdi: art\u0131k insan de\u011fillerdi, ya\u015fayanlar onlar\u0131 istemiyordu ve Lich King\u2019den \xf6zg\xfcrd\xfcler.','Arthas Icecrown\u2019a ula\u015ft\u0131, Lich King\u2019in mi\u011fferini takt\u0131 ve Frozen Throne\u2019da onunla birle\u015fti; sonra buzun ard\u0131nda sessizli\u011fe g\xf6m\xfcld\xfc. D\xfc\u015fmanlarla \xe7evrili Forsaken, Thrall\u2019\u0131n Horde\u2019una tedirgin m\xfcttefikler olarak kat\u0131ld\u0131; Plaguelands i\xe7in ise Scourge, Scarlet Crusade ve Lordaeron soylular\u0131ndan geriye kalanlar sava\u015ft\u0131. Forever\u2019\u0131n hik\xe2yesi Warcraft III: Reforged\u2019\u0131n \u2018Forsaken Kingdom\u2019 kampanyas\u0131ndan sonra ba\u015flar; bu rehber o kampanyan\u0131n olaylar\u0131n\u0131 hen\xfcz anlatm\u0131yor.']},links:{loreIds:['term:scourge','term:lich-king','term:nathrezim'],zoneIds:['tirisfal-glades','silverpine-forest','western-plaguelands','eastern-plaguelands'],instanceIds:['ruins-of-lordaeron'],raceIds:['undead'],factionIds:['horde']},image:'instance:ruins-of-lordaeron',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Forsaken'),(0,n.wiki)('Sylvanas Windrunner'),(0,n.wiki)('Undercity'),n.FOREVER.overview],basis:'established',unknowns:[{en:"What happens in Warcraft III: Reforged's 'Forsaken Kingdom' campaign, which Forever follows, is not described in the sources this guide uses.",tr:'Forever\u2019\u0131n devam etti\u011fi Warcraft III: Reforged \u2018Forsaken Kingdom\u2019 kampanyas\u0131nda neler oldu\u011fu, bu rehberin kulland\u0131\u011f\u0131 kaynaklarda anlat\u0131lm\u0131yor.'}]}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'durotar-and-theramore',order:19,era:'new-homes',when:{en:'The years after the Third War',tr:'\xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc Sava\u015f\u2019\u0131 izleyen y\u0131llar'},title:{en:'Durotar and Theramore',tr:'Durotar ve Theramore'},summary:{en:"Thrall founded Durotar and Orgrimmar, Jaina built Theramore, and the two leaders kept a fragile peace even when Jaina's father came to make war.",tr:'Thrall, Durotar\u2019\u0131 ve Orgrimmar\u2019\u0131 kurdu, Jaina Theramore\u2019u in\u015fa etti; iki lider, Jaina\u2019n\u0131n babas\u0131 sava\u015f a\xe7maya geldi\u011finde bile k\u0131r\u0131lgan bar\u0131\u015f\u0131 korudu.'},body:{en:["After Hyjal, Thrall led the orcs to a harsh red land on Kalimdor's eastern coast and named it Durotar, after his father. Their capital, Orgrimmar, honored Orgrim Doomhammer. The tauren of Cairne Bloodhoof settled the grasslands of Mulgore around the mesas of Thunder Bluff, and the Darkspear trolls of Vol'jin, whom Thrall had rescued on his voyage west, made their home on the Echo Isles off Durotar's coast.",'Jaina Proudmoore founded Theramore on an island in Dustwallow Marsh for the human survivors she had brought from Lordaeron. She and Thrall had fought side by side at Hyjal, and they agreed to keep the peace. That peace was tested when her father, Lord Admiral Daelin Proudmoore of Kul Tiras, arrived with his fleet, determined to destroy the orcs.',"Daelin attacked Durotar's coast. Rexxar, a half-ogre wanderer of the Mok'Nathal who became the Horde's champion, united orcs, trolls and tauren against him, and Jaina, torn between her people and her father, allowed the Horde to strike his forces at Theramore. Daelin died in the battle. Jaina mourned him but kept her word, and the uneasy truce between Theramore and Orgrimmar became one of the few bridges between Alliance and Horde."],tr:["Hyjal\u2019dan sonra Thrall orklar\u0131 Kalimdor\u2019un do\u011fu k\u0131y\u0131s\u0131ndaki sert, k\u0131z\u0131l bir topra\u011fa g\xf6t\xfcrd\xfc ve babas\u0131n\u0131n an\u0131s\u0131na ona Durotar ad\u0131n\u0131 verdi. Ba\u015fkentleri Orgrimmar, Orgrim Doomhammer\u2019\u0131 onurland\u0131r\u0131yordu. Cairne Bloodhoof\u2019un taurenleri Mulgore otlaklar\u0131nda Thunder Bluff\u2019\u0131n y\xfcksek d\xfczl\xfcklerinin \xe7evresine yerle\u015fti; Thrall\u2019\u0131n bat\u0131ya yolculu\u011funda kurtard\u0131\u011f\u0131 Vol'jin\u2019in Darkspear trolleri de Durotar k\u0131y\u0131s\u0131 a\xe7\u0131\u011f\u0131ndaki Echo Isles\u2019\u0131 yurt edindi.",'Jaina Proudmoore, Lordaeron\u2019dan getirdi\u011fi insan sa\u011f kalanlar i\xe7in Dustwallow Marsh\u2019taki bir adada Theramore\u2019u kurdu. Jaina ile Thrall Hyjal\u2019da omuz omuza sava\u015fm\u0131\u015ft\u0131 ve bar\u0131\u015f\u0131 korumakta anla\u015ft\u0131lar. Bu bar\u0131\u015f, babas\u0131 Kul Tiras Lord Amirali Daelin Proudmoore orklar\u0131 yok etmeye kararl\u0131 filosuyla gelince s\u0131nand\u0131.',"Daelin, Durotar k\u0131y\u0131lar\u0131na sald\u0131rd\u0131. Mok'Nathal soyundan yar\u0131 ogre bir gezgin olan ve Horde\u2019un \u015fampiyonu olacak Rexxar, orklar\u0131, trolleri ve taurenleri ona kar\u015f\u0131 birle\u015ftirdi; halk\u0131 ile babas\u0131 aras\u0131nda kalan Jaina ise Horde\u2019un Theramore\u2019daki kuvvetlerine sald\u0131rmas\u0131na g\xf6z yumdu. Daelin sava\u015fta \xf6ld\xfc. Jaina onun yas\u0131n\u0131 tuttu ama s\xf6z\xfcnden d\xf6nmedi; Theramore ile Orgrimmar aras\u0131ndaki tedirgin ate\u015fkes, \u0130ttifak ile Horde aras\u0131ndaki az say\u0131daki k\xf6pr\xfcden biri oldu."]},links:{loreIds:['item:doomhammer'],zoneIds:['durotar','mulgore','dustwallow-marsh','barrens'],raceIds:['orc','tauren','troll','human'],factionIds:['horde','alliance'],classIds:['hunter']},image:'race:tauren',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Durotar'),(0,n.wiki)('Theramore Isle'),(0,n.wiki)('Daelin Proudmoore'),(0,n.wiki)('Rexxar')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'stormwind-in-shadow',order:20,era:'classic',when:{en:'Year 25 after the Dark Portal',tr:'Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten sonra 25. y\u0131l'},title:{en:'Stormwind in Shadow',tr:'G\xf6lgedeki Stormwind'},summary:{en:'Rebuilt Stormwind faces a betrayed guild of masons, a vanished king and a dragon hiding at court, while the gnomes have lost their city.',tr:'Yeniden in\u015fa edilen Stormwind; ihanete u\u011fram\u0131\u015f bir ta\u015f ustalar\u0131 loncas\u0131, kaybolan bir kral ve sarayda saklanan bir ejderhayla y\xfczle\u015fiyor; gnomlar ise \u015fehirlerini kaybetmi\u015f durumda.'},body:{en:["After the Second War, the Stonemasons' Guild under Edwin VanCleef rebuilt Stormwind City from its ashes. When the work was done, the House of Nobles refused to pay them. The masons rioted, were driven out and became the Defias Brotherhood, which now preys on Westfall from hidden mines and plots against the crown.",'King Varian Wrynn, the boy Lothar once saved, vanished on his way to a diplomatic meeting at Theramore; rumor says the Defias took him and held him on Alcaz Island. His young son Anduin was crowned, with Highlord Bolvar Fordragon as regent. At court a gracious noblewoman, Lady Katrana Prestor, gained great influence. She was in truth Onyxia, daughter of Deathwing, quietly steering the kingdom toward ruin.',"The Alliance has changed. Lordaeron is lost, and the night elves joined the Alliance after Hyjal. In Dun Morogh, troggs boiled up from below and overran Gnomeregan; the gnomes' desperate attempt to flush them out with radiation poisoned their own city, and High Tinker Mekkatorque led the survivors to shelter in Ironforge. King Magni Bronzebeard rules there, and his Explorers' League digs for the titans' secrets across the world."],tr:["\u0130kinci Sava\u015f\u2019tan sonra Edwin VanCleef \xf6nderli\u011findeki Ta\u015f Ustalar\u0131 Loncas\u0131 (Stonemasons' Guild), Stormwind \u015fehrini k\xfcllerinden yeniden in\u015fa etti. \u0130\u015f bitti\u011finde Soylular Meclisi onlara \xf6deme yapmay\u0131 reddetti. Ustalar ayakland\u0131, \u015fehirden s\xfcr\xfcld\xfc ve Defias Karde\u015fli\u011fi\u2019ne (Defias Brotherhood) d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfc; \u015fimdi gizli madenlerden Westfall\u2019u ya\u011fmal\u0131yor ve tahta kar\u015f\u0131 entrika \xe7eviriyorlar.",'Bir zamanlar Lothar\u2019\u0131n kurtard\u0131\u011f\u0131 \xe7ocuk olan Kral Varian Wrynn, Theramore\u2019daki diplomatik bir g\xf6r\xfc\u015fmeye giderken ortadan kayboldu; s\xf6ylentiye g\xf6re Defias onu ka\xe7\u0131r\u0131p Alcaz Adas\u0131\u2019nda tuttu. K\xfc\xe7\xfck o\u011flu Anduin ta\xe7 giydi, Y\xfcce Lord Bolvar Fordragon da naip oldu. Sarayda zarif bir soylu kad\u0131n, Lady Katrana Prestor b\xfcy\xfck n\xfcfuz kazand\u0131. Asl\u0131nda Deathwing\u2019in k\u0131z\u0131 Onyxia\u2019yd\u0131 ve krall\u0131\u011f\u0131 sessizce y\u0131k\u0131ma s\xfcr\xfckl\xfcyordu.',"\u0130ttifak de\u011fi\u015fti. Lordaeron yitirildi, gece elfleri Hyjal\u2019dan sonra \u0130ttifak\u2019a kat\u0131ld\u0131. Dun Morogh\u2019da trogglar derinlerden f\u0131\u015fk\u0131r\u0131p Gnomeregan\u2019\u0131 istila etti; gnomlar\u0131n onlar\u0131 radyasyonla temizleme \xe7abas\u0131 kendi \u015fehirlerini zehirledi ve Y\xfcce Tamirci (High Tinker) Mekkatorque sa\u011f kalanlar\u0131 Ironforge\u2019a s\u0131\u011f\u0131nd\u0131rd\u0131. Orada Kral Magni Bronzebeard h\xfck\xfcm s\xfcr\xfcyor; K\xe2\u015fifler Birli\u011fi (Explorers' League) d\xfcnyan\u0131n d\xf6rt bir yan\u0131nda titanlar\u0131n s\u0131rlar\u0131n\u0131 kaz\u0131yor."]},links:{loreIds:['term:defias-brotherhood','term:explorers-league','item:head-of-onyxia'],zoneIds:['elwynn-forest','westfall','dustwallow-marsh','dun-morogh'],instanceIds:['deadmines','stormwind-stockade','alcaz-prison','gnomeregan','onyxias-lair'],raceIds:['human','gnome','dwarf','night-elf'],factionIds:['alliance']},image:'art:heroes',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Defias Brotherhood'),(0,n.wiki)('Varian Wrynn'),(0,n.wiki)('Onyxia'),(0,n.wiki)('Gnomeregan'),n.FOREVER.dungeons],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'fire-beneath-blackrock',order:21,era:'classic',when:{en:'Year 25 after the Dark Portal',tr:'Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten sonra 25. y\u0131l'},title:{en:'Fire Beneath Blackrock',tr:'Blackrock\u2019un Alt\u0131ndaki Ate\u015f'},summary:{en:"In Blackrock Mountain the Dark Iron dwarves serve Ragnaros while Nefarian's orcs hold the spire above, and Onyxia guards her brood in Dustwallow Marsh.",tr:'Blackrock Da\u011f\u0131\u2019nda Dark Iron c\xfcceleri Ragnaros\u2019a hizmet ederken Nefarian\u2019\u0131n orklar\u0131 yukar\u0131daki kuleyi tutuyor; Onyxia ise Dustwallow Marsh\u2019ta yavrular\u0131n\u0131 koruyor.'},body:{en:["Two centuries after Thaurissan's mistake, his descendants still rule beneath Blackrock Mountain. Emperor Dagran Thaurissan holds court in the Dark Iron city of Shadowforge, deep in Blackrock Depths, while Ragnaros burns in the Molten Core below and the dwarves toil for him. Princess Moira Bronzebeard, daughter of King Magni, came to the mountain as a captive and stayed as the emperor's wife, to her father's fury.","The upper halls belong to the black dragonflight. Nefarian, Deathwing's son, rules Blackwing Lair in the guise of Lord Victor Nefarius and commands the Blackrock orcs who never joined Thrall, led by Warchief Rend Blackhand in Blackrock Spire. Fire and shadow wage a cold war inside the same mountain, and the Burning Steppes and the Searing Gorge suffer for it.","Nefarian's sister Onyxia, the false Lady Prestor, keeps her lair in Dustwallow Marsh, where she guards her brood. Reaching her takes the Drakefire Amulet, earned through a long questline for each faction that leads through Blackrock Spire. In Forever, Onyxia's Lair is one of three raids that open on December 9, beside two new raids on Mount Hyjal."],tr:['Thaurissan\u2019\u0131n hatas\u0131ndan iki y\xfczy\u0131l sonra torunlar\u0131 h\xe2l\xe2 Blackrock Da\u011f\u0131\u2019n\u0131n alt\u0131nda h\xfck\xfcm s\xfcr\xfcyor. \u0130mparator Dagran Thaurissan, Blackrock Depths\u2019in derinliklerindeki Dark Iron \u015fehri Shadowforge\u2019da saray kuruyor; a\u015fa\u011f\u0131da Molten Core\u2019da Ragnaros yan\u0131yor ve c\xfcceler onun i\xe7in \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor. Kral Magni\u2019nin k\u0131z\u0131 Prenses Moira Bronzebeard da\u011fa esir olarak geldi ve babas\u0131n\u0131 \xf6fkelendirerek imparatorun kar\u0131s\u0131 olarak kald\u0131.','\xdcst salonlar kara ejderha soyuna ait. Deathwing\u2019in o\u011flu Nefarian, Lord Victor Nefarius k\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131nda Blackwing Lair\u2019e h\xfckmediyor ve Thrall\u2019a hi\xe7 kat\u0131lmam\u0131\u015f Blackrock orklar\u0131n\u0131, Blackrock Spire\u2019daki Sava\u015f Reisi Rend Blackhand arac\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131yla y\xf6netiyor. Ate\u015f ve g\xf6lge ayn\u0131 da\u011f\u0131n i\xe7inde so\u011fuk bir sava\u015f s\xfcrd\xfcr\xfcyor; bedelini Burning Steppes ve Searing Gorge \xf6d\xfcyor.',"Nefarian\u2019\u0131n k\u0131z karde\u015fi, sahte Lady Prestor olan Onyxia, Dustwallow Marsh\u2019taki ininde yavrular\u0131n\u0131 koruyor. Ona ula\u015fmak i\xe7in her taraf i\xe7in ayr\u0131, Blackrock Spire\u2019dan ge\xe7en uzun bir g\xf6rev zinciriyle kazan\u0131lan Drakefire Amulet gerekiyor. Forever\u2019da Onyxia's Lair, Mount Hyjal\u2019daki iki yeni bask\u0131nla birlikte 9 Aral\u0131k\u2019ta a\xe7\u0131lan \xfc\xe7 bask\u0131ndan biri."]},links:{loreIds:['item:sulfuras','item:thunderfury','item:seal-of-ascension','item:drakefire-amulet','item:head-of-onyxia','term:elemental-lords'],zoneIds:['burning-steppes','searing-gorge','dustwallow-marsh'],instanceIds:['blackrock-depths','lower-blackrock-spire','onyxias-lair','barrow-deeps','hyjal-summit'],raceIds:['dwarf','orc']},image:'icon:inv_misc_head_dragon_01',sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Blackrock Mountain'),(0,n.wiki)('Dagran Thaurissan'),(0,n.wiki)('Nefarian'),(0,n.wiki)('Onyxia'),n.FOREVER.raids],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'plaguelands-and-the-scarlet-crusade',order:22,era:'classic',when:{en:'Year 25 after the Dark Portal',tr:'Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019ten sonra 25. y\u0131l'},title:{en:'The Plaguelands and the Scarlet Crusade',tr:'Plaguelands ve Scarlet Crusade'},summary:{en:"Kel'Thuzad's Scourge holds the north, zealots of the Scarlet Crusade fight undead and living alike, and a few steadfast orders hold the line.",tr:"Kel'Thuzad\u2019\u0131n Scourge\u2019u kuzeyi tutuyor, Scarlet Crusade ba\u011fnazlar\u0131 \xf6l\xfcms\xfczlerle de ya\u015fayanlarla da sava\u015f\u0131yor; birka\xe7 kararl\u0131 tarikat ise hatt\u0131 koruyor."},body:{en:["Lordaeron's heartland is now the Plaguelands. Kel'Thuzad commands the Scourge there from the floating necropolis Naxxramas, Baron Rivendare rules the undead in ruined Stratholme, and in the Barov family's old school, Scholomance, the Cult of the Damned trains new necromancers.","Survivors of the Silver Hand regrouped as the Scarlet Crusade, sworn to burn the plague from the land. Their Grand Crusader, Saidan Dathrohan, is secretly the dreadlord Balnazzar, and the Crusade has grown so fanatical that it kills any outsider it suspects of taint. Its strongholds include the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades, Hearthglen, Tyr's Hand and a bastion in Stratholme. Even its heroes carry darker stories: Renault Mograine betrayed his father Alexandros, the Ashbringer, to his death.","Not every paladin became a zealot. Those who refused the Crusade's cruelty formed the Argent Dawn, which works with anyone who fights the Scourge, from Light's Hope Chapel. The exiled paladin Tirion Fordring lives as a hermit near Hearthglen, and the Forsaken push north from Tirisfal. The fate of Lordaeron is still undecided."],tr:["Lordaeron\u2019un kalbi art\u0131k Plaguelands. Kel'Thuzad orada Scourge\u2019u u\xe7an nekropol Naxxramas\u2019tan y\xf6netiyor; Baron Rivendare y\u0131k\u0131k Stratholme\u2019daki \xf6l\xfcms\xfczlere h\xfckmediyor ve Barov ailesinin eski okulu Scholomance\u2019ta Lanetliler Tarikat\u0131 yeni nekromanslar yeti\u015ftiriyor.","G\xfcm\xfc\u015f El\u2019in sa\u011f kalanlar\u0131, vebay\u0131 topraktan yakarak silmeye yeminli Scarlet Crusade olarak yeniden topland\u0131. B\xfcy\xfck Ha\xe7l\u0131 (Grand Crusader) Saidan Dathrohan asl\u0131nda gizlice deh\u015fet lordu Balnazzar ve tarikat \xf6yle ba\u011fnazla\u015ft\u0131 ki lekeli oldu\u011fundan \u015f\xfcphelendi\u011fi her yabanc\u0131y\u0131 \xf6ld\xfcr\xfcyor. Kaleleri aras\u0131nda Tirisfal Glades\u2019teki Scarlet Monastery, Hearthglen, Tyr's Hand ve Stratholme\u2019daki bir bur\xe7 var. Kahramanlar\u0131n\u0131n bile karanl\u0131k hik\xe2yeleri var: Renault Mograine, Ashbringer diye bilinen babas\u0131 Alexandros\u2019a ihanet ederek \xf6l\xfcm\xfcne yol a\xe7t\u0131.","Her Paladin ba\u011fnaz olmad\u0131. Tarikat\u0131n zalimli\u011fini reddedenler, Light's Hope Chapel\u2019dan Scourge\u2019la sava\u015fan herkesle i\u015f birli\u011fi yapan Argent Dawn\u2019u kurdu. S\xfcrg\xfcndeki Paladin Tirion Fordring, Hearthglen yak\u0131nlar\u0131nda bir m\xfcnzevi gibi ya\u015f\u0131yor; Forsaken ise Tirisfal\u2019dan kuzeye ilerliyor. Lordaeron\u2019un kaderi hen\xfcz belirlenmedi."]},links:{loreIds:['term:scarlet-crusade','term:argent-dawn','term:scourge','term:cult-of-the-damned','item:ashbringer','item:taelans-hammer','item:phylactery-of-kelthuzad'],zoneIds:['western-plaguelands','eastern-plaguelands','tirisfal-glades'],instanceIds:['stratholme','scholomance','scarlet-monastery-graveyard','scarlet-monastery-library','scarlet-monastery-armory','scarlet-monastery-cathedral'],raceIds:['human','undead'],classIds:['paladin','priest']},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('Scarlet Crusade'),(0,n.wiki)('Argent Dawn'),(0,n.wiki)('Naxxramas'),(0,n.wiki)('Plaguelands'),(0,n.wiki)('Alexandros Mograine')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'azeroth-in-year-twenty-five',order:23,era:'classic',when:{en:'Year 25: the setting of Forever',tr:'25. y\u0131l: Forever\u2019\u0131n d\xf6nemi'},title:{en:'Azeroth in Year 25',tr:'25. Y\u0131lda Azeroth'},summary:{en:"The world of World of Warcraft's first year, where Forever's story is set: a fragile peace, old threats stirring and new places on the map.",tr:'World of Warcraft\u2019\u0131n ilk y\u0131l\u0131ndaki d\xfcnya; Forever\u2019\u0131n hik\xe2yesi burada ge\xe7er: k\u0131r\u0131lgan bir bar\u0131\u015f, k\u0131p\u0131rdanan eski tehditler ve haritadaki yeni yerler.'},body:{en:["Twenty-five years after the Dark Portal first opened, Azeroth is a world of survivors. The Alliance of Stormwind, Ironforge, the gnomes and the night elves faces a Horde of orcs, trolls, tauren and Forsaken, and neither side trusts the other. Old enemies wake at the edges of the map: servants of the Old God C'Thun in Silithus, priests of the blood god Hakkar in the troll ruins of the south, and the corruption of the Emerald Nightmare creeping into the dreams of druids.","World of Warcraft: Forever is set in exactly this moment. Blizzard keeps it there indefinitely, after Warcraft III: Reforged's 'Forsaken Kingdom' campaign and before The Burning Crusade, and says its story does not share retail World of Warcraft's continuity. Forever adds places the original game never had: the Riverglades east of the Badlands, where Farholde Keep holds out against the Twilight's Hammer; a Dalaran under restoration whose hiding barrier has fallen; and dungeons from the royal tombs of the Hall of Thanes to the titan facility of Shaper's Terrace.",'Forever also opens a new people to players: the Skyborne of Zephras Isle, an island floating in Skywall, the Elemental Plane of Air. Its air elementals vanished centuries ago and the magic holding the island aloft is fading; its High Order serve the Alliance and its Windshapers the Horde. How these stories end is still being written. Blizzard has announced new raids, dungeons and a legendary questline for 2027, and the raids of Mount Hyjal open on December 9.'],tr:["Kara Ge\xe7it\u2019in ilk a\xe7\u0131l\u0131\u015f\u0131ndan yirmi be\u015f y\u0131l sonra Azeroth, hayatta kalanlar\u0131n d\xfcnyas\u0131. Stormwind, Ironforge, gnomlar ve gece elflerinden olu\u015fan \u0130ttifak; orklar, troller, taurenler ve Forsaken\u2019dan olu\u015fan Horde\u2019la kar\u015f\u0131 kar\u015f\u0131ya ve iki taraf birbirine g\xfcvenmiyor. Haritan\u0131n kenarlar\u0131nda eski d\xfc\u015fmanlar uyan\u0131yor: Silithus\u2019ta Kadim Tanr\u0131 C'Thun\u2019un hizmetk\xe2rlar\u0131, g\xfcneyin trol harabelerinde kan tanr\u0131s\u0131 Hakkar\u2019\u0131n Priest\u2019leri ve Druid\u2019lerin r\xfcyalar\u0131na s\u0131zan Z\xfcmr\xfct K\xe2bus (Emerald Nightmare) yozla\u015fmas\u0131.","World of Warcraft: Forever tam olarak bu anda ge\xe7er. Blizzard onu s\xfcresiz olarak burada, Warcraft III: Reforged\u2019\u0131n \u2018Forsaken Kingdom\u2019 kampanyas\u0131ndan sonra ve The Burning Crusade\u2019den \xf6nce tutuyor; hik\xe2yesinin g\xfcn\xfcm\xfcz World of Warcraft\u2019\u0131n\u0131n s\xfcreklili\u011fini payla\u015fmad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 s\xf6yl\xfcyor. Forever, \xf6zg\xfcn oyunda hi\xe7 olmayan yerler ekliyor: Farholde Kalesi\u2019nin Twilight's Hammer\u2019a kar\u015f\u0131 direndi\u011fi, Badlands\u2019in do\u011fusundaki Riverglades; gizleyen bariyeri d\xfc\u015fm\xfc\u015f, yeniden in\u015fa edilen bir Dalaran; ve Hall of Thanes\u2019in kraliyet mezarlar\u0131ndan titan tesisi Shaper's Terrace\u2019a uzanan zindanlar.",'Forever oyunculara yeni bir halk\u0131 da a\xe7\u0131yor: Hava\u2019n\u0131n Elemental D\xfczlemi Skywall\u2019da s\xfcz\xfclen bir ada olan Zephras Isle\u2019\u0131n Skyborne\u2019u. Adan\u0131n hava elementalleri y\xfczy\u0131llar \xf6nce kayboldu ve aday\u0131 havada tutan b\xfcy\xfc zay\u0131fl\u0131yor; High Order \u0130ttifak\u2019a, Windshaper\u2019lar ise Horde\u2019a hizmet ediyor. Bu hik\xe2yelerin nas\u0131l bitece\u011fi h\xe2l\xe2 yaz\u0131l\u0131yor. Blizzard 2027 i\xe7in yeni bask\u0131nlar, zindanlar ve efsanevi bir g\xf6rev zinciri duyurdu; Mount Hyjal bask\u0131nlar\u0131 ise 9 Aral\u0131k\u2019ta a\xe7\u0131l\u0131yor.']},links:{loreIds:['term:old-gods','term:emerald-dream','term:skywall','term:ley-lines','term:twilights-hammer','item:heart-of-hakkar','item:scepter-of-the-shifting-sands'],zoneIds:['silithus','riverglades','badlands','alterac-mountains','zephras-isle'],instanceIds:['city-of-dalaran','hall-of-thanes','shapers-terrace','temple-of-atalhakkar','wailing-caverns','barrow-deeps','hyjal-summit'],raceIds:['skyborne-high-order','skyborne-windshaper'],factionIds:['alliance','horde']},image:'art:forever',sources:[n.FOREVER.overview,n.FOREVER.dungeons,n.FOREVER.raids,n.FOREVER.riverglades,n.FOREVER.zephrasIsle,(0,n.wiki)("C'Thun"),(0,n.wiki)('Hakkar the Soulflayer'),(0,n.wiki)('Emerald Nightmare')],basis:'established'}),(0,n.lore)({category:'chapter',slug:'after-classic',order:24,era:'beyond',when:{en:'Later expansions (not part of Forever)',tr:'Sonraki geni\u015fleme paketleri (Forever\u2019da yok)'},title:{en:'Epilogue: After Classic',tr:'Son S\xf6z: Classic\u2019ten Sonra'},summary:{en:'In the original timeline the story went on through Outland, Northrend and beyond; Forever stays in year 25 and tells its own.',tr:'\xd6zg\xfcn zaman \xe7izgisinde hik\xe2ye Outland\u2019den, Northrend\u2019den ve \xf6tesinden devam etti; Forever ise 25. y\u0131lda kal\u0131p kendi hik\xe2yesini anlat\u0131yor.'},body:{en:["In World of Warcraft's original timeline, the story kept moving. The Dark Portal reopened, and The Burning Crusade carried adventurers to Outland, where Illidan and Kael'thas Sunstrider fell. In Wrath of the Lich King, Alliance and Horde marched on Northrend, and Arthas was defeated atop Icecrown Citadel. In Cataclysm, Deathwing burst from the depths and broke the face of the world before the Aspects and their mortal allies struck him down.","Later expansions carried the saga to Pandaria, an alternate Draenor, the Burning Legion's final defeat at Argus, open war between the factions, the realms of the dead, the Dragon Isles and the long struggle around Azeroth's own world-soul. Many places in this guide changed beyond recognition along the way.","World of Warcraft: Forever takes none of these roads. It stays in year 25, in a 'time bubble' outside retail continuity, and builds its future on the foundations of the original world. Blizzard's roadmap promises new raids, dungeons, quests and a revamped iconic raid in 2027, so the next chapters of this story will be Forever's own."],tr:["World of Warcraft\u2019\u0131n \xf6zg\xfcn zaman \xe7izgisinde hik\xe2ye ilerlemeye devam etti. Kara Ge\xe7it yeniden a\xe7\u0131ld\u0131 ve The Burning Crusade macerac\u0131lar\u0131 Illidan\u2019\u0131n ve Kael'thas Sunstrider\u2019\u0131n d\xfc\u015ft\xfc\u011f\xfc Outland\u2019e ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131. Wrath of the Lich King\u2019de \u0130ttifak ve Horde Northrend\u2019e y\xfcr\xfcd\xfc ve Arthas, Icecrown Citadel\u2019in tepesinde yenildi. Cataclysm\u2019de Deathwing derinliklerden f\u0131rlad\u0131 ve d\xfcnyan\u0131n y\xfcz\xfcn\xfc par\xe7alad\u0131; sonunda Aspect\u2019ler ve \xf6l\xfcml\xfc m\xfcttefikleri onu yere serdi.",'Sonraki geni\u015fleme paketleri destan\u0131 Pandaria\u2019ya, alternatif bir Draenor\u2019a, Yanan Lejyon\u2019un Argus\u2019taki son yenilgisine, taraflar aras\u0131 a\xe7\u0131k sava\u015fa, \xf6l\xfcler diyarlar\u0131na, Dragon Isles\u2019a ve Azeroth\u2019un kendi d\xfcnya ruhu etraf\u0131ndaki uzun m\xfccadeleye ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131. Bu rehberdeki pek \xe7ok yer bu yolculukta tan\u0131nmayacak kadar de\u011fi\u015fti.','World of Warcraft: Forever bu yollar\u0131n hi\xe7birine girmiyor. G\xfcn\xfcm\xfcz s\xfcreklili\u011finin d\u0131\u015f\u0131nda, bir \u2018zaman balonu\u2019 i\xe7inde 25. y\u0131lda kal\u0131yor ve gelece\u011fini \xf6zg\xfcn d\xfcnyan\u0131n temelleri \xfczerine kuruyor. Blizzard\u2019\u0131n yol haritas\u0131 2027 i\xe7in yeni bask\u0131nlar, zindanlar, g\xf6revler ve yenilenmi\u015f ikonik bir bask\u0131n vaat ediyor; yani bu hik\xe2yenin sonraki b\xf6l\xfcmleri Forever\u2019\u0131n kendisine ait olacak.']},links:{},sources:[(0,n.wiki)('World of Warcraft: The Burning Crusade'),(0,n.wiki)('World of Warcraft: Wrath of the Lich King'),(0,n.wiki)('World of Warcraft: Cataclysm'),n.FOREVER.overview],basis:'established'})]},871,[866]);
